{"jobs":[{"id":"3c0780fd-6a71-44cf-8fa8-33cd5fb4431a","title":"Billing Specialist","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-18T10:32:53.615+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/3c0780fd-6a71-44cf-8fa8-33cd5fb4431a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/3c0780fd-6a71-44cf-8fa8-33cd5fb4431a/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a <strong>Billing Specialist</strong> to support accurate and timely billing processes across the organization. You will review invoices and billing information, maintain records, resolve discrepancies, and work with internal teams to keep billing activities running smoothly.</p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare, review, and process invoices</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Verify billing information for accuracy and completeness</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Update billing records and account information</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Investigate and resolve billing discrepancies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Respond to basic billing questions and requests</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain organized billing documentation and records</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with internal teams to resolve billing issues</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous billing, accounts receivable, bookkeeping, or administrative experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and accuracy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with spreadsheets and financial information</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good organization and time-management skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and problem-solving skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working independently in a remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable internet connection and suitable workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with billing or accounting software</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Accounts payable or accounts receivable experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in food service, retail, hospitality, or healthcare</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$20–$27 per hour</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Application review → Initial conversation → Interview → Offer</strong></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p>","descriptionPlain":"We are looking for a Billing Specialist to support accurate and timely billing processes across the organization. You will review invoices and billing information, maintain records, resolve discrepancies, and work with internal teams to keep billing activities running smoothly.\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Prepare, review, and process invoices\n\n - Verify billing information for accuracy and completeness\n\n - Update billing records and account information\n\n - Investigate and resolve billing discrepancies\n\n - Respond to basic billing questions and requests\n\n - Maintain organized billing documentation and records\n\n - Work with internal teams to resolve billing issues\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - Previous billing, accounts receivable, bookkeeping, or administrative experience\n\n - Strong attention to detail and accuracy\n\n - Comfortable working with spreadsheets and financial information\n\n - Good organization and time-management skills\n\n - Strong communication and problem-solving skills\n\n - Comfortable working independently in a remote environment\n\n - Reliable internet connection and suitable workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with billing or accounting software\n\n - Accounts payable or accounts receivable experience\n\n - Experience in food service, retail, hospitality, or healthcare\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$20–$27 per hour, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → Initial conversation → Interview → Offer\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nBilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\n\n\n","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"1f9d119f-e628-48c9-9574-5daf61b3978a","title":"Scheduling Coordinator","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-18T10:36:26.742+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/1f9d119f-e628-48c9-9574-5daf61b3978a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/1f9d119f-e628-48c9-9574-5daf61b3978a/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a <strong>Scheduling Coordinator</strong> to help keep schedules organized across our operations. You will coordinate appointments and availability, update schedules, communicate changes, and help ensure teams have the coverage they need.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is ideal for someone who is organized, responsive, and comfortable managing multiple scheduling requests throughout the day.</p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate schedules, appointments, and availability</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Update scheduling systems and maintain accurate records</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate schedule changes to employees, managers, and other teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Resolve scheduling conflicts and identify coverage gaps</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow up on schedule requests and outstanding changes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support managers with day-to-day scheduling needs</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous experience in scheduling, administration, customer service, or a similar role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organization and attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good communication and follow-up skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable managing multiple priorities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic computer and spreadsheet skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently in a remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable internet connection and suitable workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Scheduling or workforce management experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in hospitality, food service, healthcare, or retail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with scheduling or workforce management software</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$19–$25 per hour</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Application review → Initial conversation → Interview → Offer</strong></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Seniority Level:</strong> Junior</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p>","descriptionPlain":"We are looking for a Scheduling Coordinator to help keep schedules organized across our operations. You will coordinate appointments and availability, update schedules, communicate changes, and help ensure teams have the coverage they need.\n\nThis role is ideal for someone who is organized, responsive, and comfortable managing multiple scheduling requests throughout the day.\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Coordinate schedules, appointments, and availability\n\n - Update scheduling systems and maintain accurate records\n\n - Communicate schedule changes to employees, managers, and other teams\n\n - Resolve scheduling conflicts and identify coverage gaps\n\n - Follow up on schedule requests and outstanding changes\n\n - Support managers with day-to-day scheduling needs\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - Previous experience in scheduling, administration, customer service, or a similar role\n\n - Strong organization and attention to detail\n\n - Good communication and follow-up skills\n\n - Comfortable managing multiple priorities\n\n - Basic computer and spreadsheet skills\n\n - Ability to work independently in a remote environment\n\n - Reliable internet connection and suitable workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Scheduling or workforce management experience\n\n - Experience in hospitality, food service, healthcare, or retail\n\n - Familiarity with scheduling or workforce management software\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$19–$25 per hour, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → Initial conversation → Interview → Offer\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nBilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSeniority Level: Junior\n\n","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"d9b5d8a8-4270-4530-9460-0f6682707ec3","title":"Operations Assistant","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-18T10:34:06.732+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/d9b5d8a8-4270-4530-9460-0f6682707ec3","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/d9b5d8a8-4270-4530-9460-0f6682707ec3/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for an <strong>Operations Assistant</strong> to support day-to-day business operations and help keep administrative processes organized. You will maintain records, coordinate tasks, follow up on operational requests, and support managers and teams across the company.</p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support daily administrative and operational tasks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate records, spreadsheets, and company systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate requests and follow up with internal teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track tasks, deadlines, and operational updates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare basic reports and documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help identify and resolve routine operational issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide general support to managers and teams</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous experience in operations, administration, customer service, or a similar role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organization and attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good communication and follow-up skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with spreadsheets and business systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to manage multiple priorities independently</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good problem-solving skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working remotely</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable internet connection and suitable workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Operations or coordination experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in food service, hospitality, retail, or healthcare</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with CRM, project management, or other business systems</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$19–$25 per hour</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Application review → Initial conversation → Interview → Offer</strong></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Seniority Level:</strong> Junior</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p>","descriptionPlain":"We are looking for an Operations Assistant to support day-to-day business operations and help keep administrative processes organized. You will maintain records, coordinate tasks, follow up on operational requests, and support managers and teams across the company.\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Support daily administrative and operational tasks\n\n - Maintain accurate records, spreadsheets, and company systems\n\n - Coordinate requests and follow up with internal teams\n\n - Track tasks, deadlines, and operational updates\n\n - Prepare basic reports and documentation\n\n - Help identify and resolve routine operational issues\n\n - Provide general support to managers and teams\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - Previous experience in operations, administration, customer service, or a similar role\n\n - Strong organization and attention to detail\n\n - Good communication and follow-up skills\n\n - Comfortable working with spreadsheets and business systems\n\n - Ability to manage multiple priorities independently\n\n - Good problem-solving skills\n\n - Comfortable working remotely\n\n - Reliable internet connection and suitable workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Operations or coordination experience\n\n - Experience in food service, hospitality, retail, or healthcare\n\n - Experience with CRM, project management, or other business systems\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$19–$25 per hour, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → Initial conversation → Interview → Offer\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nBilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSeniority Level: Junior\n\n","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"f573213f-3511-4018-84a9-67cca8e58c5b","title":"Order Processing Specialist","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-18T10:37:47.430+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/f573213f-3511-4018-84a9-67cca8e58c5b","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/f573213f-3511-4018-84a9-67cca8e58c5b/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for an <strong>Order Processing Specialist</strong> to help keep our order and customer information accurate and up to date. You will review incoming orders, enter information into company systems, check details for accuracy, and work with internal teams when clarification is needed.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is a good fit for someone who is organized, detail-oriented, and comfortable working with repetitive tasks while maintaining accuracy.</p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enter and process customer orders in company systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review orders for accuracy and completeness</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Update order and customer information as needed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify missing or incorrect information and follow up when necessary</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate with internal teams to resolve order issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate records and documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Complete assigned orders and tasks within established deadlines</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous experience in data entry, order processing, customer service, administration, or a similar role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and accuracy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good computer and typing skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with spreadsheets and business systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Organized and able to manage repetitive tasks consistently</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good communication and problem-solving skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working independently in a remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable internet connection and suitable workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Order entry or order processing experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in food service, retail, hospitality, or customer service</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with CRM, ERP, or order management systems</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$18–$23 per hour</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Application review → Initial conversation → Interview → Offer</strong></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p>","descriptionPlain":"We are looking for an Order Processing Specialist to help keep our order and customer information accurate and up to date. You will review incoming orders, enter information into company systems, check details for accuracy, and work with internal teams when clarification is needed.\n\nThis role is a good fit for someone who is organized, detail-oriented, and comfortable working with repetitive tasks while maintaining accuracy.\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Enter and process customer orders in company systems\n\n - Review orders for accuracy and completeness\n\n - Update order and customer information as needed\n\n - Identify missing or incorrect information and follow up when necessary\n\n - Coordinate with internal teams to resolve order issues\n\n - Maintain accurate records and documentation\n\n - Complete assigned orders and tasks within established deadlines\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - Previous experience in data entry, order processing, customer service, administration, or a similar role\n\n - Strong attention to detail and accuracy\n\n - Good computer and typing skills\n\n - Comfortable working with spreadsheets and business systems\n\n - Organized and able to manage repetitive tasks consistently\n\n - Good communication and problem-solving skills\n\n - Comfortable working independently in a remote environment\n\n - Reliable internet connection and suitable workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Order entry or order processing experience\n\n - Experience in food service, retail, hospitality, or customer service\n\n - Experience with CRM, ERP, or order management systems\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$18–$23 per hour, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → Initial conversation → Interview → Offer\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nBilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\n","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"87399f9c-89ee-4418-814a-e1762103b4ef","title":"Records Clerk","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-18T10:31:35.005+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/87399f9c-89ee-4418-814a-e1762103b4ef","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/87399f9c-89ee-4418-814a-e1762103b4ef/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a <strong>Records Clerk</strong> to help maintain accurate and organized company records. You will enter, update, review, and organize information across digital systems and documents while ensuring records are complete and easy to access.</p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enter and update information in company systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review records for accuracy and completeness</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Organize digital files and documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify missing or incorrect information and flag it for review</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate records and databases</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with basic document and data verification</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow established record-keeping procedures</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous data entry, administrative, records, or customer service experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and accuracy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good typing and computer skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with spreadsheets and digital files</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Organized and able to manage repetitive tasks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently in a remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable internet connection and suitable workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Data entry or records management experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Excel or Google Sheets</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in food service, healthcare, retail, or administration</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$17–$22 per hour</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Application review → Initial conversation → Interview → Offer</strong></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Seniority Level:</strong> Junior</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p>","descriptionPlain":"We are looking for a Records Clerk to help maintain accurate and organized company records. You will enter, update, review, and organize information across digital systems and documents while ensuring records are complete and easy to access.\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Enter and update information in company systems\n\n - Review records for accuracy and completeness\n\n - Organize digital files and documentation\n\n - Identify missing or incorrect information and flag it for review\n\n - Maintain accurate records and databases\n\n - Assist with basic document and data verification\n\n - Follow established record-keeping procedures\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - Previous data entry, administrative, records, or customer service experience\n\n - Strong attention to detail and accuracy\n\n - Good typing and computer skills\n\n - Comfortable working with spreadsheets and digital files\n\n - Organized and able to manage repetitive tasks\n\n - Ability to work independently in a remote environment\n\n - Reliable internet connection and suitable workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Data entry or records management experience\n\n - Experience with Excel or Google Sheets\n\n - Experience in food service, healthcare, retail, or administration\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$17–$22 per hour, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → Initial conversation → Interview → Offer\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nBilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSeniority Level: Junior\n\n","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"b81aa061-1c2b-4b8e-bea3-834644d97bd6","title":"Chat Support Representative","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-18T10:35:17.129+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/b81aa061-1c2b-4b8e-bea3-834644d97bd6","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/b81aa061-1c2b-4b8e-bea3-834644d97bd6/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a <strong>Chat Support Representative</strong> to assist customers through online chat and provide quick, helpful answers to their questions and service requests.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will handle multiple conversations throughout the day, resolve common issues, and work with internal teams when additional support is needed.</p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Respond to customer questions through online chat</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Resolve common customer issues and service requests</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide accurate information about orders, services, and locations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Escalate issues that require additional support</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Document customer interactions in company systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain a friendly and professional tone across all conversations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meet established response and service-quality standards</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous customer service, chat support, retail, hospitality, or similar experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written English and communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good typing and multitasking skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Patient, friendly, and customer-focused approach</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable handling multiple conversations at once</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic computer skills and ability to learn new systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently in a remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable internet connection and suitable workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous chat or online customer support experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with CRM or customer support platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Food service, hospitality, or retail experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilingual English/Spanish skills</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$17–$23 per hour</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Application review → Initial conversation → Interview → Offer</strong></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Seniority Level:</strong> Junior</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p>","descriptionPlain":"We are looking for a Chat Support Representative to assist customers through online chat and provide quick, helpful answers to their questions and service requests.\n\nYou will handle multiple conversations throughout the day, resolve common issues, and work with internal teams when additional support is needed.\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Respond to customer questions through online chat\n\n - Resolve common customer issues and service requests\n\n - Provide accurate information about orders, services, and locations\n\n - Escalate issues that require additional support\n\n - Document customer interactions in company systems\n\n - Maintain a friendly and professional tone across all conversations\n\n - Meet established response and service-quality standards\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - Previous customer service, chat support, retail, hospitality, or similar experience\n\n - Strong written English and communication skills\n\n - Good typing and multitasking skills\n\n - Patient, friendly, and customer-focused approach\n\n - Comfortable handling multiple conversations at once\n\n - Basic computer skills and ability to learn new systems\n\n - Ability to work independently in a remote environment\n\n - Reliable internet connection and suitable workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Previous chat or online customer support experience\n\n - Experience with CRM or customer support platforms\n\n - Food service, hospitality, or retail experience\n\n - Bilingual English/Spanish skills\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$17–$23 per hour, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → Initial conversation → Interview → Offer\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nBilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSeniority Level: Junior\n\n","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"16a05400-c76d-4f15-928a-762bd3d56583","title":"Customer Support Coordinator","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-18T10:30:23.803+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/16a05400-c76d-4f15-928a-762bd3d56583","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/16a05400-c76d-4f15-928a-762bd3d56583/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a <strong>Customer Support Coordinator</strong> to help manage customer requests and coordinate their resolution. You will communicate with customers, track open issues, and work with internal teams to make sure requests are handled efficiently and professionally.</p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Respond to customer questions and service requests</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track and coordinate open customer issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with internal teams to resolve requests</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow up with customers and provide updates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate customer records and support notes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify recurring issues and share customer feedback</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help maintain a consistent, positive customer experience</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous customer service, support, coordination, or administrative experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written and verbal communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good organization and follow-up skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Customer-focused and professional approach</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable managing multiple requests at once</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic computer skills and ability to learn new systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working independently in a remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable internet connection and suitable workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Customer support or contact center experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with CRM or ticketing systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Food service, hospitality, or retail experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilingual English/Spanish skills</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$18–$24 per hour</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Application review → Initial conversation → Interview → Offer</strong></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Seniority Level:</strong> Junior</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p>","descriptionPlain":"We are looking for a Customer Support Coordinator to help manage customer requests and coordinate their resolution. You will communicate with customers, track open issues, and work with internal teams to make sure requests are handled efficiently and professionally.\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Respond to customer questions and service requests\n\n - Track and coordinate open customer issues\n\n - Work with internal teams to resolve requests\n\n - Follow up with customers and provide updates\n\n - Maintain accurate customer records and support notes\n\n - Identify recurring issues and share customer feedback\n\n - Help maintain a consistent, positive customer experience\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - Previous customer service, support, coordination, or administrative experience\n\n - Strong written and verbal communication skills\n\n - Good organization and follow-up skills\n\n - Customer-focused and professional approach\n\n - Comfortable managing multiple requests at once\n\n - Basic computer skills and ability to learn new systems\n\n - Comfortable working independently in a remote environment\n\n - Reliable internet connection and suitable workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Customer support or contact center experience\n\n - Experience with CRM or ticketing systems\n\n - Food service, hospitality, or retail experience\n\n - Bilingual English/Spanish skills\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$18–$24 per hour, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → Initial conversation → Interview → Offer\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nBilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSeniority Level: Junior\n\n","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"f46ebc98-ce0a-48db-8ce4-a06c995ef009","title":"Payer Contracting Specialist","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-07T13:59:43.086+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/f46ebc98-ce0a-48db-8ce4-a06c995ef009","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/f46ebc98-ce0a-48db-8ce4-a06c995ef009/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raventra Health</strong> is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Payer Contracting Specialist, you will support provider clients with payer contract administration, reimbursement terms, and contract-related activities. You will review payer agreements, maintain accurate contract information, support negotiations and renewals, and help ensure billing and revenue cycle teams understand applicable reimbursement requirements.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review and maintain payer contracts, amendments, fee schedules, and reimbursement terms for provider clients</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track contract effective dates, renewal timelines, and required updates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analyze reimbursement terms, payment rates, and contract provisions relevant to client billing</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support payer contract negotiations and renewals by preparing documentation and relevant financial information</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate with provider clients and internal RCM teams on contract-related questions and requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate changes in payer contracts and reimbursement terms to billing, coding, and revenue integrity teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain organized and accurate records of payer agreements and related documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify potential discrepancies between contract terms and operational billing or reimbursement practices</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support research into payer policies, contract provisions, and reimbursement requirements</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in payer contracting, healthcare revenue cycle management, healthcare administration, or a related field</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of healthcare payer contracts, reimbursement terms, and provider participation agreements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience reviewing contracts, fee schedules, and reimbursement information</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical and attention-to-detail skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to interpret contract language and translate relevant requirements into clear operational guidance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication skills and ability to work with payers, provider clients, and internal RCM teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational skills and ability to manage multiple contracts, deadlines, and priorities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently and effectively in a fully remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIPAA-compliant private workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Medicare, Medicaid, and commercial payer contracts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with reimbursement analysis or revenue integrity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge of healthcare billing and coding processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with payer contract management or credentialing platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with provider groups or hospitals</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare contracting expertise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Raventra Health is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Payer Contracting Specialist, you will support provider clients with payer contract administration, reimbursement terms, and contract-related activities. You will review payer agreements, maintain accurate contract information, support negotiations and renewals, and help ensure billing and revenue cycle teams understand applicable reimbursement requirements.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Review and maintain payer contracts, amendments, fee schedules, and reimbursement terms for provider clients\n\n - Track contract effective dates, renewal timelines, and required updates\n\n - Analyze reimbursement terms, payment rates, and contract provisions relevant to client billing\n\n - Support payer contract negotiations and renewals by preparing documentation and relevant financial information\n\n - Coordinate with provider clients and internal RCM teams on contract-related questions and requirements\n\n - Communicate changes in payer contracts and reimbursement terms to billing, coding, and revenue integrity teams\n\n - Maintain organized and accurate records of payer agreements and related documentation\n\n - Identify potential discrepancies between contract terms and operational billing or reimbursement practices\n\n - Support research into payer policies, contract provisions, and reimbursement requirements\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 2+ years of experience in payer contracting, healthcare revenue cycle management, healthcare administration, or a related field\n\n - Understanding of healthcare payer contracts, reimbursement terms, and provider participation agreements\n\n - Experience reviewing contracts, fee schedules, and reimbursement information\n\n - Strong analytical and attention-to-detail skills\n\n - Ability to interpret contract language and translate relevant requirements into clear operational guidance\n\n - Strong communication skills and ability to work with payers, provider clients, and internal RCM teams\n\n - Strong organizational skills and ability to manage multiple contracts, deadlines, and priorities\n\n - Ability to work independently and effectively in a fully remote environment\n\n - HIPAA-compliant private workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with Medicare, Medicaid, and commercial payer contracts\n\n - Experience with reimbursement analysis or revenue integrity\n\n - Knowledge of healthcare billing and coding processes\n\n - Experience with payer contract management or credentialing platforms\n\n - Experience working with provider groups or hospitals\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare contracting expertise.\n\nBenefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nRaventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"50fa86ec-be61-4f07-ab91-610078dd4884","title":"MEDICAL BILLING SPECIALIST","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-13T13:38:35.167+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/50fa86ec-be61-4f07-ab91-610078dd4884","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/50fa86ec-be61-4f07-ab91-610078dd4884/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raventra Health</strong> is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Medical Billing Specialist, you will manage key stages of the revenue cycle for assigned clients, including charge entry, claim submission, payment posting, and denial resolution. You will help ensure claims are processed accurately, payments are collected efficiently, and billing issues are resolved promptly.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage charge entry, claim submission, and payment posting for assigned clients</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work first-pass denials and resubmit or appeal claims as appropriate</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor and report on denial rates and billing performance for your assigned accounts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work directly with payer portals and maintain up-to-date payer-specific knowledge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Liaise with provider practice managers and client teams to resolve documentation and billing gaps</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meet daily productivity, accuracy, and quality standards</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review claims for billing accuracy and identify issues that could delay reimbursement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate billing records and follow established compliance and documentation procedures</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in medical billing</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with multiple insurance payers and payer-specific billing requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with a practice management or billing system such as Epic, Athena, or eClinicalWorks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of denial codes, claim corrections, and appeal processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and ability to manage multiple client accounts and priorities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to communicate effectively with provider teams, payers, and internal stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIPAA-compliant private workspace and ability to work effectively in a fully remote environment</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CPB certification</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with specialty-specific medical billing</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working in multi-payer environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with accounts receivable follow-up</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant medical billing expertise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → practical assessment → hiring manager interview → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Raventra Health is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Medical Billing Specialist, you will manage key stages of the revenue cycle for assigned clients, including charge entry, claim submission, payment posting, and denial resolution. You will help ensure claims are processed accurately, payments are collected efficiently, and billing issues are resolved promptly.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Manage charge entry, claim submission, and payment posting for assigned clients\n\n - Work first-pass denials and resubmit or appeal claims as appropriate\n\n - Monitor and report on denial rates and billing performance for your assigned accounts\n\n - Work directly with payer portals and maintain up-to-date payer-specific knowledge\n\n - Liaise with provider practice managers and client teams to resolve documentation and billing gaps\n\n - Meet daily productivity, accuracy, and quality standards\n\n - Review claims for billing accuracy and identify issues that could delay reimbursement\n\n - Maintain accurate billing records and follow established compliance and documentation procedures\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 2+ years of experience in medical billing\n\n - Experience working with multiple insurance payers and payer-specific billing requirements\n\n - Experience with a practice management or billing system such as Epic, Athena, or eClinicalWorks\n\n - Working knowledge of denial codes, claim corrections, and appeal processes\n\n - Strong attention to detail and ability to manage multiple client accounts and priorities\n\n - Ability to communicate effectively with provider teams, payers, and internal stakeholders\n\n - HIPAA-compliant private workspace and ability to work effectively in a fully remote environment\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - CPB certification\n\n - Experience with specialty-specific medical billing\n\n - Experience working in multi-payer environments\n\n - Experience with accounts receivable follow-up\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant medical billing expertise.\n\nBenefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → practical assessment → hiring manager interview → offer.\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nRaventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"11961f21-eba7-4ec3-8633-00a46754bd15","title":"EMAIL MARKETING SPECIALIST","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-11T12:43:46.577+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/11961f21-eba7-4ec3-8633-00a46754bd15","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/11961f21-eba7-4ec3-8633-00a46754bd15/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">ABOUT THE ROLE<br />Byte&amp;Kite is a digital marketing agency helping clients across a range of industries grow through effective digital marketing and customer engagement. As an Email Marketing Specialist, you will build and manage lifecycle email programmes across multiple client accounts, covering segmentation, automation, campaign planning, testing and deliverability. You will work closely with writers, designers and client teams to create email programmes that drive measurable engagement, conversions and revenue.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">WHAT YOU WILL DO</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build, manage and optimise automated email flows across multiple client accounts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own segmentation strategy and maintain healthy, engaged subscriber lists</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop campaign calendars aligned with client goals, customer journeys and key business priorities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create and manage lifecycle programmes including onboarding, nurture, retention, re-engagement and other triggered communications</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and run structured A/B tests across subject lines, content, offers, timing, segmentation and other variables</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate test results using appropriate sample sizes and meaningful performance metrics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor deliverability, including sender reputation, authentication and engagement signals, and troubleshoot issues when they arise</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with writers and designers to develop effective campaign assets and ensure they are aligned with the overall strategy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track email performance and report on conversions and revenue attributed to email, not open rates alone</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify opportunities to improve engagement, conversion and customer retention through email</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Keep client email programmes aligned with relevant privacy, consent and deliverability requirements</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of hands-on email marketing experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing email programmes across multiple campaigns, audiences or client accounts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with platforms such as Klaviyo, HubSpot, Braze or similar ESPs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong experience building and optimising automated lifecycle journeys beyond basic drip sequences</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Practical understanding of deliverability, including SPF, DKIM, DMARC, sender reputation and troubleshooting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience developing segmentation strategies based on customer behaviour, lifecycle stage and engagement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical skills and experience evaluating email performance, conversions and revenue</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Disciplined approach to A/B testing and ability to interpret results accurately</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable collaborating with writers, designers and other marketing specialists</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Able to explain email performance clearly to clients and recommend actions based on data</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">NICE TO HAVE<br />E-commerce lifecycle experience; SMS marketing; HTML and CSS for email; CDP experience; experience with customer data and analytics platforms; and familiarity with email deliverability monitoring tools.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS<br />Competitive compensation based on experience and qualifications, with the full package discussed during the interview process. Professional development and training opportunities. Fully remote across US time zones, with additional company benefits discussed during the interview process.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIRING PROCESS<br />Application review - 30-minute conversation - paid practical exercise - discussion of your work with the team - offer.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">EQUAL OPPORTUNITY<br />Byte&amp;Kite is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the process, contact our recruiting team and we will arrange it.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT THE ROLE\nByte&Kite is a digital marketing agency helping clients across a range of industries grow through effective digital marketing and customer engagement. As an Email Marketing Specialist, you will build and manage lifecycle email programmes across multiple client accounts, covering segmentation, automation, campaign planning, testing and deliverability. You will work closely with writers, designers and client teams to create email programmes that drive measurable engagement, conversions and revenue.\n\n \n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Build, manage and optimise automated email flows across multiple client accounts\n\n - Own segmentation strategy and maintain healthy, engaged subscriber lists\n\n - Develop campaign calendars aligned with client goals, customer journeys and key business priorities\n\n - Create and manage lifecycle programmes including onboarding, nurture, retention, re-engagement and other triggered communications\n\n - Design and run structured A/B tests across subject lines, content, offers, timing, segmentation and other variables\n\n - Evaluate test results using appropriate sample sizes and meaningful performance metrics\n\n - Monitor deliverability, including sender reputation, authentication and engagement signals, and troubleshoot issues when they arise\n\n - Work with writers and designers to develop effective campaign assets and ensure they are aligned with the overall strategy\n\n - Track email performance and report on conversions and revenue attributed to email, not open rates alone\n\n - Identify opportunities to improve engagement, conversion and customer retention through email\n\n - Keep client email programmes aligned with relevant privacy, consent and deliverability requirements\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 3+ years of hands-on email marketing experience\n\n - Experience managing email programmes across multiple campaigns, audiences or client accounts\n\n - Hands-on experience with platforms such as Klaviyo, HubSpot, Braze or similar ESPs\n\n - Strong experience building and optimising automated lifecycle journeys beyond basic drip sequences\n\n - Practical understanding of deliverability, including SPF, DKIM, DMARC, sender reputation and troubleshooting\n\n - Experience developing segmentation strategies based on customer behaviour, lifecycle stage and engagement\n\n - Strong analytical skills and experience evaluating email performance, conversions and revenue\n\n - Disciplined approach to A/B testing and ability to interpret results accurately\n\n - Comfortable collaborating with writers, designers and other marketing specialists\n\n - Able to explain email performance clearly to clients and recommend actions based on data\n\nNICE TO HAVE\nE-commerce lifecycle experience; SMS marketing; HTML and CSS for email; CDP experience; experience with customer data and analytics platforms; and familiarity with email deliverability monitoring tools.\n\n \n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\nCompetitive compensation based on experience and qualifications, with the full package discussed during the interview process. Professional development and training opportunities. Fully remote across US time zones, with additional company benefits discussed during the interview process.\n\n \n\nHIRING PROCESS\nApplication review - 30-minute conversation - paid practical exercise - discussion of your work with the team - offer.\n\n \n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\nByte&Kite is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the process, contact our recruiting team and we will arrange it.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"a04bb8eb-5a6b-4310-90d5-80e8207ec325","title":"MEDICAL CODER, CPC","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-13T13:39:53.623+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/a04bb8eb-5a6b-4310-90d5-80e8207ec325","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/a04bb8eb-5a6b-4310-90d5-80e8207ec325/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raventra Health</strong> is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Medical Coder, CPC, you will review clinical documentation and accurately assign CPT and ICD-10 codes for outpatient encounters. You will work closely with internal teams and provider clients to ensure coding accuracy, compliance, and timely claims processing.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Code outpatient E/M services, procedures, and diagnoses based on clinical documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review medical records and identify the appropriate CPT, HCPCS, and ICD-10 codes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Query providers when documentation is incomplete, unclear, or requires clarification</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain high coding accuracy and address feedback from internal audits</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meet daily productivity and encounter targets while maintaining quality standards</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay current with CPT, ICD-10, and other applicable coding updates and guidelines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support documentation and coding compliance for audits, claims, and appeals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with billing and claims teams to identify and resolve coding-related issues</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Active CPC, CCS, or RHIT certification</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of outpatient medical coding experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with an electronic medical record system such as Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or a comparable platform</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong working knowledge of CPT, HCPCS, and ICD-10 coding guidelines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to interpret clinical documentation and apply appropriate coding rules</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and commitment to coding accuracy and compliance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently and manage daily coding volume in a remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIPAA-compliant private workspace and ability to work effectively in a fully remote role</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Specialty coding certification</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with specialty-specific coding</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical coding auditing experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Risk adjustment or HCC coding experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting coding-related appeals or payer audits</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, certification, qualifications, and relevant specialty expertise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → practical coding assessment → hiring manager interview → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Raventra Health is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Medical Coder, CPC, you will review clinical documentation and accurately assign CPT and ICD-10 codes for outpatient encounters. You will work closely with internal teams and provider clients to ensure coding accuracy, compliance, and timely claims processing.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Code outpatient E/M services, procedures, and diagnoses based on clinical documentation\n\n - Review medical records and identify the appropriate CPT, HCPCS, and ICD-10 codes\n\n - Query providers when documentation is incomplete, unclear, or requires clarification\n\n - Maintain high coding accuracy and address feedback from internal audits\n\n - Meet daily productivity and encounter targets while maintaining quality standards\n\n - Stay current with CPT, ICD-10, and other applicable coding updates and guidelines\n\n - Support documentation and coding compliance for audits, claims, and appeals\n\n - Collaborate with billing and claims teams to identify and resolve coding-related issues\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - Active CPC, CCS, or RHIT certification\n\n - 2+ years of outpatient medical coding experience\n\n - Experience with an electronic medical record system such as Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or a comparable platform\n\n - Strong working knowledge of CPT, HCPCS, and ICD-10 coding guidelines\n\n - Ability to interpret clinical documentation and apply appropriate coding rules\n\n - Strong attention to detail and commitment to coding accuracy and compliance\n\n - Ability to work independently and manage daily coding volume in a remote environment\n\n - HIPAA-compliant private workspace and ability to work effectively in a fully remote role\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Specialty coding certification\n\n - Experience with specialty-specific coding\n\n - Medical coding auditing experience\n\n - Risk adjustment or HCC coding experience\n\n - Experience supporting coding-related appeals or payer audits\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, certification, qualifications, and relevant specialty expertise.\n\nBenefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → practical coding assessment → hiring manager interview → offer.\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nRaventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"8a35ef60-7355-4ba6-b513-4cff7e07ce54","title":"BUSINESS DEVELOPMENT REPRESENTATIVE, PROVIDER ACCOUNTS","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-13T13:51:17.717+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/8a35ef60-7355-4ba6-b513-4cff7e07ce54","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/8a35ef60-7355-4ba6-b513-4cff7e07ce54/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raventra Health</strong> is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Business Development Representative, Provider Accounts, you will help grow Raventra Health’s client base by identifying and engaging provider groups and hospital organizations that could benefit from outsourced revenue cycle services. You will build relationships with decision-makers, understand their operational and revenue cycle challenges, and support new business opportunities from initial outreach through proposal.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Generate new business opportunities through outbound prospecting, referrals, networking, and industry events</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify provider groups and hospital organizations that may benefit from Raventra Health’s services</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct discovery conversations with practice administrators, CFOs, revenue cycle leaders, and other decision-makers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understand prospects’ billing, coding, claims, and revenue cycle challenges and connect them with relevant solutions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build compelling business cases based on the prospect’s operational needs and revenue cycle priorities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage multiple opportunities and maintain momentum throughout longer, multi-stakeholder sales cycles</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Address questions and concerns related to healthcare compliance, data security, and patient information</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate prospect, opportunity, and activity information in the CRM</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with internal teams to prepare proposals and support a smooth transition from sales to client onboarding</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in B2B sales, preferably within healthcare, healthcare services, or healthcare technology</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of provider groups, hospitals, and the healthcare services buying process</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong prospecting, discovery, relationship-building, and negotiation skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to communicate confidently with healthcare executives and operational decision-makers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of healthcare compliance concepts, including HIPAA, BAAs, and handling of PHI</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing longer sales cycles involving multiple stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to understand and discuss basic revenue cycle management concepts and metrics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organization, follow-through, and CRM management skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently and effectively in a fully remote environment</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Revenue cycle management or healthcare IT sales experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Existing relationships within provider groups or hospital organizations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience selling outsourced healthcare services</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare industry conference or networking experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with CRM platforms such as Salesforce or HubSpot</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare or B2B sales expertise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Raventra Health is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Business Development Representative, Provider Accounts, you will help grow Raventra Health’s client base by identifying and engaging provider groups and hospital organizations that could benefit from outsourced revenue cycle services. You will build relationships with decision-makers, understand their operational and revenue cycle challenges, and support new business opportunities from initial outreach through proposal.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Generate new business opportunities through outbound prospecting, referrals, networking, and industry events\n\n - Identify provider groups and hospital organizations that may benefit from Raventra Health’s services\n\n - Conduct discovery conversations with practice administrators, CFOs, revenue cycle leaders, and other decision-makers\n\n - Understand prospects’ billing, coding, claims, and revenue cycle challenges and connect them with relevant solutions\n\n - Build compelling business cases based on the prospect’s operational needs and revenue cycle priorities\n\n - Manage multiple opportunities and maintain momentum throughout longer, multi-stakeholder sales cycles\n\n - Address questions and concerns related to healthcare compliance, data security, and patient information\n\n - Maintain accurate prospect, opportunity, and activity information in the CRM\n\n - Collaborate with internal teams to prepare proposals and support a smooth transition from sales to client onboarding\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 2+ years of experience in B2B sales, preferably within healthcare, healthcare services, or healthcare technology\n\n - Understanding of provider groups, hospitals, and the healthcare services buying process\n\n - Strong prospecting, discovery, relationship-building, and negotiation skills\n\n - Ability to communicate confidently with healthcare executives and operational decision-makers\n\n - Understanding of healthcare compliance concepts, including HIPAA, BAAs, and handling of PHI\n\n - Experience managing longer sales cycles involving multiple stakeholders\n\n - Ability to understand and discuss basic revenue cycle management concepts and metrics\n\n - Strong organization, follow-through, and CRM management skills\n\n - Ability to work independently and effectively in a fully remote environment\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Revenue cycle management or healthcare IT sales experience\n\n - Existing relationships within provider groups or hospital organizations\n\n - Experience selling outsourced healthcare services\n\n - Healthcare industry conference or networking experience\n\n - Experience working with CRM platforms such as Salesforce or HubSpot\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare or B2B sales expertise.\n\nBenefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nRaventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"fcde7bd4-6853-43a5-a62d-99c430a47154","title":"CLAIMS PROCESSOR","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-13T13:41:12.148+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/fcde7bd4-6853-43a5-a62d-99c430a47154","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/fcde7bd4-6853-43a5-a62d-99c430a47154/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raventra Health</strong> is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Claims Processor, you will review and process healthcare claims to ensure they are accurate, complete, and submitted according to payer requirements. You will work closely with billing and coding teams to identify discrepancies, resolve routine issues, and help ensure claims are processed efficiently and accurately.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review and process healthcare claims in accordance with payer requirements and established procedures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Verify claim information for accuracy, completeness, and consistency before submission</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Apply payer-specific requirements and billing guidelines accurately and consistently</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify claims requiring additional documentation, correction, or review and escalate as appropriate</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Resolve routine claim discrepancies and errors within established guidelines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with billing and coding teams to investigate and resolve claim-related issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate records of processed claims and follow established documentation procedures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meet productivity and quality standards while maintaining a high level of accuracy</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1+ year of experience in medical claims processing, healthcare billing, or a related revenue cycle role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of CMS-1500 and UB-04 claim forms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of basic medical billing terminology and payer requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with a claims processing, billing, or practice management system</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and ability to identify discrepancies in claim information</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to manage high-volume work while maintaining accuracy and meeting deadlines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and problem-solving skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIPAA-compliant private workspace and ability to work effectively in a fully remote role</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with multiple insurance payers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical coding knowledge or experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with claim corrections, denials, or appeals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with electronic claims submission systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with provider groups or hospitals</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare revenue cycle expertise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → practical assessment → hiring manager interview → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Raventra Health is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Claims Processor, you will review and process healthcare claims to ensure they are accurate, complete, and submitted according to payer requirements. You will work closely with billing and coding teams to identify discrepancies, resolve routine issues, and help ensure claims are processed efficiently and accurately.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Review and process healthcare claims in accordance with payer requirements and established procedures\n\n - Verify claim information for accuracy, completeness, and consistency before submission\n\n - Apply payer-specific requirements and billing guidelines accurately and consistently\n\n - Identify claims requiring additional documentation, correction, or review and escalate as appropriate\n\n - Resolve routine claim discrepancies and errors within established guidelines\n\n - Work with billing and coding teams to investigate and resolve claim-related issues\n\n - Maintain accurate records of processed claims and follow established documentation procedures\n\n - Meet productivity and quality standards while maintaining a high level of accuracy\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 1+ year of experience in medical claims processing, healthcare billing, or a related revenue cycle role\n\n - Working knowledge of CMS-1500 and UB-04 claim forms\n\n - Understanding of basic medical billing terminology and payer requirements\n\n - Experience with a claims processing, billing, or practice management system\n\n - Strong attention to detail and ability to identify discrepancies in claim information\n\n - Ability to manage high-volume work while maintaining accuracy and meeting deadlines\n\n - Strong communication and problem-solving skills\n\n - HIPAA-compliant private workspace and ability to work effectively in a fully remote role\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience working with multiple insurance payers\n\n - Medical coding knowledge or experience\n\n - Experience with claim corrections, denials, or appeals\n\n - Familiarity with electronic claims submission systems\n\n - Experience working with provider groups or hospitals\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare revenue cycle expertise.\n\nBenefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → practical assessment → hiring manager interview → offer.\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nRaventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"0f2f3dc7-876a-4c05-aafd-f28ac0a30cc6","title":"PRIOR AUTHORIZATION SPECIALIST","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-13T13:43:31.192+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/0f2f3dc7-876a-4c05-aafd-f28ac0a30cc6","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/0f2f3dc7-876a-4c05-aafd-f28ac0a30cc6/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raventra Health</strong> is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Prior Authorization Specialist, you will coordinate prior authorization requests for scheduled procedures, treatments, and services on behalf of provider clients. You will work with payer portals, provider teams, and clinical documentation to help secure timely approvals and resolve authorization-related issues.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Submit and track prior authorization requests across multiple insurance payers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gather and review clinical documentation required to support authorization requests</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate with provider teams to obtain missing information or documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow up with payers on pending requests and monitor authorization status through resolution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify authorization issues and pursue reconsiderations or appeals when requests are denied</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate records of authorization requests, decisions, and follow-up actions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay current on payer-specific authorization requirements and communicate relevant changes to the team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Escalate delays, complex cases, and potential barriers to timely patient care when appropriate</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in prior authorization, insurance verification, medical billing, or a related healthcare role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with insurance payer portals and authorization requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to understand and interpret clinical documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and ability to manage multiple authorization requests simultaneously</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Persistence and strong follow-through when working through multi-step authorization or appeal processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written and verbal communication skills when working with providers, payers, and internal teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently while meeting productivity and turnaround expectations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIPAA-compliant private workspace and ability to work effectively in a fully remote role</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with specialty-specific prior authorizations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pharmacy prior authorization experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clinical or healthcare background</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with an EMR system such as Epic, Athena, or eClinicalWorks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience handling authorization denials, reconsiderations, or appeals</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare revenue cycle expertise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Raventra Health is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Prior Authorization Specialist, you will coordinate prior authorization requests for scheduled procedures, treatments, and services on behalf of provider clients. You will work with payer portals, provider teams, and clinical documentation to help secure timely approvals and resolve authorization-related issues.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Submit and track prior authorization requests across multiple insurance payers\n\n - Gather and review clinical documentation required to support authorization requests\n\n - Communicate with provider teams to obtain missing information or documentation\n\n - Follow up with payers on pending requests and monitor authorization status through resolution\n\n - Identify authorization issues and pursue reconsiderations or appeals when requests are denied\n\n - Maintain accurate records of authorization requests, decisions, and follow-up actions\n\n - Stay current on payer-specific authorization requirements and communicate relevant changes to the team\n\n - Escalate delays, complex cases, and potential barriers to timely patient care when appropriate\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 2+ years of experience in prior authorization, insurance verification, medical billing, or a related healthcare role\n\n - Experience working with insurance payer portals and authorization requirements\n\n - Ability to understand and interpret clinical documentation\n\n - Strong attention to detail and ability to manage multiple authorization requests simultaneously\n\n - Persistence and strong follow-through when working through multi-step authorization or appeal processes\n\n - Strong written and verbal communication skills when working with providers, payers, and internal teams\n\n - Ability to work independently while meeting productivity and turnaround expectations\n\n - HIPAA-compliant private workspace and ability to work effectively in a fully remote role\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with specialty-specific prior authorizations\n\n - Pharmacy prior authorization experience\n\n - Clinical or healthcare background\n\n - Experience with an EMR system such as Epic, Athena, or eClinicalWorks\n\n - Experience handling authorization denials, reconsiderations, or appeals\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare revenue cycle expertise.\n\nBenefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nRaventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"e104d4c5-3019-47d2-9ddf-4041c08667d0","title":"PATIENT ACCESS COORDINATOR","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-13T13:46:25.068+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/e104d4c5-3019-47d2-9ddf-4041c08667d0","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/e104d4c5-3019-47d2-9ddf-4041c08667d0/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raventra Health</strong> is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Patient Access Coordinator, you will support the front end of the revenue cycle by handling patient registration, insurance verification, benefits information, and related administrative tasks. The accuracy of your work helps ensure patients receive clear information and that claims can be processed correctly downstream.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Complete patient registration accurately in the client’s EMR or registration system</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Verify insurance eligibility and benefits before scheduled services</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explain coverage, benefits, and patient responsibility clearly and professionally</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collect and post patient payments where applicable</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review patient and insurance information for accuracy and completeness</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Resolve registration and eligibility discrepancies before they create billing or claims issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate with patients, provider teams, and insurance representatives as needed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meet productivity and quality expectations while maintaining a high level of data accuracy</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1+ year of experience in patient access, patient registration, medical front office, or a related healthcare role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience verifying insurance eligibility and benefits</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with an EMR, patient registration, or practice management system</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and ability to maintain accuracy while handling multiple tasks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication skills and a patient-focused approach</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to explain insurance and financial information clearly and without unnecessary jargon</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently and effectively in a fully remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIPAA-compliant private workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or another major EMR/practice management system</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilingual Spanish skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with financial counseling or patient financial services</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical scheduling experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with provider groups or hospitals</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare revenue cycle expertise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Raventra Health is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Patient Access Coordinator, you will support the front end of the revenue cycle by handling patient registration, insurance verification, benefits information, and related administrative tasks. The accuracy of your work helps ensure patients receive clear information and that claims can be processed correctly downstream.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Complete patient registration accurately in the client’s EMR or registration system\n\n - Verify insurance eligibility and benefits before scheduled services\n\n - Explain coverage, benefits, and patient responsibility clearly and professionally\n\n - Collect and post patient payments where applicable\n\n - Review patient and insurance information for accuracy and completeness\n\n - Resolve registration and eligibility discrepancies before they create billing or claims issues\n\n - Communicate with patients, provider teams, and insurance representatives as needed\n\n - Meet productivity and quality expectations while maintaining a high level of data accuracy\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 1+ year of experience in patient access, patient registration, medical front office, or a related healthcare role\n\n - Experience verifying insurance eligibility and benefits\n\n - Experience working with an EMR, patient registration, or practice management system\n\n - Strong attention to detail and ability to maintain accuracy while handling multiple tasks\n\n - Excellent communication skills and a patient-focused approach\n\n - Ability to explain insurance and financial information clearly and without unnecessary jargon\n\n - Ability to work independently and effectively in a fully remote environment\n\n - HIPAA-compliant private workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or another major EMR/practice management system\n\n - Bilingual Spanish skills\n\n - Experience with financial counseling or patient financial services\n\n - Medical scheduling experience\n\n - Experience working with provider groups or hospitals\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare revenue cycle expertise.\n\nBenefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nRaventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"f34b5827-5992-4eaf-93e5-fb484625597d","title":"AR FOLLOW-UP SPECIALIST","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-13T13:49:58.217+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/f34b5827-5992-4eaf-93e5-fb484625597d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/f34b5827-5992-4eaf-93e5-fb484625597d/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raventra Health</strong> is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As an AR Follow-Up Specialist, you will manage aged accounts receivable for provider clients, following up on unpaid and underpaid claims and working with payers to resolve outstanding balances. You will help improve collections, reduce aging, and identify recurring issues that may be affecting reimbursement.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage an assigned accounts receivable portfolio, prioritizing accounts by age, balance, and recovery potential</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow up on unpaid and underpaid claims through payer portals and by phone</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Research claim status, payment history, and outstanding balances to determine appropriate next steps</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Submit appeals and reconsiderations with supporting documentation when appropriate</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Escalate unresolved claims through payer channels when standard follow-up does not resolve the issue</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate documentation of follow-up activities, payer responses, and next steps</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor AR aging and recovery performance for assigned accounts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify recurring denial, payment, or claims issues and communicate trends to billing and coding teams</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in healthcare accounts receivable follow-up or medical billing</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience following up with insurance payers on unpaid and underpaid claims</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of AR aging, claim status, denials, and payment discrepancies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with payer portals and telephone-based payer follow-up</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong ability to prioritize accounts based on age, balance, and likelihood of recovery</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and accurate documentation skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Persistence and problem-solving skills when resolving complex or delayed claims</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently and meet productivity and quality expectations in a remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIPAA-compliant private workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with specific payer types or payer-specific processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Appeals and reconsideration experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical coding knowledge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or another billing/practice management system</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with provider groups or hospitals</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare revenue cycle expertise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Raventra Health is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As an AR Follow-Up Specialist, you will manage aged accounts receivable for provider clients, following up on unpaid and underpaid claims and working with payers to resolve outstanding balances. You will help improve collections, reduce aging, and identify recurring issues that may be affecting reimbursement.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Manage an assigned accounts receivable portfolio, prioritizing accounts by age, balance, and recovery potential\n\n - Follow up on unpaid and underpaid claims through payer portals and by phone\n\n - Research claim status, payment history, and outstanding balances to determine appropriate next steps\n\n - Submit appeals and reconsiderations with supporting documentation when appropriate\n\n - Escalate unresolved claims through payer channels when standard follow-up does not resolve the issue\n\n - Maintain accurate documentation of follow-up activities, payer responses, and next steps\n\n - Monitor AR aging and recovery performance for assigned accounts\n\n - Identify recurring denial, payment, or claims issues and communicate trends to billing and coding teams\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 2+ years of experience in healthcare accounts receivable follow-up or medical billing\n\n - Experience following up with insurance payers on unpaid and underpaid claims\n\n - Working knowledge of AR aging, claim status, denials, and payment discrepancies\n\n - Experience with payer portals and telephone-based payer follow-up\n\n - Strong ability to prioritize accounts based on age, balance, and likelihood of recovery\n\n - Strong attention to detail and accurate documentation skills\n\n - Persistence and problem-solving skills when resolving complex or delayed claims\n\n - Ability to work independently and meet productivity and quality expectations in a remote environment\n\n - HIPAA-compliant private workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with specific payer types or payer-specific processes\n\n - Appeals and reconsideration experience\n\n - Medical coding knowledge\n\n - Experience with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or another billing/practice management system\n\n - Experience working with provider groups or hospitals\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare revenue cycle expertise.\n\nBenefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nRaventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"5b779884-6c6f-417c-8a6a-49e9cfa4048b","title":"CLIENT SUCCESS MANAGER, PROVIDER ACCOUNTS","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-13T13:34:33.115+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/5b779884-6c6f-417c-8a6a-49e9cfa4048b","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/5b779884-6c6f-417c-8a6a-49e9cfa4048b/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raventra Health</strong> is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Client Success Manager, Provider Accounts, you will own client relationships and help ensure provider organizations receive consistent, high-quality revenue cycle support. You will manage ongoing client communication, review performance, coordinate issue resolution, and identify opportunities to strengthen and expand client relationships.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own day-to-day relationships across an assigned portfolio of provider and hospital clients</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build strong relationships with practice administrators, revenue cycle leaders, CFOs, and other client stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct regular business reviews and present updates on service performance and key revenue cycle metrics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor metrics such as accounts receivable aging, clean claim rate, denial rate, and payment performance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explain performance trends, identify areas for improvement, and coordinate appropriate follow-up with internal teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage client escalations and ensure issues are addressed promptly and effectively</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify opportunities to expand services based on client needs and operational priorities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate complex billing, coding, and claims information into clear, actionable recommendations for clients</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate client records, action items, and communication history in the CRM or account management system</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience in client success, account management, or customer relationship management, preferably in healthcare services</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing relationships with healthcare providers, hospitals, or other healthcare organizations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of revenue cycle management concepts and metrics, including accounts receivable aging, clean claim rate, and denial rate</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and presentation skills, with the ability to communicate effectively with both operational and financial leadership</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing escalated or at-risk client relationships and driving issues through resolution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational skills and ability to manage multiple client priorities simultaneously</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to identify client needs and translate them into actionable internal requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently and effectively in a fully remote environment</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Revenue cycle management operations experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with EMR or practice management systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical billing or coding experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with contract renewals or negotiations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with provider groups or hospitals</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare client management expertise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Raventra Health is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Client Success Manager, Provider Accounts, you will own client relationships and help ensure provider organizations receive consistent, high-quality revenue cycle support. You will manage ongoing client communication, review performance, coordinate issue resolution, and identify opportunities to strengthen and expand client relationships.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Own day-to-day relationships across an assigned portfolio of provider and hospital clients\n\n - Build strong relationships with practice administrators, revenue cycle leaders, CFOs, and other client stakeholders\n\n - Conduct regular business reviews and present updates on service performance and key revenue cycle metrics\n\n - Monitor metrics such as accounts receivable aging, clean claim rate, denial rate, and payment performance\n\n - Explain performance trends, identify areas for improvement, and coordinate appropriate follow-up with internal teams\n\n - Manage client escalations and ensure issues are addressed promptly and effectively\n\n - Identify opportunities to expand services based on client needs and operational priorities\n\n - Translate complex billing, coding, and claims information into clear, actionable recommendations for clients\n\n - Maintain accurate client records, action items, and communication history in the CRM or account management system\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 3+ years of experience in client success, account management, or customer relationship management, preferably in healthcare services\n\n - Experience managing relationships with healthcare providers, hospitals, or other healthcare organizations\n\n - Working knowledge of revenue cycle management concepts and metrics, including accounts receivable aging, clean claim rate, and denial rate\n\n - Strong communication and presentation skills, with the ability to communicate effectively with both operational and financial leadership\n\n - Experience managing escalated or at-risk client relationships and driving issues through resolution\n\n - Strong organizational skills and ability to manage multiple client priorities simultaneously\n\n - Ability to identify client needs and translate them into actionable internal requirements\n\n - Ability to work independently and effectively in a fully remote environment\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Revenue cycle management operations experience\n\n - Familiarity with EMR or practice management systems\n\n - Medical billing or coding experience\n\n - Experience with contract renewals or negotiations\n\n - Experience working with provider groups or hospitals\n\n\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare client management expertise.\n\nBenefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nRaventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"acfca96b-7a4b-407c-bf37-be6d1388f022","title":"Full-Stack Developer","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-14T11:20:59.967+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/acfca96b-7a4b-407c-bf37-be6d1388f022","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/acfca96b-7a4b-407c-bf37-be6d1388f022/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>Job Description</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CelebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products are designed around practical business needs, with a focus on usability, reliability, and measurable impact.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As part of our next stage of product development, we are building a new analytics platform for mid-market businesses. The team will create tools that bring together operational data, reporting, and actionable insights in one intuitive product. As a Full-Stack Developer, you will be one of the engineers shaping this product from its early stages, with a meaningful voice in both technical direction and how the product evolves.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and ship features across a TypeScript/React frontend and Python/PostgreSQL backend</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop analytics functionality that turns business data into useful dashboards, reporting, and insights</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the technical design and implementation of the features you build, with support from senior engineers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with product and design to turn requirements into reliable, intuitive experiences</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Write and maintain automated tests and take responsibility for the quality of what you ship</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Investigate production issues, improve performance, and contribute to the reliability of the platform</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review pull requests and contribute thoughtful, constructive feedback</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help shape engineering practices and technical decisions as the new product team grows</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience building and maintaining production web applications</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong experience with either React/TypeScript or Python, with the ability to work comfortably across the stack</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solid understanding of relational databases and practical SQL experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building APIs and integrating frontend applications with backend services</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good understanding of testing, debugging, and production software development</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Able to explain technical decisions and trade-offs clearly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working independently and asynchronously with a distributed US-based team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Product-minded approach: you care about how the software works for customers, not just how it works technically</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">AWS or other cloud platform experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Terraform or infrastructure-as-code experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with data visualization, dashboards, or analytics products</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with large or complex datasets</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous B2B SaaS experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building products for mid-market or enterprise customers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with data pipelines, reporting systems, or business intelligence tooling</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$110,000-$140,000 determined based on experience, technical expertise, and overall fit for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CelebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → technical discussion → conversation with the team → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication at every stage.</p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CelebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please let us know and we will work with you to make the process accessible.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 110,000 - 140,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"JOB DESCRIPTION\n\nCelebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products are designed around practical business needs, with a focus on usability, reliability, and measurable impact.\n\nAs part of our next stage of product development, we are building a new analytics platform for mid-market businesses. The team will create tools that bring together operational data, reporting, and actionable insights in one intuitive product. As a Full-Stack Developer, you will be one of the engineers shaping this product from its early stages, with a meaningful voice in both technical direction and how the product evolves.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Build and ship features across a TypeScript/React frontend and Python/PostgreSQL backend\n\n - Develop analytics functionality that turns business data into useful dashboards, reporting, and insights\n\n - Own the technical design and implementation of the features you build, with support from senior engineers\n\n - Work closely with product and design to turn requirements into reliable, intuitive experiences\n\n - Write and maintain automated tests and take responsibility for the quality of what you ship\n\n - Investigate production issues, improve performance, and contribute to the reliability of the platform\n\n - Review pull requests and contribute thoughtful, constructive feedback\n\n - Help shape engineering practices and technical decisions as the new product team grows\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 3+ years of experience building and maintaining production web applications\n\n - Strong experience with either React/TypeScript or Python, with the ability to work comfortably across the stack\n\n - Solid understanding of relational databases and practical SQL experience\n\n - Experience building APIs and integrating frontend applications with backend services\n\n - Good understanding of testing, debugging, and production software development\n\n - Able to explain technical decisions and trade-offs clearly\n\n - Comfortable working independently and asynchronously with a distributed US-based team\n\n - Product-minded approach: you care about how the software works for customers, not just how it works technically\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - AWS or other cloud platform experience\n\n - Terraform or infrastructure-as-code experience\n\n - Experience with data visualization, dashboards, or analytics products\n\n - Experience working with large or complex datasets\n\n - Previous B2B SaaS experience\n\n - Experience building products for mid-market or enterprise customers\n\n - Familiarity with data pipelines, reporting systems, or business intelligence tooling\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\n$110,000-$140,000 determined based on experience, technical expertise, and overall fit for the role.\n\nCelebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → technical discussion → conversation with the team → offer.\n\nWe aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication at every stage.\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nCelebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.\n\nIf you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please let us know and we will work with you to make the process accessible.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSalary Range: 110,000 - 140,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"eb78f0a3-0850-4575-881c-163d6a60e6bf","title":"FRONTEND DEVELOPER","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-14T11:22:08.732+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/eb78f0a3-0850-4575-881c-163d6a60e6bf","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/eb78f0a3-0850-4575-881c-163d6a60e6bf/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>Job Description</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CelebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will join the engineering team behind our new mid-market analytics platform, building the interface customers rely on to explore data, understand performance, and turn complex information into actionable insights. You will work closely with product, design, and backend engineering to create a fast, accessible, and consistent experience as the platform grows.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain the customer-facing application using React and TypeScript</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create intuitive dashboards, data exploration experiences, and interactive visualization components</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help evolve CelebriOS's shared component library in close collaboration with product design</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own frontend performance for views that work with large and complex datasets</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build accessible interfaces that meet WCAG AA standards and continuously improve the user experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with backend engineers to shape APIs and data structures around real product requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to frontend architecture and technical decisions as the product and engineering team evolve</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review code, share knowledge, and contribute to a strong frontend engineering culture</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of professional experience building production frontends with React and TypeScript</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of component architecture, state management, and modern frontend patterns</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience building accessible web applications</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with data-heavy or complex user interfaces</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to explain the technical and product decisions behind work you have built</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable collaborating closely with designers and giving and receiving constructive feedback</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail without losing sight of the overall user experience</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with data-visualization libraries such as D3 or Recharts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience contributing to or building a design system</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Frontend performance profiling and optimization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Figma fluency</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building analytics, reporting, or B2B SaaS products</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$95,000-$125,000 determined based on experience, technical expertise, and overall fit for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CelebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → technical discussion → conversation with the team → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.</p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CelebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please let us know and we will work with you to make the process accessible.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 95,000 - 125,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"JOB DESCRIPTION\n\nCelebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.\n\n \n\nYou will join the engineering team behind our new mid-market analytics platform, building the interface customers rely on to explore data, understand performance, and turn complex information into actionable insights. You will work closely with product, design, and backend engineering to create a fast, accessible, and consistent experience as the platform grows.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Build and maintain the customer-facing application using React and TypeScript\n\n - Create intuitive dashboards, data exploration experiences, and interactive visualization components\n\n - Help evolve CelebriOS's shared component library in close collaboration with product design\n\n - Own frontend performance for views that work with large and complex datasets\n\n - Build accessible interfaces that meet WCAG AA standards and continuously improve the user experience\n\n - Work with backend engineers to shape APIs and data structures around real product requirements\n\n - Contribute to frontend architecture and technical decisions as the product and engineering team evolve\n\n - Review code, share knowledge, and contribute to a strong frontend engineering culture\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 3+ years of professional experience building production frontends with React and TypeScript\n\n - Strong understanding of component architecture, state management, and modern frontend patterns\n\n - Hands-on experience building accessible web applications\n\n - Experience working with data-heavy or complex user interfaces\n\n - Ability to explain the technical and product decisions behind work you have built\n\n - Comfortable collaborating closely with designers and giving and receiving constructive feedback\n\n - Strong attention to detail without losing sight of the overall user experience\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with data-visualization libraries such as D3 or Recharts\n\n - Experience contributing to or building a design system\n\n - Frontend performance profiling and optimization\n\n - Figma fluency\n\n - Experience building analytics, reporting, or B2B SaaS products\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\n$95,000-$125,000 determined based on experience, technical expertise, and overall fit for the role.\n\nCelebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → technical discussion → conversation with the team → offer.\n\nWe aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nCelebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.\n\nIf you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please let us know and we will work with you to make the process accessible.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSalary Range: 95,000 - 125,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"8887e73c-cf6f-4362-b0f9-327ba70878bf","title":"DATA ANALYST","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-14T11:25:56.996+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/8887e73c-cf6f-4362-b0f9-327ba70878bf","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/8887e73c-cf6f-4362-b0f9-327ba70878bf/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>Job Description</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CelebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will join the team building our new mid-market analytics platform, working at the intersection of product, data, and business strategy. You will turn product usage, customer, and commercial data into insights that help shape product decisions and business priorities. You will also play an important role in establishing clear, trusted metrics and analytical practices as the new product grows.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define, maintain, and document the core metrics used across the product and business</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain recurring dashboards and reporting in a BI platform</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analyze product, customer, and commercial data to answer questions from product, sales, and business teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with product and engineering teams on experiment design, analysis, and interpretation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Investigate data quality issues and work with engineering to address problems at the source</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify trends, opportunities, and potential risks through exploratory analysis</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Present analytical findings clearly to non-technical stakeholders, including limitations and areas where the data does not provide a reliable answer</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help establish a consistent, data-informed approach to product and business decision-making</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in a data or analytics role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong SQL skills, including window functions and query optimization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with a BI platform such as Looker, Tableau, or Metabase</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical thinking and the ability to connect data to real business decisions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience presenting insights to non-technical stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to explain analytical methodology, assumptions, and limitations clearly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable challenging assumptions when the available data does not support a conclusion</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Python or R</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">dbt</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with experiment design and A/B testing</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with B2B SaaS metrics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Data warehouse and dimensional modeling experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with product analytics or customer behavior data</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$75,000-$100,000 determined based on experience, technical expertise, and overall fit for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CelebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → technical discussion → conversation with the team → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.</p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CelebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please let us know and we will work with you to make the process accessible.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 75,000 - 100,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"JOB DESCRIPTION\n\nCelebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.\n\n \n\nYou will join the team building our new mid-market analytics platform, working at the intersection of product, data, and business strategy. You will turn product usage, customer, and commercial data into insights that help shape product decisions and business priorities. You will also play an important role in establishing clear, trusted metrics and analytical practices as the new product grows.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Define, maintain, and document the core metrics used across the product and business\n\n - Build and maintain recurring dashboards and reporting in a BI platform\n\n - Analyze product, customer, and commercial data to answer questions from product, sales, and business teams\n\n - Partner with product and engineering teams on experiment design, analysis, and interpretation\n\n - Investigate data quality issues and work with engineering to address problems at the source\n\n - Identify trends, opportunities, and potential risks through exploratory analysis\n\n - Present analytical findings clearly to non-technical stakeholders, including limitations and areas where the data does not provide a reliable answer\n\n - Help establish a consistent, data-informed approach to product and business decision-making\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 2+ years of experience in a data or analytics role\n\n - Strong SQL skills, including window functions and query optimization\n\n - Hands-on experience with a BI platform such as Looker, Tableau, or Metabase\n\n - Strong analytical thinking and the ability to connect data to real business decisions\n\n - Experience presenting insights to non-technical stakeholders\n\n - Ability to explain analytical methodology, assumptions, and limitations clearly\n\n - Comfortable challenging assumptions when the available data does not support a conclusion\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Python or R\n\n - dbt\n\n - Experience with experiment design and A/B testing\n\n - Familiarity with B2B SaaS metrics\n\n - Data warehouse and dimensional modeling experience\n\n - Experience working with product analytics or customer behavior data\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\n$75,000-$100,000 determined based on experience, technical expertise, and overall fit for the role.\n\nCelebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → technical discussion → conversation with the team → offer.\n\nWe aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nCelebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.\n\nIf you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please let us know and we will work with you to make the process accessible.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSalary Range: 75,000 - 100,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"59d13e89-be91-4cd8-8380-bf14141cae7d","title":"QA ENGINEER","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-14T11:23:23.059+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/59d13e89-be91-4cd8-8380-bf14141cae7d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/59d13e89-be91-4cd8-8380-bf14141cae7d/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>Job Description</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CelebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will join the engineering team behind our new mid-market analytics platform, helping ensure that the product customers rely on for exploring data and understanding business performance is reliable, accurate, and easy to use. You will own the overall test strategy and automation coverage, working closely with developers and product teams to build quality into the product from the start.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and extend the automated regression suite using a modern testing framework such as Playwright or Cypress</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define test strategy for new features alongside the engineers and product team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Triage incoming bugs, assess severity and prioritize issues based on evidence and customer impact</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain test execution in CI and keep the suite reliable and fast enough to support frequent releases</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Run release verification and ensure agreed quality criteria are met before deployment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify gaps in test coverage and proactively improve the overall quality strategy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track and communicate meaningful quality metrics, including coverage, escaped defects, and test stability</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with developers to investigate complex issues and identify their root causes</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of QA experience working on production web applications</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with automated testing using a framework such as Playwright or Cypress</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience integrating automated tests into CI/CD pipelines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of test strategy and how to balance automated and manual testing</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good judgment when assessing bugs, risks, and release readiness</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to create clear, practical test plans that developers and product teams can use</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working closely with engineers and product stakeholders in a collaborative environment</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">API and contract testing</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Performance and load testing</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Accessibility testing</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">SQL and relational database experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience testing analytics, reporting, or data-heavy applications</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous B2B SaaS experience</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$85,000-$110,000 determined based on experience, technical expertise, and overall fit for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CelebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → technical discussion → conversation with the team → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.</p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CelebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please let us know and we will work with you to make the process accessible.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 85,000 - 110,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"JOB DESCRIPTION\n\nCelebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.\n\n \n\nYou will join the engineering team behind our new mid-market analytics platform, helping ensure that the product customers rely on for exploring data and understanding business performance is reliable, accurate, and easy to use. You will own the overall test strategy and automation coverage, working closely with developers and product teams to build quality into the product from the start.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Own and extend the automated regression suite using a modern testing framework such as Playwright or Cypress\n\n - Define test strategy for new features alongside the engineers and product team\n\n - Triage incoming bugs, assess severity and prioritize issues based on evidence and customer impact\n\n - Maintain test execution in CI and keep the suite reliable and fast enough to support frequent releases\n\n - Run release verification and ensure agreed quality criteria are met before deployment\n\n - Identify gaps in test coverage and proactively improve the overall quality strategy\n\n - Track and communicate meaningful quality metrics, including coverage, escaped defects, and test stability\n\n - Collaborate with developers to investigate complex issues and identify their root causes\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 3+ years of QA experience working on production web applications\n\n - Hands-on experience with automated testing using a framework such as Playwright or Cypress\n\n - Experience integrating automated tests into CI/CD pipelines\n\n - Strong understanding of test strategy and how to balance automated and manual testing\n\n - Good judgment when assessing bugs, risks, and release readiness\n\n - Ability to create clear, practical test plans that developers and product teams can use\n\n - Comfortable working closely with engineers and product stakeholders in a collaborative environment\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - API and contract testing\n\n - Performance and load testing\n\n - Accessibility testing\n\n - SQL and relational database experience\n\n - Experience testing analytics, reporting, or data-heavy applications\n\n - Previous B2B SaaS experience\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\n$85,000-$110,000 determined based on experience, technical expertise, and overall fit for the role.\n\nCelebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → technical discussion → conversation with the team → offer.\n\nWe aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nCelebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.\n\nIf you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please let us know and we will work with you to make the process accessible.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSalary Range: 85,000 - 110,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"1b5e5aef-42a9-45d4-ac9f-9f39d2408afb","title":"DevOps Engineer","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-14T11:24:31.875+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/1b5e5aef-42a9-45d4-ac9f-9f39d2408afb","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/1b5e5aef-42a9-45d4-ac9f-9f39d2408afb/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>Job Description</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CelebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will join the engineering team behind our new mid-market analytics platform, building and maintaining the infrastructure that keeps the product secure, reliable, and ready to scale. You will play a key role in shaping our cloud environment, deployment practices, observability, and incident response as the platform grows from its early stages into a dependable product for business customers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own infrastructure as code across development, staging, and production environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build, maintain, and improve CI/CD pipelines to make deployments reliable and efficient</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage cloud infrastructure and help establish scalable engineering practices as the platform grows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own monitoring, alerting, observability, and on-call runbooks while continuously reducing unnecessary alert noise</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead incident response, coordinate technical resolution, and run blameless post-mortems that result in meaningful improvements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor and optimize cloud usage and infrastructure costs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strengthen infrastructure security and work with the wider engineering team on security and compliance requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with developers to improve reliability, deployment workflows, and developer experience</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of experience in infrastructure, platform, or DevOps engineering</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong production experience with AWS or GCP</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with Terraform or another infrastructure-as-code solution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Real-world experience participating in an on-call rotation and handling production incidents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with containers and container orchestration in production environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of CI/CD, monitoring, networking, and cloud infrastructure</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to investigate complex infrastructure issues and explain technical decisions clearly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable taking ownership of reliability and operational improvements in a growing product environment</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience operating Kubernetes at scale</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with SOC 2, HIPAA, or similar compliance requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cloud cost optimization experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Go or Python experience for infrastructure and developer tooling</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting data-intensive or analytics platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience establishing infrastructure practices for a growing engineering team</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$120,000-$155,000 determined based on experience, technical expertise, and overall fit for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CelebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → technical discussion → conversation with the team → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.</p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CelebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please let us know and we will work with you to make the process accessible.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 120,000 - 155,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"JOB DESCRIPTION\n\nCelebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.\n\n \n\nYou will join the engineering team behind our new mid-market analytics platform, building and maintaining the infrastructure that keeps the product secure, reliable, and ready to scale. You will play a key role in shaping our cloud environment, deployment practices, observability, and incident response as the platform grows from its early stages into a dependable product for business customers.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Own infrastructure as code across development, staging, and production environments\n\n - Build, maintain, and improve CI/CD pipelines to make deployments reliable and efficient\n\n - Manage cloud infrastructure and help establish scalable engineering practices as the platform grows\n\n - Own monitoring, alerting, observability, and on-call runbooks while continuously reducing unnecessary alert noise\n\n - Lead incident response, coordinate technical resolution, and run blameless post-mortems that result in meaningful improvements\n\n - Monitor and optimize cloud usage and infrastructure costs\n\n - Strengthen infrastructure security and work with the wider engineering team on security and compliance requirements\n\n - Partner with developers to improve reliability, deployment workflows, and developer experience\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 4+ years of experience in infrastructure, platform, or DevOps engineering\n\n - Strong production experience with AWS or GCP\n\n - Hands-on experience with Terraform or another infrastructure-as-code solution\n\n - Real-world experience participating in an on-call rotation and handling production incidents\n\n - Experience with containers and container orchestration in production environments\n\n - Strong understanding of CI/CD, monitoring, networking, and cloud infrastructure\n\n - Ability to investigate complex infrastructure issues and explain technical decisions clearly\n\n - Comfortable taking ownership of reliability and operational improvements in a growing product environment\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience operating Kubernetes at scale\n\n - Experience with SOC 2, HIPAA, or similar compliance requirements\n\n - Cloud cost optimization experience\n\n - Go or Python experience for infrastructure and developer tooling\n\n - Experience supporting data-intensive or analytics platforms\n\n - Experience establishing infrastructure practices for a growing engineering team\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\n$120,000-$155,000 determined based on experience, technical expertise, and overall fit for the role.\n\nCelebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → technical discussion → conversation with the team → offer.\n\nWe aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nCelebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.\n\nIf you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please let us know and we will work with you to make the process accessible.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSalary Range: 120,000 - 155,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"90833e01-246c-4e30-97a6-4dd3ac317876","title":"JUNIOR SOFTWARE DEVELOPER","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-14T11:27:06.575+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/90833e01-246c-4e30-97a6-4dd3ac317876","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/90833e01-246c-4e30-97a6-4dd3ac317876/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>Job Description</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CelebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will join the engineering team behind our new mid-market analytics platform in a supported entry-level role designed for developers who are ready to grow their professional experience. You will work alongside experienced engineers, contribute to well-scoped features, and gradually take on more ownership as you become familiar with the product and codebase. We care more about how you think, learn, and approach problems than the number of years on your resume.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build small features, improvements, and bug fixes with guidance from experienced engineers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in code reviews and learn how to give and receive constructive feedback</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Write tests for the code you contribute and develop good engineering habits from the start</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work through a structured development plan with support from a mentor</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Break down unfamiliar problems, ask thoughtful questions, and seek guidance when needed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to technical documentation and improve it as you learn the product</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gradually take ownership of larger and more complex pieces of work as your skills develop</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrable programming ability in a modern programming language</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Personal, academic, or open-source projects that you can explain clearly, including the decisions behind them</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A structured approach to solving problems you have not encountered before</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Curiosity, willingness to learn, and an ability to apply feedback</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication skills and a collaborative approach to working with experienced engineers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">No professional software development experience required — degree, bootcamp, self-taught, and other learning paths are all welcome</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to React, TypeScript, Python, PostgreSQL, or similar technologies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Internship or project-based software development experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Open-source contributions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with Git and collaborative development workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Interest in data, analytics, or B2B SaaS products</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$65,000-$85,000 determined based on experience, technical skills, and overall fit for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CelebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, mentorship and professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → technical discussion → conversation with the team → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.</p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CelebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please let us know and we will work with you to make the process accessible.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Seniority Level:</strong> Junior</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 65,000 - 85,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"JOB DESCRIPTION\n\nCelebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.\n\n \n\nYou will join the engineering team behind our new mid-market analytics platform in a supported entry-level role designed for developers who are ready to grow their professional experience. You will work alongside experienced engineers, contribute to well-scoped features, and gradually take on more ownership as you become familiar with the product and codebase. We care more about how you think, learn, and approach problems than the number of years on your resume.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Build small features, improvements, and bug fixes with guidance from experienced engineers\n\n - Participate in code reviews and learn how to give and receive constructive feedback\n\n - Write tests for the code you contribute and develop good engineering habits from the start\n\n - Work through a structured development plan with support from a mentor\n\n - Break down unfamiliar problems, ask thoughtful questions, and seek guidance when needed\n\n - Contribute to technical documentation and improve it as you learn the product\n\n - Gradually take ownership of larger and more complex pieces of work as your skills develop\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - Demonstrable programming ability in a modern programming language\n\n - Personal, academic, or open-source projects that you can explain clearly, including the decisions behind them\n\n - A structured approach to solving problems you have not encountered before\n\n - Curiosity, willingness to learn, and an ability to apply feedback\n\n - Strong communication skills and a collaborative approach to working with experienced engineers\n\n - No professional software development experience required — degree, bootcamp, self-taught, and other learning paths are all welcome\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Exposure to React, TypeScript, Python, PostgreSQL, or similar technologies\n\n - Internship or project-based software development experience\n\n - Open-source contributions\n\n - Experience working with Git and collaborative development workflows\n\n - Interest in data, analytics, or B2B SaaS products\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\n$65,000-$85,000 determined based on experience, technical skills, and overall fit for the role.\n\nCelebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, mentorship and professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → technical discussion → conversation with the team → offer.\n\nWe aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nCelebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.\n\nIf you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please let us know and we will work with you to make the process accessible.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSeniority Level: Junior\n\nSalary Range: 65,000 - 85,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"d432ef07-6d09-481b-977b-db4c54dbee8b","title":"PRODUCT MANAGER","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-14T11:28:11.326+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/d432ef07-6d09-481b-977b-db4c54dbee8b","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/d432ef07-6d09-481b-977b-db4c54dbee8b/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>Job Description</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CelebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will join the team building our new mid-market analytics platform and take ownership of a key product area from discovery through launch and iteration. Working closely with engineering, design, data, and commercial teams, you will help define what we build, why it matters, and how we measure whether it is delivering value for customers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the roadmap and product direction for a defined area of the analytics platform</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead customer discovery and translate customer needs, feedback, and market signals into clear product requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with engineering and design throughout the product development cycle rather than treating handoff as the end of the process</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define measurable outcomes and success criteria before launching new features, then evaluate results after release</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prioritize opportunities based on customer value, business impact, evidence, and engineering effort</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Make clear trade-offs and communicate what the team is not building and why</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with sales and customer success to provide product context and support customer conversations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use product analytics and qualitative feedback to continuously improve the product roadmap</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of product management experience in B2B software or SaaS</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of owning and shipping meaningful product outcomes from discovery through launch</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong product judgment and a clear approach to prioritization and trade-offs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable challenging assumptions and saying no when the evidence does not support an idea</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to define meaningful product metrics and use data to evaluate hypotheses</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication skills and the ability to work effectively with technical and non-technical stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Customer-focused mindset with an understanding of how product decisions translate into business value</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with analytics, data, reporting, or business intelligence products</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Technical or engineering background</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with product-led growth</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous B2B SaaS experience serving mid-market customers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with data-intensive workflows or complex business software</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$120,000-$150,000 determined based on experience, product expertise, and overall fit for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CelebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → product discussion → conversation with the team → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.</p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CelebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please let us know and we will work with you to make the process accessible.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 120,000 - 150,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"JOB DESCRIPTION\n\nCelebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.\n\n \n\nYou will join the team building our new mid-market analytics platform and take ownership of a key product area from discovery through launch and iteration. Working closely with engineering, design, data, and commercial teams, you will help define what we build, why it matters, and how we measure whether it is delivering value for customers.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Own the roadmap and product direction for a defined area of the analytics platform\n\n - Lead customer discovery and translate customer needs, feedback, and market signals into clear product requirements\n\n - Work closely with engineering and design throughout the product development cycle rather than treating handoff as the end of the process\n\n - Define measurable outcomes and success criteria before launching new features, then evaluate results after release\n\n - Prioritize opportunities based on customer value, business impact, evidence, and engineering effort\n\n - Make clear trade-offs and communicate what the team is not building and why\n\n - Partner with sales and customer success to provide product context and support customer conversations\n\n - Use product analytics and qualitative feedback to continuously improve the product roadmap\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 3+ years of product management experience in B2B software or SaaS\n\n - A track record of owning and shipping meaningful product outcomes from discovery through launch\n\n - Strong product judgment and a clear approach to prioritization and trade-offs\n\n - Comfortable challenging assumptions and saying no when the evidence does not support an idea\n\n - Ability to define meaningful product metrics and use data to evaluate hypotheses\n\n - Strong communication skills and the ability to work effectively with technical and non-technical stakeholders\n\n - Customer-focused mindset with an understanding of how product decisions translate into business value\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with analytics, data, reporting, or business intelligence products\n\n - Technical or engineering background\n\n - Experience with product-led growth\n\n - Previous B2B SaaS experience serving mid-market customers\n\n - Familiarity with data-intensive workflows or complex business software\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\n$120,000-$150,000 determined based on experience, product expertise, and overall fit for the role.\n\nCelebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → product discussion → conversation with the team → offer.\n\nWe aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nCelebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.\n\nIf you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please let us know and we will work with you to make the process accessible.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSalary Range: 120,000 - 150,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"c06856e7-449d-4443-95e1-d099c792f18d","title":"SALES DEVELOPMENT REPRESENTATIVE","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-14T11:29:17.764+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/c06856e7-449d-4443-95e1-d099c792f18d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/c06856e7-449d-4443-95e1-d099c792f18d/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>Job Description</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CelebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will join the commercial team supporting the launch and growth of our new analytics platform for mid-market businesses. You will be one of the first points of contact for prospective customers, helping them understand the value of the product, identify relevant use cases, and connect qualified opportunities with the right members of the sales team.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and manage outbound prospecting campaigns across email, phone, and LinkedIn</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Research target accounts and identify relevant contacts and business opportunities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Respond to inbound interest, understand prospect needs, and qualify potential opportunities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Schedule discovery conversations for Account Executives and provide clear context on each opportunity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and test personalized outreach messaging based on audience, industry, and customer needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate and up-to-date activity and prospect information in the CRM</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with Account Executives and marketing to improve lead quality and conversion</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in regular call reviews, coaching sessions, and team development activities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track outreach performance and use results to continuously improve your approach</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1+ year of experience in sales development, business development, lead generation, or another high-volume customer-facing role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable with proactive outreach across multiple channels</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written and verbal English communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Able to research prospects and tailor messaging rather than relying entirely on generic scripts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational skills and consistent CRM discipline</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working toward measurable goals and learning from performance data</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coachable, curious, resilient, and able to apply feedback to improve your approach</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working independently in a remote environment while collaborating closely with the wider sales team</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous B2B SaaS experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience selling to or working with mid-market businesses</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with analytics, data, or business software</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Salesforce, HubSpot, Outreach, or Salesloft</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Multilingual communication skills</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$55,000-$75,000 base will be determined based on experience, sales expertise, and overall fit for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CelebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, variable compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → sales-focused discussion → conversation with the team → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.</p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CelebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please let us know and we will work with you to make the process accessible.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 55,000 - 75,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"JOB DESCRIPTION\n\nCelebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.\n\nYou will join the commercial team supporting the launch and growth of our new analytics platform for mid-market businesses. You will be one of the first points of contact for prospective customers, helping them understand the value of the product, identify relevant use cases, and connect qualified opportunities with the right members of the sales team.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Build and manage outbound prospecting campaigns across email, phone, and LinkedIn\n\n - Research target accounts and identify relevant contacts and business opportunities\n\n - Respond to inbound interest, understand prospect needs, and qualify potential opportunities\n\n - Schedule discovery conversations for Account Executives and provide clear context on each opportunity\n\n - Develop and test personalized outreach messaging based on audience, industry, and customer needs\n\n - Maintain accurate and up-to-date activity and prospect information in the CRM\n\n - Work closely with Account Executives and marketing to improve lead quality and conversion\n\n - Participate in regular call reviews, coaching sessions, and team development activities\n\n - Track outreach performance and use results to continuously improve your approach\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 1+ year of experience in sales development, business development, lead generation, or another high-volume customer-facing role\n\n - Comfortable with proactive outreach across multiple channels\n\n - Strong written and verbal English communication skills\n\n - Able to research prospects and tailor messaging rather than relying entirely on generic scripts\n\n - Strong organizational skills and consistent CRM discipline\n\n - Comfortable working toward measurable goals and learning from performance data\n\n - Coachable, curious, resilient, and able to apply feedback to improve your approach\n\n - Comfortable working independently in a remote environment while collaborating closely with the wider sales team\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Previous B2B SaaS experience\n\n - Experience selling to or working with mid-market businesses\n\n - Familiarity with analytics, data, or business software\n\n - Experience with Salesforce, HubSpot, Outreach, or Salesloft\n\n - Multilingual communication skills\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\n$55,000-$75,000 base will be determined based on experience, sales expertise, and overall fit for the role.\n\nCelebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, variable compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → sales-focused discussion → conversation with the team → offer.\n\nWe aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nCelebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.\n\nIf you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please let us know and we will work with you to make the process accessible.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSalary Range: 55,000 - 75,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"592587c2-9f4b-4ea4-81fa-4ba11d5b8020","title":"ACCOUNT EXECUTIVE, SMB","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-14T11:30:17.924+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/592587c2-9f4b-4ea4-81fa-4ba11d5b8020","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/592587c2-9f4b-4ea4-81fa-4ba11d5b8020/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>Job Description</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CelebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will join the commercial team supporting the launch and growth of our new analytics platform for mid-market businesses. As an Account Executive, you will own the full sales cycle with SMB customers, from initial discovery and product demonstration through negotiation and close. You will work closely with SDRs, marketing, product, and customer-facing teams to build a strong pipeline and turn qualified opportunities into long-term customers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the full sales cycle from discovery through negotiation and close</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work inbound and SDR-generated opportunities while building additional pipeline through proactive prospecting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Run product demonstrations tailored to each prospect's business needs and use cases</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understand customer challenges and connect them to relevant product capabilities and outcomes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage multiple opportunities through the pipeline while maintaining clear next steps and momentum</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Negotiate commercial terms within established company guidelines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate opportunity data and forecasting in the CRM</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with SDRs and marketing to improve pipeline quality and conversion</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Share customer feedback and loss insights with product and leadership teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build strong relationships with prospects and create a thoughtful, consultative buying experience</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience closing B2B software or SaaS deals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated success meeting or exceeding sales targets</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing a full sales cycle from qualification through close</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong discovery and qualification skills, with a structured approach to evaluating opportunities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to understand a prospect's business challenges and connect them to meaningful product value</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable running product demonstrations independently</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong negotiation, communication, and objection-handling skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to analyze both successful and unsuccessful deals and apply those lessons to future opportunities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong CRM discipline and forecasting habits</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Self-motivated and comfortable working independently in a remote environment</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience selling analytics, data, reporting, or business intelligence products</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with SMB or high-velocity sales</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with MEDDIC, Command of the Message, or another structured sales methodology</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous experience selling to mid-market businesses</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Salesforce or similar CRM platforms</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$70,000-$95,000 base will be determined based on experience, sales expertise, and overall fit for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CelebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, variable compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → sales-focused discussion → conversation with the team → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.</p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CelebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please let us know and we will work with you to make the process accessible.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 70,000 - 95,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"JOB DESCRIPTION\n\nCelebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.\n\nYou will join the commercial team supporting the launch and growth of our new analytics platform for mid-market businesses. As an Account Executive, you will own the full sales cycle with SMB customers, from initial discovery and product demonstration through negotiation and close. You will work closely with SDRs, marketing, product, and customer-facing teams to build a strong pipeline and turn qualified opportunities into long-term customers.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Own the full sales cycle from discovery through negotiation and close\n\n - Work inbound and SDR-generated opportunities while building additional pipeline through proactive prospecting\n\n - Run product demonstrations tailored to each prospect's business needs and use cases\n\n - Understand customer challenges and connect them to relevant product capabilities and outcomes\n\n - Manage multiple opportunities through the pipeline while maintaining clear next steps and momentum\n\n - Negotiate commercial terms within established company guidelines\n\n - Maintain accurate opportunity data and forecasting in the CRM\n\n - Work closely with SDRs and marketing to improve pipeline quality and conversion\n\n - Share customer feedback and loss insights with product and leadership teams\n\n - Build strong relationships with prospects and create a thoughtful, consultative buying experience\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 2+ years of experience closing B2B software or SaaS deals\n\n - Demonstrated success meeting or exceeding sales targets\n\n - Experience managing a full sales cycle from qualification through close\n\n - Strong discovery and qualification skills, with a structured approach to evaluating opportunities\n\n - Ability to understand a prospect's business challenges and connect them to meaningful product value\n\n - Comfortable running product demonstrations independently\n\n - Strong negotiation, communication, and objection-handling skills\n\n - Ability to analyze both successful and unsuccessful deals and apply those lessons to future opportunities\n\n - Strong CRM discipline and forecasting habits\n\n - Self-motivated and comfortable working independently in a remote environment\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience selling analytics, data, reporting, or business intelligence products\n\n - Experience with SMB or high-velocity sales\n\n - Familiarity with MEDDIC, Command of the Message, or another structured sales methodology\n\n - Previous experience selling to mid-market businesses\n\n - Experience with Salesforce or similar CRM platforms\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\n$70,000-$95,000 base will be determined based on experience, sales expertise, and overall fit for the role.\n\nCelebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, variable compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → sales-focused discussion → conversation with the team → offer.\n\nWe aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nCelebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.\n\nIf you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please let us know and we will work with you to make the process accessible.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSalary Range: 70,000 - 95,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"0085be20-f11b-49de-bec2-5d7146eb8be7","title":"Full Stack Developer","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-17T12:42:57.638+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/0085be20-f11b-49de-bec2-5d7146eb8be7","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/0085be20-f11b-49de-bec2-5d7146eb8be7/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a <strong>Full Stack Developer</strong> to join our engineering team and help build and enhance our health services platform. In this role, you will work across both frontend and backend technologies to develop secure, scalable, and user-friendly applications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will collaborate with product managers, designers, QA engineers, and other developers to deliver high-quality features and contribute throughout the entire software development lifecycle.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and maintain both frontend and backend components of web applications.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build responsive user interfaces using modern frontend technologies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, develop, and integrate RESTful APIs and backend services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with cross-functional teams to deliver new features and product enhancements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Write clean, maintainable, and well-documented code following best practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Troubleshoot, debug, and resolve technical issues across the application stack.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Optimize application performance, scalability, and security.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in code reviews and contribute to improving development standards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work in an Agile environment and actively contribute to sprint planning and delivery.</p></li></ul><h2>Requirements</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>3+ years</strong> of commercial experience as a Full Stack Developer or in a similar role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong experience with <strong>JavaScript/TypeScript</strong> and modern frontend frameworks such as <strong>React</strong>.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with backend technologies such as <strong>Node.js, Java, or .NET</strong>.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience developing and integrating REST APIs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good knowledge of HTML5, CSS3, and responsive web development.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with relational databases such as PostgreSQL, MySQL, or SQL Server.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with Git and collaborative development workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical and problem-solving skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good English communication skills.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with GraphQL.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with Docker and Kubernetes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with cloud platforms such as AWS, Azure, or GCP.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge of CI/CD pipelines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with microservices architecture.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working in healthcare, SaaS, or other regulated industries.</p></li></ul><h2>What We Offer</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fully remote work with flexible working hours.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunity to work on an innovative health services platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Modern technology stack and collaborative engineering environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional development and learning opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive compensation based on experience and skills.</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$110000–$130000 depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Equal Opportunity</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CareerSwift is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Seniority Level:</strong> Middle</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 110,000 - 130,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"We are looking for a Full Stack Developer to join our engineering team and help build and enhance our health services platform. In this role, you will work across both frontend and backend technologies to develop secure, scalable, and user-friendly applications.\n\nYou will collaborate with product managers, designers, QA engineers, and other developers to deliver high-quality features and contribute throughout the entire software development lifecycle.\n\n\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Develop and maintain both frontend and backend components of web applications.\n\n - Build responsive user interfaces using modern frontend technologies.\n\n - Design, develop, and integrate RESTful APIs and backend services.\n\n - Collaborate with cross-functional teams to deliver new features and product enhancements.\n\n - Write clean, maintainable, and well-documented code following best practices.\n\n - Troubleshoot, debug, and resolve technical issues across the application stack.\n\n - Optimize application performance, scalability, and security.\n\n - Participate in code reviews and contribute to improving development standards.\n\n - Work in an Agile environment and actively contribute to sprint planning and delivery.\n\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n\n - 3+ years of commercial experience as a Full Stack Developer or in a similar role.\n\n - Strong experience with JavaScript/TypeScript and modern frontend frameworks such as React.\n\n - Experience with backend technologies such as Node.js, Java, or .NET.\n\n - Experience developing and integrating REST APIs.\n\n - Good knowledge of HTML5, CSS3, and responsive web development.\n\n - Experience working with relational databases such as PostgreSQL, MySQL, or SQL Server.\n\n - Familiarity with Git and collaborative development workflows.\n\n - Strong analytical and problem-solving skills.\n\n - Good English communication skills.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with GraphQL.\n\n - Familiarity with Docker and Kubernetes.\n\n - Experience with cloud platforms such as AWS, Azure, or GCP.\n\n - Knowledge of CI/CD pipelines.\n\n - Experience with microservices architecture.\n\n - Experience working in healthcare, SaaS, or other regulated industries.\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Fully remote work with flexible working hours.\n\n - Opportunity to work on an innovative health services platform.\n\n - Modern technology stack and collaborative engineering environment.\n\n - Professional development and learning opportunities.\n\n - Competitive compensation based on experience and skills.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$110000–$130000 depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n \n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nCareerSwift is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSeniority Level: Middle\n\nSalary Range: 110,000 - 130,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"06bcd96b-b5be-4fa1-9fd2-2206eb2ac065","title":"Спеціаліст з розвитку продажів (SDR)","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-17T12:44:22.906+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/06bcd96b-b5be-4fa1-9fd2-2206eb2ac065","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/06bcd96b-b5be-4fa1-9fd2-2206eb2ac065/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>Job Description</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a motivated and results-driven <strong>Sales Development Representative (SDR)</strong> to join our growing sales team. In this role, you will help generate new business opportunities by identifying potential customers, engaging with prospects, and supporting the sales pipeline.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will work closely with the Sales and Marketing teams to research target markets, reach out to potential customers, qualify leads, and schedule meetings with prospective clients. This is a great opportunity for someone who wants to build a career in B2B sales within a technology-driven environment.</p><h2>Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Research and identify potential customers and target accounts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct outbound outreach through email, LinkedIn, and other communication channels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Qualify inbound and outbound leads based on business needs and fit.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Schedule discovery meetings for the sales team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate lead and activity records in CRM systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with marketing and sales teams on campaigns and lead generation activities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track outreach performance and provide feedback to improve sales processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay informed about industry trends, customer needs, and company solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support continuous improvement of sales outreach strategies.</p></li></ul><h2>Requirements</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>0–2 years</strong> of experience in sales, business development, customer-facing roles, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong interest in B2B sales and technology solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication and interpersonal skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to research, identify opportunities, and engage with potential customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational skills and attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Self-motivated, proactive, and comfortable working toward goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently in a remote environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent English communication skills.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous experience with sales outreach, lead generation, or customer support.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with CRM tools such as Salesforce, HubSpot, or similar.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience using LinkedIn Sales Navigator or similar prospecting tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Interest in SaaS, healthcare technology, or B2B software solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of sales funnels and qualification processes.</p></li></ul><h2>What We Offer</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fully remote work with flexible working hours.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunity to start and grow your career in B2B technology sales.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with modern sales tools and processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaboration with international sales, marketing, and product teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional development and career growth opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive compensation with performance-based incentives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Supportive and collaborative team environment.</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">OTE (base + commission) $60K – $85K depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Equal Opportunity</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CareerSwift is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.</p>","descriptionPlain":"JOB DESCRIPTION\n\nWe are looking for a motivated and results-driven Sales Development Representative (SDR) to join our growing sales team. In this role, you will help generate new business opportunities by identifying potential customers, engaging with prospects, and supporting the sales pipeline.\n\nYou will work closely with the Sales and Marketing teams to research target markets, reach out to potential customers, qualify leads, and schedule meetings with prospective clients. This is a great opportunity for someone who wants to build a career in B2B sales within a technology-driven environment.\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Research and identify potential customers and target accounts.\n\n - Conduct outbound outreach through email, LinkedIn, and other communication channels.\n\n - Qualify inbound and outbound leads based on business needs and fit.\n\n - Schedule discovery meetings for the sales team.\n\n - Maintain accurate lead and activity records in CRM systems.\n\n - Collaborate with marketing and sales teams on campaigns and lead generation activities.\n\n - Track outreach performance and provide feedback to improve sales processes.\n\n - Stay informed about industry trends, customer needs, and company solutions.\n\n - Support continuous improvement of sales outreach strategies.\n\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n\n - 0–2 years of experience in sales, business development, customer-facing roles, or a related field.\n\n - Strong interest in B2B sales and technology solutions.\n\n - Excellent communication and interpersonal skills.\n\n - Ability to research, identify opportunities, and engage with potential customers.\n\n - Strong organizational skills and attention to detail.\n\n - Self-motivated, proactive, and comfortable working toward goals.\n\n - Ability to work independently in a remote environment.\n\n - Excellent English communication skills.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Previous experience with sales outreach, lead generation, or customer support.\n\n - Familiarity with CRM tools such as Salesforce, HubSpot, or similar.\n\n - Experience using LinkedIn Sales Navigator or similar prospecting tools.\n\n - Interest in SaaS, healthcare technology, or B2B software solutions.\n\n - Understanding of sales funnels and qualification processes.\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Fully remote work with flexible working hours.\n\n - Opportunity to start and grow your career in B2B technology sales.\n\n - Hands-on experience with modern sales tools and processes.\n\n - Collaboration with international sales, marketing, and product teams.\n\n - Professional development and career growth opportunities.\n\n - Competitive compensation with performance-based incentives.\n\n - Supportive and collaborative team environment.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\nOTE (base + commission) $60K – $85K depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n \n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nCareerSwift is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"35c3514d-6a5e-4336-bb35-b94e77a61282","title":"QA Engineer (Manual) – Junior / Middle","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-17T12:32:15.931+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/35c3514d-6a5e-4336-bb35-b94e77a61282","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/35c3514d-6a5e-4336-bb35-b94e77a61282/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a <strong>QA Engineer (Manual)</strong> to join our engineering team and help ensure the quality, reliability, and usability of our health services platform.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is suitable for both <strong>Junior QA Engineers looking to grow their skills</strong> and <strong>Middle QA Engineers who can independently own testing activities</strong>. You will work closely with developers, product managers, and other team members to identify issues, improve product quality, and help deliver reliable solutions for healthcare providers and users.</p><h2>Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create and execute test cases, test scenarios, and test plans.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Perform functional, regression, integration, and exploratory testing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analyze requirements and identify potential quality risks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify, document, and track defects throughout the development lifecycle.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with developers and product teams to investigate and resolve issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Validate new features and ensure they meet business and user requirements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in release testing and support deployment activities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain testing documentation and provide clear quality reports.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to improving QA processes and testing practices.</p></li></ul><h2>Requirements</h2><h3>Junior Level</h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>1+ year</strong> of experience in software testing or quality assurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of software testing principles and QA methodologies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience creating test cases and reporting defects.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with web application testing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of Agile/Scrum development processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with bug-tracking tools such as Jira or similar.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and analytical thinking.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Willingness to learn and develop QA skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good English communication skills.</p></li></ul><h3>Middle Level</h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>3+ years</strong> of experience in software testing or quality assurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven experience with manual testing of web applications.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong knowledge of testing methodologies and software development lifecycle.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to independently create test strategies, test scenarios, and test documentation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working closely with development and product teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with defect management and release validation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with API testing and tools such as Postman.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to identify risks and suggest improvements to product quality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good English communication skills.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience testing SaaS platforms or complex web applications.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic knowledge of SQL and database testing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of automated testing concepts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with test management tools (TestRail, Zephyr, Xray, or similar).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with CI/CD processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working in healthcare, fintech, or other regulated industries.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge of data privacy and security requirements.</p></li></ul><h2>What We Offer</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fully remote work with flexible working hours.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunity to work on an innovative health services platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaboration with experienced engineering and product teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional growth and learning opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Supportive and collaborative team environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive compensation based on experience and skills.</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$55000–$75000 for Junior level depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$90000-$115000 for Middle level depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Equal Opportunity</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CareerSwift is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Seniority Level:</strong> Junior/Middle</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 55,000 - 115,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"We are looking for a QA Engineer (Manual) to join our engineering team and help ensure the quality, reliability, and usability of our health services platform.\n\nThis role is suitable for both Junior QA Engineers looking to grow their skills and Middle QA Engineers who can independently own testing activities. You will work closely with developers, product managers, and other team members to identify issues, improve product quality, and help deliver reliable solutions for healthcare providers and users.\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Create and execute test cases, test scenarios, and test plans.\n\n - Perform functional, regression, integration, and exploratory testing.\n\n - Analyze requirements and identify potential quality risks.\n\n - Identify, document, and track defects throughout the development lifecycle.\n\n - Collaborate with developers and product teams to investigate and resolve issues.\n\n - Validate new features and ensure they meet business and user requirements.\n\n - Participate in release testing and support deployment activities.\n\n - Maintain testing documentation and provide clear quality reports.\n\n - Contribute to improving QA processes and testing practices.\n\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n\n\nJUNIOR LEVEL\n\n - 1+ year of experience in software testing or quality assurance.\n\n - Understanding of software testing principles and QA methodologies.\n\n - Experience creating test cases and reporting defects.\n\n - Familiarity with web application testing.\n\n - Understanding of Agile/Scrum development processes.\n\n - Familiarity with bug-tracking tools such as Jira or similar.\n\n - Strong attention to detail and analytical thinking.\n\n - Willingness to learn and develop QA skills.\n\n - Good English communication skills.\n\n\nMIDDLE LEVEL\n\n - 3+ years of experience in software testing or quality assurance.\n\n - Proven experience with manual testing of web applications.\n\n - Strong knowledge of testing methodologies and software development lifecycle.\n\n - Ability to independently create test strategies, test scenarios, and test documentation.\n\n - Experience working closely with development and product teams.\n\n - Experience with defect management and release validation.\n\n - Familiarity with API testing and tools such as Postman.\n\n - Ability to identify risks and suggest improvements to product quality.\n\n - Good English communication skills.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience testing SaaS platforms or complex web applications.\n\n - Basic knowledge of SQL and database testing.\n\n - Understanding of automated testing concepts.\n\n - Experience with test management tools (TestRail, Zephyr, Xray, or similar).\n\n - Familiarity with CI/CD processes.\n\n - Experience working in healthcare, fintech, or other regulated industries.\n\n - Knowledge of data privacy and security requirements.\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Fully remote work with flexible working hours.\n\n - Opportunity to work on an innovative health services platform.\n\n - Collaboration with experienced engineering and product teams.\n\n - Professional growth and learning opportunities.\n\n - Supportive and collaborative team environment.\n\n - Competitive compensation based on experience and skills.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$55000–$75000 for Junior level depending on experience and qualifications.\n\n$90000-$115000 for Middle level depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n \n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nCareerSwift is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSeniority Level: Junior/Middle\n\nSalary Range: 55,000 - 115,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"e43acb2e-2eb0-443a-a2f4-539474dc6533","title":"Scrum master","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-17T12:38:47.592+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/e43acb2e-2eb0-443a-a2f4-539474dc6533","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/e43acb2e-2eb0-443a-a2f4-539474dc6533/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for an experienced <strong>Scrum Master</strong> to support an Agile development team of approximately <strong>10 members</strong> working on a modern health services platform.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you will facilitate Agile practices, remove impediments, and help the team deliver high-quality solutions effectively. You will work closely with engineers, product managers, architects, and business stakeholders to improve collaboration, optimize delivery processes, and foster a culture of continuous improvement.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ideal candidate is a strong facilitator and servant leader who understands Agile principles, can coach teams toward greater autonomy, and has experience working in software development environments.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Facilitate Scrum ceremonies, including Daily Stand-ups, Sprint Planning, Sprint Reviews, and Retrospectives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support a development team of around 10 members in applying Agile and Scrum principles effectively.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coach the team on Agile practices, collaboration, and continuous improvement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with the Product Owner to support backlog refinement, prioritization, and sprint planning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and remove impediments that impact team productivity and delivery.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor team progress, identify risks, and support effective delivery planning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Promote transparency through effective use of Agile metrics and reporting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Encourage collaboration between engineering, product, design, and business stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help improve team processes, workflows, and communication practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support the team in maintaining a sustainable delivery pace.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Facilitate discussions around technical challenges, dependencies, and process improvements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to building a positive, collaborative, and high-performing team culture.</p></li></ul><h2>Requirements</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>2+ years</strong> of experience as a Scrum Master, Agile Coach, or similar Agile delivery role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven experience supporting software development teams using Scrum methodology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with cross-functional engineering teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of Agile principles, Scrum framework, and team dynamics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience facilitating Scrum ceremonies and Agile workshops.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to identify blockers and drive effective resolution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication, facilitation, and conflict-resolution skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with Agile tools such as Jira, Confluence, or similar platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work effectively with distributed and remote teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good English communication skills.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working in HealthTech, SaaS, fintech, or other technology-driven industries.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Scrum Master certification (PSM, CSM, or equivalent).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting teams through Agile transformation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with software development lifecycle and engineering practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience using Agile metrics such as velocity, cycle time, burndown charts, and flow metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous experience working with product managers and technical stakeholders.</p></li></ul><h2>What We Offer</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fully remote work with flexible working hours.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunity to support a team building impactful healthcare technology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaboration with experienced engineers, architects, and product teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional development and Agile coaching opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A culture focused on transparency, ownership, and continuous improvement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive compensation based on experience and skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Supportive and collaborative working environment.</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$80000–$100000 depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Equal Opportunity</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CareerSwift is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 80,000 - 100,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"We are looking for an experienced Scrum Master to support an Agile development team of approximately 10 members working on a modern health services platform.\n\nIn this role, you will facilitate Agile practices, remove impediments, and help the team deliver high-quality solutions effectively. You will work closely with engineers, product managers, architects, and business stakeholders to improve collaboration, optimize delivery processes, and foster a culture of continuous improvement.\n\nThe ideal candidate is a strong facilitator and servant leader who understands Agile principles, can coach teams toward greater autonomy, and has experience working in software development environments.\n\n\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Facilitate Scrum ceremonies, including Daily Stand-ups, Sprint Planning, Sprint Reviews, and Retrospectives.\n\n - Support a development team of around 10 members in applying Agile and Scrum principles effectively.\n\n - Coach the team on Agile practices, collaboration, and continuous improvement.\n\n - Work closely with the Product Owner to support backlog refinement, prioritization, and sprint planning.\n\n - Identify and remove impediments that impact team productivity and delivery.\n\n - Monitor team progress, identify risks, and support effective delivery planning.\n\n - Promote transparency through effective use of Agile metrics and reporting.\n\n - Encourage collaboration between engineering, product, design, and business stakeholders.\n\n - Help improve team processes, workflows, and communication practices.\n\n - Support the team in maintaining a sustainable delivery pace.\n\n - Facilitate discussions around technical challenges, dependencies, and process improvements.\n\n - Contribute to building a positive, collaborative, and high-performing team culture.\n\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n\n - 2+ years of experience as a Scrum Master, Agile Coach, or similar Agile delivery role.\n\n - Proven experience supporting software development teams using Scrum methodology.\n\n - Experience working with cross-functional engineering teams.\n\n - Strong understanding of Agile principles, Scrum framework, and team dynamics.\n\n - Experience facilitating Scrum ceremonies and Agile workshops.\n\n - Ability to identify blockers and drive effective resolution.\n\n - Strong communication, facilitation, and conflict-resolution skills.\n\n - Experience working with Agile tools such as Jira, Confluence, or similar platforms.\n\n - Ability to work effectively with distributed and remote teams.\n\n - Good English communication skills.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience working in HealthTech, SaaS, fintech, or other technology-driven industries.\n\n - Scrum Master certification (PSM, CSM, or equivalent).\n\n - Experience supporting teams through Agile transformation.\n\n - Familiarity with software development lifecycle and engineering practices.\n\n - Experience using Agile metrics such as velocity, cycle time, burndown charts, and flow metrics.\n\n - Previous experience working with product managers and technical stakeholders.\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Fully remote work with flexible working hours.\n\n - Opportunity to support a team building impactful healthcare technology.\n\n - Collaboration with experienced engineers, architects, and product teams.\n\n - Professional development and Agile coaching opportunities.\n\n - A culture focused on transparency, ownership, and continuous improvement.\n\n - Competitive compensation based on experience and skills.\n\n - Supportive and collaborative working environment.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$80000–$100000 depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n \n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nCareerSwift is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSalary Range: 80,000 - 100,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"bdc1f0f1-0a94-4bb6-a99a-fd5ce0e14612","title":"Marketing Coordinator","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-17T12:40:05.745+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/bdc1f0f1-0a94-4bb6-a99a-fd5ce0e14612","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/bdc1f0f1-0a94-4bb6-a99a-fd5ce0e14612/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a creative and organized <strong>Marketing Coordinator</strong> to support our marketing activities across digital channels. This is an entry-level opportunity for someone looking to build experience in digital marketing, content coordination, and campaign execution.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will work closely with the marketing team, designers, and external partners to support campaigns, manage content schedules, and track marketing performance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support planning and execution of digital marketing campaigns.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage content calendars and coordinate social media publishing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with email marketing campaigns and newsletters.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate with designers and external agencies on marketing materials.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor campaign performance and prepare basic reports.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track social media engagement and website metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support market research and competitor analysis.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain marketing assets and documentation.</p></li></ul><h2>Requirements</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>0–2 years</strong> of experience in marketing, communications, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic understanding of digital marketing and social media platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with content scheduling and analytics tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written communication skills and attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good organizational skills and ability to manage multiple tasks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Creative mindset and willingness to learn.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently in a remote environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good English communication skills.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with tools such as Canva, HubSpot, Mailchimp, Google Analytics, or similar.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic knowledge of SEO and email marketing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience creating social media content.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Interest in technology, SaaS, or healthcare industries.</p></li></ul><h2>What We Offer</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fully remote work with flexible working hours.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunity to grow your marketing skills in an international environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with digital campaigns and modern marketing tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Supportive and collaborative team environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional development opportunities.</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$42000–$55000 depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Equal Opportunity</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CareerSwift is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Seniority Level:</strong> Junior</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 42,000 - 55,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"We are looking for a creative and organized Marketing Coordinator to support our marketing activities across digital channels. This is an entry-level opportunity for someone looking to build experience in digital marketing, content coordination, and campaign execution.\n\nYou will work closely with the marketing team, designers, and external partners to support campaigns, manage content schedules, and track marketing performance.\n\n\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Support planning and execution of digital marketing campaigns.\n\n - Manage content calendars and coordinate social media publishing.\n\n - Assist with email marketing campaigns and newsletters.\n\n - Coordinate with designers and external agencies on marketing materials.\n\n - Monitor campaign performance and prepare basic reports.\n\n - Track social media engagement and website metrics.\n\n - Support market research and competitor analysis.\n\n - Maintain marketing assets and documentation.\n\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n\n - 0–2 years of experience in marketing, communications, or a related field.\n\n - Basic understanding of digital marketing and social media platforms.\n\n - Familiarity with content scheduling and analytics tools.\n\n - Strong written communication skills and attention to detail.\n\n - Good organizational skills and ability to manage multiple tasks.\n\n - Creative mindset and willingness to learn.\n\n - Ability to work independently in a remote environment.\n\n - Good English communication skills.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with tools such as Canva, HubSpot, Mailchimp, Google Analytics, or similar.\n\n - Basic knowledge of SEO and email marketing.\n\n - Experience creating social media content.\n\n - Interest in technology, SaaS, or healthcare industries.\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Fully remote work with flexible working hours.\n\n - Opportunity to grow your marketing skills in an international environment.\n\n - Hands-on experience with digital campaigns and modern marketing tools.\n\n - Supportive and collaborative team environment.\n\n - Professional development opportunities.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$42000–$55000 depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n \n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nCareerSwift is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSeniority Level: Junior\n\nSalary Range: 42,000 - 55,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"46cf175c-56c7-44a9-b3f6-d9ab48c68b2e","title":"Frontend Developer (React) – Junior / Middle","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-17T12:33:49.437+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/46cf175c-56c7-44a9-b3f6-d9ab48c68b2e","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/46cf175c-56c7-44a9-b3f6-d9ab48c68b2e/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a <strong>Frontend Developer (React)</strong> to join our growing engineering team. Whether you're a strong Junior ready to take the next step or a Middle-level developer looking for new challenges, we'd love to hear from you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you'll work closely with designers, backend developers, and product managers to build intuitive, responsive, and high-performance web applications. You'll contribute to new feature development, improve user experience, and help maintain a scalable and maintainable frontend architecture.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and maintain modern web applications using <strong>React</strong>.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build responsive, user-friendly interfaces based on UI/UX designs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with backend developers to integrate RESTful APIs and GraphQL services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Write clean, reusable, and maintainable code following best practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Optimize application performance, accessibility, and responsiveness.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Debug, troubleshoot, and resolve frontend issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in code reviews and contribute to improving development standards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay up to date with modern frontend technologies and best practices.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Requirements</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Junior Level</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>2+ years</strong> of commercial experience with <strong>React</strong>.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good knowledge of <strong>JavaScript (ES6+)</strong> and/or <strong>TypeScript</strong>.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of <strong>HTML5</strong>, <strong>CSS3</strong>, and responsive web development.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Git and version control workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with REST APIs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic understanding of component-based architecture.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong problem-solving skills and willingness to learn.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good English communication skills.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Middle Level</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>4+ years</strong> of commercial frontend development experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong experience with <strong>React</strong> and modern JavaScript/TypeScript.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with state management solutions (Redux, Zustand, Context API, etc.).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience integrating REST and/or GraphQL APIs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solid understanding of performance optimization and frontend best practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with modern CSS solutions (Tailwind CSS, Styled Components, SCSS, Material UI, etc.).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge of testing frameworks (Jest, React Testing Library, Cypress) is a plus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently and collaborate in an agile environment.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Next.js.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with CI/CD pipelines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Docker.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge of accessibility (WCAG) standards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with cloud platforms such as AWS, Azure, or GCP.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of modern frontend build tools (Vite, Webpack).</p></li></ul><h2>What We Offer</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">100% remote work with flexible working hours.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunity to work on modern, scalable web applications.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Supportive and collaborative engineering team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional growth and learning opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive salary based on experience and skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Interesting international projects using modern technologies.</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$65000–$85000 for Junior level depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$90000-$115000 for Middle level depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Equal Opportunity</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CareerSwift is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Seniority Level:</strong> Junior/Middle</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 65,000 - 115,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"We are looking for a Frontend Developer (React) to join our growing engineering team. Whether you're a strong Junior ready to take the next step or a Middle-level developer looking for new challenges, we'd love to hear from you.\n\nIn this role, you'll work closely with designers, backend developers, and product managers to build intuitive, responsive, and high-performance web applications. You'll contribute to new feature development, improve user experience, and help maintain a scalable and maintainable frontend architecture.\n\n\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Develop and maintain modern web applications using React.\n\n - Build responsive, user-friendly interfaces based on UI/UX designs.\n\n - Collaborate with backend developers to integrate RESTful APIs and GraphQL services.\n\n - Write clean, reusable, and maintainable code following best practices.\n\n - Optimize application performance, accessibility, and responsiveness.\n\n - Debug, troubleshoot, and resolve frontend issues.\n\n - Participate in code reviews and contribute to improving development standards.\n\n - Stay up to date with modern frontend technologies and best practices.\n\n\n\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n\nJunior Level\n\n - 2+ years of commercial experience with React.\n\n - Good knowledge of JavaScript (ES6+) and/or TypeScript.\n\n - Understanding of HTML5, CSS3, and responsive web development.\n\n - Experience with Git and version control workflows.\n\n - Familiarity with REST APIs.\n\n - Basic understanding of component-based architecture.\n\n - Strong problem-solving skills and willingness to learn.\n\n - Good English communication skills.\n\nMiddle Level\n\n - 4+ years of commercial frontend development experience.\n\n - Strong experience with React and modern JavaScript/TypeScript.\n\n - Experience with state management solutions (Redux, Zustand, Context API, etc.).\n\n - Experience integrating REST and/or GraphQL APIs.\n\n - Solid understanding of performance optimization and frontend best practices.\n\n - Experience with modern CSS solutions (Tailwind CSS, Styled Components, SCSS, Material UI, etc.).\n\n - Knowledge of testing frameworks (Jest, React Testing Library, Cypress) is a plus.\n\n - Ability to work independently and collaborate in an agile environment.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with Next.js.\n\n - Familiarity with CI/CD pipelines.\n\n - Experience with Docker.\n\n - Knowledge of accessibility (WCAG) standards.\n\n - Experience working with cloud platforms such as AWS, Azure, or GCP.\n\n - Understanding of modern frontend build tools (Vite, Webpack).\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - 100% remote work with flexible working hours.\n\n - Opportunity to work on modern, scalable web applications.\n\n - Supportive and collaborative engineering team.\n\n - Professional growth and learning opportunities.\n\n - Competitive salary based on experience and skills.\n\n - Interesting international projects using modern technologies.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$65000–$85000 for Junior level depending on experience and qualifications.\n\n$90000-$115000 for Middle level depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n \n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nCareerSwift is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSeniority Level: Junior/Middle\n\nSalary Range: 65,000 - 115,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"b014dea8-f186-418a-b562-ba681ce82afc","title":"QA Automation Engineer (Middle)","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-17T12:37:26.541+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/b014dea8-f186-418a-b562-ba681ce82afc","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/b014dea8-f186-418a-b562-ba681ce82afc/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a <strong>Middle QA Automation Engineer</strong> to join our engineering team and help ensure the quality, reliability, and performance of our health services platform.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you will design, implement, and maintain automated testing solutions, collaborate with developers and product teams, and contribute to improving our testing processes. You will play an important role in delivering secure, stable, and user-friendly solutions that support healthcare providers and users.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, develop, and maintain automated test frameworks and test scripts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create and execute automated tests for web applications, APIs, and backend services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with developers, product managers, and QA team members to define testing strategies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analyze requirements and prepare test scenarios, test cases, and test plans.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify, document, and track defects, ensuring timely resolution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Perform regression, integration, and end-to-end testing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Integrate automated tests into CI/CD pipelines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Investigate test failures and provide clear feedback to development teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in code reviews and contribute to improving software quality practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help establish and improve QA processes, standards, and best practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure applications meet quality, performance, and reliability expectations.</p></li></ul><h2>Requirements</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>3+ years</strong> of experience in software testing and quality assurance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong experience with <strong>test automation</strong> and building automated test solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with automation frameworks such as <strong>Selenium, Playwright, Cypress, or similar</strong>.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience testing web applications and REST APIs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good understanding of software development lifecycle (SDLC) and QA methodologies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience writing clear test cases, test scenarios, and defect reports.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with CI/CD tools and automated testing pipelines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with version control systems (Git).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of Agile/Scrum development processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical and problem-solving skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good communication skills in English.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with API testing tools such as Postman, REST Assured, or similar.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge of performance testing tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with cloud-based applications and services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with Docker and containerized environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with SQL and database testing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge of security testing practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working in healthcare, fintech, or other regulated industries.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with healthcare data standards such as HL7 or FHIR.</p></li></ul><h2>What We Offer</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fully remote work with flexible working hours.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunity to work on a modern healthcare technology platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaboration with experienced engineers and product teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional growth and learning opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to influence QA processes and engineering practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive compensation based on experience and skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Supportive and collaborative team environment.</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$100000–$125000 depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Equal Opportunity</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CareerSwift is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Seniority Level:</strong> Middle</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 100,000 - 125,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"We are looking for a Middle QA Automation Engineer to join our engineering team and help ensure the quality, reliability, and performance of our health services platform.\n\nIn this role, you will design, implement, and maintain automated testing solutions, collaborate with developers and product teams, and contribute to improving our testing processes. You will play an important role in delivering secure, stable, and user-friendly solutions that support healthcare providers and users.\n\n\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Design, develop, and maintain automated test frameworks and test scripts.\n\n - Create and execute automated tests for web applications, APIs, and backend services.\n\n - Collaborate with developers, product managers, and QA team members to define testing strategies.\n\n - Analyze requirements and prepare test scenarios, test cases, and test plans.\n\n - Identify, document, and track defects, ensuring timely resolution.\n\n - Perform regression, integration, and end-to-end testing.\n\n - Integrate automated tests into CI/CD pipelines.\n\n - Investigate test failures and provide clear feedback to development teams.\n\n - Participate in code reviews and contribute to improving software quality practices.\n\n - Help establish and improve QA processes, standards, and best practices.\n\n - Ensure applications meet quality, performance, and reliability expectations.\n\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n\n - 3+ years of experience in software testing and quality assurance.\n\n - Strong experience with test automation and building automated test solutions.\n\n - Experience with automation frameworks such as Selenium, Playwright, Cypress, or similar.\n\n - Experience testing web applications and REST APIs.\n\n - Good understanding of software development lifecycle (SDLC) and QA methodologies.\n\n - Experience writing clear test cases, test scenarios, and defect reports.\n\n - Familiarity with CI/CD tools and automated testing pipelines.\n\n - Experience working with version control systems (Git).\n\n - Understanding of Agile/Scrum development processes.\n\n - Strong analytical and problem-solving skills.\n\n - Good communication skills in English.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with API testing tools such as Postman, REST Assured, or similar.\n\n - Knowledge of performance testing tools.\n\n - Experience with cloud-based applications and services.\n\n - Familiarity with Docker and containerized environments.\n\n - Experience with SQL and database testing.\n\n - Knowledge of security testing practices.\n\n - Experience working in healthcare, fintech, or other regulated industries.\n\n - Familiarity with healthcare data standards such as HL7 or FHIR.\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Fully remote work with flexible working hours.\n\n - Opportunity to work on a modern healthcare technology platform.\n\n - Collaboration with experienced engineers and product teams.\n\n - Professional growth and learning opportunities.\n\n - Ability to influence QA processes and engineering practices.\n\n - Competitive compensation based on experience and skills.\n\n - Supportive and collaborative team environment.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$100000–$125000 depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n \n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nCareerSwift is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSeniority Level: Middle\n\nSalary Range: 100,000 - 125,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"2fc23dda-2360-4658-bf25-3c97de488831","title":"Backend Developer (Node.js / Java / .NET)","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-17T12:41:23.253+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/2fc23dda-2360-4658-bf25-3c97de488831","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/2fc23dda-2360-4658-bf25-3c97de488831/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a <strong>Backend Developer</strong> to join our engineering team and help build a secure, scalable, and high-performing health services platform. In this role, you will develop backend services, APIs, and system integrations that power our applications and deliver reliable experiences for healthcare providers and users.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will collaborate closely with frontend developers, QA engineers, product managers, and architects to design and implement high-quality software solutions.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, develop, and maintain backend services and APIs using <strong>Node.js, Java, or .NET</strong>.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build scalable and maintainable server-side applications.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and integrate RESTful APIs and third-party services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with frontend developers to deliver seamless application functionality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Optimize application performance, reliability, and security.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Write clean, reusable, and well-documented code following best practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Troubleshoot, debug, and resolve technical issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in code reviews and contribute to improving engineering standards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work in an Agile environment and collaborate with cross-functional teams.</p></li></ul><h2>Requirements</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>3+ years</strong> of commercial backend development experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong experience with <strong>Node.js, Java, or .NET</strong>.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing and consuming REST APIs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good understanding of relational databases such as PostgreSQL, MySQL, or SQL Server.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with Git and collaborative development workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of software design principles and object-oriented programming.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with cloud platforms (AWS, Azure, or GCP) is a plus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical and problem-solving skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good English communication skills.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with GraphQL.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with Docker and Kubernetes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with CI/CD pipelines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge of microservices architecture.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with NoSQL databases.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working in healthcare, SaaS, or other regulated industries.</p></li></ul><h2>What We Offer</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fully remote work with flexible working hours.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunity to work on an innovative health services platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Modern technology stack and collaborative engineering culture.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional growth and learning opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive compensation based on experience and skills.</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$100000–$120000 depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Equal Opportunity</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CareerSwift is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 100,000 - 120,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"We are looking for a Backend Developer to join our engineering team and help build a secure, scalable, and high-performing health services platform. In this role, you will develop backend services, APIs, and system integrations that power our applications and deliver reliable experiences for healthcare providers and users.\n\nYou will collaborate closely with frontend developers, QA engineers, product managers, and architects to design and implement high-quality software solutions.\n\n\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Design, develop, and maintain backend services and APIs using Node.js, Java, or .NET.\n\n - Build scalable and maintainable server-side applications.\n\n - Develop and integrate RESTful APIs and third-party services.\n\n - Collaborate with frontend developers to deliver seamless application functionality.\n\n - Optimize application performance, reliability, and security.\n\n - Write clean, reusable, and well-documented code following best practices.\n\n - Troubleshoot, debug, and resolve technical issues.\n\n - Participate in code reviews and contribute to improving engineering standards.\n\n - Work in an Agile environment and collaborate with cross-functional teams.\n\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n\n - 3+ years of commercial backend development experience.\n\n - Strong experience with Node.js, Java, or .NET.\n\n - Experience designing and consuming REST APIs.\n\n - Good understanding of relational databases such as PostgreSQL, MySQL, or SQL Server.\n\n - Familiarity with Git and collaborative development workflows.\n\n - Understanding of software design principles and object-oriented programming.\n\n - Experience working with cloud platforms (AWS, Azure, or GCP) is a plus.\n\n - Strong analytical and problem-solving skills.\n\n - Good English communication skills.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with GraphQL.\n\n - Familiarity with Docker and Kubernetes.\n\n - Experience with CI/CD pipelines.\n\n - Knowledge of microservices architecture.\n\n - Experience with NoSQL databases.\n\n - Experience working in healthcare, SaaS, or other regulated industries.\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Fully remote work with flexible working hours.\n\n - Opportunity to work on an innovative health services platform.\n\n - Modern technology stack and collaborative engineering culture.\n\n - Professional growth and learning opportunities.\n\n - Competitive compensation based on experience and skills.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$100000–$120000 depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n \n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nCareerSwift is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSalary Range: 100,000 - 120,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"6a83523c-5c4b-4272-a3dd-57a0da7c3784","title":"Software Engineer (Platform Development) – Junior","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-17T12:36:02.846+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/6a83523c-5c4b-4272-a3dd-57a0da7c3784","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/6a83523c-5c4b-4272-a3dd-57a0da7c3784/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a motivated <strong>Junior Software Engineer</strong> to join our Platform Development team. In this role, you will help build and enhance a modern platform that supports digital health services, enabling healthcare providers and patients to access reliable, secure, and scalable solutions.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll work alongside experienced engineers, product managers, and designers to develop new features, improve system performance, and contribute to building a high-quality platform that makes a positive impact on healthcare.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop, test, and maintain platform features and services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with cross-functional teams to implement new functionality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Write clean, maintainable, and well-documented code.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in code reviews and follow engineering best practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Debug, troubleshoot, and resolve software issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to improving platform performance, reliability, and scalability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with API development and integration.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn and work with modern development tools, frameworks, and cloud technologies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay up to date with software engineering best practices and emerging technologies.</p></li></ul><h2>Requirements</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>2+ years</strong> of commercial software development experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in at least one programming language such as Java, C#, Python, or JavaScript/TypeScript.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of object-oriented programming principles and software design fundamentals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with REST APIs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with relational databases such as PostgreSQL or MySQL.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic knowledge of Git and collaborative development workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of Agile development methodologies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical and problem-solving skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good written and verbal communication skills in English.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Eagerness to learn and grow in a collaborative environment.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with cloud platforms such as AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with Docker and containerized applications.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge of CI/CD pipelines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of microservices architecture.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with healthcare, medical, or health-tech applications.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Awareness of security best practices and data privacy principles.</p></li></ul><h2>What We Offer</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fully remote work with flexible working hours.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mentorship from experienced software engineers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunity to contribute to innovative healthcare technology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional development and learning opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Supportive and collaborative engineering culture.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive salary based on experience and skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunity to work with modern technologies and cloud-based solutions.</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$90000–$110000 depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Equal Opportunity</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CareerSwift is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Seniority Level:</strong> Junior</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 90,000 - 110,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"We are looking for a motivated Junior Software Engineer to join our Platform Development team. In this role, you will help build and enhance a modern platform that supports digital health services, enabling healthcare providers and patients to access reliable, secure, and scalable solutions.\n\nYou'll work alongside experienced engineers, product managers, and designers to develop new features, improve system performance, and contribute to building a high-quality platform that makes a positive impact on healthcare.\n\n\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Develop, test, and maintain platform features and services.\n\n - Collaborate with cross-functional teams to implement new functionality.\n\n - Write clean, maintainable, and well-documented code.\n\n - Participate in code reviews and follow engineering best practices.\n\n - Debug, troubleshoot, and resolve software issues.\n\n - Contribute to improving platform performance, reliability, and scalability.\n\n - Assist with API development and integration.\n\n - Learn and work with modern development tools, frameworks, and cloud technologies.\n\n - Stay up to date with software engineering best practices and emerging technologies.\n\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n\n - 2+ years of commercial software development experience.\n\n - Proficiency in at least one programming language such as Java, C#, Python, or JavaScript/TypeScript.\n\n - Understanding of object-oriented programming principles and software design fundamentals.\n\n - Experience working with REST APIs.\n\n - Familiarity with relational databases such as PostgreSQL or MySQL.\n\n - Basic knowledge of Git and collaborative development workflows.\n\n - Understanding of Agile development methodologies.\n\n - Strong analytical and problem-solving skills.\n\n - Good written and verbal communication skills in English.\n\n - Eagerness to learn and grow in a collaborative environment.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with cloud platforms such as AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud.\n\n - Familiarity with Docker and containerized applications.\n\n - Knowledge of CI/CD pipelines.\n\n - Understanding of microservices architecture.\n\n - Experience with healthcare, medical, or health-tech applications.\n\n - Awareness of security best practices and data privacy principles.\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Fully remote work with flexible working hours.\n\n - Mentorship from experienced software engineers.\n\n - Opportunity to contribute to innovative healthcare technology.\n\n - Professional development and learning opportunities.\n\n - Supportive and collaborative engineering culture.\n\n - Competitive salary based on experience and skills.\n\n - Opportunity to work with modern technologies and cloud-based solutions.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$90000–$110000 depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n \n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nCareerSwift is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSeniority Level: Junior\n\nSalary Range: 90,000 - 110,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"fed447ec-47f6-48eb-9637-63995a7b5606","title":"Provider Credentialing Specialist","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-20T14:20:52.452+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/fed447ec-47f6-48eb-9637-63995a7b5606","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/fed447ec-47f6-48eb-9637-63995a7b5606/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raventra Health</strong> is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Provider Credentialing Specialist, you will support provider clients with payer enrollment, credentialing, and recredentialing activities. You will maintain accurate provider information, track applications and renewals, and help ensure providers remain properly enrolled and eligible to participate with applicable insurance plans.</p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare and submit provider credentialing and payer enrollment applications</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collect, review, and maintain provider documentation, including licenses, certifications, and professional information</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Verify provider credentials and ensure required documentation remains current</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track credentialing applications, approvals, expirations, and recredentialing deadlines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow up with insurance payers and credentialing organizations regarding application status</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate provider records in credentialing databases and internal systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify missing or inconsistent information and work with provider teams to resolve documentation issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support updates to provider information, including practice locations, specialties, and payer participation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain organized documentation and follow established privacy and compliance procedures</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1+ year of experience in provider credentialing, payer enrollment, medical administration, or a related healthcare role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of provider credentialing and payer enrollment processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with insurance payers, credentialing organizations, or provider networks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and ability to manage multiple applications, deadlines, and follow-ups</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience reviewing and maintaining professional licenses, certifications, and provider documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational and time-management skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to communicate effectively with providers, payer representatives, and internal teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently and effectively in a fully remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIPAA-compliant private workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with CAQH and other provider credentialing or enrollment platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Medicare, Medicaid, or commercial payer enrollment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge of NPI, taxonomy codes, and provider enrollment requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with hospital or multi-specialty provider credentialing</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or other healthcare systems</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare administration expertise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.</p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Raventra Health is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Provider Credentialing Specialist, you will support provider clients with payer enrollment, credentialing, and recredentialing activities. You will maintain accurate provider information, track applications and renewals, and help ensure providers remain properly enrolled and eligible to participate with applicable insurance plans.\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Prepare and submit provider credentialing and payer enrollment applications\n\n - Collect, review, and maintain provider documentation, including licenses, certifications, and professional information\n\n - Verify provider credentials and ensure required documentation remains current\n\n - Track credentialing applications, approvals, expirations, and recredentialing deadlines\n\n - Follow up with insurance payers and credentialing organizations regarding application status\n\n - Maintain accurate provider records in credentialing databases and internal systems\n\n - Identify missing or inconsistent information and work with provider teams to resolve documentation issues\n\n - Support updates to provider information, including practice locations, specialties, and payer participation\n\n - Maintain organized documentation and follow established privacy and compliance procedures\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 1+ year of experience in provider credentialing, payer enrollment, medical administration, or a related healthcare role\n\n - Understanding of provider credentialing and payer enrollment processes\n\n - Experience working with insurance payers, credentialing organizations, or provider networks\n\n - Strong attention to detail and ability to manage multiple applications, deadlines, and follow-ups\n\n - Experience reviewing and maintaining professional licenses, certifications, and provider documentation\n\n - Strong organizational and time-management skills\n\n - Ability to communicate effectively with providers, payer representatives, and internal teams\n\n - Ability to work independently and effectively in a fully remote environment\n\n - HIPAA-compliant private workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with CAQH and other provider credentialing or enrollment platforms\n\n - Experience with Medicare, Medicaid, or commercial payer enrollment\n\n - Knowledge of NPI, taxonomy codes, and provider enrollment requirements\n\n - Experience with hospital or multi-specialty provider credentialing\n\n - Familiarity with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or other healthcare systems\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare administration expertise.\n\nBenefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nRaventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"5eb94ac8-19b6-48b7-a1c4-bc385a41a008","title":"Denials & Appeals Specialist","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-20T14:21:57.435+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/5eb94ac8-19b6-48b7-a1c4-bc385a41a008","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/5eb94ac8-19b6-48b7-a1c4-bc385a41a008/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raventra Health</strong> is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Denials &amp; Appeals Specialist, you will investigate denied healthcare claims, determine the reason for denial, and take the appropriate steps to correct, resubmit, or appeal claims. You will work closely with billing, coding, and client teams to recover missed revenue and identify recurring issues that contribute to denials.</p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review denied claims and identify the specific reason for denial</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Research payer policies, claim history, and supporting documentation to determine the appropriate resolution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Correct claim errors and resubmit claims when appropriate</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare and submit reconsiderations and appeals with accurate supporting documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow up with payers on outstanding appeals and document all actions and responses</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor denial trends and identify recurring issues affecting reimbursement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with billing and coding teams to address root causes of recurring denials</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate records of denials, appeals, payer responses, and resolution outcomes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meet productivity and quality expectations while maintaining accuracy and timely follow-up</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in healthcare denials, appeals, medical billing, or a related revenue cycle role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of common claim denial reasons and payer requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience researching denied claims and determining appropriate corrective action</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience preparing and submitting insurance claim appeals or reconsiderations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to interpret EOBs, ERAs, denial codes, and payer correspondence</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and ability to manage multiple claims and deadlines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written communication skills for preparing clear and well-supported appeals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong problem-solving skills and ability to work independently in a remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIPAA-compliant private workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or another major billing or practice management system</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical coding knowledge or certification</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with specific payer types or specialty-specific denials</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience analyzing denial trends and root causes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with provider groups or hospitals</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare revenue cycle expertise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.</p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Raventra Health is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Denials & Appeals Specialist, you will investigate denied healthcare claims, determine the reason for denial, and take the appropriate steps to correct, resubmit, or appeal claims. You will work closely with billing, coding, and client teams to recover missed revenue and identify recurring issues that contribute to denials.\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Review denied claims and identify the specific reason for denial\n\n - Research payer policies, claim history, and supporting documentation to determine the appropriate resolution\n\n - Correct claim errors and resubmit claims when appropriate\n\n - Prepare and submit reconsiderations and appeals with accurate supporting documentation\n\n - Follow up with payers on outstanding appeals and document all actions and responses\n\n - Monitor denial trends and identify recurring issues affecting reimbursement\n\n - Collaborate with billing and coding teams to address root causes of recurring denials\n\n - Maintain accurate records of denials, appeals, payer responses, and resolution outcomes\n\n - Meet productivity and quality expectations while maintaining accuracy and timely follow-up\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 2+ years of experience in healthcare denials, appeals, medical billing, or a related revenue cycle role\n\n - Strong understanding of common claim denial reasons and payer requirements\n\n - Experience researching denied claims and determining appropriate corrective action\n\n - Experience preparing and submitting insurance claim appeals or reconsiderations\n\n - Ability to interpret EOBs, ERAs, denial codes, and payer correspondence\n\n - Strong attention to detail and ability to manage multiple claims and deadlines\n\n - Excellent written communication skills for preparing clear and well-supported appeals\n\n - Strong problem-solving skills and ability to work independently in a remote environment\n\n - HIPAA-compliant private workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or another major billing or practice management system\n\n - Medical coding knowledge or certification\n\n - Experience with specific payer types or specialty-specific denials\n\n - Experience analyzing denial trends and root causes\n\n - Experience working with provider groups or hospitals\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare revenue cycle expertise.\n\nBenefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nRaventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"bd76f3a3-bf59-4672-b958-719c4005e6e4","title":"Payment Posting Specialist","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-20T14:23:14.257+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/bd76f3a3-bf59-4672-b958-719c4005e6e4","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/bd76f3a3-bf59-4672-b958-719c4005e6e4/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raventra Health</strong> is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Payment Posting Specialist, you will process and reconcile insurance and patient payments for provider clients, ensuring payments, adjustments, and remittance information are accurately recorded. Your work will help maintain accurate account balances and support timely and effective accounts receivable follow-up.</p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Post insurance payments, patient payments, adjustments, and contractual write-offs accurately</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review electronic and paper remittance information to ensure payments are applied to the correct accounts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reconcile posted payments against remittance advice and identify discrepancies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Research unidentified, misapplied, or incomplete payments and take appropriate corrective action</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review explanation of benefits and electronic remittance advice for payment and adjustment details</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify underpayments, overpayments, and other discrepancies and route them for appropriate follow-up</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate payment posting records and documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate payment-related issues to billing, AR, and other internal teams as needed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meet productivity and quality expectations while maintaining a high level of accuracy</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1+ year of experience in healthcare payment posting, medical billing, or a related revenue cycle role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of insurance payments, remittance advice, adjustments, and contractual write-offs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience reviewing EOBs and ERAs and applying payments to patient accounts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with a billing, practice management, or electronic health record system</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and ability to identify payment discrepancies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good understanding of basic medical billing and accounts receivable processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational skills and ability to manage payment posting volume and deadlines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently and effectively in a fully remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIPAA-compliant private workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or another major billing or practice management system</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with electronic remittance advice (ERA) and electronic funds transfer (EFT)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience identifying insurance underpayments and overpayments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge of medical billing codes and payer requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with provider groups or hospitals</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare revenue cycle expertise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.</p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Raventra Health is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Payment Posting Specialist, you will process and reconcile insurance and patient payments for provider clients, ensuring payments, adjustments, and remittance information are accurately recorded. Your work will help maintain accurate account balances and support timely and effective accounts receivable follow-up.\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Post insurance payments, patient payments, adjustments, and contractual write-offs accurately\n\n - Review electronic and paper remittance information to ensure payments are applied to the correct accounts\n\n - Reconcile posted payments against remittance advice and identify discrepancies\n\n - Research unidentified, misapplied, or incomplete payments and take appropriate corrective action\n\n - Review explanation of benefits and electronic remittance advice for payment and adjustment details\n\n - Identify underpayments, overpayments, and other discrepancies and route them for appropriate follow-up\n\n - Maintain accurate payment posting records and documentation\n\n - Communicate payment-related issues to billing, AR, and other internal teams as needed\n\n - Meet productivity and quality expectations while maintaining a high level of accuracy\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 1+ year of experience in healthcare payment posting, medical billing, or a related revenue cycle role\n\n - Working knowledge of insurance payments, remittance advice, adjustments, and contractual write-offs\n\n - Experience reviewing EOBs and ERAs and applying payments to patient accounts\n\n - Experience with a billing, practice management, or electronic health record system\n\n - Strong attention to detail and ability to identify payment discrepancies\n\n - Good understanding of basic medical billing and accounts receivable processes\n\n - Strong organizational skills and ability to manage payment posting volume and deadlines\n\n - Ability to work independently and effectively in a fully remote environment\n\n - HIPAA-compliant private workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or another major billing or practice management system\n\n - Experience with electronic remittance advice (ERA) and electronic funds transfer (EFT)\n\n - Experience identifying insurance underpayments and overpayments\n\n - Knowledge of medical billing codes and payer requirements\n\n - Experience working with provider groups or hospitals\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare revenue cycle expertise.\n\nBenefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nRaventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"da465b16-ee94-4482-9b0a-f48c40b4c40d","title":"Medical Records Specialist","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-20T14:29:33.789+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/da465b16-ee94-4482-9b0a-f48c40b4c40d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/da465b16-ee94-4482-9b0a-f48c40b4c40d/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raventra Health</strong> is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Medical Records Specialist, you will manage the collection, organization, and maintenance of medical documentation needed to support billing, coding, claims, and authorization processes. You will work with provider teams and internal RCM specialists to ensure required records are complete, accurate, and available when needed.</p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Request and collect medical records and supporting documentation from provider clients</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review records for completeness and ensure required documentation is available for billing, coding, and claims processing</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Organize and maintain electronic medical records in accordance with established procedures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track outstanding documentation requests and follow up with provider teams as needed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Route medical records and supporting documents to the appropriate billing, coding, authorization, or claims team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify missing, inconsistent, or incomplete documentation and communicate issues to the appropriate stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate records of documentation requests, receipt status, and follow-up activities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support record retrieval for claim appeals, audits, and other revenue cycle activities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Handle protected health information in accordance with HIPAA and company privacy procedures</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1+ year of experience in medical records, health information management, medical administration, or a related healthcare role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with electronic medical records or health information systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of medical terminology and common healthcare documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and ability to identify missing or inconsistent information</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent organizational skills and ability to manage multiple documentation requests and deadlines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to communicate effectively with provider teams and internal stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of confidentiality and appropriate handling of protected health information</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently and effectively in a fully remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIPAA-compliant private workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or another major EMR system</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">RHIT or RHIA certification</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Health Information Management or Medical Records training</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting medical billing, coding, prior authorization, or claims appeals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with provider groups or hospitals</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare administration expertise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.</p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Raventra Health is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Medical Records Specialist, you will manage the collection, organization, and maintenance of medical documentation needed to support billing, coding, claims, and authorization processes. You will work with provider teams and internal RCM specialists to ensure required records are complete, accurate, and available when needed.\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Request and collect medical records and supporting documentation from provider clients\n\n - Review records for completeness and ensure required documentation is available for billing, coding, and claims processing\n\n - Organize and maintain electronic medical records in accordance with established procedures\n\n - Track outstanding documentation requests and follow up with provider teams as needed\n\n - Route medical records and supporting documents to the appropriate billing, coding, authorization, or claims team\n\n - Identify missing, inconsistent, or incomplete documentation and communicate issues to the appropriate stakeholders\n\n - Maintain accurate records of documentation requests, receipt status, and follow-up activities\n\n - Support record retrieval for claim appeals, audits, and other revenue cycle activities\n\n - Handle protected health information in accordance with HIPAA and company privacy procedures\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 1+ year of experience in medical records, health information management, medical administration, or a related healthcare role\n\n - Experience working with electronic medical records or health information systems\n\n - Understanding of medical terminology and common healthcare documentation\n\n - Strong attention to detail and ability to identify missing or inconsistent information\n\n - Excellent organizational skills and ability to manage multiple documentation requests and deadlines\n\n - Ability to communicate effectively with provider teams and internal stakeholders\n\n - Strong understanding of confidentiality and appropriate handling of protected health information\n\n - Ability to work independently and effectively in a fully remote environment\n\n - HIPAA-compliant private workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or another major EMR system\n\n - RHIT or RHIA certification\n\n - Health Information Management or Medical Records training\n\n - Experience supporting medical billing, coding, prior authorization, or claims appeals\n\n - Experience working with provider groups or hospitals\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare administration expertise.\n\nBenefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nRaventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"0c7b8f64-18d5-4921-867d-2f78b845d4c8","title":"Revenue Integrity Specialist","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-20T15:17:18.530+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/0c7b8f64-18d5-4921-867d-2f78b845d4c8","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/0c7b8f64-18d5-4921-867d-2f78b845d4c8/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raventra Health</strong> is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Revenue Integrity Specialist, you will help provider clients identify and prevent revenue leakage across the revenue cycle. You will review charge capture, billing workflows, payer reimbursement, and account activity to identify discrepancies and opportunities for improved accuracy, compliance, and reimbursement.</p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review charge capture and billing workflows to identify missed or inaccurate charges</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analyze claims, payments, adjustments, and reimbursement data to identify revenue discrepancies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify potential revenue leakage and recommend corrective actions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review payer reimbursement against contracted rates and established billing guidelines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Investigate underpayments, incorrect adjustments, and other payment discrepancies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with billing, coding, payment posting, and AR teams to resolve revenue-related issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor recurring billing and reimbursement trends and identify opportunities for process improvement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare reports and communicate findings and recommendations to internal teams and client stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support audits and reviews related to charge capture, billing accuracy, and reimbursement</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in revenue integrity, healthcare revenue cycle management, medical billing, or a related healthcare finance role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of healthcare billing, claims, payments, and reimbursement processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience analyzing charges, payments, adjustments, and payer reimbursement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to identify discrepancies and investigate the root cause of revenue leakage</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with excellent attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to interpret billing and reimbursement data and communicate findings clearly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of payer requirements and healthcare revenue cycle workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently and manage multiple priorities in a remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIPAA-compliant private workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience reviewing payer contracts or reimbursement rates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical coding or billing knowledge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or another major EMR or practice management system</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with revenue cycle reporting and data analysis</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with provider groups or hospitals</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare revenue cycle expertise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.</p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Raventra Health is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Revenue Integrity Specialist, you will help provider clients identify and prevent revenue leakage across the revenue cycle. You will review charge capture, billing workflows, payer reimbursement, and account activity to identify discrepancies and opportunities for improved accuracy, compliance, and reimbursement.\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Review charge capture and billing workflows to identify missed or inaccurate charges\n\n - Analyze claims, payments, adjustments, and reimbursement data to identify revenue discrepancies\n\n - Identify potential revenue leakage and recommend corrective actions\n\n - Review payer reimbursement against contracted rates and established billing guidelines\n\n - Investigate underpayments, incorrect adjustments, and other payment discrepancies\n\n - Collaborate with billing, coding, payment posting, and AR teams to resolve revenue-related issues\n\n - Monitor recurring billing and reimbursement trends and identify opportunities for process improvement\n\n - Prepare reports and communicate findings and recommendations to internal teams and client stakeholders\n\n - Support audits and reviews related to charge capture, billing accuracy, and reimbursement\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 2+ years of experience in revenue integrity, healthcare revenue cycle management, medical billing, or a related healthcare finance role\n\n - Strong understanding of healthcare billing, claims, payments, and reimbursement processes\n\n - Experience analyzing charges, payments, adjustments, and payer reimbursement\n\n - Ability to identify discrepancies and investigate the root cause of revenue leakage\n\n - Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with excellent attention to detail\n\n - Ability to interpret billing and reimbursement data and communicate findings clearly\n\n - Strong understanding of payer requirements and healthcare revenue cycle workflows\n\n - Ability to work independently and manage multiple priorities in a remote environment\n\n - HIPAA-compliant private workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience reviewing payer contracts or reimbursement rates\n\n - Medical coding or billing knowledge\n\n - Experience with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or another major EMR or practice management system\n\n - Experience with revenue cycle reporting and data analysis\n\n - Experience working with provider groups or hospitals\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare revenue cycle expertise.\n\nBenefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nRaventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"24b078a9-6454-44b4-a756-77e8306cc1bd","title":"Clinical Documentation Improvement Specialist","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-20T14:33:39.638+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/24b078a9-6454-44b4-a756-77e8306cc1bd","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/24b078a9-6454-44b4-a756-77e8306cc1bd/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raventra Health</strong> is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Clinical Documentation Improvement Specialist, you will review clinical documentation to identify gaps, inconsistencies, and opportunities for greater accuracy and completeness. You will work with provider and coding teams to support documentation that accurately reflects the care provided and supports appropriate coding, claims processing, and reimbursement.</p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review clinical documentation for completeness, accuracy, and consistency with the services provided</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify documentation gaps or inconsistencies that may affect coding, claims, or reimbursement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct appropriate provider queries to clarify clinical documentation when needed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with medical coders and provider teams to improve documentation quality</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review clinical records and supporting documentation to identify opportunities for more accurate code assignment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support documentation requirements related to payer policies, audits, and compliance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track recurring documentation issues and communicate trends to internal teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide feedback and education to providers and coding staff on documentation requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate records of CDI activities, queries, and outcomes</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in clinical documentation improvement, medical coding, clinical documentation review, or a related healthcare role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of clinical documentation, medical terminology, and coding principles</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience reviewing medical records and identifying documentation gaps</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to communicate effectively with physicians, providers, coders, and other healthcare professionals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong knowledge of documentation requirements and their impact on coding and reimbursement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent attention to detail and analytical skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to manage multiple cases and priorities while meeting quality and productivity expectations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently and effectively in a fully remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIPAA-compliant private workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">RN, RHIA, RHIT, CCS, or CPC certification</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with inpatient or outpatient CDI</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge of ICD-10-CM, CPT, and HCC coding</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or another major EMR system</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting provider education, coding audits, or payer audits</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, certifications, and relevant healthcare expertise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.</p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Raventra Health is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Clinical Documentation Improvement Specialist, you will review clinical documentation to identify gaps, inconsistencies, and opportunities for greater accuracy and completeness. You will work with provider and coding teams to support documentation that accurately reflects the care provided and supports appropriate coding, claims processing, and reimbursement.\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Review clinical documentation for completeness, accuracy, and consistency with the services provided\n\n - Identify documentation gaps or inconsistencies that may affect coding, claims, or reimbursement\n\n - Conduct appropriate provider queries to clarify clinical documentation when needed\n\n - Collaborate with medical coders and provider teams to improve documentation quality\n\n - Review clinical records and supporting documentation to identify opportunities for more accurate code assignment\n\n - Support documentation requirements related to payer policies, audits, and compliance\n\n - Track recurring documentation issues and communicate trends to internal teams\n\n - Provide feedback and education to providers and coding staff on documentation requirements\n\n - Maintain accurate records of CDI activities, queries, and outcomes\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 2+ years of experience in clinical documentation improvement, medical coding, clinical documentation review, or a related healthcare role\n\n - Strong understanding of clinical documentation, medical terminology, and coding principles\n\n - Experience reviewing medical records and identifying documentation gaps\n\n - Ability to communicate effectively with physicians, providers, coders, and other healthcare professionals\n\n - Strong knowledge of documentation requirements and their impact on coding and reimbursement\n\n - Excellent attention to detail and analytical skills\n\n - Ability to manage multiple cases and priorities while meeting quality and productivity expectations\n\n - Ability to work independently and effectively in a fully remote environment\n\n - HIPAA-compliant private workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - RN, RHIA, RHIT, CCS, or CPC certification\n\n - Experience with inpatient or outpatient CDI\n\n - Knowledge of ICD-10-CM, CPT, and HCC coding\n\n - Experience with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or another major EMR system\n\n - Experience supporting provider education, coding audits, or payer audits\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, certifications, and relevant healthcare expertise.\n\nBenefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nRaventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"50f5eb6f-27d7-4a7a-ba0c-b9663a8f19e1","title":"RCM Reporting & Analytics Specialist","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-20T15:23:27.294+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/50f5eb6f-27d7-4a7a-ba0c-b9663a8f19e1","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/50f5eb6f-27d7-4a7a-ba0c-b9663a8f19e1/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raventra Health</strong> is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As an RCM Reporting &amp; Analytics Specialist, you will turn revenue cycle data into clear, actionable insights for internal teams and provider clients. You will build and maintain reports, monitor key performance indicators, identify trends, and help teams understand opportunities to improve billing, collections, claims performance, and overall revenue cycle operations.</p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain recurring reports and dashboards covering key revenue cycle metrics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analyze accounts receivable, claims, denials, payments, collections, and reimbursement data</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor metrics such as AR aging, denial rates, clean claim rates, collection performance, and payment trends</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify significant changes, trends, and anomalies in client and operational performance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare regular performance reports for internal teams and provider clients</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate complex revenue cycle data into clear findings and actionable recommendations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with billing, coding, AR, and client success teams to investigate performance issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Validate data accuracy and resolve reporting discrepancies before information is shared with stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support ad hoc analysis and reporting requests related to client performance and operational improvement</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in healthcare analytics, revenue cycle reporting, business intelligence, or a related analytical role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of healthcare revenue cycle processes and key performance metrics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong Excel skills, including pivot tables, lookups, data analysis, and reporting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience creating dashboards or reports using a business intelligence or reporting platform</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with excellent attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to identify meaningful trends and explain their business impact clearly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication skills and ability to present data to both operational and non-technical stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to manage multiple reporting priorities and meet deadlines in a remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIPAA-compliant private workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Power BI, Tableau, or a similar business intelligence platform</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">SQL experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or another healthcare system</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Revenue cycle management or healthcare operations background</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience preparing client-facing performance reports</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare analytics expertise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.</p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Raventra Health is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As an RCM Reporting & Analytics Specialist, you will turn revenue cycle data into clear, actionable insights for internal teams and provider clients. You will build and maintain reports, monitor key performance indicators, identify trends, and help teams understand opportunities to improve billing, collections, claims performance, and overall revenue cycle operations.\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Build and maintain recurring reports and dashboards covering key revenue cycle metrics\n\n - Analyze accounts receivable, claims, denials, payments, collections, and reimbursement data\n\n - Monitor metrics such as AR aging, denial rates, clean claim rates, collection performance, and payment trends\n\n - Identify significant changes, trends, and anomalies in client and operational performance\n\n - Prepare regular performance reports for internal teams and provider clients\n\n - Translate complex revenue cycle data into clear findings and actionable recommendations\n\n - Partner with billing, coding, AR, and client success teams to investigate performance issues\n\n - Validate data accuracy and resolve reporting discrepancies before information is shared with stakeholders\n\n - Support ad hoc analysis and reporting requests related to client performance and operational improvement\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 2+ years of experience in healthcare analytics, revenue cycle reporting, business intelligence, or a related analytical role\n\n - Working knowledge of healthcare revenue cycle processes and key performance metrics\n\n - Strong Excel skills, including pivot tables, lookups, data analysis, and reporting\n\n - Experience creating dashboards or reports using a business intelligence or reporting platform\n\n - Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with excellent attention to detail\n\n - Ability to identify meaningful trends and explain their business impact clearly\n\n - Strong communication skills and ability to present data to both operational and non-technical stakeholders\n\n - Ability to manage multiple reporting priorities and meet deadlines in a remote environment\n\n - HIPAA-compliant private workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with Power BI, Tableau, or a similar business intelligence platform\n\n - SQL experience\n\n - Experience working with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or another healthcare system\n\n - Revenue cycle management or healthcare operations background\n\n - Experience preparing client-facing performance reports\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare analytics expertise.\n\nBenefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nRaventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"a4b57619-68e7-4aa6-a039-83cd2f807667","title":"RCM Quality Assurance Specialist","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-20T15:34:42.463+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/a4b57619-68e7-4aa6-a039-83cd2f807667","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/a4b57619-68e7-4aa6-a039-83cd2f807667/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raventra Health</strong> is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As an RCM Quality Assurance Specialist, you will review revenue cycle work for accuracy, consistency, and compliance with established processes and client requirements. You will identify errors and recurring issues, provide actionable feedback, and help improve the quality and reliability of Raventra Health’s billing, coding, and claims operations.</p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct quality reviews of billing, coding, claims, payment posting, and other revenue cycle activities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review work samples for accuracy, completeness, and compliance with established procedures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify errors, process gaps, and recurring quality issues and document findings</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track quality results and identify trends across teams, workflows, and client accounts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide clear and constructive feedback to team members and operational managers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with billing, coding, claims, and AR teams to address root causes of recurring errors</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support the development and maintenance of quality standards, checklists, and review procedures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with internal audits and client quality reviews when required</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare quality reports and communicate findings and recommendations to relevant stakeholders</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in healthcare revenue cycle, medical billing, coding, claims, quality assurance, or a related healthcare operations role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of healthcare revenue cycle processes and billing workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience reviewing work for accuracy, completeness, and compliance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and ability to identify both individual errors and broader process issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analytical skills with the ability to identify trends and determine root causes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written and verbal communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to provide constructive feedback and work collaboratively with operational teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational skills and ability to manage multiple quality reviews and deadlines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently and effectively in a fully remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIPAA-compliant private workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical billing or coding certification such as CPC, CCS, or CPB</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with quality assurance or auditing in healthcare RCM</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or another major healthcare system</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience developing quality metrics, audit reports, or performance dashboards</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with provider groups or hospitals</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, certifications, and relevant healthcare revenue cycle expertise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.</p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Raventra Health is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As an RCM Quality Assurance Specialist, you will review revenue cycle work for accuracy, consistency, and compliance with established processes and client requirements. You will identify errors and recurring issues, provide actionable feedback, and help improve the quality and reliability of Raventra Health’s billing, coding, and claims operations.\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Conduct quality reviews of billing, coding, claims, payment posting, and other revenue cycle activities\n\n - Review work samples for accuracy, completeness, and compliance with established procedures\n\n - Identify errors, process gaps, and recurring quality issues and document findings\n\n - Track quality results and identify trends across teams, workflows, and client accounts\n\n - Provide clear and constructive feedback to team members and operational managers\n\n - Collaborate with billing, coding, claims, and AR teams to address root causes of recurring errors\n\n - Support the development and maintenance of quality standards, checklists, and review procedures\n\n - Assist with internal audits and client quality reviews when required\n\n - Prepare quality reports and communicate findings and recommendations to relevant stakeholders\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 2+ years of experience in healthcare revenue cycle, medical billing, coding, claims, quality assurance, or a related healthcare operations role\n\n - Strong understanding of healthcare revenue cycle processes and billing workflows\n\n - Experience reviewing work for accuracy, completeness, and compliance\n\n - Strong attention to detail and ability to identify both individual errors and broader process issues\n\n - Analytical skills with the ability to identify trends and determine root causes\n\n - Strong written and verbal communication skills\n\n - Ability to provide constructive feedback and work collaboratively with operational teams\n\n - Strong organizational skills and ability to manage multiple quality reviews and deadlines\n\n - Ability to work independently and effectively in a fully remote environment\n\n - HIPAA-compliant private workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Medical billing or coding certification such as CPC, CCS, or CPB\n\n - Experience with quality assurance or auditing in healthcare RCM\n\n - Experience with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or another major healthcare system\n\n - Experience developing quality metrics, audit reports, or performance dashboards\n\n - Experience working with provider groups or hospitals\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, certifications, and relevant healthcare revenue cycle expertise.\n\nBenefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nRaventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"cf4be0e2-ec56-4755-9316-3feb0f813993","title":"Digital Marketing Analyst","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-21T14:43:19.425+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/cf4be0e2-ec56-4755-9316-3feb0f813993","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/cf4be0e2-ec56-4755-9316-3feb0f813993/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>Job Description</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Byte&amp;Kite is a digital marketing agency helping clients across a range of industries grow through effective digital marketing. As a Digital Marketing Analyst, you will turn campaign, website and customer data into clear insights that help clients make better marketing decisions. You will work across SEO, paid media, email and other digital channels, partnering with channel specialists to measure performance, identify opportunities and communicate what the data actually shows.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">WHAT YOU WILL DO</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analyse performance across digital marketing channels and client accounts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain dashboards and recurring performance reports</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track traffic, conversions, customer acquisition and other key marketing metrics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Investigate performance changes and identify meaningful trends and opportunities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Connect marketing activity to business outcomes and flag gaps in attribution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support channel teams with analysis for campaign planning, optimisation and testing</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Present findings and recommendations clearly to internal teams and clients</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain consistent reporting definitions and data quality across accounts</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in digital marketing analytics, marketing analytics or a related role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical skills and ability to turn data into actionable recommendations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with GA4 and marketing reporting platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong Excel or Google Sheets skills, including working with large datasets and formulas</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of key digital marketing metrics across paid media, SEO, email and website performance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable building dashboards and presenting insights to non-technical stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and ability to question data when results do not make sense</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Able to distinguish correlation from causation when analysing marketing performance</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">NICE TO HAVE<br />Agency experience; Looker Studio or similar dashboarding tools; experience with Google Tag Manager; SQL or basic data querying skills; familiarity with CRM and advertising platforms; and experience with attribution or marketing mix analysis.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS<br />Competitive compensation based on experience and qualifications, with the full package discussed during the interview process. Professional development and training opportunities. Fully remote across US time zones, with additional company benefits discussed during the interview process.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIRING PROCESS<br />Application review - 30-minute conversation - hiring manager interview - offer. Every applicant receives a response.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">EQUAL OPPORTUNITY<br />Byte&amp;Kite is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the process, contact our recruiting team and we will arrange it.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"JOB DESCRIPTION\n\nByte&Kite is a digital marketing agency helping clients across a range of industries grow through effective digital marketing. As a Digital Marketing Analyst, you will turn campaign, website and customer data into clear insights that help clients make better marketing decisions. You will work across SEO, paid media, email and other digital channels, partnering with channel specialists to measure performance, identify opportunities and communicate what the data actually shows.\n\n \n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Analyse performance across digital marketing channels and client accounts\n\n - Build and maintain dashboards and recurring performance reports\n\n - Track traffic, conversions, customer acquisition and other key marketing metrics\n\n - Investigate performance changes and identify meaningful trends and opportunities\n\n - Connect marketing activity to business outcomes and flag gaps in attribution\n\n - Support channel teams with analysis for campaign planning, optimisation and testing\n\n - Present findings and recommendations clearly to internal teams and clients\n\n - Maintain consistent reporting definitions and data quality across accounts\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 2+ years of experience in digital marketing analytics, marketing analytics or a related role\n\n - Strong analytical skills and ability to turn data into actionable recommendations\n\n - Experience with GA4 and marketing reporting platforms\n\n - Strong Excel or Google Sheets skills, including working with large datasets and formulas\n\n - Understanding of key digital marketing metrics across paid media, SEO, email and website performance\n\n - Comfortable building dashboards and presenting insights to non-technical stakeholders\n\n - Strong attention to detail and ability to question data when results do not make sense\n\n - Able to distinguish correlation from causation when analysing marketing performance\n\nNICE TO HAVE\nAgency experience; Looker Studio or similar dashboarding tools; experience with Google Tag Manager; SQL or basic data querying skills; familiarity with CRM and advertising platforms; and experience with attribution or marketing mix analysis.\n\n \n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\nCompetitive compensation based on experience and qualifications, with the full package discussed during the interview process. Professional development and training opportunities. Fully remote across US time zones, with additional company benefits discussed during the interview process.\n\n \n\nHIRING PROCESS\nApplication review - 30-minute conversation - hiring manager interview - offer. Every applicant receives a response.\n\n \n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\nByte&Kite is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the process, contact our recruiting team and we will arrange it.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"ae1db5ac-29fa-4562-94aa-625e6ad2bf2e","title":"Conversion Rate Optimization Specialist","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-21T14:44:35.931+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/ae1db5ac-29fa-4562-94aa-625e6ad2bf2e","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/ae1db5ac-29fa-4562-94aa-625e6ad2bf2e/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>Job Description</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Byte&amp;Kite is a digital marketing agency helping clients across a range of industries improve their digital performance. As a CRO Specialist, you will identify opportunities to improve website and landing page conversion rates through research, analytics and structured experimentation. You will work with designers, developers, copywriters and marketing specialists to turn user insights into measurable improvements in conversion and customer experience.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">WHAT YOU WILL DO</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analyse website and landing page performance to identify conversion opportunities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use analytics, heatmaps, session recordings and user behaviour data to identify friction points</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop hypotheses and prioritised testing plans based on evidence</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Plan and manage A/B and multivariate tests from hypothesis through analysis</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with designers, developers and copywriters to implement and test improvements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate test results and communicate clear conclusions and next steps</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor conversion funnels and identify opportunities to improve key user journeys</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Present CRO findings and recommendations to clients and internal teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain documentation of tests, results and learnings across client accounts</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience in CRO, experimentation, growth marketing or a closely related field</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of conversion funnels, user behaviour and landing page optimisation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with A/B testing and experimentation platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with GA4 and tools such as Hotjar, Microsoft Clarity or similar</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical skills and ability to turn behavioural data into actionable hypotheses</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of statistical significance and responsible interpretation of test results</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong collaboration skills across design, development, content and marketing teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable presenting findings and recommendations directly to clients</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">NICE TO HAVE<br />Agency experience; experience with e-commerce or B2B conversion funnels; UX research; familiarity with Optimizely, VWO or similar experimentation platforms; basic HTML/CSS knowledge; and experience with Google Tag Manager.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS<br />Competitive compensation based on experience and qualifications, with the full package discussed during the interview process. Professional development and training opportunities. Fully remote across US time zones, with additional company benefits discussed during the interview process.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIRING PROCESS<br />Application review - 30-minute conversation - hiring manager interview - offer. Every applicant receives a response.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">EQUAL OPPORTUNITY<br />Byte&amp;Kite is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the process, contact our recruiting team and we will arrange it.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"JOB DESCRIPTION\n\nByte&Kite is a digital marketing agency helping clients across a range of industries improve their digital performance. As a CRO Specialist, you will identify opportunities to improve website and landing page conversion rates through research, analytics and structured experimentation. You will work with designers, developers, copywriters and marketing specialists to turn user insights into measurable improvements in conversion and customer experience.\n\n \n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Analyse website and landing page performance to identify conversion opportunities\n\n - Use analytics, heatmaps, session recordings and user behaviour data to identify friction points\n\n - Develop hypotheses and prioritised testing plans based on evidence\n\n - Plan and manage A/B and multivariate tests from hypothesis through analysis\n\n - Work with designers, developers and copywriters to implement and test improvements\n\n - Evaluate test results and communicate clear conclusions and next steps\n\n - Monitor conversion funnels and identify opportunities to improve key user journeys\n\n - Present CRO findings and recommendations to clients and internal teams\n\n - Maintain documentation of tests, results and learnings across client accounts\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 3+ years of experience in CRO, experimentation, growth marketing or a closely related field\n\n - Strong understanding of conversion funnels, user behaviour and landing page optimisation\n\n - Hands-on experience with A/B testing and experimentation platforms\n\n - Comfortable working with GA4 and tools such as Hotjar, Microsoft Clarity or similar\n\n - Strong analytical skills and ability to turn behavioural data into actionable hypotheses\n\n - Understanding of statistical significance and responsible interpretation of test results\n\n - Strong collaboration skills across design, development, content and marketing teams\n\n - Comfortable presenting findings and recommendations directly to clients\n\nNICE TO HAVE\nAgency experience; experience with e-commerce or B2B conversion funnels; UX research; familiarity with Optimizely, VWO or similar experimentation platforms; basic HTML/CSS knowledge; and experience with Google Tag Manager.\n\n \n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\nCompetitive compensation based on experience and qualifications, with the full package discussed during the interview process. Professional development and training opportunities. Fully remote across US time zones, with additional company benefits discussed during the interview process.\n\n \n\nHIRING PROCESS\nApplication review - 30-minute conversation - hiring manager interview - offer. Every applicant receives a response.\n\n \n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\nByte&Kite is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the process, contact our recruiting team and we will arrange it.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"645a83bc-a502-422f-b6e1-7fba323b0c30","title":"Marketing Strategist","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-21T14:45:46.853+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/645a83bc-a502-422f-b6e1-7fba323b0c30","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/645a83bc-a502-422f-b6e1-7fba323b0c30/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>Job Description</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Byte&amp;Kite is a digital marketing agency helping clients across a range of industries grow through effective digital marketing. As a Marketing Strategist, you will develop and guide marketing strategies across multiple client accounts, connecting business goals with audience insights, positioning, channels and measurable outcomes. You will work closely with clients and internal specialists across content, SEO, paid media, social and creative to turn strategy into effective campaigns.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">WHAT YOU WILL DO</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop marketing strategies based on client goals, audiences, market position and growth opportunities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct audience, competitor and market research to identify actionable insights</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define channel strategies, campaign priorities and measurable marketing objectives</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate business goals into clear marketing plans, recommendations and KPIs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with channel specialists to ensure campaigns are aligned with the overall strategy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review campaign and client performance and recommend strategic adjustments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Present marketing strategies and recommendations directly to clients</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify opportunities to expand client relationships through new initiatives and services</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of marketing strategy or digital marketing experience, ideally in an agency or consulting environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of digital marketing channels, including SEO, paid media, content, email and social</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience developing marketing strategies and integrated campaigns for business clients</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical and research skills, with the ability to turn data into clear recommendations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to connect marketing activities to broader business goals and measurable outcomes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong presentation and communication skills, with confidence working directly with clients</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable managing multiple accounts and priorities in a fast-paced environment</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">NICE TO HAVE<br />Agency experience; B2B marketing; experience with SaaS or technology clients; market research and competitive analysis; GA4 and marketing analytics experience; and experience developing go-to-market or positioning strategies.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS<br />Competitive compensation based on experience and qualifications, with the full package discussed during the interview process. Professional development and training opportunities. Fully remote across US time zones, with additional company benefits discussed during the interview process.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIRING PROCESS<br />Application review - 30-minute conversation - hiring manager interview - offer. Every applicant receives a response.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">EQUAL OPPORTUNITY<br />Byte&amp;Kite is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the process, contact our recruiting team and we will arrange it.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"JOB DESCRIPTION\n\nByte&Kite is a digital marketing agency helping clients across a range of industries grow through effective digital marketing. As a Marketing Strategist, you will develop and guide marketing strategies across multiple client accounts, connecting business goals with audience insights, positioning, channels and measurable outcomes. You will work closely with clients and internal specialists across content, SEO, paid media, social and creative to turn strategy into effective campaigns.\n\n \n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Develop marketing strategies based on client goals, audiences, market position and growth opportunities\n\n - Conduct audience, competitor and market research to identify actionable insights\n\n - Define channel strategies, campaign priorities and measurable marketing objectives\n\n - Translate business goals into clear marketing plans, recommendations and KPIs\n\n - Work with channel specialists to ensure campaigns are aligned with the overall strategy\n\n - Review campaign and client performance and recommend strategic adjustments\n\n - Present marketing strategies and recommendations directly to clients\n\n - Identify opportunities to expand client relationships through new initiatives and services\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 4+ years of marketing strategy or digital marketing experience, ideally in an agency or consulting environment\n\n - Strong understanding of digital marketing channels, including SEO, paid media, content, email and social\n\n - Experience developing marketing strategies and integrated campaigns for business clients\n\n - Strong analytical and research skills, with the ability to turn data into clear recommendations\n\n - Ability to connect marketing activities to broader business goals and measurable outcomes\n\n - Strong presentation and communication skills, with confidence working directly with clients\n\n - Comfortable managing multiple accounts and priorities in a fast-paced environment\n\nNICE TO HAVE\nAgency experience; B2B marketing; experience with SaaS or technology clients; market research and competitive analysis; GA4 and marketing analytics experience; and experience developing go-to-market or positioning strategies.\n\n \n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\nCompetitive compensation based on experience and qualifications, with the full package discussed during the interview process. Professional development and training opportunities. Fully remote across US time zones, with additional company benefits discussed during the interview process.\n\n \n\nHIRING PROCESS\nApplication review - 30-minute conversation - hiring manager interview - offer. Every applicant receives a response.\n\n \n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\nByte&Kite is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the process, contact our recruiting team and we will arrange it.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"ff362ca5-34f4-47c9-895a-b6a79ddda23d","title":"PAID MEDIA SPECIALIST","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-21T14:46:49.269+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/ff362ca5-34f4-47c9-895a-b6a79ddda23d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/ff362ca5-34f4-47c9-895a-b6a79ddda23d/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>Job Description</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Byte&amp;Kite is a digital marketing agency helping clients across a range of industries grow through effective digital marketing. As a Paid Media Specialist, you will manage paid acquisition campaigns across multiple client accounts, from strategy and campaign setup through optimisation, testing and reporting. You will work closely with clients and internal content, creative and analytics teams to improve campaign performance and turn media spend into measurable business results.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">WHAT YOU WILL DO</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Plan, launch and optimise paid media campaigns across Google, Meta and LinkedIn</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage campaign budgets and allocate spend based on performance and client goals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct keyword, audience and competitor research to inform campaign strategy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain campaign structures, targeting, bidding strategies and ad variations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor performance and identify opportunities to improve efficiency, conversions and return on ad spend</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Run structured tests across audiences, creative, messaging, landing pages and bidding strategies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with designers and copywriters to develop and improve ad creative</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analyse campaign and conversion data to diagnose performance changes and recommend actions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare regular performance reports and explain results and recommendations to clients</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with SEO, content, email and other marketing specialists on integrated campaigns</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of hands-on paid media experience, ideally managing multiple client accounts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong experience with Google Ads and Meta Ads; LinkedIn Ads experience is a plus</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven experience managing meaningful advertising budgets and optimising spend against business goals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of campaign structure, targeting, bidding, attribution and conversion tracking</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with A/B testing and using performance data to make optimisation decisions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with GA4, Google Ads reporting and other marketing analytics tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Able to explain campaign performance clearly and distinguish meaningful insights from surface-level metrics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical skills and attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable presenting results and recommendations directly to clients</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">NICE TO HAVE<br />Agency experience; B2B lead generation; e-commerce advertising; experience with LinkedIn Ads; familiarity with Google Tag Manager and conversion tracking; landing page optimisation; and experience working with multi-channel paid media strategies.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS<br />Competitive compensation based on experience and qualifications, with the full package discussed during the interview process. Professional development and training opportunities. Fully remote across US time zones, with additional company benefits discussed during the interview process.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIRING PROCESS<br />Application review - 30-minute conversation - hiring manager interview - offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Every applicant receives a response.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">EQUAL OPPORTUNITY<br />Byte&amp;Kite is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the process, contact our recruiting team and we will arrange it.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"JOB DESCRIPTION\n\nByte&Kite is a digital marketing agency helping clients across a range of industries grow through effective digital marketing. As a Paid Media Specialist, you will manage paid acquisition campaigns across multiple client accounts, from strategy and campaign setup through optimisation, testing and reporting. You will work closely with clients and internal content, creative and analytics teams to improve campaign performance and turn media spend into measurable business results.\n\n \n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Plan, launch and optimise paid media campaigns across Google, Meta and LinkedIn\n\n - Manage campaign budgets and allocate spend based on performance and client goals\n\n - Conduct keyword, audience and competitor research to inform campaign strategy\n\n - Build and maintain campaign structures, targeting, bidding strategies and ad variations\n\n - Monitor performance and identify opportunities to improve efficiency, conversions and return on ad spend\n\n - Run structured tests across audiences, creative, messaging, landing pages and bidding strategies\n\n - Work with designers and copywriters to develop and improve ad creative\n\n - Analyse campaign and conversion data to diagnose performance changes and recommend actions\n\n - Prepare regular performance reports and explain results and recommendations to clients\n\n - Collaborate with SEO, content, email and other marketing specialists on integrated campaigns\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 3+ years of hands-on paid media experience, ideally managing multiple client accounts\n\n - Strong experience with Google Ads and Meta Ads; LinkedIn Ads experience is a plus\n\n - Proven experience managing meaningful advertising budgets and optimising spend against business goals\n\n - Strong understanding of campaign structure, targeting, bidding, attribution and conversion tracking\n\n - Experience with A/B testing and using performance data to make optimisation decisions\n\n - Comfortable working with GA4, Google Ads reporting and other marketing analytics tools\n\n - Able to explain campaign performance clearly and distinguish meaningful insights from surface-level metrics\n\n - Strong analytical skills and attention to detail\n\n - Comfortable presenting results and recommendations directly to clients\n\nNICE TO HAVE\nAgency experience; B2B lead generation; e-commerce advertising; experience with LinkedIn Ads; familiarity with Google Tag Manager and conversion tracking; landing page optimisation; and experience working with multi-channel paid media strategies.\n\n \n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\nCompetitive compensation based on experience and qualifications, with the full package discussed during the interview process. Professional development and training opportunities. Fully remote across US time zones, with additional company benefits discussed during the interview process.\n\n \n\nHIRING PROCESS\nApplication review - 30-minute conversation - hiring manager interview - offer.\n\nEvery applicant receives a response.\n\n \n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\nByte&Kite is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the process, contact our recruiting team and we will arrange it.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"0ab820a9-fce5-4060-a94a-284ddb80fc2c","title":"Marketing Project Manager","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-21T14:51:11.164+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/0ab820a9-fce5-4060-a94a-284ddb80fc2c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/0ab820a9-fce5-4060-a94a-284ddb80fc2c/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>Job Description</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Byte&amp;Kite is a digital marketing agency helping clients across a range of industries grow through effective digital marketing. As a Marketing Project Manager, you will coordinate campaigns and client deliverables across multiple accounts, keeping teams aligned on scope, timelines, priorities and dependencies. You will work closely with account managers, strategists, designers, writers, SEO and paid media specialists to keep projects moving and ensure work is delivered to a high standard.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">WHAT YOU WILL DO</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage timelines, deliverables and dependencies across multiple marketing projects</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate work between creative, content, SEO, paid media and other specialists</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate client requirements into clear project plans, tasks and deadlines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track project progress and proactively address risks, blockers and changes in scope</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Keep internal teams and clients aligned on priorities and delivery expectations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Facilitate project meetings and provide clear status updates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage multiple projects simultaneously while maintaining attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure final deliverables meet agreed requirements and are ready for client review</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of project management experience, ideally in a marketing agency or digital environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience coordinating cross-functional teams and multiple concurrent projects</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of project planning, timelines, dependencies and scope management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent organisation and communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable managing changing priorities and raising risks early</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and ability to keep projects moving without constant supervision</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working directly with clients and internal stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with project management tools such as Asana, <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Monday.com\">Monday.com</a>, ClickUp or similar</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">NICE TO HAVE<br />Digital marketing agency experience; Agile or other project management methodology experience; familiarity with SEO, paid media, content and creative workflows; client-facing experience; and relevant project management certification.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS<br />Competitive compensation based on experience and qualifications, with the full package discussed during the interview process. Professional development and training opportunities. Fully remote across US time zones, with additional company benefits discussed during the interview process.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIRING PROCESS<br />Application review - 30-minute conversation - hiring manager interview - offer. Every applicant receives a response.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">EQUAL OPPORTUNITY<br />Byte&amp;Kite is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the process, contact our recruiting team and we will arrange it.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"JOB DESCRIPTION\n\nByte&Kite is a digital marketing agency helping clients across a range of industries grow through effective digital marketing. As a Marketing Project Manager, you will coordinate campaigns and client deliverables across multiple accounts, keeping teams aligned on scope, timelines, priorities and dependencies. You will work closely with account managers, strategists, designers, writers, SEO and paid media specialists to keep projects moving and ensure work is delivered to a high standard.\n\n \n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Manage timelines, deliverables and dependencies across multiple marketing projects\n\n - Coordinate work between creative, content, SEO, paid media and other specialists\n\n - Translate client requirements into clear project plans, tasks and deadlines\n\n - Track project progress and proactively address risks, blockers and changes in scope\n\n - Keep internal teams and clients aligned on priorities and delivery expectations\n\n - Facilitate project meetings and provide clear status updates\n\n - Manage multiple projects simultaneously while maintaining attention to detail\n\n - Ensure final deliverables meet agreed requirements and are ready for client review\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 3+ years of project management experience, ideally in a marketing agency or digital environment\n\n - Experience coordinating cross-functional teams and multiple concurrent projects\n\n - Strong understanding of project planning, timelines, dependencies and scope management\n\n - Excellent organisation and communication skills\n\n - Comfortable managing changing priorities and raising risks early\n\n - Strong attention to detail and ability to keep projects moving without constant supervision\n\n - Comfortable working directly with clients and internal stakeholders\n\n - Experience with project management tools such as Asana, Monday.com http://Monday.com, ClickUp or similar\n\nNICE TO HAVE\nDigital marketing agency experience; Agile or other project management methodology experience; familiarity with SEO, paid media, content and creative workflows; client-facing experience; and relevant project management certification.\n\n \n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\nCompetitive compensation based on experience and qualifications, with the full package discussed during the interview process. Professional development and training opportunities. Fully remote across US time zones, with additional company benefits discussed during the interview process.\n\n \n\nHIRING PROCESS\nApplication review - 30-minute conversation - hiring manager interview - offer. Every applicant receives a response.\n\n \n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\nByte&Kite is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the process, contact our recruiting team and we will arrange it.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"f9d6b6da-48af-4e85-8297-3318298c8de7","title":"Web Designer","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-21T14:56:22.527+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/f9d6b6da-48af-4e85-8297-3318298c8de7","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/f9d6b6da-48af-4e85-8297-3318298c8de7/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>Job Description</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Byte&amp;Kite is a digital marketing agency helping clients across a range of industries grow through effective digital marketing. As a Web Designer, you will design websites and landing pages that combine strong visual design with intuitive user experiences and clear business goals. You will work closely with strategists, copywriters, developers, and clients to turn briefs into responsive, conversion-focused digital experiences.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">WHAT YOU WILL DO</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design websites and landing pages from initial concepts through final designs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create wireframes, page layouts and high-fidelity designs in Figma</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate brand guidelines into consistent and engaging digital experiences</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design responsive layouts for desktop, tablet and mobile</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with copywriters, strategists and developers throughout the design process</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Present designs to clients and incorporate feedback into final work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Consider usability, accessibility and conversion goals when making design decisions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare organised, developer-ready design files and assets</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review implemented pages to ensure they match approved designs and provide a consistent user experience</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of professional web or digital design experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong portfolio demonstrating website and landing page design</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advanced Figma skills and strong understanding of modern web design practices</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of layout, typography, visual hierarchy, responsive design and UX principles</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing conversion-focused landing pages and marketing websites</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work from written briefs and translate business objectives into effective design solutions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable presenting design decisions and receiving feedback directly from clients</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and ability to collaborate effectively with developers</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">NICE TO HAVE<br />Webflow experience; basic HTML and CSS knowledge; UX research experience; familiarity with CRO and analytics; experience with design systems; and experience designing websites for B2B or SaaS companies.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS<br />Competitive compensation based on experience and qualifications, with the full package discussed during the interview process. Professional development and training opportunities. Fully remote across US time zones, with additional company benefits discussed during the interview process.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIRING PROCESS<br />Application review - 30-minute conversation - hiring manager interview - offer. Every applicant receives a response.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">EQUAL OPPORTUNITY<br />Byte&amp;Kite is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the process, contact our recruiting team and we will arrange it.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"JOB DESCRIPTION\n\nByte&Kite is a digital marketing agency helping clients across a range of industries grow through effective digital marketing. As a Web Designer, you will design websites and landing pages that combine strong visual design with intuitive user experiences and clear business goals. You will work closely with strategists, copywriters, developers, and clients to turn briefs into responsive, conversion-focused digital experiences.\n\n \n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Design websites and landing pages from initial concepts through final designs\n\n - Create wireframes, page layouts and high-fidelity designs in Figma\n\n - Translate brand guidelines into consistent and engaging digital experiences\n\n - Design responsive layouts for desktop, tablet and mobile\n\n - Collaborate with copywriters, strategists and developers throughout the design process\n\n - Present designs to clients and incorporate feedback into final work\n\n - Consider usability, accessibility and conversion goals when making design decisions\n\n - Prepare organised, developer-ready design files and assets\n\n - Review implemented pages to ensure they match approved designs and provide a consistent user experience\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 3+ years of professional web or digital design experience\n\n - Strong portfolio demonstrating website and landing page design\n\n - Advanced Figma skills and strong understanding of modern web design practices\n\n - Strong understanding of layout, typography, visual hierarchy, responsive design and UX principles\n\n - Experience designing conversion-focused landing pages and marketing websites\n\n - Ability to work from written briefs and translate business objectives into effective design solutions\n\n - Comfortable presenting design decisions and receiving feedback directly from clients\n\n - Strong attention to detail and ability to collaborate effectively with developers\n\nNICE TO HAVE\nWebflow experience; basic HTML and CSS knowledge; UX research experience; familiarity with CRO and analytics; experience with design systems; and experience designing websites for B2B or SaaS companies.\n\n \n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\nCompetitive compensation based on experience and qualifications, with the full package discussed during the interview process. Professional development and training opportunities. Fully remote across US time zones, with additional company benefits discussed during the interview process.\n\n \n\nHIRING PROCESS\nApplication review - 30-minute conversation - hiring manager interview - offer. Every applicant receives a response.\n\n \n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\nByte&Kite is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the process, contact our recruiting team and we will arrange it.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"e519af16-e3c3-4433-a6fb-7bf92309cffe","title":"Web Developer","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-21T15:01:10.324+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/e519af16-e3c3-4433-a6fb-7bf92309cffe","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/e519af16-e3c3-4433-a6fb-7bf92309cffe/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>Job Description</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Byte&amp;Kite is a digital marketing agency helping clients across a range of industries grow through effective digital marketing. As a Web Developer, you will build and maintain marketing websites and landing pages that are fast, responsive, and aligned with business and conversion goals. You will work closely with web designers, strategists, SEO specialists, and clients to turn approved designs into high-quality digital experiences.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">WHAT YOU WILL DO</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain responsive websites and landing pages from approved designs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop reusable components and ensure consistent implementation across pages</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with designers and marketers to deliver websites that meet both visual and functional requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Implement SEO, analytics and conversion tracking requirements alongside marketing specialists</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Optimise websites for performance, accessibility and cross-browser compatibility</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Troubleshoot and resolve technical issues across client websites</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain and update existing websites while minimising disruption to live experiences</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review implemented designs with the design team and address visual or functional issues before launch</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of professional web development experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong HTML, CSS and JavaScript skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building responsive, production-ready websites</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with modern CMS platforms and website builders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to translate Figma designs into accurate, functional web pages</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of web performance, accessibility and basic technical SEO</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience integrating analytics and conversion tracking tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and ability to troubleshoot issues independently</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable collaborating with designers, marketers, SEO specialists and clients</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">NICE TO HAVE<br />Webflow experience; WordPress development; familiarity with React or another modern JavaScript framework; basic PHP knowledge; experience with Google Tag Manager and GA4; and experience building B2B or SaaS marketing websites.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS<br />Competitive compensation based on experience and qualifications, with the full package discussed during the interview process. Professional development and training opportunities. Fully remote across US time zones, with additional company benefits discussed during the interview process.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIRING PROCESS<br />Application review - 30-minute conversation - practical exercise - hiring manager interview - offer. Every applicant receives a response.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">EQUAL OPPORTUNITY<br />Byte&amp;Kite is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the process, contact our recruiting team and we will arrange it.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"JOB DESCRIPTION\n\nByte&Kite is a digital marketing agency helping clients across a range of industries grow through effective digital marketing. As a Web Developer, you will build and maintain marketing websites and landing pages that are fast, responsive, and aligned with business and conversion goals. You will work closely with web designers, strategists, SEO specialists, and clients to turn approved designs into high-quality digital experiences.\n\n \n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Build and maintain responsive websites and landing pages from approved designs\n\n - Develop reusable components and ensure consistent implementation across pages\n\n - Collaborate with designers and marketers to deliver websites that meet both visual and functional requirements\n\n - Implement SEO, analytics and conversion tracking requirements alongside marketing specialists\n\n - Optimise websites for performance, accessibility and cross-browser compatibility\n\n - Troubleshoot and resolve technical issues across client websites\n\n - Maintain and update existing websites while minimising disruption to live experiences\n\n - Review implemented designs with the design team and address visual or functional issues before launch\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 3+ years of professional web development experience\n\n - Strong HTML, CSS and JavaScript skills\n\n - Experience building responsive, production-ready websites\n\n - Experience working with modern CMS platforms and website builders\n\n - Ability to translate Figma designs into accurate, functional web pages\n\n - Understanding of web performance, accessibility and basic technical SEO\n\n - Experience integrating analytics and conversion tracking tools\n\n - Strong attention to detail and ability to troubleshoot issues independently\n\n - Comfortable collaborating with designers, marketers, SEO specialists and clients\n\nNICE TO HAVE\nWebflow experience; WordPress development; familiarity with React or another modern JavaScript framework; basic PHP knowledge; experience with Google Tag Manager and GA4; and experience building B2B or SaaS marketing websites.\n\n \n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\nCompetitive compensation based on experience and qualifications, with the full package discussed during the interview process. Professional development and training opportunities. Fully remote across US time zones, with additional company benefits discussed during the interview process.\n\n \n\nHIRING PROCESS\nApplication review - 30-minute conversation - practical exercise - hiring manager interview - offer. Every applicant receives a response.\n\n \n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\nByte&Kite is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the process, contact our recruiting team and we will arrange it.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"5d0305a6-6b67-4034-b35d-ad7162374eaf","title":"Claims Processing Specialist","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-27T12:56:17.269+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/5d0305a6-6b67-4034-b35d-ad7162374eaf","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/5d0305a6-6b67-4034-b35d-ad7162374eaf/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a <strong>Claims Processing Specialist</strong> to review and process claims and related documentation. You will verify information, update records, identify missing details, and help ensure claims are processed accurately and on time.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review and process incoming claims and supporting documents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Verify information for accuracy and completeness</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enter and update claim information in company systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify missing or inconsistent information</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow up on documentation needed to complete a claim</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate claim records and documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Escalate issues that require additional review</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous claims processing, data entry, administrative, or customer service experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and accuracy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good computer and typing skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable reviewing and working with documents and data</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good organization and follow-up skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to handle repetitive tasks consistently</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working independently in a remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legally authorized to work in the United States</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable internet connection and suitable workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous claims or insurance experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with databases or claims management systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare, insurance, or administrative experience</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$19–$24 per hour</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Application review → Initial conversation → Interview → Offer</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"We are looking for a Claims Processing Specialist to review and process claims and related documentation. You will verify information, update records, identify missing details, and help ensure claims are processed accurately and on time.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Review and process incoming claims and supporting documents\n\n - Verify information for accuracy and completeness\n\n - Enter and update claim information in company systems\n\n - Identify missing or inconsistent information\n\n - Follow up on documentation needed to complete a claim\n\n - Maintain accurate claim records and documentation\n\n - Escalate issues that require additional review\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - Previous claims processing, data entry, administrative, or customer service experience\n\n - Strong attention to detail and accuracy\n\n - Good computer and typing skills\n\n - Comfortable reviewing and working with documents and data\n\n - Good organization and follow-up skills\n\n - Ability to handle repetitive tasks consistently\n\n - Comfortable working independently in a remote environment\n\n - Legally authorized to work in the United States\n\n - Reliable internet connection and suitable workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Previous claims or insurance experience\n\n - Experience with databases or claims management systems\n\n - Healthcare, insurance, or administrative experience\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$19–$24 per hour, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → Initial conversation → Interview → Offer\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nBilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"93379945-2522-4cc8-8d31-810e7e483f97","title":"Data Entry Specialist","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-27T12:57:45.467+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/93379945-2522-4cc8-8d31-810e7e483f97","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/93379945-2522-4cc8-8d31-810e7e483f97/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a <strong>Data Entry Specialist</strong> to help maintain accurate and up-to-date company information. You will enter, review, and update data across internal systems and spreadsheets, while ensuring information is complete and accurate.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is a good fit for someone who is detail-oriented, organized, and comfortable working independently with repetitive tasks.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enter and update information in company systems and spreadsheets</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review data for accuracy and correct errors</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain organized digital records</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify missing or inconsistent information</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow established data entry procedures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Complete assigned tasks accurately and on time</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous data entry, administrative, customer service, or similar experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and accuracy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good typing and computer skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with spreadsheets and digital systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Organized and able to manage repetitive tasks consistently</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently in a remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legally authorized to work in the United States</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable internet connection and suitable workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Microsoft Excel or Google Sheets</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous remote work experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with CRM, database, or business management systems</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$18–$23 per hour</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Application review → Initial conversation → Interview → Offer</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"We are looking for a Data Entry Specialist to help maintain accurate and up-to-date company information. You will enter, review, and update data across internal systems and spreadsheets, while ensuring information is complete and accurate.\n\nThis role is a good fit for someone who is detail-oriented, organized, and comfortable working independently with repetitive tasks.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Enter and update information in company systems and spreadsheets\n\n - Review data for accuracy and correct errors\n\n - Maintain organized digital records\n\n - Identify missing or inconsistent information\n\n - Follow established data entry procedures\n\n - Complete assigned tasks accurately and on time\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - Previous data entry, administrative, customer service, or similar experience\n\n - Strong attention to detail and accuracy\n\n - Good typing and computer skills\n\n - Comfortable working with spreadsheets and digital systems\n\n - Organized and able to manage repetitive tasks consistently\n\n - Ability to work independently in a remote environment\n\n - Legally authorized to work in the United States\n\n - Reliable internet connection and suitable workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with Microsoft Excel or Google Sheets\n\n - Previous remote work experience\n\n - Experience with CRM, database, or business management systems\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$18–$23 per hour, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → Initial conversation → Interview → Offer\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nBilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"8d9f066d-6af8-43e9-8320-ccdedef3068d","title":"Order Entry Clerk","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-27T12:59:02.276+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/8d9f066d-6af8-43e9-8320-ccdedef3068d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/8d9f066d-6af8-43e9-8320-ccdedef3068d/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for an <strong>Order Entry Clerk</strong> to help process and maintain accurate customer and order information. You will enter orders into company systems, review details for accuracy, and help resolve missing or incorrect information.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enter customer orders into company systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review orders for accuracy and completeness</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Update order and customer information when needed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and flag missing or incorrect details</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow up on order-related questions and discrepancies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate order records</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Complete assigned orders and tasks on time</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous experience in order entry, data entry, customer service, administration, or a similar role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and accuracy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good typing and computer skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with spreadsheets and digital systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Organized and able to handle repetitive tasks consistently</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good communication and follow-up skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working independently in a remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legally authorized to work in the United States</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable internet connection and suitable workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous order entry or processing experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Excel or Google Sheets</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with CRM, ERP, or order management systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Food service, retail, or hospitality experience</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$17–$22 per hour</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Application review → Initial conversation → Interview → Offer</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"We are looking for an Order Entry Clerk to help process and maintain accurate customer and order information. You will enter orders into company systems, review details for accuracy, and help resolve missing or incorrect information.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Enter customer orders into company systems\n\n - Review orders for accuracy and completeness\n\n - Update order and customer information when needed\n\n - Identify and flag missing or incorrect details\n\n - Follow up on order-related questions and discrepancies\n\n - Maintain accurate order records\n\n - Complete assigned orders and tasks on time\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - Previous experience in order entry, data entry, customer service, administration, or a similar role\n\n - Strong attention to detail and accuracy\n\n - Good typing and computer skills\n\n - Comfortable working with spreadsheets and digital systems\n\n - Organized and able to handle repetitive tasks consistently\n\n - Good communication and follow-up skills\n\n - Comfortable working independently in a remote environment\n\n - Legally authorized to work in the United States\n\n - Reliable internet connection and suitable workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Previous order entry or processing experience\n\n - Experience with Excel or Google Sheets\n\n - Experience with CRM, ERP, or order management systems\n\n - Food service, retail, or hospitality experience\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$17–$22 per hour, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → Initial conversation → Interview → Offer\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nBilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"e2ca3a76-b285-4933-a762-9dab9db9f20c","title":"Team Administrative Assistant","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-26T13:44:17.925+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/e2ca3a76-b285-4933-a762-9dab9db9f20c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/e2ca3a76-b285-4933-a762-9dab9db9f20c/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will support the team building our new mid-market analytics platform, helping keep day-to-day team operations organized and running smoothly. You will work closely with Product, Engineering, Design, and other teams, coordinating meetings, documentation, schedules, onboarding activities, and administrative tasks so the team can stay focused on building the product.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate meetings, calendars, team events, and recurring team activities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare agendas, capture action items, and help follow up on open tasks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain team documentation, shared resources, and internal information</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support onboarding activities for new team members, including scheduling and coordination</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help organize internal communications, team updates, and important announcements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate travel, equipment, supplies, and other administrative needs when required</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support project and team planning with scheduling, documentation, and follow-up</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help maintain organized records and ensure important information is easy for the team to find</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate with People, Finance, IT, and other internal teams on requests affecting the team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify opportunities to improve administrative processes and make team operations more efficient</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1+ year of experience in administrative support, team coordination, office operations, or a similar role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational skills and attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and verbal English communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable managing calendars, meetings, documents, and multiple priorities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactive approach to following up and keeping things moving without constant supervision</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong sense of discretion when handling internal or sensitive information</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with remote teams and collaborating across different functions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Confident using common workplace tools such as Google Workspace or Microsoft Office</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting a technology, SaaS, or other fast-growing company</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with tools such as Jira, Confluence, Slack, Notion, or Asana</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting engineering, product, or other technical teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience coordinating onboarding or team events</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic project coordination experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working in a fully remote environment</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be determined based on experience, administrative expertise, and overall fit for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → practical discussion → conversation with the team/manager → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 50,000 - 70,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"CerebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.\n\nYou will support the team building our new mid-market analytics platform, helping keep day-to-day team operations organized and running smoothly. You will work closely with Product, Engineering, Design, and other teams, coordinating meetings, documentation, schedules, onboarding activities, and administrative tasks so the team can stay focused on building the product.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Coordinate meetings, calendars, team events, and recurring team activities\n\n - Prepare agendas, capture action items, and help follow up on open tasks\n\n - Maintain team documentation, shared resources, and internal information\n\n - Support onboarding activities for new team members, including scheduling and coordination\n\n - Help organize internal communications, team updates, and important announcements\n\n - Coordinate travel, equipment, supplies, and other administrative needs when required\n\n - Support project and team planning with scheduling, documentation, and follow-up\n\n - Help maintain organized records and ensure important information is easy for the team to find\n\n - Coordinate with People, Finance, IT, and other internal teams on requests affecting the team\n\n - Identify opportunities to improve administrative processes and make team operations more efficient\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 1+ year of experience in administrative support, team coordination, office operations, or a similar role\n\n - Strong organizational skills and attention to detail\n\n - Excellent written and verbal English communication skills\n\n - Comfortable managing calendars, meetings, documents, and multiple priorities\n\n - Proactive approach to following up and keeping things moving without constant supervision\n\n - Strong sense of discretion when handling internal or sensitive information\n\n - Comfortable working with remote teams and collaborating across different functions\n\n - Confident using common workplace tools such as Google Workspace or Microsoft Office\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience supporting a technology, SaaS, or other fast-growing company\n\n - Familiarity with tools such as Jira, Confluence, Slack, Notion, or Asana\n\n - Experience supporting engineering, product, or other technical teams\n\n - Experience coordinating onboarding or team events\n\n - Basic project coordination experience\n\n - Experience working in a fully remote environment\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be determined based on experience, administrative expertise, and overall fit for the role.\n\nCerebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → practical discussion → conversation with the team/manager → offer.\n\nWe aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nCerebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSalary Range: 50,000 - 70,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"9ed272cf-89e1-40ac-8708-cd084553b459","title":"Operations Coordinator","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-26T13:42:59.920+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/9ed272cf-89e1-40ac-8708-cd084553b459","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/9ed272cf-89e1-40ac-8708-cd084553b459/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will support the day-to-day operations behind our growing business and the team building our new mid-market analytics platform. You will help keep internal processes organized, coordinate requests across teams, maintain operational information, and identify ways to make routine workflows more efficient as CerebriOS grows.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate day-to-day operational requests across internal teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain internal processes, documentation, trackers, and operational records</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate recurring business activities, deadlines, and follow-ups</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with Finance, People, IT, Product, and other teams to keep operational tasks moving</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support onboarding and offboarding processes by coordinating required activities across teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help manage vendors, subscriptions, supplies, and other operational resources</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare routine reports, updates, and summaries for internal stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify process gaps and help introduce simple, scalable improvements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Keep track of open requests, dependencies, and deadlines and follow up with owners</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support team projects and other operational initiatives as the company grows</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1+ year of experience in operations, administration, coordination, or a similar role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational skills and attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to manage multiple requests and priorities without losing track of deadlines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written and verbal English communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactive approach to problem-solving and follow-up</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with different teams and coordinating tasks across functions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to create and maintain clear documentation and operational processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working independently in a remote environment</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in a SaaS, technology, or other fast-growing company</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with tools such as Google Workspace, Microsoft Office, Jira, Confluence, Notion, or Asana</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic experience with reporting, spreadsheets, or operational data</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Vendor or subscription management experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting remote or distributed teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous project coordination experience</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be determined based on experience, operational expertise, and overall fit for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → practical discussion → conversation with the team/manager → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 55,000 - 75,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"CerebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.\n\nYou will support the day-to-day operations behind our growing business and the team building our new mid-market analytics platform. You will help keep internal processes organized, coordinate requests across teams, maintain operational information, and identify ways to make routine workflows more efficient as CerebriOS grows.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Coordinate day-to-day operational requests across internal teams\n\n - Maintain internal processes, documentation, trackers, and operational records\n\n - Coordinate recurring business activities, deadlines, and follow-ups\n\n - Work with Finance, People, IT, Product, and other teams to keep operational tasks moving\n\n - Support onboarding and offboarding processes by coordinating required activities across teams\n\n - Help manage vendors, subscriptions, supplies, and other operational resources\n\n - Prepare routine reports, updates, and summaries for internal stakeholders\n\n - Identify process gaps and help introduce simple, scalable improvements\n\n - Keep track of open requests, dependencies, and deadlines and follow up with owners\n\n - Support team projects and other operational initiatives as the company grows\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 1+ year of experience in operations, administration, coordination, or a similar role\n\n - Strong organizational skills and attention to detail\n\n - Ability to manage multiple requests and priorities without losing track of deadlines\n\n - Strong written and verbal English communication skills\n\n - Proactive approach to problem-solving and follow-up\n\n - Comfortable working with different teams and coordinating tasks across functions\n\n - Ability to create and maintain clear documentation and operational processes\n\n - Comfortable working independently in a remote environment\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience in a SaaS, technology, or other fast-growing company\n\n - Experience with tools such as Google Workspace, Microsoft Office, Jira, Confluence, Notion, or Asana\n\n - Basic experience with reporting, spreadsheets, or operational data\n\n - Vendor or subscription management experience\n\n - Experience supporting remote or distributed teams\n\n - Previous project coordination experience\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be determined based on experience, operational expertise, and overall fit for the role.\n\nCerebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → practical discussion → conversation with the team/manager → offer.\n\nWe aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nCerebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSalary Range: 55,000 - 75,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"8c9e3d01-8fba-49cb-bc02-96d7b3426241","title":"Project Manager","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-26T13:45:30.215+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/8c9e3d01-8fba-49cb-bc02-96d7b3426241","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/8c9e3d01-8fba-49cb-bc02-96d7b3426241/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will join the team building our new mid-market analytics platform, coordinating work across Product, Engineering, Design, Data, and QA. You will help turn product priorities into organized execution, keeping teams aligned on scope, timelines, dependencies, and risks while ensuring important work moves forward.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate cross-functional projects from planning through delivery</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with Product and Engineering to translate priorities into clear plans, milestones, and deliverables</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track project progress, dependencies, risks, and blockers and make sure they are addressed early</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Facilitate planning meetings, status updates, and other project ceremonies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Keep stakeholders informed about progress, changes, risks, and important decisions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate work across Engineering, Product, Design, Data, and QA teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help teams maintain realistic timelines while balancing changing priorities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify opportunities to improve project workflows, communication, and delivery processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain project documentation, decisions, and action items in appropriate collaboration tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support post-project reviews and help turn lessons learned into improvements for future work</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in project management, program coordination, or a similar role within a technology or software environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience coordinating cross-functional teams and software development projects</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational skills and attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to manage multiple priorities while maintaining visibility into deadlines and dependencies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication skills and confidence working with both technical and non-technical stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable identifying risks, raising concerns, and following up on unresolved issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Practical understanding of software development lifecycles and Agile ways of working</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Able to work independently while keeping distributed teams aligned</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with B2B SaaS products</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with analytics, data, or business intelligence projects</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Scrum Master, Agile, or project management certification</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with Jira, Confluence, Asana, or similar project management tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience coordinating remote or distributed engineering teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic understanding of software development, QA, and release processes</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be determined based on experience, project management expertise, and overall fit for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → conversation with the manager→ offer.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 85,000 - 115,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"CerebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.\n\nYou will join the team building our new mid-market analytics platform, coordinating work across Product, Engineering, Design, Data, and QA. You will help turn product priorities into organized execution, keeping teams aligned on scope, timelines, dependencies, and risks while ensuring important work moves forward.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Coordinate cross-functional projects from planning through delivery\n\n - Work with Product and Engineering to translate priorities into clear plans, milestones, and deliverables\n\n - Track project progress, dependencies, risks, and blockers and make sure they are addressed early\n\n - Facilitate planning meetings, status updates, and other project ceremonies\n\n - Keep stakeholders informed about progress, changes, risks, and important decisions\n\n - Coordinate work across Engineering, Product, Design, Data, and QA teams\n\n - Help teams maintain realistic timelines while balancing changing priorities\n\n - Identify opportunities to improve project workflows, communication, and delivery processes\n\n - Maintain project documentation, decisions, and action items in appropriate collaboration tools\n\n - Support post-project reviews and help turn lessons learned into improvements for future work\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 2+ years of experience in project management, program coordination, or a similar role within a technology or software environment\n\n - Experience coordinating cross-functional teams and software development projects\n\n - Strong organizational skills and attention to detail\n\n - Ability to manage multiple priorities while maintaining visibility into deadlines and dependencies\n\n - Strong communication skills and confidence working with both technical and non-technical stakeholders\n\n - Comfortable identifying risks, raising concerns, and following up on unresolved issues\n\n - Practical understanding of software development lifecycles and Agile ways of working\n\n - Able to work independently while keeping distributed teams aligned\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience working with B2B SaaS products\n\n - Experience with analytics, data, or business intelligence projects\n\n - Scrum Master, Agile, or project management certification\n\n - Familiarity with Jira, Confluence, Asana, or similar project management tools\n\n - Experience coordinating remote or distributed engineering teams\n\n - Basic understanding of software development, QA, and release processes\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be determined based on experience, project management expertise, and overall fit for the role.\n\nCerebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → conversation with the manager→ offer.\n\n \n\nWe aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nCerebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSalary Range: 85,000 - 115,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"e3c55f29-b6e6-4d77-a9ba-2883648fc670","title":"Technical Support Specialist","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-26T13:46:36.785+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/e3c55f29-b6e6-4d77-a9ba-2883648fc670","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/e3c55f29-b6e6-4d77-a9ba-2883648fc670/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will join the customer-facing team supporting our new analytics platform for mid-market businesses. You will help customers troubleshoot product issues, understand how to use the platform effectively, and resolve technical questions around data, reporting, integrations, and account configuration. You will work closely with Customer Success, Engineering, and Product to make sure customer issues are resolved quickly and recurring problems are addressed at the source.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide technical support to customers through email, chat, and other support channels</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Investigate and resolve issues related to dashboards, reports, data, integrations, and product functionality</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reproduce reported issues and gather the technical information needed to identify their cause</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Guide customers through product configuration and troubleshooting in a clear, practical way</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Escalate complex technical issues to Engineering with clear reproduction steps and relevant context</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track support requests and maintain accurate documentation in the support system</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify recurring customer issues and work with Product and Engineering to improve the product</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create and maintain help articles, troubleshooting guides, and internal support documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor support trends and help identify opportunities to improve customer experience and product reliability</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with Customer Success and Implementation teams during onboarding and ongoing customer support</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1+ year of experience in technical support, customer support, application support, or a similar role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting SaaS, web applications, or other business software</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong troubleshooting and problem-solving skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable investigating technical issues rather than relying only on predefined scripts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good understanding of web applications, APIs, integrations, and common software issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written and verbal English communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to explain technical concepts clearly to both technical and non-technical customers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Organized approach to managing multiple support requests and priorities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable collaborating with Engineering, Product, Customer Success, and other teams</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting analytics, reporting, data, or business intelligence products</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic SQL knowledge</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with APIs and tools such as Postman</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Zendesk, Intercom, Jira, or similar platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience troubleshooting data integrations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous B2B SaaS experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience creating customer-facing technical documentation</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be determined based on experience, technical expertise, and overall fit for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → technical support discussion → conversation with the manager → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 65,000 - 85,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"CerebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.\n\nYou will join the customer-facing team supporting our new analytics platform for mid-market businesses. You will help customers troubleshoot product issues, understand how to use the platform effectively, and resolve technical questions around data, reporting, integrations, and account configuration. You will work closely with Customer Success, Engineering, and Product to make sure customer issues are resolved quickly and recurring problems are addressed at the source.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Provide technical support to customers through email, chat, and other support channels\n\n - Investigate and resolve issues related to dashboards, reports, data, integrations, and product functionality\n\n - Reproduce reported issues and gather the technical information needed to identify their cause\n\n - Guide customers through product configuration and troubleshooting in a clear, practical way\n\n - Escalate complex technical issues to Engineering with clear reproduction steps and relevant context\n\n - Track support requests and maintain accurate documentation in the support system\n\n - Identify recurring customer issues and work with Product and Engineering to improve the product\n\n - Create and maintain help articles, troubleshooting guides, and internal support documentation\n\n - Monitor support trends and help identify opportunities to improve customer experience and product reliability\n\n - Work closely with Customer Success and Implementation teams during onboarding and ongoing customer support\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 1+ year of experience in technical support, customer support, application support, or a similar role\n\n - Experience supporting SaaS, web applications, or other business software\n\n - Strong troubleshooting and problem-solving skills\n\n - Comfortable investigating technical issues rather than relying only on predefined scripts\n\n - Good understanding of web applications, APIs, integrations, and common software issues\n\n - Strong written and verbal English communication skills\n\n - Ability to explain technical concepts clearly to both technical and non-technical customers\n\n - Organized approach to managing multiple support requests and priorities\n\n - Comfortable collaborating with Engineering, Product, Customer Success, and other teams\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience supporting analytics, reporting, data, or business intelligence products\n\n - Basic SQL knowledge\n\n - Familiarity with APIs and tools such as Postman\n\n - Experience with Zendesk, Intercom, Jira, or similar platforms\n\n - Experience troubleshooting data integrations\n\n - Previous B2B SaaS experience\n\n - Experience creating customer-facing technical documentation\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be determined based on experience, technical expertise, and overall fit for the role.\n\nCerebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → technical support discussion → conversation with the manager → offer.\n\nWe aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nCerebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSalary Range: 65,000 - 85,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"a8e46b4a-10d8-4e81-ab16-557ee7cbe54c","title":"Implementation Specialist","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-26T13:48:15.918+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/a8e46b4a-10d8-4e81-ab16-557ee7cbe54c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/a8e46b4a-10d8-4e81-ab16-557ee7cbe54c/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will join the customer-facing team supporting the growth of our new analytics platform for mid-market businesses. You will help customers move from a successful sale to a successful implementation, guiding them through setup, data connections, configuration, and initial adoption. You will work closely with Customer Success, Product, Engineering, and Sales to make sure each customer gets up and running smoothly and sees value from the platform early.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage the implementation process for new customers from kickoff through launch</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with customers to understand their workflows, data sources, and technical requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate product configuration, integrations, data connections, and other implementation activities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate customer requirements into clear tasks for internal technical and product teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create implementation plans, track milestones, and keep customers informed about progress</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and resolve implementation risks, dependencies, and blockers before they affect the launch</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Validate data, configurations, and workflows before handing customers over to the Customer Success team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create onboarding materials and documentation that make future implementations more efficient</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gather implementation feedback and identify recurring issues or opportunities to improve the product</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help develop scalable implementation processes as the CerebriOS customer base grows</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in implementation, onboarding, customer success, project coordination, or a similar role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with B2B SaaS or other business software</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong project coordination and organizational skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to understand customer requirements and translate them into clear implementation steps</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with technical concepts, data, integrations, and software configuration</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written and verbal communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Able to manage multiple customer implementations while keeping timelines and priorities organized</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactive approach to identifying risks and resolving issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable collaborating with customers and cross-functional internal teams</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience implementing analytics, reporting, CRM, ERP, or other data-driven software</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with APIs, data integrations, or SQL</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with mid-market customers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with project management or customer onboarding platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous experience working closely with Engineering or Product teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience creating implementation documentation and repeatable processes</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be determined based on experience, implementation expertise, and overall fit for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → technical exercise → conversation with the team/manager → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 65,000 - 90,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"CerebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.\n\nYou will join the customer-facing team supporting the growth of our new analytics platform for mid-market businesses. You will help customers move from a successful sale to a successful implementation, guiding them through setup, data connections, configuration, and initial adoption. You will work closely with Customer Success, Product, Engineering, and Sales to make sure each customer gets up and running smoothly and sees value from the platform early.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Manage the implementation process for new customers from kickoff through launch\n\n - Work with customers to understand their workflows, data sources, and technical requirements\n\n - Coordinate product configuration, integrations, data connections, and other implementation activities\n\n - Translate customer requirements into clear tasks for internal technical and product teams\n\n - Create implementation plans, track milestones, and keep customers informed about progress\n\n - Identify and resolve implementation risks, dependencies, and blockers before they affect the launch\n\n - Validate data, configurations, and workflows before handing customers over to the Customer Success team\n\n - Create onboarding materials and documentation that make future implementations more efficient\n\n - Gather implementation feedback and identify recurring issues or opportunities to improve the product\n\n - Help develop scalable implementation processes as the CerebriOS customer base grows\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 2+ years of experience in implementation, onboarding, customer success, project coordination, or a similar role\n\n - Experience working with B2B SaaS or other business software\n\n - Strong project coordination and organizational skills\n\n - Ability to understand customer requirements and translate them into clear implementation steps\n\n - Comfortable working with technical concepts, data, integrations, and software configuration\n\n - Strong written and verbal communication skills\n\n - Able to manage multiple customer implementations while keeping timelines and priorities organized\n\n - Proactive approach to identifying risks and resolving issues\n\n - Comfortable collaborating with customers and cross-functional internal teams\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience implementing analytics, reporting, CRM, ERP, or other data-driven software\n\n - Familiarity with APIs, data integrations, or SQL\n\n - Experience working with mid-market customers\n\n - Experience with project management or customer onboarding platforms\n\n - Previous experience working closely with Engineering or Product teams\n\n - Experience creating implementation documentation and repeatable processes\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be determined based on experience, implementation expertise, and overall fit for the role.\n\nCerebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → technical exercise → conversation with the team/manager → offer.\n\nWe aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nCerebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSalary Range: 65,000 - 90,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"2a1a53b0-61c8-4ab1-80e5-b804f8761579","title":"Customer Success Manager","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-26T13:49:40.476+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/2a1a53b0-61c8-4ab1-80e5-b804f8761579","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/2a1a53b0-61c8-4ab1-80e5-b804f8761579/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will join the customer-facing team supporting the growth of our new analytics platform for mid-market businesses. You will work with customers throughout their journey with CerebriOS — from onboarding and adoption to ongoing relationship management — helping them get meaningful value from the platform and sharing customer insights with our product and engineering teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage relationships with a portfolio of B2B customers and become a trusted point of contact throughout their journey</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Guide new customers through onboarding, configuration, and initial product adoption</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understand customer goals and help them identify ways to get greater value from the analytics platform</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor customer engagement and proactively identify adoption risks or opportunities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct regular customer check-ins and business reviews to understand needs, progress, and priorities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Sales, Product, and Support teams to resolve customer issues and improve the overall customer experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collect and communicate customer feedback, feature requests, and recurring pain points to internal teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help develop scalable onboarding, education, and customer success processes as the customer base grows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track customer health and success metrics and use them to prioritize your work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support renewals and identify opportunities for deeper product adoption and account growth</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in customer success, account management, client services, or a similar customer-facing role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with B2B SaaS or other technology products</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and relationship-building skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to understand customer needs and translate them into practical next steps</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with product usage data and customer health metrics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational skills and ability to manage multiple customer relationships independently</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactive approach to identifying problems before they become escalations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working cross-functionally with Sales, Product, Engineering, and Support teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Customer-focused mindset combined with strong business judgment</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting mid-market or enterprise customers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with analytics, reporting, business intelligence, or data products</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with customer success platforms such as Gainsight, ChurnZero, or HubSpot</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with SaaS onboarding and implementation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting renewals or expansion opportunities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical skills and comfort working with customer metrics</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be determined based on experience, customer success expertise, and overall fit for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → interview with manager → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 75,000 - 105,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"CerebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.\n\nYou will join the customer-facing team supporting the growth of our new analytics platform for mid-market businesses. You will work with customers throughout their journey with CerebriOS — from onboarding and adoption to ongoing relationship management — helping them get meaningful value from the platform and sharing customer insights with our product and engineering teams.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Manage relationships with a portfolio of B2B customers and become a trusted point of contact throughout their journey\n\n - Guide new customers through onboarding, configuration, and initial product adoption\n\n - Understand customer goals and help them identify ways to get greater value from the analytics platform\n\n - Monitor customer engagement and proactively identify adoption risks or opportunities\n\n - Conduct regular customer check-ins and business reviews to understand needs, progress, and priorities\n\n - Partner with Sales, Product, and Support teams to resolve customer issues and improve the overall customer experience\n\n - Collect and communicate customer feedback, feature requests, and recurring pain points to internal teams\n\n - Help develop scalable onboarding, education, and customer success processes as the customer base grows\n\n - Track customer health and success metrics and use them to prioritize your work\n\n - Support renewals and identify opportunities for deeper product adoption and account growth\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 2+ years of experience in customer success, account management, client services, or a similar customer-facing role\n\n - Experience working with B2B SaaS or other technology products\n\n - Strong communication and relationship-building skills\n\n - Ability to understand customer needs and translate them into practical next steps\n\n - Comfortable working with product usage data and customer health metrics\n\n - Strong organizational skills and ability to manage multiple customer relationships independently\n\n - Proactive approach to identifying problems before they become escalations\n\n - Comfortable working cross-functionally with Sales, Product, Engineering, and Support teams\n\n - Customer-focused mindset combined with strong business judgment\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience supporting mid-market or enterprise customers\n\n - Experience with analytics, reporting, business intelligence, or data products\n\n - Familiarity with customer success platforms such as Gainsight, ChurnZero, or HubSpot\n\n - Experience with SaaS onboarding and implementation\n\n - Experience supporting renewals or expansion opportunities\n\n - Strong analytical skills and comfort working with customer metrics\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be determined based on experience, customer success expertise, and overall fit for the role.\n\nCerebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → interview with manager → offer.\n\nWe aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nCerebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSalary Range: 75,000 - 105,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"a1906606-4a24-4c24-8526-9d7f9f2a8201","title":"Data Engineer","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-26T13:50:51.753+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/a1906606-4a24-4c24-8526-9d7f9f2a8201","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/a1906606-4a24-4c24-8526-9d7f9f2a8201/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will join the engineering team behind our new mid-market analytics platform, building the data foundations that power reporting, dashboards, and product insights. You will work across data pipelines, integrations, and storage, helping turn data from different sources into reliable, well-structured information that customers and internal teams can use with confidence.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, build, and maintain reliable data pipelines for the analytics platform</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop data ingestion and transformation processes for multiple data sources</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with backend engineers and analysts to define data structures that support reporting and analytics use cases</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve data quality, consistency, and reliability across the platform</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and optimize SQL-based data transformations and workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor data pipelines and investigate failures, performance issues, and unexpected data behavior</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to data architecture and help establish scalable practices as the platform grows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Document data models, pipelines, and important business logic so others can work confidently with the data</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with product and engineering teams to understand how data should support new product capabilities</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of professional experience in data engineering or a closely related role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong SQL skills and experience working with relational databases</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience building and maintaining data pipelines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Python or another language commonly used for data engineering</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of data modeling, ETL/ELT processes, and data quality practices</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with cloud-based data infrastructure</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong troubleshooting and analytical skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to explain technical decisions clearly and collaborate with engineers, analysts, and product stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working independently in a remote, cross-functional environment</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with AWS or GCP</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">dbt, Airflow, Dagster, or similar data tooling</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with modern data warehouses such as Snowflake, BigQuery, or Redshift</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with APIs and third-party data integrations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with analytics, reporting, or business intelligence products</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous B2B SaaS experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with large or rapidly changing datasets</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be discussed during the interview process and determined based on experience, technical expertise, and overall fit for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → technical discussion → conversation with the team → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 105,000 - 140,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"CerebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.\n\nYou will join the engineering team behind our new mid-market analytics platform, building the data foundations that power reporting, dashboards, and product insights. You will work across data pipelines, integrations, and storage, helping turn data from different sources into reliable, well-structured information that customers and internal teams can use with confidence.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Design, build, and maintain reliable data pipelines for the analytics platform\n\n - Develop data ingestion and transformation processes for multiple data sources\n\n - Work with backend engineers and analysts to define data structures that support reporting and analytics use cases\n\n - Improve data quality, consistency, and reliability across the platform\n\n - Build and optimize SQL-based data transformations and workflows\n\n - Monitor data pipelines and investigate failures, performance issues, and unexpected data behavior\n\n - Contribute to data architecture and help establish scalable practices as the platform grows\n\n - Document data models, pipelines, and important business logic so others can work confidently with the data\n\n - Collaborate with product and engineering teams to understand how data should support new product capabilities\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 3+ years of professional experience in data engineering or a closely related role\n\n - Strong SQL skills and experience working with relational databases\n\n - Hands-on experience building and maintaining data pipelines\n\n - Experience with Python or another language commonly used for data engineering\n\n - Understanding of data modeling, ETL/ELT processes, and data quality practices\n\n - Experience working with cloud-based data infrastructure\n\n - Strong troubleshooting and analytical skills\n\n - Ability to explain technical decisions clearly and collaborate with engineers, analysts, and product stakeholders\n\n - Comfortable working independently in a remote, cross-functional environment\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with AWS or GCP\n\n - dbt, Airflow, Dagster, or similar data tooling\n\n - Experience with modern data warehouses such as Snowflake, BigQuery, or Redshift\n\n - Experience working with APIs and third-party data integrations\n\n - Familiarity with analytics, reporting, or business intelligence products\n\n - Previous B2B SaaS experience\n\n - Experience working with large or rapidly changing datasets\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be discussed during the interview process and determined based on experience, technical expertise, and overall fit for the role.\n\nCerebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → technical discussion → conversation with the team → offer.\n\nWe aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nCerebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSalary Range: 105,000 - 140,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"3e97fd93-8df5-4b78-909a-1462108b2317","title":"Administrative Coordinator","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-27T12:42:03.965+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/3e97fd93-8df5-4b78-909a-1462108b2317","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/3e97fd93-8df5-4b78-909a-1462108b2317/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for an <strong>Administrative Coordinator</strong> to support day-to-day administrative activities and help keep information, requests, and processes organized. You will coordinate tasks, maintain records, communicate with internal teams, and provide administrative support to managers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate administrative tasks and requests</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain records, spreadsheets, and company systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Schedule meetings and manage calendars as needed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare basic documents and reports</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow up on outstanding requests and deadlines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate with internal teams to keep tasks moving</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide general administrative support to managers</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous administrative, coordination, customer service, or similar experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organization and attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good written and verbal communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with spreadsheets and digital systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Able to manage multiple tasks and deadlines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working independently in a remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legally authorized to work in the United States</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable internet connection and suitable workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Administrative coordination experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Microsoft Office or Google Workspace</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with scheduling, CRM, or project management systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Food service, hospitality, retail, or healthcare experience</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$20–$27 per hour</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Application review → Initial conversation → Interview → Offer</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"We are looking for an Administrative Coordinator to support day-to-day administrative activities and help keep information, requests, and processes organized. You will coordinate tasks, maintain records, communicate with internal teams, and provide administrative support to managers.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Coordinate administrative tasks and requests\n\n - Maintain records, spreadsheets, and company systems\n\n - Schedule meetings and manage calendars as needed\n\n - Prepare basic documents and reports\n\n - Follow up on outstanding requests and deadlines\n\n - Communicate with internal teams to keep tasks moving\n\n - Provide general administrative support to managers\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - Previous administrative, coordination, customer service, or similar experience\n\n - Strong organization and attention to detail\n\n - Good written and verbal communication skills\n\n - Comfortable working with spreadsheets and digital systems\n\n - Able to manage multiple tasks and deadlines\n\n - Comfortable working independently in a remote environment\n\n - Legally authorized to work in the United States\n\n - Reliable internet connection and suitable workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Administrative coordination experience\n\n - Experience with Microsoft Office or Google Workspace\n\n - Experience with scheduling, CRM, or project management systems\n\n - Food service, hospitality, retail, or healthcare experience\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$20–$27 per hour, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → Initial conversation → Interview → Offer\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nBilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"2cb62c56-2dcb-40c7-8efa-b5a6b84452cc","title":"Front Desk Coordinator","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-27T12:43:56.665+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/2cb62c56-2dcb-40c7-8efa-b5a6b84452cc","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/2cb62c56-2dcb-40c7-8efa-b5a6b84452cc/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a <strong>Front Desk Coordinator</strong> to support customers, visitors, and internal teams with day-to-day questions and requests. Working remotely, you will help coordinate incoming calls and inquiries, manage information, and make sure requests are directed to the right team.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Respond to incoming calls, messages, and general inquiries</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide basic information and assistance to customers and visitors</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Direct requests to the appropriate team or location</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Schedule appointments and coordinate requests when needed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate records and contact information</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow up on outstanding requests</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide friendly and professional customer service</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous front desk, customer service, administrative, or hospitality experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and organization skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Friendly and professional approach</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable handling calls, messages, and multiple requests</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good computer skills and ability to learn new systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working independently in a remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legally authorized to work in the United States</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable internet connection and suitable workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reception or front desk experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with scheduling or appointment systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Food service, hospitality, retail, or care industry experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilingual English/Spanish skills</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$18–$24 per hour</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Application review → Initial conversation → Interview → Offer</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"We are looking for a Front Desk Coordinator to support customers, visitors, and internal teams with day-to-day questions and requests. Working remotely, you will help coordinate incoming calls and inquiries, manage information, and make sure requests are directed to the right team.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Respond to incoming calls, messages, and general inquiries\n\n - Provide basic information and assistance to customers and visitors\n\n - Direct requests to the appropriate team or location\n\n - Schedule appointments and coordinate requests when needed\n\n - Maintain accurate records and contact information\n\n - Follow up on outstanding requests\n\n - Provide friendly and professional customer service\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - Previous front desk, customer service, administrative, or hospitality experience\n\n - Strong communication and organization skills\n\n - Friendly and professional approach\n\n - Comfortable handling calls, messages, and multiple requests\n\n - Good computer skills and ability to learn new systems\n\n - Comfortable working independently in a remote environment\n\n - Legally authorized to work in the United States\n\n - Reliable internet connection and suitable workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Reception or front desk experience\n\n - Experience with scheduling or appointment systems\n\n - Food service, hospitality, retail, or care industry experience\n\n - Bilingual English/Spanish skills\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$18–$24 per hour, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → Initial conversation → Interview → Offer\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nBilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"ddc0ee23-8f6e-4a66-833d-03c8f0f71ace","title":"Customer Service Specialist","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-27T12:46:37.541+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/ddc0ee23-8f6e-4a66-833d-03c8f0f71ace","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/ddc0ee23-8f6e-4a66-833d-03c8f0f71ace/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a <strong>Customer Service Specialist</strong> to support customers with questions, requests, and service issues. You will communicate with customers, provide accurate information, resolve routine issues, and work with internal teams when additional support is needed.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Respond to customer questions and service requests</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Resolve routine customer issues professionally and efficiently</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide accurate information about orders, services, and locations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow up on open requests and customer concerns</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate customer records and notes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Escalate issues when additional support is needed</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous customer service, retail, hospitality, or similar experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and customer-service skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good organization and attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable using computers and learning new systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to handle multiple customer requests</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working independently in a remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legally authorized to work in the United States</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable internet connection and suitable workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous remote customer service experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with CRM or customer support systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Food service, hospitality, or retail experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilingual English/Spanish skills</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$18–$24 per hour</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Application review → Initial conversation → Interview → Offer</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"We are looking for a Customer Service Specialist to support customers with questions, requests, and service issues. You will communicate with customers, provide accurate information, resolve routine issues, and work with internal teams when additional support is needed.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Respond to customer questions and service requests\n\n - Resolve routine customer issues professionally and efficiently\n\n - Provide accurate information about orders, services, and locations\n\n - Follow up on open requests and customer concerns\n\n - Maintain accurate customer records and notes\n\n - Escalate issues when additional support is needed\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - Previous customer service, retail, hospitality, or similar experience\n\n - Strong communication and customer-service skills\n\n - Good organization and attention to detail\n\n - Comfortable using computers and learning new systems\n\n - Ability to handle multiple customer requests\n\n - Comfortable working independently in a remote environment\n\n - Legally authorized to work in the United States\n\n - Reliable internet connection and suitable workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Previous remote customer service experience\n\n - Experience with CRM or customer support systems\n\n - Food service, hospitality, or retail experience\n\n - Bilingual English/Spanish skills\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$18–$24 per hour, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → Initial conversation → Interview → Offer\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nBilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"00ea245f-675a-4194-a4c3-348f06a5b59a","title":"Operations Coordinator","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-27T12:49:49.864+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/00ea245f-675a-4194-a4c3-348f06a5b59a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/00ea245f-675a-4194-a4c3-348f06a5b59a/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for an <strong>Operations Coordinator</strong> to support day-to-day business operations and help keep tasks, information, and processes organized. You will coordinate requests, maintain records, follow up on operational tasks, and support managers and teams across the company.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate day-to-day operational requests and tasks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate records, spreadsheets, and company systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track tasks, deadlines, and operational updates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate with internal teams to coordinate requests</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow up on outstanding items and resolve routine issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare basic reports and documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support managers with day-to-day operational needs</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous experience in operations, administration, coordination, or customer service</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organization and attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good communication and follow-up skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable managing multiple priorities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good computer and spreadsheet skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently and solve routine problems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legally authorized to work in the United States</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable internet connection and suitable workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Operations or coordination experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in food service, hospitality, retail, or care</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with CRM, scheduling, or project management systems</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$21–$27 per hour</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Application review → Initial conversation → Interview → Offer</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"We are looking for an Operations Coordinator to support day-to-day business operations and help keep tasks, information, and processes organized. You will coordinate requests, maintain records, follow up on operational tasks, and support managers and teams across the company.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Coordinate day-to-day operational requests and tasks\n\n - Maintain accurate records, spreadsheets, and company systems\n\n - Track tasks, deadlines, and operational updates\n\n - Communicate with internal teams to coordinate requests\n\n - Follow up on outstanding items and resolve routine issues\n\n - Prepare basic reports and documentation\n\n - Support managers with day-to-day operational needs\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - Previous experience in operations, administration, coordination, or customer service\n\n - Strong organization and attention to detail\n\n - Good communication and follow-up skills\n\n - Comfortable managing multiple priorities\n\n - Good computer and spreadsheet skills\n\n - Ability to work independently and solve routine problems\n\n - Legally authorized to work in the United States\n\n - Reliable internet connection and suitable workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Operations or coordination experience\n\n - Experience in food service, hospitality, retail, or care\n\n - Familiarity with CRM, scheduling, or project management systems\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$21–$27 per hour, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → Initial conversation → Interview → Offer\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nBilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"bc70aa17-126f-4e18-b677-cbbff3ece6c2","title":"Document Processing Specialist","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-27T12:51:43.497+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/bc70aa17-126f-4e18-b677-cbbff3ece6c2","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/bc70aa17-126f-4e18-b677-cbbff3ece6c2/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a <strong>Document Processing Specialist</strong> to help process, organize, and maintain company documents and information. You will review documents, enter and update information, and make sure records are complete and accurate.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review and process incoming documents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enter and update information in company systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Check documents for completeness and accuracy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Organize digital files and records</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify missing or inconsistent information</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow established document-processing procedures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate documentation and records</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous experience in data entry, document processing, administration, or customer service</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and accuracy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good typing and computer skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with spreadsheets and digital documents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Organized and able to handle repetitive tasks consistently</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently in a remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legally authorized to work in the United States</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable internet connection and suitable workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Microsoft Excel or Google Sheets</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous document processing or records experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with document management or CRM systems</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$18–$23 per hour</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Application review → Initial conversation → Interview → Offer</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"We are looking for a Document Processing Specialist to help process, organize, and maintain company documents and information. You will review documents, enter and update information, and make sure records are complete and accurate.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Review and process incoming documents\n\n - Enter and update information in company systems\n\n - Check documents for completeness and accuracy\n\n - Organize digital files and records\n\n - Identify missing or inconsistent information\n\n - Follow established document-processing procedures\n\n - Maintain accurate documentation and records\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - Previous experience in data entry, document processing, administration, or customer service\n\n - Strong attention to detail and accuracy\n\n - Good typing and computer skills\n\n - Comfortable working with spreadsheets and digital documents\n\n - Organized and able to handle repetitive tasks consistently\n\n - Ability to work independently in a remote environment\n\n - Legally authorized to work in the United States\n\n - Reliable internet connection and suitable workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with Microsoft Excel or Google Sheets\n\n - Previous document processing or records experience\n\n - Familiarity with document management or CRM systems\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$18–$23 per hour, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → Initial conversation → Interview → Offer\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nBilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"7bbcf379-8106-4926-8943-ae1d8cf34f71","title":"Technical Support Specialist (Junior / Middle)","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T15:42:13.926+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/7bbcf379-8106-4926-8943-ae1d8cf34f71","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/7bbcf379-8106-4926-8943-ae1d8cf34f71/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a <strong>Technical Support Specialist</strong> to join our team and help customers resolve technical issues while using our health services platform.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is suitable for both <strong>Junior and Middle-level candidates</strong>, depending on experience. You will work closely with customers and internal technical teams to troubleshoot issues, answer technical questions, and ensure a smooth user experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide technical support to customers via email, chat, and other communication channels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Troubleshoot and resolve technical issues related to the platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Investigate reported problems and identify possible causes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Escalate complex technical issues to development or engineering teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Document support requests, solutions, and recurring issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist customers with platform functionality and basic troubleshooting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor support tickets and ensure timely resolution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with Product and Engineering teams to communicate customer feedback and recurring issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to internal support documentation and knowledge bases.</p></li></ul><h2>Requirements</h2><h3>Junior Level</h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>1+ year</strong> of experience in technical support, IT support, customer support, or a related role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic understanding of software applications and troubleshooting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with web-based platforms and business software.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong problem-solving and communication skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to explain technical information in a clear and simple way.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good organizational skills and attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good English communication skills.</p></li></ul><h3>Middle Level</h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>3+ years</strong> of experience in technical support or a similar role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong troubleshooting and problem-solving skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting SaaS or web-based applications.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to investigate technical issues and work with engineering teams on resolution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with APIs, logs, databases, or basic SQL is a plus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with ticketing and support platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good English communication skills.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with tools such as Zendesk, Intercom, Jira, or similar.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic knowledge of APIs and Postman.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with SQL and database concepts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting SaaS, healthcare, or technology products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of data privacy and security principles.</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$55,000 - $75,000 per year</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>What We Offer</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fully remote work with flexible working hours.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Supportive and collaborative team environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunity to work with modern technology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional growth and learning opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in a growing HealthTech company.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Seniority Level:</strong> Junior / Middle</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 55,000 - 75,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"We are looking for a Technical Support Specialist to join our team and help customers resolve technical issues while using our health services platform.\n\nThis role is suitable for both Junior and Middle-level candidates, depending on experience. You will work closely with customers and internal technical teams to troubleshoot issues, answer technical questions, and ensure a smooth user experience.\n\n\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Provide technical support to customers via email, chat, and other communication channels.\n\n - Troubleshoot and resolve technical issues related to the platform.\n\n - Investigate reported problems and identify possible causes.\n\n - Escalate complex technical issues to development or engineering teams.\n\n - Document support requests, solutions, and recurring issues.\n\n - Assist customers with platform functionality and basic troubleshooting.\n\n - Monitor support tickets and ensure timely resolution.\n\n - Work with Product and Engineering teams to communicate customer feedback and recurring issues.\n\n - Contribute to internal support documentation and knowledge bases.\n\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n\n\nJUNIOR LEVEL\n\n - 1+ year of experience in technical support, IT support, customer support, or a related role.\n\n - Basic understanding of software applications and troubleshooting.\n\n - Comfortable working with web-based platforms and business software.\n\n - Strong problem-solving and communication skills.\n\n - Ability to explain technical information in a clear and simple way.\n\n - Good organizational skills and attention to detail.\n\n - Good English communication skills.\n\n\nMIDDLE LEVEL\n\n - 3+ years of experience in technical support or a similar role.\n\n - Strong troubleshooting and problem-solving skills.\n\n - Experience supporting SaaS or web-based applications.\n\n - Ability to investigate technical issues and work with engineering teams on resolution.\n\n - Familiarity with APIs, logs, databases, or basic SQL is a plus.\n\n - Experience working with ticketing and support platforms.\n\n - Good English communication skills.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with tools such as Zendesk, Intercom, Jira, or similar.\n\n - Basic knowledge of APIs and Postman.\n\n - Familiarity with SQL and database concepts.\n\n - Experience supporting SaaS, healthcare, or technology products.\n\n - Understanding of data privacy and security principles.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$55,000 - $75,000 per year, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Fully remote work with flexible working hours.\n\n - Supportive and collaborative team environment.\n\n - Opportunity to work with modern technology.\n\n - Professional growth and learning opportunities.\n\n - Experience in a growing HealthTech company.\n\n \n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSeniority Level: Junior / Middle\n\nSalary Range: 55,000 - 75,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"c889b880-ff70-4437-abab-296355a21fcc","title":"Project Coordinator","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T16:04:36.931+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/c889b880-ff70-4437-abab-296355a21fcc","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/c889b880-ff70-4437-abab-296355a21fcc/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for an organized and proactive <strong>Project Coordinator</strong> to support our teams with day-to-day project activities. You will help coordinate tasks, timelines, meetings, and communication to keep projects moving forward.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is an entry-level opportunity for someone who is organized, detail-oriented, and interested in building a career in project management.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support project planning, scheduling, and coordination.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track project tasks, deadlines, and deliverables.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Organize meetings and prepare agendas and documentation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain project documentation and status updates.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow up with team members on assigned tasks and deadlines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate communication between project stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help prepare project reports and presentations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track project risks, issues, and dependencies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support project managers with administrative and coordination tasks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with improving project processes and workflows.</p></li></ul><h2>Requirements</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>0–2 years</strong> of experience in project coordination, administration, operations, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational and time-management skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good written and verbal communication skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to manage multiple tasks and deadlines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with Microsoft Office or Google Workspace.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently in a remote environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good English communication skills.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with Jira, Asana, Trello, <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Monday.com\">Monday.com</a>, or similar tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic understanding of Agile or project management methodologies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous experience supporting software or technology projects.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with remote or international teams.</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$45,000 - $65,000 per year</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>What We Offer</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fully remote work with flexible working hours.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Supportive and collaborative team environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunity to develop project management skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional growth and learning opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to cross-functional technology projects.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Seniority Level:</strong> Junior</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 45,000 - 65,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"We are looking for an organized and proactive Project Coordinator to support our teams with day-to-day project activities. You will help coordinate tasks, timelines, meetings, and communication to keep projects moving forward.\n\nThis is an entry-level opportunity for someone who is organized, detail-oriented, and interested in building a career in project management.\n\n\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Support project planning, scheduling, and coordination.\n\n - Track project tasks, deadlines, and deliverables.\n\n - Organize meetings and prepare agendas and documentation.\n\n - Maintain project documentation and status updates.\n\n - Follow up with team members on assigned tasks and deadlines.\n\n - Coordinate communication between project stakeholders.\n\n - Help prepare project reports and presentations.\n\n - Track project risks, issues, and dependencies.\n\n - Support project managers with administrative and coordination tasks.\n\n - Assist with improving project processes and workflows.\n\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n\n - 0–2 years of experience in project coordination, administration, operations, or a related field.\n\n - Strong organizational and time-management skills.\n\n - Excellent attention to detail.\n\n - Good written and verbal communication skills.\n\n - Ability to manage multiple tasks and deadlines.\n\n - Comfortable working with Microsoft Office or Google Workspace.\n\n - Ability to work independently in a remote environment.\n\n - Good English communication skills.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Familiarity with Jira, Asana, Trello, Monday.com http://Monday.com, or similar tools.\n\n - Basic understanding of Agile or project management methodologies.\n\n - Previous experience supporting software or technology projects.\n\n - Experience working with remote or international teams.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$45,000 - $65,000 per year, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Fully remote work with flexible working hours.\n\n - Supportive and collaborative team environment.\n\n - Opportunity to develop project management skills.\n\n - Professional growth and learning opportunities.\n\n - Exposure to cross-functional technology projects.\n\n \n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSeniority Level: Junior\n\nSalary Range: 45,000 - 65,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"c6654507-a60f-430e-bfe1-5ea32029da11","title":"Data Entry Clerk","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T15:38:34.547+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/c6654507-a60f-430e-bfe1-5ea32029da11","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/c6654507-a60f-430e-bfe1-5ea32029da11/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a detail-oriented and reliable <strong>Data Entry Clerk</strong> to join our team. In this role, you will be responsible for entering, updating, and maintaining accurate information across internal systems and databases.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is an entry-level opportunity suitable for someone who is organized, comfortable working with data, and able to maintain a high level of accuracy.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enter and update information in databases and internal systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review data for accuracy and completeness.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain and organize digital records and files.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Verify information and identify discrepancies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Process documents and update records in a timely manner.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Perform basic data searches and reporting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow established data entry and documentation procedures.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate with team members to resolve missing or incorrect information.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain confidentiality of company and customer information.</p></li></ul><h2>Requirements</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>0–2 years</strong> of experience in data entry, administration, office support, or a related role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and accuracy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic computer skills and ability to work with online systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good knowledge of Microsoft Excel or Google Sheets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to type accurately and efficiently.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational and time-management skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently in a remote environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good English communication skills.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous experience with data entry or administrative tasks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with CRM, ERP, or database systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with large amounts of information.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic knowledge of reporting or data management tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working in a technology, SaaS, or healthcare environment.</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$35,000 - $45,000 per year</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>What We Offer</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fully remote work with flexible working hours.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Simple and well-structured onboarding process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Supportive and collaborative team environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunities for professional growth and development.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with a growing technology company.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Seniority Level:</strong> Junior</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 35,000 - 45,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"We are looking for a detail-oriented and reliable Data Entry Clerk to join our team. In this role, you will be responsible for entering, updating, and maintaining accurate information across internal systems and databases.\n\nThis is an entry-level opportunity suitable for someone who is organized, comfortable working with data, and able to maintain a high level of accuracy.\n\n\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Enter and update information in databases and internal systems.\n\n - Review data for accuracy and completeness.\n\n - Maintain and organize digital records and files.\n\n - Verify information and identify discrepancies.\n\n - Process documents and update records in a timely manner.\n\n - Perform basic data searches and reporting.\n\n - Follow established data entry and documentation procedures.\n\n - Communicate with team members to resolve missing or incorrect information.\n\n - Maintain confidentiality of company and customer information.\n\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n\n - 0–2 years of experience in data entry, administration, office support, or a related role.\n\n - Strong attention to detail and accuracy.\n\n - Basic computer skills and ability to work with online systems.\n\n - Good knowledge of Microsoft Excel or Google Sheets.\n\n - Ability to type accurately and efficiently.\n\n - Strong organizational and time-management skills.\n\n - Ability to work independently in a remote environment.\n\n - Good English communication skills.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Previous experience with data entry or administrative tasks.\n\n - Familiarity with CRM, ERP, or database systems.\n\n - Experience working with large amounts of information.\n\n - Basic knowledge of reporting or data management tools.\n\n - Experience working in a technology, SaaS, or healthcare environment.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$35,000 - $45,000 per year, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Fully remote work with flexible working hours.\n\n - Simple and well-structured onboarding process.\n\n - Supportive and collaborative team environment.\n\n - Opportunities for professional growth and development.\n\n - Experience working with a growing technology company.\n\n \n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSeniority Level: Junior\n\nSalary Range: 35,000 - 45,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"9e61ef7c-890f-409e-b9bc-9e791d552f2a","title":"Administrative Assistant","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T15:46:49.721+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/9e61ef7c-890f-409e-b9bc-9e791d552f2a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/9e61ef7c-890f-409e-b9bc-9e791d552f2a/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a reliable and organized <strong>Administrative Assistant</strong> to support our team with day-to-day administrative and coordination tasks. This is an entry-level opportunity for someone who is detail-oriented, proactive, and comfortable working in a remote environment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will help keep internal processes organized, coordinate information and schedules, and provide administrative support across different teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide day-to-day administrative support to team members.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage calendars, meetings, and scheduling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare and organize documents, reports, and presentations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate records and internal files.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Handle email communication and follow up on routine requests.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate meetings and assist with meeting preparation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support data entry and basic reporting tasks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help coordinate internal projects and team activities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate with internal teams and external partners when needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with other administrative tasks as required.</p></li></ul><h2>Requirements</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>0–2 years</strong> of experience in administration, office support, customer service, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational skills and attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good written and verbal communication skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency with Microsoft Office or Google Workspace.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to manage multiple tasks and meet deadlines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable, proactive, and willing to learn.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently in a remote environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good English communication skills.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with tools such as Slack, Microsoft Teams, Asana, Trello, or similar.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with scheduling and calendar management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic knowledge of Excel or Google Sheets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous experience in a technology, SaaS, or healthcare company.</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$45,000 - $60,000 per year</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>What We Offer</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fully remote work with flexible working hours.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Supportive and collaborative team environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunity to develop professional and administrative skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Career growth and learning opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to different areas of a growing technology company.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Seniority Level:</strong> Junior</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 45,000 - 60,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"We are looking for a reliable and organized Administrative Assistant to support our team with day-to-day administrative and coordination tasks. This is an entry-level opportunity for someone who is detail-oriented, proactive, and comfortable working in a remote environment.\n\nYou will help keep internal processes organized, coordinate information and schedules, and provide administrative support across different teams.\n\n\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Provide day-to-day administrative support to team members.\n\n - Manage calendars, meetings, and scheduling.\n\n - Prepare and organize documents, reports, and presentations.\n\n - Maintain accurate records and internal files.\n\n - Handle email communication and follow up on routine requests.\n\n - Coordinate meetings and assist with meeting preparation.\n\n - Support data entry and basic reporting tasks.\n\n - Help coordinate internal projects and team activities.\n\n - Communicate with internal teams and external partners when needed.\n\n - Assist with other administrative tasks as required.\n\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n\n - 0–2 years of experience in administration, office support, customer service, or a related field.\n\n - Strong organizational skills and attention to detail.\n\n - Good written and verbal communication skills.\n\n - Proficiency with Microsoft Office or Google Workspace.\n\n - Ability to manage multiple tasks and meet deadlines.\n\n - Reliable, proactive, and willing to learn.\n\n - Ability to work independently in a remote environment.\n\n - Good English communication skills.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with tools such as Slack, Microsoft Teams, Asana, Trello, or similar.\n\n - Experience with scheduling and calendar management.\n\n - Basic knowledge of Excel or Google Sheets.\n\n - Previous experience in a technology, SaaS, or healthcare company.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$45,000 - $60,000 per year, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Fully remote work with flexible working hours.\n\n - Supportive and collaborative team environment.\n\n - Opportunity to develop professional and administrative skills.\n\n - Career growth and learning opportunities.\n\n - Exposure to different areas of a growing technology company.\n\n \n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSeniority Level: Junior\n\nSalary Range: 45,000 - 60,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"a3265022-3e44-4d64-bda3-537be8ab0dd9","title":"Data Analyst – Junior / Middle","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T15:48:10.848+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/a3265022-3e44-4d64-bda3-537be8ab0dd9","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/a3265022-3e44-4d64-bda3-537be8ab0dd9/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a <strong>Data Analyst</strong> to join our team and help turn data into actionable insights. You will work with business and product teams to analyze data, identify trends, and create reports that support better decision-making.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is suitable for both <strong>Junior and Middle-level candidates</strong>, depending on experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collect, clean, and analyze data from different sources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare reports, dashboards, and data visualizations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify trends, patterns, and opportunities in business and product data.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with stakeholders to understand reporting and analytical needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track key performance indicators (KPIs) and provide regular insights.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support data-driven decision-making across the business.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Validate data quality and investigate discrepancies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with Product, Engineering, Marketing, and Operations teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain clear documentation of reports, metrics, and analytical processes.</p></li></ul><h2>Requirements</h2><h3>Junior Level</h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>1+ year</strong> of experience in data analysis, reporting, business intelligence, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good knowledge of <strong>Excel or Google Sheets</strong>.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic knowledge of <strong>SQL</strong>.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with data visualization and reporting tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical and problem-solving skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to communicate findings clearly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good English communication skills.</p></li></ul><h3>Middle Level</h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>3+ years</strong> of experience in data analysis or a similar role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong SQL skills and experience working with databases.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advanced Excel or Google Sheets skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with BI and visualization tools such as <strong>Power BI, Tableau, or Looker</strong>.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to analyze large datasets and translate findings into actionable insights.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience defining and tracking KPIs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and stakeholder management skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good English communication skills.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Python or R for data analysis.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with cloud data platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with product, marketing, or customer analytics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with SaaS or technology companies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge of A/B testing and basic statistical concepts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working in healthcare or other data-sensitive industries.</p></li></ul><h2>What We Offer</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fully remote work with flexible working hours.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunity to work with real-world business and product data.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaboration with international and cross-functional teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional growth and learning opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Supportive and collaborative environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive compensation based on experience and skills.</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$65,000 - $100,000 per year</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Seniority Level:</strong> Junior / Middle</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 65,000 - 100,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"We are looking for a Data Analyst to join our team and help turn data into actionable insights. You will work with business and product teams to analyze data, identify trends, and create reports that support better decision-making.\n\nThis role is suitable for both Junior and Middle-level candidates, depending on experience.\n\n\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Collect, clean, and analyze data from different sources.\n\n - Prepare reports, dashboards, and data visualizations.\n\n - Identify trends, patterns, and opportunities in business and product data.\n\n - Work with stakeholders to understand reporting and analytical needs.\n\n - Track key performance indicators (KPIs) and provide regular insights.\n\n - Support data-driven decision-making across the business.\n\n - Validate data quality and investigate discrepancies.\n\n - Collaborate with Product, Engineering, Marketing, and Operations teams.\n\n - Maintain clear documentation of reports, metrics, and analytical processes.\n\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n\n\nJUNIOR LEVEL\n\n - 1+ year of experience in data analysis, reporting, business intelligence, or a related field.\n\n - Good knowledge of Excel or Google Sheets.\n\n - Basic knowledge of SQL.\n\n - Familiarity with data visualization and reporting tools.\n\n - Strong analytical and problem-solving skills.\n\n - Good attention to detail.\n\n - Ability to communicate findings clearly.\n\n - Good English communication skills.\n\n\nMIDDLE LEVEL\n\n - 3+ years of experience in data analysis or a similar role.\n\n - Strong SQL skills and experience working with databases.\n\n - Advanced Excel or Google Sheets skills.\n\n - Experience with BI and visualization tools such as Power BI, Tableau, or Looker.\n\n - Ability to analyze large datasets and translate findings into actionable insights.\n\n - Experience defining and tracking KPIs.\n\n - Strong communication and stakeholder management skills.\n\n - Good English communication skills.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with Python or R for data analysis.\n\n - Experience with cloud data platforms.\n\n - Familiarity with product, marketing, or customer analytics.\n\n - Experience working with SaaS or technology companies.\n\n - Knowledge of A/B testing and basic statistical concepts.\n\n - Experience working in healthcare or other data-sensitive industries.\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Fully remote work with flexible working hours.\n\n - Opportunity to work with real-world business and product data.\n\n - Collaboration with international and cross-functional teams.\n\n - Professional growth and learning opportunities.\n\n - Supportive and collaborative environment.\n\n - Competitive compensation based on experience and skills.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$65,000 - $100,000 per year, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSeniority Level: Junior / Middle\n\nSalary Range: 65,000 - 100,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"86520da4-cb6a-400a-9179-255b545726d4","title":"Operations Coordinator","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T16:03:20.968+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/86520da4-cb6a-400a-9179-255b545726d4","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/86520da4-cb6a-400a-9179-255b545726d4/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a reliable and organized <strong>Operations Coordinator</strong> to support our day-to-day business operations. You will help coordinate internal processes, maintain accurate information, and work with different teams to ensure tasks are completed efficiently.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is an entry-level opportunity for someone who is detail-oriented, proactive, and interested in building a career in business operations.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support daily operational and administrative activities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate tasks and requests across different teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain internal records, documents, and databases.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track operational tasks, deadlines, and follow-ups.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare basic reports and status updates.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help coordinate meetings, schedules, and internal communications.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and escalate operational issues when needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support process improvement initiatives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate with internal teams and external partners.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with other operational tasks as required.</p></li></ul><h2>Requirements</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>0–2 years</strong> of experience in operations, administration, customer service, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational and time-management skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good attention to detail and accuracy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and interpersonal skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to manage multiple tasks and priorities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency with Microsoft Office or Google Workspace.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently in a remote environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good English communication skills.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with tools such as Slack, Microsoft Teams, Asana, Trello, or similar.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic knowledge of Excel or Google Sheets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with CRM or business management systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous experience in a technology, SaaS, or healthcare company.</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$42,000 - $60,000 per year</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>What We Offer</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fully remote work with flexible working hours.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Supportive and collaborative team environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunity to develop professional and operational skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional growth and learning opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to different areas of a growing technology company.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Seniority Level:</strong> Junior</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 42,000 - 60,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"We are looking for a reliable and organized Operations Coordinator to support our day-to-day business operations. You will help coordinate internal processes, maintain accurate information, and work with different teams to ensure tasks are completed efficiently.\n\nThis is an entry-level opportunity for someone who is detail-oriented, proactive, and interested in building a career in business operations.\n\n\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Support daily operational and administrative activities.\n\n - Coordinate tasks and requests across different teams.\n\n - Maintain internal records, documents, and databases.\n\n - Track operational tasks, deadlines, and follow-ups.\n\n - Prepare basic reports and status updates.\n\n - Help coordinate meetings, schedules, and internal communications.\n\n - Identify and escalate operational issues when needed.\n\n - Support process improvement initiatives.\n\n - Communicate with internal teams and external partners.\n\n - Assist with other operational tasks as required.\n\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n\n - 0–2 years of experience in operations, administration, customer service, or a related field.\n\n - Strong organizational and time-management skills.\n\n - Good attention to detail and accuracy.\n\n - Strong communication and interpersonal skills.\n\n - Ability to manage multiple tasks and priorities.\n\n - Proficiency with Microsoft Office or Google Workspace.\n\n - Ability to work independently in a remote environment.\n\n - Good English communication skills.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Familiarity with tools such as Slack, Microsoft Teams, Asana, Trello, or similar.\n\n - Basic knowledge of Excel or Google Sheets.\n\n - Experience with CRM or business management systems.\n\n - Previous experience in a technology, SaaS, or healthcare company.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$42,000 - $60,000 per year, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Fully remote work with flexible working hours.\n\n - Supportive and collaborative team environment.\n\n - Opportunity to develop professional and operational skills.\n\n - Professional growth and learning opportunities.\n\n - Exposure to different areas of a growing technology company.\n\n \n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSeniority Level: Junior\n\nSalary Range: 42,000 - 60,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"05e6676f-dab9-400b-8616-d363967994d9","title":"Customer Success Specialist","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T16:05:56.029+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/05e6676f-dab9-400b-8616-d363967994d9","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/05e6676f-dab9-400b-8616-d363967994d9/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a <strong>Customer Success Specialist</strong> to help our customers get the most value from our health services platform. You will build relationships with customers, support their onboarding and ongoing use of the platform, and work with internal teams to ensure a positive customer experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is suitable for both <strong>Junior and Middle-level candidates</strong>, depending on experience.</p><h2>Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support customers throughout onboarding and their ongoing use of the platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build strong relationships with customers and understand their needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Respond to customer questions and help resolve issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor customer satisfaction, engagement, and overall experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct onboarding sessions, product demonstrations, and follow-ups.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with Support, Product, and Engineering teams to resolve customer needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collect customer feedback and communicate insights to internal teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify opportunities to improve customer adoption and retention.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate customer information and activity in CRM systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare basic reports on customer activity and satisfaction.</p></li></ul><h2>Requirements</h2><h3>Junior Level</h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>1+ year</strong> of experience in customer service, customer success, account support, or a related role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and interpersonal skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Customer-focused and proactive approach.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good organizational and problem-solving skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to manage multiple customer requests and priorities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable learning new software and digital tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good English communication skills.</p></li></ul><h3>Middle Level</h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>3+ years</strong> of experience in Customer Success, Account Management, Customer Support, or a similar role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing customer relationships independently.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with SaaS or digital products is a plus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong ability to identify customer needs and drive product adoption.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience using CRM and customer success tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication, problem-solving, and stakeholder management skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good English communication skills.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with tools such as Salesforce, HubSpot, Zendesk, Intercom, or similar.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with SaaS or healthcare technology products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with customer onboarding and product training.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of customer success metrics such as retention, churn, CSAT, or NPS.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional language skills are a plus.</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$50,000 - $70,000 per year</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>What We Offer</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fully remote work with flexible working hours.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunity to work with an innovative health services platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Supportive and collaborative team environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional growth and learning opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunity to work closely with Product, Engineering, and Sales teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive compensation based on experience and skills.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Seniority Level:</strong> Junior / Middle</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 50,000 - 70,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"We are looking for a Customer Success Specialist to help our customers get the most value from our health services platform. You will build relationships with customers, support their onboarding and ongoing use of the platform, and work with internal teams to ensure a positive customer experience.\n\nThis role is suitable for both Junior and Middle-level candidates, depending on experience.\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Support customers throughout onboarding and their ongoing use of the platform.\n\n - Build strong relationships with customers and understand their needs.\n\n - Respond to customer questions and help resolve issues.\n\n - Monitor customer satisfaction, engagement, and overall experience.\n\n - Conduct onboarding sessions, product demonstrations, and follow-ups.\n\n - Work closely with Support, Product, and Engineering teams to resolve customer needs.\n\n - Collect customer feedback and communicate insights to internal teams.\n\n - Identify opportunities to improve customer adoption and retention.\n\n - Maintain accurate customer information and activity in CRM systems.\n\n - Prepare basic reports on customer activity and satisfaction.\n\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n\n\nJUNIOR LEVEL\n\n - 1+ year of experience in customer service, customer success, account support, or a related role.\n\n - Strong communication and interpersonal skills.\n\n - Customer-focused and proactive approach.\n\n - Good organizational and problem-solving skills.\n\n - Ability to manage multiple customer requests and priorities.\n\n - Comfortable learning new software and digital tools.\n\n - Good English communication skills.\n\n\nMIDDLE LEVEL\n\n - 3+ years of experience in Customer Success, Account Management, Customer Support, or a similar role.\n\n - Experience managing customer relationships independently.\n\n - Experience with SaaS or digital products is a plus.\n\n - Strong ability to identify customer needs and drive product adoption.\n\n - Experience using CRM and customer success tools.\n\n - Strong communication, problem-solving, and stakeholder management skills.\n\n - Good English communication skills.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with tools such as Salesforce, HubSpot, Zendesk, Intercom, or similar.\n\n - Experience working with SaaS or healthcare technology products.\n\n - Experience with customer onboarding and product training.\n\n - Understanding of customer success metrics such as retention, churn, CSAT, or NPS.\n\n - Additional language skills are a plus.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$50,000 - $70,000 per year, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Fully remote work with flexible working hours.\n\n - Opportunity to work with an innovative health services platform.\n\n - Supportive and collaborative team environment.\n\n - Professional growth and learning opportunities.\n\n - Opportunity to work closely with Product, Engineering, and Sales teams.\n\n - Competitive compensation based on experience and skills.\n\n \n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSeniority Level: Junior / Middle\n\nSalary Range: 50,000 - 70,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"e82ed270-7a4a-4e5d-9494-908eda58c2a9","title":"Customer Service Representative","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T15:40:43.906+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/e82ed270-7a4a-4e5d-9494-908eda58c2a9","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/e82ed270-7a4a-4e5d-9494-908eda58c2a9/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a friendly and customer-focused <strong>Customer Service Representative</strong> to join our team and support customers using our health services platform.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is an entry-level opportunity for someone who enjoys helping people, solving problems, and communicating with customers. You will respond to inquiries, resolve issues, and help ensure a positive customer experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Respond to customer questions and requests via email, chat, and other communication channels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide accurate information about products and services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Troubleshoot customer issues and help find appropriate solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Escalate complex issues to the relevant teams when needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate records of customer interactions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow up on customer requests and ensure timely resolution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with internal teams to resolve customer issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify recurring customer questions and provide feedback to improve processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain a professional and helpful customer experience.</p></li></ul><h2>Requirements</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>0–2 years</strong> of experience in customer service, support, administration, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and interpersonal skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Customer-focused and patient approach.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good problem-solving and organizational skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to manage multiple requests and prioritize tasks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with computers and common business software.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently in a remote environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good English communication skills.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous experience in customer support or a customer-facing role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with CRM or help desk tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with chat or ticketing systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working in SaaS, technology, or healthcare.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional language skills are a plus.</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$38,000 - $50,000 per year</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>What We Offer</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fully remote work with flexible working hours.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Supportive and collaborative team environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Training and onboarding to help you succeed in the role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunities for professional growth and development.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with a growing technology company.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Seniority Level:</strong> Junior</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 38,000 - 50,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"We are looking for a friendly and customer-focused Customer Service Representative to join our team and support customers using our health services platform.\n\nThis is an entry-level opportunity for someone who enjoys helping people, solving problems, and communicating with customers. You will respond to inquiries, resolve issues, and help ensure a positive customer experience.\n\n\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Respond to customer questions and requests via email, chat, and other communication channels.\n\n - Provide accurate information about products and services.\n\n - Troubleshoot customer issues and help find appropriate solutions.\n\n - Escalate complex issues to the relevant teams when needed.\n\n - Maintain accurate records of customer interactions.\n\n - Follow up on customer requests and ensure timely resolution.\n\n - Work with internal teams to resolve customer issues.\n\n - Identify recurring customer questions and provide feedback to improve processes.\n\n - Maintain a professional and helpful customer experience.\n\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n\n - 0–2 years of experience in customer service, support, administration, or a related field.\n\n - Strong communication and interpersonal skills.\n\n - Customer-focused and patient approach.\n\n - Good problem-solving and organizational skills.\n\n - Ability to manage multiple requests and prioritize tasks.\n\n - Comfortable working with computers and common business software.\n\n - Ability to work independently in a remote environment.\n\n - Good English communication skills.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Previous experience in customer support or a customer-facing role.\n\n - Familiarity with CRM or help desk tools.\n\n - Experience with chat or ticketing systems.\n\n - Experience working in SaaS, technology, or healthcare.\n\n - Additional language skills are a plus.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$38,000 - $50,000 per year, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Fully remote work with flexible working hours.\n\n - Supportive and collaborative team environment.\n\n - Training and onboarding to help you succeed in the role.\n\n - Opportunities for professional growth and development.\n\n - Experience working with a growing technology company.\n\n \n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSeniority Level: Junior\n\nSalary Range: 38,000 - 50,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"3b7c791b-ca62-4655-a4b7-1425741bc3cf","title":"Medical Billing Team Lead","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-31T11:09:10.684+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/3b7c791b-ca62-4655-a4b7-1425741bc3cf","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/3b7c791b-ca62-4655-a4b7-1425741bc3cf/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raventra Health</strong> is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Medical Billing Team Lead, you will support the day-to-day performance of Raventra Health’s billing team and help ensure client accounts are processed accurately and efficiently. You will coordinate workloads, monitor quality and productivity, provide guidance to billing specialists, and help resolve complex billing issues.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate daily workloads and priorities across the medical billing team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor billing productivity, accuracy, claim submission, and turnaround-time metrics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review billing work and provide feedback to ensure client and company standards are met</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support team members with complex billing issues, payer requirements, and claim corrections</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate with coding, claims, payment posting, denials, and AR teams to resolve issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify recurring billing errors and recommend process improvements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with onboarding, training, and ongoing coaching for billing team members</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain and update billing procedures, guidelines, and process documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Escalate significant client or operational issues to the Billing Operations Manager</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare team performance updates and communicate key issues, trends, and priorities to management</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in medical billing or healthcare revenue cycle management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience providing guidance, mentoring, or day-to-day leadership to billing staff</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of healthcare billing, claim submission, payer requirements, and reimbursement processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with CMS-1500 and UB-04 claim forms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong knowledge of billing workflows and common claim and payment issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to review work for accuracy and provide clear, constructive feedback</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational and communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to prioritize workloads and support a team in a remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently and handle escalated billing issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIPAA-compliant private workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CPB, CPC, or another relevant healthcare revenue cycle certification</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or another major billing or practice management system</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with multiple payer types</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Denials, appeals, payment posting, or AR follow-up experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with provider groups or hospitals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous experience in outsourced RCM or multi-client healthcare operations</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, certifications, and relevant healthcare revenue cycle expertise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Raventra Health is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Medical Billing Team Lead, you will support the day-to-day performance of Raventra Health’s billing team and help ensure client accounts are processed accurately and efficiently. You will coordinate workloads, monitor quality and productivity, provide guidance to billing specialists, and help resolve complex billing issues.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Coordinate daily workloads and priorities across the medical billing team\n\n - Monitor billing productivity, accuracy, claim submission, and turnaround-time metrics\n\n - Review billing work and provide feedback to ensure client and company standards are met\n\n - Support team members with complex billing issues, payer requirements, and claim corrections\n\n - Coordinate with coding, claims, payment posting, denials, and AR teams to resolve issues\n\n - Identify recurring billing errors and recommend process improvements\n\n - Assist with onboarding, training, and ongoing coaching for billing team members\n\n - Maintain and update billing procedures, guidelines, and process documentation\n\n - Escalate significant client or operational issues to the Billing Operations Manager\n\n - Prepare team performance updates and communicate key issues, trends, and priorities to management\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 2+ years of experience in medical billing or healthcare revenue cycle management\n\n - Experience providing guidance, mentoring, or day-to-day leadership to billing staff\n\n - Strong understanding of healthcare billing, claim submission, payer requirements, and reimbursement processes\n\n - Experience working with CMS-1500 and UB-04 claim forms\n\n - Strong knowledge of billing workflows and common claim and payment issues\n\n - Ability to review work for accuracy and provide clear, constructive feedback\n\n - Strong organizational and communication skills\n\n - Ability to prioritize workloads and support a team in a remote environment\n\n - Ability to work independently and handle escalated billing issues\n\n - HIPAA-compliant private workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - CPB, CPC, or another relevant healthcare revenue cycle certification\n\n - Experience with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or another major billing or practice management system\n\n - Experience working with multiple payer types\n\n - Denials, appeals, payment posting, or AR follow-up experience\n\n - Experience working with provider groups or hospitals\n\n - Previous experience in outsourced RCM or multi-client healthcare operations\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, certifications, and relevant healthcare revenue cycle expertise.\n\nBenefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nRaventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"9b07d4b4-ad90-4620-aa4d-fe15bd59b336","title":"Provider Enrollment Specialist","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-31T11:10:13.214+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/9b07d4b4-ad90-4620-aa4d-fe15bd59b336","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/9b07d4b4-ad90-4620-aa4d-fe15bd59b336/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raventra Health</strong> is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Provider Enrollment Specialist, you will manage payer enrollment activities for provider clients, helping ensure providers and practices are properly enrolled with Medicare, Medicaid, and commercial insurance plans. You will prepare applications, track enrollment status, resolve issues, and maintain accurate payer and provider information.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare and submit provider enrollment applications to Medicare, Medicaid, and commercial payers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gather and review provider information and supporting documentation required for enrollment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track enrollment applications, payer requests, approvals, and effective dates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow up with payers and enrollment organizations on pending or delayed applications</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Research and resolve enrollment discrepancies, rejections, and missing information</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate provider and payer enrollment records in internal systems and online portals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Process updates to provider information, including practice locations, specialties, and affiliations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate enrollment-related information with credentialing, billing, and client teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor enrollment deadlines and support timely revalidation, renewals, and payer updates</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1+ year of experience in provider enrollment, payer enrollment, credentialing, medical billing, or a related healthcare administrative role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of Medicare, Medicaid, and commercial payer enrollment processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience preparing and submitting enrollment applications and supporting documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with payer portals and online provider enrollment systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and ability to manage multiple applications and deadlines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational and follow-up skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to research enrollment issues and communicate effectively with payers and provider teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently and effectively in a fully remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIPAA-compliant private workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with CAQH</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge of NPI, taxonomy codes, PECOS, and other provider enrollment requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Medicare and Medicaid revalidation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with multiple commercial payers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with hospital or multi-specialty provider enrollment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or other healthcare systems</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare administration expertise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Raventra Health is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Provider Enrollment Specialist, you will manage payer enrollment activities for provider clients, helping ensure providers and practices are properly enrolled with Medicare, Medicaid, and commercial insurance plans. You will prepare applications, track enrollment status, resolve issues, and maintain accurate payer and provider information.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Prepare and submit provider enrollment applications to Medicare, Medicaid, and commercial payers\n\n - Gather and review provider information and supporting documentation required for enrollment\n\n - Track enrollment applications, payer requests, approvals, and effective dates\n\n - Follow up with payers and enrollment organizations on pending or delayed applications\n\n - Research and resolve enrollment discrepancies, rejections, and missing information\n\n - Maintain accurate provider and payer enrollment records in internal systems and online portals\n\n - Process updates to provider information, including practice locations, specialties, and affiliations\n\n - Coordinate enrollment-related information with credentialing, billing, and client teams\n\n - Monitor enrollment deadlines and support timely revalidation, renewals, and payer updates\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 1+ year of experience in provider enrollment, payer enrollment, credentialing, medical billing, or a related healthcare administrative role\n\n - Understanding of Medicare, Medicaid, and commercial payer enrollment processes\n\n - Experience preparing and submitting enrollment applications and supporting documentation\n\n - Familiarity with payer portals and online provider enrollment systems\n\n - Strong attention to detail and ability to manage multiple applications and deadlines\n\n - Strong organizational and follow-up skills\n\n - Ability to research enrollment issues and communicate effectively with payers and provider teams\n\n - Ability to work independently and effectively in a fully remote environment\n\n - HIPAA-compliant private workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with CAQH\n\n - Knowledge of NPI, taxonomy codes, PECOS, and other provider enrollment requirements\n\n - Experience with Medicare and Medicaid revalidation\n\n - Experience working with multiple commercial payers\n\n - Experience with hospital or multi-specialty provider enrollment\n\n - Familiarity with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or other healthcare systems\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare administration expertise.\n\nBenefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nRaventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"4781fe42-2075-454e-a21d-d69395415926","title":"Billing Operations Manager","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-31T11:11:27.438+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/4781fe42-2075-454e-a21d-d69395415926","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/4781fe42-2075-454e-a21d-d69395415926/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raventra Health</strong> is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Billing Operations Manager, you will oversee billing operations for assigned provider and hospital clients, ensuring claims are prepared and submitted accurately and efficiently. You will lead billing teams, monitor performance, resolve operational issues, and work with other revenue cycle functions to support timely reimbursement.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Oversee daily billing operations for assigned provider and hospital accounts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead and support billing team members, including workload coordination and performance management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor claim submission volume, billing accuracy, turnaround times, and other operational metrics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review billing workflows and identify opportunities to improve efficiency and reduce errors</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate with coding, claims, payment posting, AR, and denials teams to resolve billing issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Investigate recurring claim errors and implement corrective actions to prevent future issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support client escalations and communicate billing-related updates and resolutions to internal stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and maintain billing procedures, process documentation, and quality standards</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide training, coaching, and ongoing guidance to billing team members</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare operational reports and communicate billing performance, risks, and improvement opportunities to leadership</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience in medical billing, revenue cycle management, or healthcare operations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience leading or supervising a medical billing team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of healthcare billing, claim submission, payer requirements, and reimbursement processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience monitoring billing productivity, quality, and turnaround-time metrics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong knowledge of CMS-1500 and UB-04 claim forms and electronic claims submission</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to investigate billing issues and identify root causes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong leadership, communication, and organizational skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to manage multiple client accounts and operational priorities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently and effectively in a fully remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIPAA-compliant private workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CPB, CPC, or other relevant healthcare revenue cycle certification</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or another major billing or practice management system</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with multiple payer types</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with denials, appeals, or accounts receivable processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with provider groups or hospitals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in outsourced RCM or multi-client healthcare operations</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, certifications, and relevant healthcare revenue cycle expertise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Raventra Health is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Billing Operations Manager, you will oversee billing operations for assigned provider and hospital clients, ensuring claims are prepared and submitted accurately and efficiently. You will lead billing teams, monitor performance, resolve operational issues, and work with other revenue cycle functions to support timely reimbursement.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Oversee daily billing operations for assigned provider and hospital accounts\n\n - Lead and support billing team members, including workload coordination and performance management\n\n - Monitor claim submission volume, billing accuracy, turnaround times, and other operational metrics\n\n - Review billing workflows and identify opportunities to improve efficiency and reduce errors\n\n - Coordinate with coding, claims, payment posting, AR, and denials teams to resolve billing issues\n\n - Investigate recurring claim errors and implement corrective actions to prevent future issues\n\n - Support client escalations and communicate billing-related updates and resolutions to internal stakeholders\n\n - Develop and maintain billing procedures, process documentation, and quality standards\n\n - Provide training, coaching, and ongoing guidance to billing team members\n\n - Prepare operational reports and communicate billing performance, risks, and improvement opportunities to leadership\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 3+ years of experience in medical billing, revenue cycle management, or healthcare operations\n\n - Experience leading or supervising a medical billing team\n\n - Strong understanding of healthcare billing, claim submission, payer requirements, and reimbursement processes\n\n - Experience monitoring billing productivity, quality, and turnaround-time metrics\n\n - Strong knowledge of CMS-1500 and UB-04 claim forms and electronic claims submission\n\n - Ability to investigate billing issues and identify root causes\n\n - Strong leadership, communication, and organizational skills\n\n - Ability to manage multiple client accounts and operational priorities\n\n - Ability to work independently and effectively in a fully remote environment\n\n - HIPAA-compliant private workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - CPB, CPC, or other relevant healthcare revenue cycle certification\n\n - Experience with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or another major billing or practice management system\n\n - Experience working with multiple payer types\n\n - Experience with denials, appeals, or accounts receivable processes\n\n - Experience working with provider groups or hospitals\n\n - Experience in outsourced RCM or multi-client healthcare operations\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, certifications, and relevant healthcare revenue cycle expertise.\n\nBenefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nRaventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"17efee31-6fd1-434b-908a-56913317b895","title":"Healthcare Operations Manager","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-31T11:12:26.979+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/17efee31-6fd1-434b-908a-56913317b895","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/17efee31-6fd1-434b-908a-56913317b895/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raventra Health</strong> is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Healthcare Operations Manager, you will oversee day-to-day revenue cycle operations and help ensure services are delivered accurately, efficiently, and consistently across client accounts. You will coordinate operational teams, monitor performance, resolve escalations, and identify opportunities to improve workflows and service quality.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Oversee day-to-day operations across billing, coding, claims, payment posting, and accounts receivable functions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate workloads and priorities across operational teams to support client requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor productivity, quality, turnaround times, and other operational performance metrics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review operational reports and identify trends, bottlenecks, and opportunities for improvement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage escalated operational issues and coordinate timely resolution with the appropriate teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with Client Success Managers to address client concerns and maintain service standards</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and improve processes, procedures, and internal operating standards</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support training, coaching, and performance development for operational team members</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure teams follow established healthcare privacy, security, and compliance procedures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate operational priorities, risks, and performance updates to leadership</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience in healthcare operations, revenue cycle management, or healthcare services</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing or coordinating healthcare operations teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of revenue cycle workflows, including billing, coding, claims, payment posting, and AR</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience monitoring operational KPIs and using data to improve performance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong leadership, organization, and problem-solving skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to manage competing priorities and make effective operational decisions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication skills and ability to work with both internal teams and client stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing escalations and resolving operational issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently and effectively in a fully remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIPAA-compliant private workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with provider groups or hospitals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare revenue cycle management certification</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or other healthcare systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lean, Six Sigma, or other process improvement experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with outsourced healthcare services or multi-client operations</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare operations expertise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Raventra Health is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Healthcare Operations Manager, you will oversee day-to-day revenue cycle operations and help ensure services are delivered accurately, efficiently, and consistently across client accounts. You will coordinate operational teams, monitor performance, resolve escalations, and identify opportunities to improve workflows and service quality.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Oversee day-to-day operations across billing, coding, claims, payment posting, and accounts receivable functions\n\n - Coordinate workloads and priorities across operational teams to support client requirements\n\n - Monitor productivity, quality, turnaround times, and other operational performance metrics\n\n - Review operational reports and identify trends, bottlenecks, and opportunities for improvement\n\n - Manage escalated operational issues and coordinate timely resolution with the appropriate teams\n\n - Work with Client Success Managers to address client concerns and maintain service standards\n\n - Develop and improve processes, procedures, and internal operating standards\n\n - Support training, coaching, and performance development for operational team members\n\n - Ensure teams follow established healthcare privacy, security, and compliance procedures\n\n - Communicate operational priorities, risks, and performance updates to leadership\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 3+ years of experience in healthcare operations, revenue cycle management, or healthcare services\n\n - Experience managing or coordinating healthcare operations teams\n\n - Strong understanding of revenue cycle workflows, including billing, coding, claims, payment posting, and AR\n\n - Experience monitoring operational KPIs and using data to improve performance\n\n - Strong leadership, organization, and problem-solving skills\n\n - Ability to manage competing priorities and make effective operational decisions\n\n - Strong communication skills and ability to work with both internal teams and client stakeholders\n\n - Experience managing escalations and resolving operational issues\n\n - Ability to work independently and effectively in a fully remote environment\n\n - HIPAA-compliant private workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience working with provider groups or hospitals\n\n - Healthcare revenue cycle management certification\n\n - Familiarity with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or other healthcare systems\n\n - Lean, Six Sigma, or other process improvement experience\n\n - Experience with outsourced healthcare services or multi-client operations\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare operations expertise.\n\nBenefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nRaventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"d553ab0b-a396-4eb9-856f-17966c78419a","title":"RCM Business Analyst","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-31T11:13:33.915+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/d553ab0b-a396-4eb9-856f-17966c78419a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/d553ab0b-a396-4eb9-856f-17966c78419a/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raventra Health</strong> is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As an RCM Business Analyst, you will analyze revenue cycle workflows, business requirements, and operational performance to identify opportunities for improvement. You will work across billing, coding, claims, accounts receivable, and client-facing teams to help improve processes, systems, and service delivery.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analyze existing revenue cycle workflows and identify process gaps, inefficiencies, and improvement opportunities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gather and document business requirements from operational teams and client stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Map current and future-state processes across billing, coding, claims, payment posting, and AR</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analyze operational and financial data to identify trends and support business decisions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate business needs into clear requirements for system, process, or reporting improvements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with RCM teams to investigate operational issues and develop practical solutions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support the implementation and testing of new processes, system enhancements, and workflow changes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare process documentation, requirements, reports, and presentations for relevant stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track improvement initiatives and communicate progress, risks, and outcomes to project and operational teams</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience as a Business Analyst, preferably within healthcare, healthcare services, or revenue cycle management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of healthcare revenue cycle processes, including billing, coding, claims, payment posting, and AR</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience gathering, documenting, and analyzing business requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong process mapping and workflow analysis skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong Excel and data analysis skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to translate complex operational needs into clear, actionable requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and stakeholder management skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analytical and problem-solving mindset with strong attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to manage multiple priorities and work independently in a remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIPAA-compliant private workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with healthcare RCM or practice management systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or similar healthcare platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">SQL, Power BI, or other data analysis skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with process improvement methodologies such as Lean or Six Sigma</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting software implementations or system enhancements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with provider groups or hospitals</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare business analysis expertise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Raventra Health is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As an RCM Business Analyst, you will analyze revenue cycle workflows, business requirements, and operational performance to identify opportunities for improvement. You will work across billing, coding, claims, accounts receivable, and client-facing teams to help improve processes, systems, and service delivery.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Analyze existing revenue cycle workflows and identify process gaps, inefficiencies, and improvement opportunities\n\n - Gather and document business requirements from operational teams and client stakeholders\n\n - Map current and future-state processes across billing, coding, claims, payment posting, and AR\n\n - Analyze operational and financial data to identify trends and support business decisions\n\n - Translate business needs into clear requirements for system, process, or reporting improvements\n\n - Collaborate with RCM teams to investigate operational issues and develop practical solutions\n\n - Support the implementation and testing of new processes, system enhancements, and workflow changes\n\n - Prepare process documentation, requirements, reports, and presentations for relevant stakeholders\n\n - Track improvement initiatives and communicate progress, risks, and outcomes to project and operational teams\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 2+ years of experience as a Business Analyst, preferably within healthcare, healthcare services, or revenue cycle management\n\n - Working knowledge of healthcare revenue cycle processes, including billing, coding, claims, payment posting, and AR\n\n - Experience gathering, documenting, and analyzing business requirements\n\n - Strong process mapping and workflow analysis skills\n\n - Strong Excel and data analysis skills\n\n - Ability to translate complex operational needs into clear, actionable requirements\n\n - Strong communication and stakeholder management skills\n\n - Analytical and problem-solving mindset with strong attention to detail\n\n - Ability to manage multiple priorities and work independently in a remote environment\n\n - HIPAA-compliant private workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with healthcare RCM or practice management systems\n\n - Experience with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or similar healthcare platforms\n\n - SQL, Power BI, or other data analysis skills\n\n - Experience with process improvement methodologies such as Lean or Six Sigma\n\n - Experience supporting software implementations or system enhancements\n\n - Experience working with provider groups or hospitals\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare business analysis expertise.\n\nBenefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nRaventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"96919dac-26ea-4e86-987e-8381a37b0578","title":"Healthcare Data Analyst","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-31T11:14:44.389+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/96919dac-26ea-4e86-987e-8381a37b0578","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/96919dac-26ea-4e86-987e-8381a37b0578/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raventra Health</strong> is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Healthcare Data Analyst, you will analyze healthcare and revenue cycle data to identify trends, performance gaps, and opportunities for improvement. You will work with operational and client-facing teams to turn complex data into clear insights that support better financial and operational outcomes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analyze healthcare and revenue cycle data from billing, claims, payment, and accounts receivable systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor key performance indicators such as collections, denial rates, claim volumes, reimbursement, and AR aging</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify trends, anomalies, and performance gaps across client accounts and operational workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain analytical reports and dashboards for internal and client-facing teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Investigate data discrepancies and work with relevant teams to validate and resolve data issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate analytical findings into clear insights and actionable recommendations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support client performance reviews with data analysis and relevant metrics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct ad hoc analysis to answer operational and business questions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with billing, coding, claims, AR, and client success teams on data-driven improvement initiatives</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in data analysis, healthcare analytics, revenue cycle analytics, or a related analytical role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with healthcare, financial, or operational datasets</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong Excel skills, including pivot tables, lookups, formulas, and data analysis</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with reporting or business intelligence tools such as Power BI or Tableau</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of healthcare revenue cycle processes and related performance metrics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with excellent attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to communicate complex findings clearly to both technical and non-technical stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to manage multiple analytical requests and meet deadlines in a remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIPAA-compliant private workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">SQL experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or another healthcare system</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare RCM or medical billing experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience analyzing claims, reimbursement, denials, or collections data</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience preparing client-facing reports or presentations</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare analytics expertise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Raventra Health is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Healthcare Data Analyst, you will analyze healthcare and revenue cycle data to identify trends, performance gaps, and opportunities for improvement. You will work with operational and client-facing teams to turn complex data into clear insights that support better financial and operational outcomes.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Analyze healthcare and revenue cycle data from billing, claims, payment, and accounts receivable systems\n\n - Monitor key performance indicators such as collections, denial rates, claim volumes, reimbursement, and AR aging\n\n - Identify trends, anomalies, and performance gaps across client accounts and operational workflows\n\n - Build and maintain analytical reports and dashboards for internal and client-facing teams\n\n - Investigate data discrepancies and work with relevant teams to validate and resolve data issues\n\n - Translate analytical findings into clear insights and actionable recommendations\n\n - Support client performance reviews with data analysis and relevant metrics\n\n - Conduct ad hoc analysis to answer operational and business questions\n\n - Collaborate with billing, coding, claims, AR, and client success teams on data-driven improvement initiatives\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 2+ years of experience in data analysis, healthcare analytics, revenue cycle analytics, or a related analytical role\n\n - Experience working with healthcare, financial, or operational datasets\n\n - Strong Excel skills, including pivot tables, lookups, formulas, and data analysis\n\n - Experience with reporting or business intelligence tools such as Power BI or Tableau\n\n - Working knowledge of healthcare revenue cycle processes and related performance metrics\n\n - Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with excellent attention to detail\n\n - Ability to communicate complex findings clearly to both technical and non-technical stakeholders\n\n - Ability to manage multiple analytical requests and meet deadlines in a remote environment\n\n - HIPAA-compliant private workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - SQL experience\n\n - Experience with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or another healthcare system\n\n - Healthcare RCM or medical billing experience\n\n - Experience analyzing claims, reimbursement, denials, or collections data\n\n - Experience preparing client-facing reports or presentations\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare analytics expertise.\n\nBenefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nRaventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"d24b51f8-0504-407a-a598-a87ebcaf3e6e","title":"Healthcare Data Entry Specialist","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-31T11:06:56.179+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/d24b51f8-0504-407a-a598-a87ebcaf3e6e","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/d24b51f8-0504-407a-a598-a87ebcaf3e6e/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raventra Health</strong> is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Healthcare Data Entry Specialist, you will accurately enter, update, and maintain patient, insurance, provider, and claims information across healthcare systems. Your attention to detail will help ensure accurate data flows across Raventra’s billing, coding, claims, and revenue cycle operations.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enter and update patient, insurance, provider, and claim information in healthcare systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review source documents to ensure information is complete and accurately entered</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Verify data for accuracy and identify missing, inconsistent, or duplicate information</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Update account and insurance information based on documentation received from provider clients</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enter claim-related information and supporting data according to established procedures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Research and correct data entry errors and discrepancies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate records and follow established data management procedures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support billing, coding, claims, and administrative teams with data-related tasks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Handle protected health information in accordance with HIPAA and company privacy procedures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meet productivity and quality expectations while maintaining a high level of accuracy</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1+ year of experience in data entry, healthcare administration, medical billing, or a related role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and ability to identify errors and inconsistencies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience entering and maintaining information in electronic systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic understanding of medical terminology, insurance information, or healthcare documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong typing and computer skills with proficiency in Microsoft Office</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to follow detailed procedures and maintain consistent data quality</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational skills and ability to manage repetitive tasks accurately</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently and meet deadlines in a remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIPAA-compliant private workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or another healthcare system</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical billing or claims processing experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge of insurance terminology and healthcare revenue cycle processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with provider groups or hospitals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience handling large volumes of healthcare data</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare operations expertise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Raventra Health is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Healthcare Data Entry Specialist, you will accurately enter, update, and maintain patient, insurance, provider, and claims information across healthcare systems. Your attention to detail will help ensure accurate data flows across Raventra’s billing, coding, claims, and revenue cycle operations.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Enter and update patient, insurance, provider, and claim information in healthcare systems\n\n - Review source documents to ensure information is complete and accurately entered\n\n - Verify data for accuracy and identify missing, inconsistent, or duplicate information\n\n - Update account and insurance information based on documentation received from provider clients\n\n - Enter claim-related information and supporting data according to established procedures\n\n - Research and correct data entry errors and discrepancies\n\n - Maintain accurate records and follow established data management procedures\n\n - Support billing, coding, claims, and administrative teams with data-related tasks\n\n - Handle protected health information in accordance with HIPAA and company privacy procedures\n\n - Meet productivity and quality expectations while maintaining a high level of accuracy\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 1+ year of experience in data entry, healthcare administration, medical billing, or a related role\n\n - Strong attention to detail and ability to identify errors and inconsistencies\n\n - Experience entering and maintaining information in electronic systems\n\n - Basic understanding of medical terminology, insurance information, or healthcare documentation\n\n - Strong typing and computer skills with proficiency in Microsoft Office\n\n - Ability to follow detailed procedures and maintain consistent data quality\n\n - Strong organizational skills and ability to manage repetitive tasks accurately\n\n - Ability to work independently and meet deadlines in a remote environment\n\n - HIPAA-compliant private workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or another healthcare system\n\n - Medical billing or claims processing experience\n\n - Knowledge of insurance terminology and healthcare revenue cycle processes\n\n - Experience working with provider groups or hospitals\n\n - Experience handling large volumes of healthcare data\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare operations expertise.\n\nBenefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nRaventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"315d686c-6b25-4fc5-bb9f-2c48f1b0adc3","title":"Healthcare Compliance Specialist","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-31T11:08:08.133+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/315d686c-6b25-4fc5-bb9f-2c48f1b0adc3","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/315d686c-6b25-4fc5-bb9f-2c48f1b0adc3/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raventra Health</strong> is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Healthcare Compliance Specialist, you will help ensure Raventra’s operations follow applicable healthcare privacy, security, billing, and compliance requirements. You will support internal reviews, monitor compliance practices, investigate potential issues, and help teams maintain appropriate standards when handling healthcare information.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor operational activities for compliance with healthcare policies and established procedures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support compliance reviews of billing, coding, claims, and documentation processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review how protected health information is handled and identify potential compliance risks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with internal audits, compliance assessments, and corrective action plans</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Investigate potential compliance issues and document findings and follow-up actions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain compliance policies, procedures, training materials, and related documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track regulatory and policy updates that may affect Raventra’s healthcare operations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide guidance to operational teams on HIPAA, PHI handling, privacy, and compliance requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with management and operational teams to address identified compliance gaps</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in healthcare compliance, healthcare administration, revenue cycle management, or a related field</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of HIPAA, PHI, healthcare privacy, and compliance principles</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting audits, compliance reviews, or internal investigations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of confidentiality and appropriate handling of healthcare information</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and ability to identify potential compliance risks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent documentation, analytical, and organizational skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to communicate compliance requirements clearly to operational teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently and manage multiple priorities in a remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIPAA-compliant private workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CHC, CHPC, or another healthcare compliance certification</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with healthcare billing or coding compliance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge of Medicare and Medicaid requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with internal audits or compliance monitoring programs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with provider groups or hospitals</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare compliance expertise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Raventra Health is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Healthcare Compliance Specialist, you will help ensure Raventra’s operations follow applicable healthcare privacy, security, billing, and compliance requirements. You will support internal reviews, monitor compliance practices, investigate potential issues, and help teams maintain appropriate standards when handling healthcare information.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Monitor operational activities for compliance with healthcare policies and established procedures\n\n - Support compliance reviews of billing, coding, claims, and documentation processes\n\n - Review how protected health information is handled and identify potential compliance risks\n\n - Assist with internal audits, compliance assessments, and corrective action plans\n\n - Investigate potential compliance issues and document findings and follow-up actions\n\n - Maintain compliance policies, procedures, training materials, and related documentation\n\n - Track regulatory and policy updates that may affect Raventra’s healthcare operations\n\n - Provide guidance to operational teams on HIPAA, PHI handling, privacy, and compliance requirements\n\n - Collaborate with management and operational teams to address identified compliance gaps\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 2+ years of experience in healthcare compliance, healthcare administration, revenue cycle management, or a related field\n\n - Working knowledge of HIPAA, PHI, healthcare privacy, and compliance principles\n\n - Experience supporting audits, compliance reviews, or internal investigations\n\n - Strong understanding of confidentiality and appropriate handling of healthcare information\n\n - Strong attention to detail and ability to identify potential compliance risks\n\n - Excellent documentation, analytical, and organizational skills\n\n - Ability to communicate compliance requirements clearly to operational teams\n\n - Ability to work independently and manage multiple priorities in a remote environment\n\n - HIPAA-compliant private workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - CHC, CHPC, or another healthcare compliance certification\n\n - Experience with healthcare billing or coding compliance\n\n - Knowledge of Medicare and Medicaid requirements\n\n - Experience with internal audits or compliance monitoring programs\n\n - Experience working with provider groups or hospitals\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare compliance expertise.\n\nBenefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nRaventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"d459573f-366e-48a3-a913-57b5d204ba9d","title":"Marketing Operations Specialist","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-01T13:51:35.746+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/d459573f-366e-48a3-a913-57b5d204ba9d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/d459573f-366e-48a3-a913-57b5d204ba9d/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Byte&amp;Kite is a digital marketing agency helping clients across a range of industries grow through effective digital marketing. As a Marketing Operations Specialist, you will help build the processes, systems and reporting that keep marketing programmes organised and measurable. You will work across CRM, marketing automation, data and reporting, partnering with strategists and channel specialists to improve campaign execution and data quality.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">WHAT YOU WILL DO</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain and improve marketing processes, workflows and systems across client accounts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support CRM and marketing automation setup, data management and campaign workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain dashboards and recurring marketing reports</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor data quality, tracking and consistency across marketing platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate campaign setup and ensure required tracking and assets are in place</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify process gaps and recommend improvements that make marketing operations more efficient</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with marketing specialists to support lead tracking, attribution and reporting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Document processes, workflows and best practices for internal and client use</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Troubleshoot operational and data issues and coordinate resolution with relevant teams</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in marketing operations, marketing technology, analytics or a related role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organisational and analytical skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with CRM, marketing automation or reporting platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with spreadsheets, dashboards and marketing data</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of lead management, campaign tracking and marketing attribution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and ability to identify data or process inconsistencies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to document processes clearly and improve workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable collaborating with marketing, creative and client-facing teams</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">NICE TO HAVE<br />Agency experience; HubSpot or Salesforce experience; familiarity with GA4 and Google Tag Manager; experience with Looker Studio or similar reporting tools; basic SQL knowledge; and experience with marketing automation platforms.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS<br />Competitive compensation based on experience and qualifications, with the full package discussed during the interview process. Professional development and training opportunities. Fully remote across US time zones, with additional company benefits discussed during the interview process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIRING PROCESS<br />Application review - 30-minute conversation - hiring manager interview - offer. Every applicant receives a response.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">READY TO JOIN BYTE&amp;KITE?<br />If you’re organised, analytical and enjoy improving the systems behind effective marketing, we’d love to hear from you. Apply today and take the next step toward joining the Byte&amp;Kite team.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">EQUAL OPPORTUNITY<br />Byte&amp;Kite is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the process, contact our recruiting team and we will arrange it.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Byte&Kite is a digital marketing agency helping clients across a range of industries grow through effective digital marketing. As a Marketing Operations Specialist, you will help build the processes, systems and reporting that keep marketing programmes organised and measurable. You will work across CRM, marketing automation, data and reporting, partnering with strategists and channel specialists to improve campaign execution and data quality.\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Maintain and improve marketing processes, workflows and systems across client accounts\n\n - Support CRM and marketing automation setup, data management and campaign workflows\n\n - Build and maintain dashboards and recurring marketing reports\n\n - Monitor data quality, tracking and consistency across marketing platforms\n\n - Coordinate campaign setup and ensure required tracking and assets are in place\n\n - Identify process gaps and recommend improvements that make marketing operations more efficient\n\n - Work with marketing specialists to support lead tracking, attribution and reporting\n\n - Document processes, workflows and best practices for internal and client use\n\n - Troubleshoot operational and data issues and coordinate resolution with relevant teams\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 2+ years of experience in marketing operations, marketing technology, analytics or a related role\n\n - Strong organisational and analytical skills\n\n - Experience working with CRM, marketing automation or reporting platforms\n\n - Comfortable working with spreadsheets, dashboards and marketing data\n\n - Understanding of lead management, campaign tracking and marketing attribution\n\n - Strong attention to detail and ability to identify data or process inconsistencies\n\n - Ability to document processes clearly and improve workflows\n\n - Comfortable collaborating with marketing, creative and client-facing teams\n\nNICE TO HAVE\nAgency experience; HubSpot or Salesforce experience; familiarity with GA4 and Google Tag Manager; experience with Looker Studio or similar reporting tools; basic SQL knowledge; and experience with marketing automation platforms.\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\nCompetitive compensation based on experience and qualifications, with the full package discussed during the interview process. Professional development and training opportunities. Fully remote across US time zones, with additional company benefits discussed during the interview process.\n\nHIRING PROCESS\nApplication review - 30-minute conversation - hiring manager interview - offer. Every applicant receives a response.\n\nREADY TO JOIN BYTE&KITE?\nIf you’re organised, analytical and enjoy improving the systems behind effective marketing, we’d love to hear from you. Apply today and take the next step toward joining the Byte&Kite team.\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\nByte&Kite is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the process, contact our recruiting team and we will arrange it.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"94579c65-8a53-48b0-98e2-d3e5bf93f3a0","title":"Digital Advertising Specialist","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-01T13:52:46.075+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/94579c65-8a53-48b0-98e2-d3e5bf93f3a0","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/94579c65-8a53-48b0-98e2-d3e5bf93f3a0/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Byte&amp;Kite is a digital marketing agency helping clients across a range of industries grow through effective digital marketing. As a Digital Advertising Specialist, you will plan, launch and optimise paid advertising campaigns across multiple platforms and client accounts. You will work closely with strategists, designers, copywriters and analytics specialists to improve campaign performance and deliver measurable results.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">WHAT YOU WILL DO</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Plan and manage paid advertising campaigns across Google, Meta, LinkedIn and other relevant platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop audience targeting, campaign structures, budgets and testing plans</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor campaign performance and identify opportunities to improve efficiency and conversions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Test ad creative, messaging, audiences and landing pages to improve results</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with designers and copywriters to develop effective advertising assets</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track campaign performance, conversions and return on advertising spend</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Investigate performance changes and recommend data-driven adjustments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare performance reports and communicate key findings to clients</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with other marketing specialists on integrated campaigns</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in digital advertising, paid media or performance marketing</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with platforms such as Google Ads, Meta Ads or LinkedIn Ads</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of audience targeting, campaign structure, bidding and conversion tracking</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing advertising budgets and optimising campaigns against business goals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable analysing campaign data and turning insights into clear actions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of A/B testing and performance measurement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and ability to manage multiple campaigns</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable presenting campaign performance and recommendations to clients</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">NICE TO HAVE<br />Agency experience; B2B or e-commerce advertising; Google Ads certification; experience with GA4 and Google Tag Manager; landing page optimisation; and familiarity with additional advertising platforms.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS<br />Competitive compensation based on experience and qualifications, with the full package discussed during the interview process. Professional development and training opportunities. Fully remote across US time zones, with additional company benefits discussed during the interview process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIRING PROCESS<br />Application review - 30-minute conversation - paid practical exercise - discussion of your work with the team / interview with the manager - offer. Every applicant receives a response.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">READY TO JOIN BYTE&amp;KITE?<br />If you’re analytical, performance-driven and excited to turn advertising spend into measurable business results, we’d love to hear from you. Apply today and take the next step toward joining the Byte&amp;Kite team.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">EQUAL OPPORTUNITY<br />Byte&amp;Kite is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the process, contact our recruiting team and we will arrange it.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Byte&Kite is a digital marketing agency helping clients across a range of industries grow through effective digital marketing. As a Digital Advertising Specialist, you will plan, launch and optimise paid advertising campaigns across multiple platforms and client accounts. You will work closely with strategists, designers, copywriters and analytics specialists to improve campaign performance and deliver measurable results.\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Plan and manage paid advertising campaigns across Google, Meta, LinkedIn and other relevant platforms\n\n - Develop audience targeting, campaign structures, budgets and testing plans\n\n - Monitor campaign performance and identify opportunities to improve efficiency and conversions\n\n - Test ad creative, messaging, audiences and landing pages to improve results\n\n - Work with designers and copywriters to develop effective advertising assets\n\n - Track campaign performance, conversions and return on advertising spend\n\n - Investigate performance changes and recommend data-driven adjustments\n\n - Prepare performance reports and communicate key findings to clients\n\n - Collaborate with other marketing specialists on integrated campaigns\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 2+ years of experience in digital advertising, paid media or performance marketing\n\n - Hands-on experience with platforms such as Google Ads, Meta Ads or LinkedIn Ads\n\n - Strong understanding of audience targeting, campaign structure, bidding and conversion tracking\n\n - Experience managing advertising budgets and optimising campaigns against business goals\n\n - Comfortable analysing campaign data and turning insights into clear actions\n\n - Understanding of A/B testing and performance measurement\n\n - Strong attention to detail and ability to manage multiple campaigns\n\n - Comfortable presenting campaign performance and recommendations to clients\n\nNICE TO HAVE\nAgency experience; B2B or e-commerce advertising; Google Ads certification; experience with GA4 and Google Tag Manager; landing page optimisation; and familiarity with additional advertising platforms.\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\nCompetitive compensation based on experience and qualifications, with the full package discussed during the interview process. Professional development and training opportunities. Fully remote across US time zones, with additional company benefits discussed during the interview process.\n\nHIRING PROCESS\nApplication review - 30-minute conversation - paid practical exercise - discussion of your work with the team / interview with the manager - offer. Every applicant receives a response.\n\nREADY TO JOIN BYTE&KITE?\nIf you’re analytical, performance-driven and excited to turn advertising spend into measurable business results, we’d love to hear from you. Apply today and take the next step toward joining the Byte&Kite team.\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\nByte&Kite is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the process, contact our recruiting team and we will arrange it.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"cef3f861-bae3-4771-8812-b9e9f261de17","title":"Content Marketing Specialist","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-01T13:53:45.144+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/cef3f861-bae3-4771-8812-b9e9f261de17","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/cef3f861-bae3-4771-8812-b9e9f261de17/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Byte&amp;Kite is a digital marketing agency helping clients across a range of industries grow through effective digital marketing. As a Content Marketing Specialist, you will plan and execute content strategies across multiple client accounts, turning business goals and audience insights into useful, engaging content. You will work closely with strategists, SEO specialists, writers, designers and clients to create content that supports brand awareness, organic growth and lead generation.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">WHAT YOU WILL DO</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and coordinate content plans aligned with client goals and marketing strategies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Research audiences, industries, competitors and relevant topics to identify content opportunities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Plan content across blogs, landing pages, case studies, email and other marketing channels</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create content briefs and work with writers and subject-matter experts to develop high-quality content</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with SEO specialists to align content with search intent and organic growth opportunities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review and edit content to ensure accuracy, consistency, quality and brand alignment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track content performance and identify opportunities to improve engagement and conversions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate content production timelines and keep stakeholders aligned on deliverables</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Present content recommendations and performance insights to clients</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in content marketing, digital marketing or a related role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience developing content for business or professional audiences</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of content strategy, audience research and the customer journey</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent writing, editing and communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of SEO and how content supports organic growth</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organisational skills and ability to manage multiple content projects</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with writers, designers, SEO specialists and clients</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analytical mindset with the ability to use performance data to improve content decisions</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">NICE TO HAVE<br />Digital marketing agency experience; B2B or SaaS content experience; familiarity with CMS and SEO tools; experience with email marketing or social content; and knowledge of content analytics and reporting platforms.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS<br />Competitive compensation based on experience and qualifications, with the full package discussed during the interview process. Professional development and training opportunities. Fully remote across US time zones, with additional company benefits discussed during the interview process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIRING PROCESS<br />Application review - 30-minute conversation - practical exercise - discussion of your work with the team / interview with manager - offer. Every applicant receives a response.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">READY TO JOIN BYTE&amp;KITE?<br />If you’re a strategic, organised marketer who enjoys turning ideas into content that delivers measurable results, we’d love to hear from you. Apply today and take the next step toward joining the Byte&amp;Kite team.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">EQUAL OPPORTUNITY<br />Byte&amp;Kite is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the process, contact our recruiting team and we will arrange it.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Byte&Kite is a digital marketing agency helping clients across a range of industries grow through effective digital marketing. As a Content Marketing Specialist, you will plan and execute content strategies across multiple client accounts, turning business goals and audience insights into useful, engaging content. You will work closely with strategists, SEO specialists, writers, designers and clients to create content that supports brand awareness, organic growth and lead generation.\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Develop and coordinate content plans aligned with client goals and marketing strategies\n\n - Research audiences, industries, competitors and relevant topics to identify content opportunities\n\n - Plan content across blogs, landing pages, case studies, email and other marketing channels\n\n - Create content briefs and work with writers and subject-matter experts to develop high-quality content\n\n - Collaborate with SEO specialists to align content with search intent and organic growth opportunities\n\n - Review and edit content to ensure accuracy, consistency, quality and brand alignment\n\n - Track content performance and identify opportunities to improve engagement and conversions\n\n - Coordinate content production timelines and keep stakeholders aligned on deliverables\n\n - Present content recommendations and performance insights to clients\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 2+ years of experience in content marketing, digital marketing or a related role\n\n - Experience developing content for business or professional audiences\n\n - Strong understanding of content strategy, audience research and the customer journey\n\n - Excellent writing, editing and communication skills\n\n - Understanding of SEO and how content supports organic growth\n\n - Strong organisational skills and ability to manage multiple content projects\n\n - Comfortable working with writers, designers, SEO specialists and clients\n\n - Analytical mindset with the ability to use performance data to improve content decisions\n\nNICE TO HAVE\nDigital marketing agency experience; B2B or SaaS content experience; familiarity with CMS and SEO tools; experience with email marketing or social content; and knowledge of content analytics and reporting platforms.\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\nCompetitive compensation based on experience and qualifications, with the full package discussed during the interview process. Professional development and training opportunities. Fully remote across US time zones, with additional company benefits discussed during the interview process.\n\nHIRING PROCESS\nApplication review - 30-minute conversation - practical exercise - discussion of your work with the team / interview with manager - offer. Every applicant receives a response.\n\nREADY TO JOIN BYTE&KITE?\nIf you’re a strategic, organised marketer who enjoys turning ideas into content that delivers measurable results, we’d love to hear from you. Apply today and take the next step toward joining the Byte&Kite team.\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\nByte&Kite is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the process, contact our recruiting team and we will arrange it.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"ac2b6758-301d-43a2-a658-6329686229eb","title":"PPC Coordinator","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-01T13:55:03.351+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/ac2b6758-301d-43a2-a658-6329686229eb","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/ac2b6758-301d-43a2-a658-6329686229eb/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Byte&amp;Kite is a digital marketing agency helping clients across a range of industries grow through effective digital marketing. As a PPC Coordinator, you will support the planning, setup and optimisation of paid search campaigns across multiple client accounts. You will work closely with Paid Media Specialists, strategists, designers and copywriters to keep campaigns organised, accurately implemented and focused on measurable results.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">WHAT YOU WILL DO</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support the setup and management of Google Ads and other paid search campaigns</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct keyword research and help organise campaign structures and targeting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor campaign performance, budgets and key metrics on a regular basis</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with ad copy testing, bid adjustments and campaign optimisation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Check campaigns for tracking, targeting and setup issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare performance reports and highlight important changes or opportunities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate with designers and copywriters on ad creative and landing page assets</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support Paid Media Specialists with campaign research, analysis and client deliverables</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1+ years of experience in PPC, paid search, digital marketing or a related role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic understanding of Google Ads, keywords, bidding, targeting and campaign structure</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with spreadsheets and marketing performance data</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and ability to spot campaign setup or tracking issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analytical mindset and willingness to investigate why performance changes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Organised and able to manage multiple campaigns, tasks and deadlines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear communication skills and ability to work effectively with a wider marketing team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Eagerness to learn and develop deeper paid media expertise</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">NICE TO HAVE<br />Google Ads certification; agency experience; familiarity with Microsoft Advertising or LinkedIn Ads; experience with GA4 or Google Tag Manager; basic understanding of conversion tracking; and experience with reporting or dashboard tools.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS<br />Competitive compensation based on experience and qualifications, with the full package discussed during the interview process. Professional development and training opportunities. Fully remote across US time zones, with additional company benefits discussed during the interview process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIRING PROCESS<br />Application review - 30-minute conversation - practical exercise - discussion of your work with the team / interview with manager - offer. Every applicant receives a response.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">READY TO JOIN BYTE&amp;KITE?<br />If you’re analytical, detail-oriented and excited to build your career in paid digital marketing, we’d love to hear from you. Apply today and take the next step toward joining the Byte&amp;Kite team.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">EQUAL OPPORTUNITY<br />Byte&amp;Kite is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the process, contact our recruiting team and we will arrange it.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Byte&Kite is a digital marketing agency helping clients across a range of industries grow through effective digital marketing. As a PPC Coordinator, you will support the planning, setup and optimisation of paid search campaigns across multiple client accounts. You will work closely with Paid Media Specialists, strategists, designers and copywriters to keep campaigns organised, accurately implemented and focused on measurable results.\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Support the setup and management of Google Ads and other paid search campaigns\n\n - Conduct keyword research and help organise campaign structures and targeting\n\n - Monitor campaign performance, budgets and key metrics on a regular basis\n\n - Assist with ad copy testing, bid adjustments and campaign optimisation\n\n - Check campaigns for tracking, targeting and setup issues\n\n - Prepare performance reports and highlight important changes or opportunities\n\n - Coordinate with designers and copywriters on ad creative and landing page assets\n\n - Support Paid Media Specialists with campaign research, analysis and client deliverables\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 1+ years of experience in PPC, paid search, digital marketing or a related role\n\n - Basic understanding of Google Ads, keywords, bidding, targeting and campaign structure\n\n - Comfortable working with spreadsheets and marketing performance data\n\n - Strong attention to detail and ability to spot campaign setup or tracking issues\n\n - Analytical mindset and willingness to investigate why performance changes\n\n - Organised and able to manage multiple campaigns, tasks and deadlines\n\n - Clear communication skills and ability to work effectively with a wider marketing team\n\n - Eagerness to learn and develop deeper paid media expertise\n\nNICE TO HAVE\nGoogle Ads certification; agency experience; familiarity with Microsoft Advertising or LinkedIn Ads; experience with GA4 or Google Tag Manager; basic understanding of conversion tracking; and experience with reporting or dashboard tools.\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\nCompetitive compensation based on experience and qualifications, with the full package discussed during the interview process. Professional development and training opportunities. Fully remote across US time zones, with additional company benefits discussed during the interview process.\n\nHIRING PROCESS\nApplication review - 30-minute conversation - practical exercise - discussion of your work with the team / interview with manager - offer. Every applicant receives a response.\n\nREADY TO JOIN BYTE&KITE?\nIf you’re analytical, detail-oriented and excited to build your career in paid digital marketing, we’d love to hear from you. Apply today and take the next step toward joining the Byte&Kite team.\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\nByte&Kite is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the process, contact our recruiting team and we will arrange it.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"0e60eb41-94cb-417d-a128-6bf87a243366","title":"Account Coordinator","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-01T13:56:04.965+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/0e60eb41-94cb-417d-a128-6bf87a243366","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/0e60eb41-94cb-417d-a128-6bf87a243366/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Byte&amp;Kite is a digital marketing agency helping clients across a range of industries grow through effective digital marketing. As an Account Coordinator, you will support the management of client accounts and help keep communication, deliverables and priorities organised. You will work closely with Account Managers and marketing specialists to ensure client needs are understood, projects stay on track and commitments are followed through.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">WHAT YOU WILL DO</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support Account Managers with day-to-day client communication and account coordination</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track client requests, deliverables, deadlines and approvals across multiple accounts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate with internal marketing teams to keep client work moving on schedule</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare meeting notes, status updates, reports and presentation materials</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow up on outstanding tasks and approvals with clients and internal teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help maintain accurate account information, project documentation and client records</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with preparing client meetings and quarterly business reviews</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify potential issues or delays and raise them with the Account Manager early</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1+ years of experience in account coordination, customer service, marketing or a related role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organisation and ability to manage multiple priorities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear, professional written and verbal communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable communicating with clients and following up on requests</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and ability to keep accurate records</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactive approach to identifying issues and next steps</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with spreadsheets, presentations, CRM and project management tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Interest in digital marketing and willingness to learn different marketing channels</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">NICE TO HAVE<br />Digital marketing agency experience; B2B client experience; familiarity with SEO, paid media, content or social media; experience with HubSpot or similar CRM platforms; and experience with project management tools such as Asana, ClickUp or <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Monday.com\">Monday.com</a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS<br />Competitive compensation based on experience and qualifications, with the full package discussed during the interview process. Professional development and training opportunities. Fully remote across US time zones, with additional company benefits discussed during the interview process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIRING PROCESS<br />Application review - 30-minute conversation - hiring manager interview - offer. Every applicant receives a response.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">READY TO JOIN BYTE&amp;KITE?<br />If you’re organised, proactive and enjoy working with people and keeping projects moving, we’d love to hear from you. Apply today and take the next step toward joining the Byte&amp;Kite team.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">EQUAL OPPORTUNITY<br />Byte&amp;Kite is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the process, contact our recruiting team and we will arrange it.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Byte&Kite is a digital marketing agency helping clients across a range of industries grow through effective digital marketing. As an Account Coordinator, you will support the management of client accounts and help keep communication, deliverables and priorities organised. You will work closely with Account Managers and marketing specialists to ensure client needs are understood, projects stay on track and commitments are followed through.\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Support Account Managers with day-to-day client communication and account coordination\n\n - Track client requests, deliverables, deadlines and approvals across multiple accounts\n\n - Coordinate with internal marketing teams to keep client work moving on schedule\n\n - Prepare meeting notes, status updates, reports and presentation materials\n\n - Follow up on outstanding tasks and approvals with clients and internal teams\n\n - Help maintain accurate account information, project documentation and client records\n\n - Assist with preparing client meetings and quarterly business reviews\n\n - Identify potential issues or delays and raise them with the Account Manager early\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 1+ years of experience in account coordination, customer service, marketing or a related role\n\n - Strong organisation and ability to manage multiple priorities\n\n - Clear, professional written and verbal communication skills\n\n - Comfortable communicating with clients and following up on requests\n\n - Strong attention to detail and ability to keep accurate records\n\n - Proactive approach to identifying issues and next steps\n\n - Comfortable working with spreadsheets, presentations, CRM and project management tools\n\n - Interest in digital marketing and willingness to learn different marketing channels\n\nNICE TO HAVE\nDigital marketing agency experience; B2B client experience; familiarity with SEO, paid media, content or social media; experience with HubSpot or similar CRM platforms; and experience with project management tools such as Asana, ClickUp or Monday.com http://Monday.com.\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\nCompetitive compensation based on experience and qualifications, with the full package discussed during the interview process. Professional development and training opportunities. Fully remote across US time zones, with additional company benefits discussed during the interview process.\n\nHIRING PROCESS\nApplication review - 30-minute conversation - hiring manager interview - offer. Every applicant receives a response.\n\nREADY TO JOIN BYTE&KITE?\nIf you’re organised, proactive and enjoy working with people and keeping projects moving, we’d love to hear from you. Apply today and take the next step toward joining the Byte&Kite team.\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\nByte&Kite is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the process, contact our recruiting team and we will arrange it.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"42c9e71b-63ca-4b92-94e1-c93f3c9c5427","title":"Marketing Assistant","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-01T13:57:01.886+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/42c9e71b-63ca-4b92-94e1-c93f3c9c5427","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/42c9e71b-63ca-4b92-94e1-c93f3c9c5427/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Byte&amp;Kite is a digital marketing agency helping clients across a range of industries grow through effective digital marketing. As a Marketing Assistant, you will support the day-to-day execution of marketing campaigns across multiple client accounts. You will work with strategists, project managers, designers, writers and channel specialists to keep marketing activities organised, timely and aligned with client goals.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">WHAT YOU WILL DO</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support the planning and execution of digital marketing campaigns across client accounts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help coordinate content, creative assets and campaign materials across different channels</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain campaign calendars, task lists and project documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with preparing client reports, presentations and marketing updates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct basic research on audiences, competitors, industries and marketing trends</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help monitor campaign performance and maintain accurate marketing data</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow up on outstanding tasks, approvals and deliverables with internal teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support marketing team members with day-to-day administrative and coordination tasks</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">0–2 years of experience in marketing, communications, administration or a related field</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organisation and time-management skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and verbal communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to manage multiple tasks and meet deadlines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and willingness to learn</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with spreadsheets, presentation tools and digital platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic understanding of digital marketing channels such as social media, email, SEO and paid advertising</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactive, dependable and comfortable working as part of a remote team</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">NICE TO HAVE<br />Internship or academic experience in marketing; familiarity with tools such as Canva, Google Analytics, HubSpot or similar platforms; social media experience; and basic knowledge of content creation or marketing analytics.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS<br />Competitive compensation based on experience and qualifications, with the full package discussed during the interview process. Professional development and training opportunities. Fully remote across US time zones, with additional company benefits discussed during the interview process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIRING PROCESS<br />Application review - 30-minute conversation - hiring manager interview - offer. Every applicant receives a response.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">READY TO JOIN BYTE&amp;KITE?<br />If you’re organised, curious and excited to start or grow your career in digital marketing, we’d love to hear from you. Apply today and take the next step toward joining the Byte&amp;Kite team.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">EQUAL OPPORTUNITY<br />Byte&amp;Kite is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the process, contact our recruiting team and we will arrange it.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Byte&Kite is a digital marketing agency helping clients across a range of industries grow through effective digital marketing. As a Marketing Assistant, you will support the day-to-day execution of marketing campaigns across multiple client accounts. You will work with strategists, project managers, designers, writers and channel specialists to keep marketing activities organised, timely and aligned with client goals.\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Support the planning and execution of digital marketing campaigns across client accounts\n\n - Help coordinate content, creative assets and campaign materials across different channels\n\n - Maintain campaign calendars, task lists and project documentation\n\n - Assist with preparing client reports, presentations and marketing updates\n\n - Conduct basic research on audiences, competitors, industries and marketing trends\n\n - Help monitor campaign performance and maintain accurate marketing data\n\n - Follow up on outstanding tasks, approvals and deliverables with internal teams\n\n - Support marketing team members with day-to-day administrative and coordination tasks\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 0–2 years of experience in marketing, communications, administration or a related field\n\n - Strong organisation and time-management skills\n\n - Excellent written and verbal communication skills\n\n - Ability to manage multiple tasks and meet deadlines\n\n - Strong attention to detail and willingness to learn\n\n - Comfortable working with spreadsheets, presentation tools and digital platforms\n\n - Basic understanding of digital marketing channels such as social media, email, SEO and paid advertising\n\n - Proactive, dependable and comfortable working as part of a remote team\n\nNICE TO HAVE\nInternship or academic experience in marketing; familiarity with tools such as Canva, Google Analytics, HubSpot or similar platforms; social media experience; and basic knowledge of content creation or marketing analytics.\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\nCompetitive compensation based on experience and qualifications, with the full package discussed during the interview process. Professional development and training opportunities. Fully remote across US time zones, with additional company benefits discussed during the interview process.\n\nHIRING PROCESS\nApplication review - 30-minute conversation - hiring manager interview - offer. Every applicant receives a response.\n\nREADY TO JOIN BYTE&KITE?\nIf you’re organised, curious and excited to start or grow your career in digital marketing, we’d love to hear from you. Apply today and take the next step toward joining the Byte&Kite team.\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\nByte&Kite is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the process, contact our recruiting team and we will arrange it.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"104e6d13-a72f-466a-a7c8-7ab07aeada80","title":"Marketing Coordinator","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-01T13:58:01.753+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/104e6d13-a72f-466a-a7c8-7ab07aeada80","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/104e6d13-a72f-466a-a7c8-7ab07aeada80/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Byte&amp;Kite is a digital marketing agency helping clients across a range of industries grow through effective digital marketing. As a Marketing Coordinator, you will support the planning and execution of marketing campaigns across multiple client accounts. You will work closely with project managers, strategists, designers, writers and channel specialists to keep campaigns organised, deliverables on track and communication clear.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">WHAT YOU WILL DO</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate marketing campaigns, deliverables and timelines across multiple client accounts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support the creation and maintenance of campaign calendars, briefs and project documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with internal teams to make sure tasks, deadlines and priorities are clearly communicated</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with preparing client reports, presentations and campaign updates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate content, creative and digital assets across marketing channels</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track project progress and follow up on outstanding actions or approvals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support campaign launches by checking that required materials and information are ready</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help maintain organised client files, marketing materials and internal documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with basic performance tracking and reporting across campaigns</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1+ years of experience in marketing, project coordination, administration or a related role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organisation and time-management skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to manage multiple tasks and deadlines without losing attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear written and verbal communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with cross-functional teams and following up on deliverables</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with common digital marketing channels and campaign workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Confident using spreadsheets, presentation tools and project management platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactive approach to identifying missing information, blockers or next steps</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">NICE TO HAVE<br />Digital marketing agency experience; familiarity with SEO, paid media, email or social media campaigns; experience with tools such as Asana, ClickUp, <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Monday.com\">Monday.com</a> or similar; CRM experience; and basic knowledge of marketing analytics.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS<br />Competitive compensation based on experience and qualifications, with the full package discussed during the interview process. Professional development and training opportunities. Fully remote across US time zones, with additional company benefits discussed during the interview process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIRING PROCESS<br />Application review - 30-minute conversation - hiring manager interview - offer. Every applicant receives a response.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">READY TO JOIN BYTE&amp;KITE?<br />If you’re organised, proactive and excited to build your career in digital marketing, we’d love to hear from you. Apply today and tell us why you’d be a great addition to the Byte&amp;Kite team.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">EQUAL OPPORTUNITY<br />Byte&amp;Kite is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the process, contact our recruiting team and we will arrange it.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Byte&Kite is a digital marketing agency helping clients across a range of industries grow through effective digital marketing. As a Marketing Coordinator, you will support the planning and execution of marketing campaigns across multiple client accounts. You will work closely with project managers, strategists, designers, writers and channel specialists to keep campaigns organised, deliverables on track and communication clear.\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Coordinate marketing campaigns, deliverables and timelines across multiple client accounts\n\n - Support the creation and maintenance of campaign calendars, briefs and project documentation\n\n - Work with internal teams to make sure tasks, deadlines and priorities are clearly communicated\n\n - Assist with preparing client reports, presentations and campaign updates\n\n - Coordinate content, creative and digital assets across marketing channels\n\n - Track project progress and follow up on outstanding actions or approvals\n\n - Support campaign launches by checking that required materials and information are ready\n\n - Help maintain organised client files, marketing materials and internal documentation\n\n - Assist with basic performance tracking and reporting across campaigns\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 1+ years of experience in marketing, project coordination, administration or a related role\n\n - Strong organisation and time-management skills\n\n - Ability to manage multiple tasks and deadlines without losing attention to detail\n\n - Clear written and verbal communication skills\n\n - Comfortable working with cross-functional teams and following up on deliverables\n\n - Familiarity with common digital marketing channels and campaign workflows\n\n - Confident using spreadsheets, presentation tools and project management platforms\n\n - Proactive approach to identifying missing information, blockers or next steps\n\nNICE TO HAVE\nDigital marketing agency experience; familiarity with SEO, paid media, email or social media campaigns; experience with tools such as Asana, ClickUp, Monday.com http://Monday.com or similar; CRM experience; and basic knowledge of marketing analytics.\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\nCompetitive compensation based on experience and qualifications, with the full package discussed during the interview process. Professional development and training opportunities. Fully remote across US time zones, with additional company benefits discussed during the interview process.\n\nHIRING PROCESS\nApplication review - 30-minute conversation - hiring manager interview - offer. Every applicant receives a response.\n\nREADY TO JOIN BYTE&KITE?\nIf you’re organised, proactive and excited to build your career in digital marketing, we’d love to hear from you. Apply today and tell us why you’d be a great addition to the Byte&Kite team.\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\nByte&Kite is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the process, contact our recruiting team and we will arrange it.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"e1c8712b-6499-40e0-932a-aba0a2adfcd9","title":"IT Support Specialist — Entry Level","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-02T15:21:11.027+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/e1c8712b-6499-40e0-932a-aba0a2adfcd9","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/e1c8712b-6499-40e0-932a-aba0a2adfcd9/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for an Entry-Level IT Support Specialist to help our team resolve day-to-day technical issues and keep employees productive in a remote working environment. You will provide first-line technical support, troubleshoot common hardware and software issues, manage support requests, and help maintain clear internal IT documentation.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is designed for someone who enjoys solving technical problems, helping others, and building their IT skills in a growing technology company.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide first-line technical support to employees</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Respond to IT support requests and troubleshoot common issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with software, account, access, and connectivity problems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support employee onboarding and offboarding from an IT perspective</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help configure and troubleshoot laptops, peripherals, and other workplace technology</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage and document support requests and their resolution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Escalate more complex technical issues to the appropriate team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain internal IT documentation and troubleshooting guides</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help manage software access, user accounts, and basic permissions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support routine software and device setup</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify recurring technical issues and suggest improvements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help maintain an organized and reliable remote IT environment</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">0–2 years of experience in IT support, technical support, help desk, or a related role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic understanding of computers, operating systems, networks, and common software</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong troubleshooting and problem-solving skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Patient and service-oriented approach to supporting users</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written and verbal English communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to explain technical issues clearly to non-technical users</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good organizational skills and attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Willingness to learn and take ownership of issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working independently in a remote environment</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CompTIA A+, Google IT Support, or similar certification</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Windows and macOS</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with Microsoft 365 or Google Workspace</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Jira, Zendesk, or other ticketing systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic understanding of identity and access management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with remote-support tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous experience supporting a remote or distributed team</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$48,000–$62,000 annually</strong>, depending on experience, qualifications, and overall fit for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → practical discussion → conversation with the team/manager → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.</p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please let us know and we will work with you to make the process accessible.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 48,000 - 62,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"CerebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.\n\n \n\nWe are looking for an Entry-Level IT Support Specialist to help our team resolve day-to-day technical issues and keep employees productive in a remote working environment. You will provide first-line technical support, troubleshoot common hardware and software issues, manage support requests, and help maintain clear internal IT documentation.\n\n \n\nThis role is designed for someone who enjoys solving technical problems, helping others, and building their IT skills in a growing technology company.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Provide first-line technical support to employees\n\n - Respond to IT support requests and troubleshoot common issues\n\n - Assist with software, account, access, and connectivity problems\n\n - Support employee onboarding and offboarding from an IT perspective\n\n - Help configure and troubleshoot laptops, peripherals, and other workplace technology\n\n - Manage and document support requests and their resolution\n\n - Escalate more complex technical issues to the appropriate team\n\n - Maintain internal IT documentation and troubleshooting guides\n\n - Help manage software access, user accounts, and basic permissions\n\n - Support routine software and device setup\n\n - Identify recurring technical issues and suggest improvements\n\n - Help maintain an organized and reliable remote IT environment\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 0–2 years of experience in IT support, technical support, help desk, or a related role\n\n - Basic understanding of computers, operating systems, networks, and common software\n\n - Strong troubleshooting and problem-solving skills\n\n - Patient and service-oriented approach to supporting users\n\n - Strong written and verbal English communication skills\n\n - Ability to explain technical issues clearly to non-technical users\n\n - Good organizational skills and attention to detail\n\n - Willingness to learn and take ownership of issues\n\n - Comfortable working independently in a remote environment\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - CompTIA A+, Google IT Support, or similar certification\n\n - Experience with Windows and macOS\n\n - Familiarity with Microsoft 365 or Google Workspace\n\n - Experience with Jira, Zendesk, or other ticketing systems\n\n - Basic understanding of identity and access management\n\n - Familiarity with remote-support tools\n\n - Previous experience supporting a remote or distributed team\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\n$48,000–$62,000 annually, depending on experience, qualifications, and overall fit for the role.\n\nCerebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → practical discussion → conversation with the team/manager → offer.\n\nWe aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nCerebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.\n\nIf you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please let us know and we will work with you to make the process accessible.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSalary Range: 48,000 - 62,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"a400d376-5cdb-47f9-87b1-ec59c8fea9e6","title":"Reporting Specialist","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-02T15:22:17.929+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/a400d376-5cdb-47f9-87b1-ec59c8fea9e6","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/a400d376-5cdb-47f9-87b1-ec59c8fea9e6/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a Reporting Specialist to help turn business and operational data into clear, reliable reports that support decision-making across the company. You will work with structured data, maintain recurring reports and dashboards, investigate inconsistencies, and collaborate with Data, Product, and Operations teams.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is a good fit for someone who enjoys working with data and reporting but also wants to understand the business questions behind the numbers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare and maintain recurring business and operational reports</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collect, organize, and validate data from multiple sources</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and update dashboards, spreadsheets, and reporting materials</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor reporting accuracy and investigate data discrepancies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analyse trends and changes in key business metrics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with stakeholders to understand reporting requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate business questions into clear reporting requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Document reporting processes, definitions, and data sources</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support ad hoc analysis and reporting requests</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with Data, Product, Engineering, and Operations teams to resolve reporting issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify opportunities to improve reporting processes and automation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Present findings and key information in a clear, easy-to-understand format</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1+ year of experience in reporting, data analysis, business operations, or a similar role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical and problem-solving skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with spreadsheets and structured data</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and data accuracy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to explain data and findings clearly to non-technical stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written and verbal English communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Organized approach to managing recurring and ad hoc requests</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working independently in a remote environment</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with SaaS or technology companies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Excel or Google Sheets, including formulas and pivot tables</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with SQL</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Power BI, Tableau, Looker, or similar BI tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience creating dashboards or KPI reports</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with Jira, Confluence, or similar tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with analytics or business intelligence products</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$55,000–$72,000 annually</strong>, depending on experience, qualifications, and overall fit for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → practical discussion → conversation with the team/manager → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.</p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please let us know and we will work with you to make the process accessible.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 55,000 - 72,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"CerebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.\n\n \n\nWe are looking for a Reporting Specialist to help turn business and operational data into clear, reliable reports that support decision-making across the company. You will work with structured data, maintain recurring reports and dashboards, investigate inconsistencies, and collaborate with Data, Product, and Operations teams.\n\n \n\nThis role is a good fit for someone who enjoys working with data and reporting but also wants to understand the business questions behind the numbers.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Prepare and maintain recurring business and operational reports\n\n - Collect, organize, and validate data from multiple sources\n\n - Build and update dashboards, spreadsheets, and reporting materials\n\n - Monitor reporting accuracy and investigate data discrepancies\n\n - Analyse trends and changes in key business metrics\n\n - Work with stakeholders to understand reporting requirements\n\n - Translate business questions into clear reporting requirements\n\n - Document reporting processes, definitions, and data sources\n\n - Support ad hoc analysis and reporting requests\n\n - Collaborate with Data, Product, Engineering, and Operations teams to resolve reporting issues\n\n - Identify opportunities to improve reporting processes and automation\n\n - Present findings and key information in a clear, easy-to-understand format\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 1+ year of experience in reporting, data analysis, business operations, or a similar role\n\n - Strong analytical and problem-solving skills\n\n - Comfortable working with spreadsheets and structured data\n\n - Strong attention to detail and data accuracy\n\n - Ability to explain data and findings clearly to non-technical stakeholders\n\n - Strong written and verbal English communication skills\n\n - Organized approach to managing recurring and ad hoc requests\n\n - Comfortable working independently in a remote environment\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience working with SaaS or technology companies\n\n - Experience with Excel or Google Sheets, including formulas and pivot tables\n\n - Familiarity with SQL\n\n - Experience with Power BI, Tableau, Looker, or similar BI tools\n\n - Experience creating dashboards or KPI reports\n\n - Familiarity with Jira, Confluence, or similar tools\n\n - Experience working with analytics or business intelligence products\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\n$55,000–$72,000 annually, depending on experience, qualifications, and overall fit for the role.\n\nCerebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → practical discussion → conversation with the team/manager → offer.\n\nWe aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nCerebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.\n\nIf you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please let us know and we will work with you to make the process accessible.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSalary Range: 55,000 - 72,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"62a8d14a-91eb-492c-b441-43f73f29e6cc","title":"Data Operations Specialist","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-02T15:23:27.981+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/62a8d14a-91eb-492c-b441-43f73f29e6cc","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/62a8d14a-91eb-492c-b441-43f73f29e6cc/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a Data Operations Specialist to help maintain the quality, accuracy, and consistency of the data supporting our products and internal operations. You will work with data workflows, investigate inconsistencies, maintain records, and collaborate with Data, Product, Engineering, and Operations teams to keep information reliable and useful.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is a strong fit for someone who is analytical and detail-oriented but enjoys practical, operational work with data rather than purely analytical or software development tasks.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Process, review, and maintain operational and product-related data</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Perform regular data quality checks and identify inconsistencies or missing information</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Investigate data issues and coordinate resolution with relevant teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain data records, spreadsheets, documentation, and operational trackers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support recurring data imports, updates, and validation processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor data workflows and flag errors or unusual results</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare routine reports and data summaries for internal teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help document data processes, business rules, and standard procedures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with Data, Product, Engineering, and Operations teams to resolve data-related issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify opportunities to improve data accuracy and operational workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support testing and validation of changes that affect data processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help establish and maintain consistent data-handling practices</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1+ year of experience in data operations, data entry, reporting, business operations, or a similar role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and data accuracy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with spreadsheets and structured data</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical and problem-solving skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good written and verbal English communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to identify discrepancies and investigate their causes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Organized approach to repetitive and detail-oriented tasks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working independently in a remote environment</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with SaaS or technology products</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with SQL or basic database concepts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Excel or Google Sheets, including formulas and data validation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Jira, Confluence, or similar tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with data quality, reporting, or business intelligence tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with APIs, data imports, or integrations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous experience supporting analytics or data teams</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$55,000–$72,000 annually</strong>, depending on experience, qualifications, and overall fit for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → practical discussion → conversation with the team/manager → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.</p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please let us know and we will work with you to make the process accessible.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 55,000 - 72,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"CerebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.\n\n \n\nWe are looking for a Data Operations Specialist to help maintain the quality, accuracy, and consistency of the data supporting our products and internal operations. You will work with data workflows, investigate inconsistencies, maintain records, and collaborate with Data, Product, Engineering, and Operations teams to keep information reliable and useful.\n\n \n\nThis role is a strong fit for someone who is analytical and detail-oriented but enjoys practical, operational work with data rather than purely analytical or software development tasks.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Process, review, and maintain operational and product-related data\n\n - Perform regular data quality checks and identify inconsistencies or missing information\n\n - Investigate data issues and coordinate resolution with relevant teams\n\n - Maintain data records, spreadsheets, documentation, and operational trackers\n\n - Support recurring data imports, updates, and validation processes\n\n - Monitor data workflows and flag errors or unusual results\n\n - Prepare routine reports and data summaries for internal teams\n\n - Help document data processes, business rules, and standard procedures\n\n - Work with Data, Product, Engineering, and Operations teams to resolve data-related issues\n\n - Identify opportunities to improve data accuracy and operational workflows\n\n - Support testing and validation of changes that affect data processes\n\n - Help establish and maintain consistent data-handling practices\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 1+ year of experience in data operations, data entry, reporting, business operations, or a similar role\n\n - Strong attention to detail and data accuracy\n\n - Comfortable working with spreadsheets and structured data\n\n - Strong analytical and problem-solving skills\n\n - Good written and verbal English communication skills\n\n - Ability to identify discrepancies and investigate their causes\n\n - Organized approach to repetitive and detail-oriented tasks\n\n - Comfortable working independently in a remote environment\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience working with SaaS or technology products\n\n - Familiarity with SQL or basic database concepts\n\n - Experience with Excel or Google Sheets, including formulas and data validation\n\n - Experience with Jira, Confluence, or similar tools\n\n - Experience with data quality, reporting, or business intelligence tools\n\n - Experience working with APIs, data imports, or integrations\n\n - Previous experience supporting analytics or data teams\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\n$55,000–$72,000 annually, depending on experience, qualifications, and overall fit for the role.\n\nCerebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → practical discussion → conversation with the team/manager → offer.\n\nWe aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nCerebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.\n\nIf you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please let us know and we will work with you to make the process accessible.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSalary Range: 55,000 - 72,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"510102c0-2a26-4260-888b-051ba902feba","title":"Customer Support Representative","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-02T15:24:36.241+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/510102c0-2a26-4260-888b-051ba902feba","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/510102c0-2a26-4260-888b-051ba902feba/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a Customer Support Representative to help our customers get the most value from CerebriOS products. You will respond to customer questions, troubleshoot common issues, document interactions, and work with Product and Technology teams when more complex problems need to be investigated.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a great opportunity for someone who enjoys helping people, solving problems, and learning how software products work.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Respond to customer questions and support requests through available channels</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help customers understand product features, workflows, and best practices</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Troubleshoot common technical and account-related issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Investigate reported problems and determine the appropriate next steps</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Escalate complex issues to Product, Engineering, or other teams when needed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate records of customer interactions and reported issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow up with customers to ensure issues are resolved</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create and update support documentation and frequently asked questions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify recurring customer issues and share feedback with internal teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help identify opportunities to improve the customer experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support customers during product updates and changes</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1+ year of experience in customer service, customer support, technical support, or a similar role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written and verbal English communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Customer-focused and patient approach</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong problem-solving and troubleshooting skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to explain information clearly to non-technical users</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good attention to detail and follow-through</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable learning new software and digital tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently in a remote environment</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting B2B SaaS or software products</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with ticketing or customer support platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic technical troubleshooting experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with Jira, Confluence, or similar tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with analytics or data-related products</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with remote or distributed teams</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$45,000–$62,000 annually</strong>, depending on experience, qualifications, and overall fit for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → practical discussion → conversation with the team/manager → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.</p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please let us know and we will work with you to make the process accessible.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 45,000 - 62,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"CerebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.\n\n \n\nWe are looking for a Customer Support Representative to help our customers get the most value from CerebriOS products. You will respond to customer questions, troubleshoot common issues, document interactions, and work with Product and Technology teams when more complex problems need to be investigated.\n\n \n\nThis is a great opportunity for someone who enjoys helping people, solving problems, and learning how software products work.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Respond to customer questions and support requests through available channels\n\n - Help customers understand product features, workflows, and best practices\n\n - Troubleshoot common technical and account-related issues\n\n - Investigate reported problems and determine the appropriate next steps\n\n - Escalate complex issues to Product, Engineering, or other teams when needed\n\n - Maintain accurate records of customer interactions and reported issues\n\n - Follow up with customers to ensure issues are resolved\n\n - Create and update support documentation and frequently asked questions\n\n - Identify recurring customer issues and share feedback with internal teams\n\n - Help identify opportunities to improve the customer experience\n\n - Support customers during product updates and changes\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 1+ year of experience in customer service, customer support, technical support, or a similar role\n\n - Strong written and verbal English communication skills\n\n - Customer-focused and patient approach\n\n - Strong problem-solving and troubleshooting skills\n\n - Ability to explain information clearly to non-technical users\n\n - Good attention to detail and follow-through\n\n - Comfortable learning new software and digital tools\n\n - Ability to work independently in a remote environment\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience supporting B2B SaaS or software products\n\n - Familiarity with ticketing or customer support platforms\n\n - Basic technical troubleshooting experience\n\n - Experience working with Jira, Confluence, or similar tools\n\n - Experience working with analytics or data-related products\n\n - Experience working with remote or distributed teams\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\n$45,000–$62,000 annually, depending on experience, qualifications, and overall fit for the role.\n\nCerebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → practical discussion → conversation with the team/manager → offer.\n\nWe aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nCerebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.\n\nIf you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please let us know and we will work with you to make the process accessible.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSalary Range: 45,000 - 62,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"88a9cc36-dcf0-4ecc-b3a2-12e2a04dcb6a","title":"Project Coordinator","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-02T15:25:46.137+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/88a9cc36-dcf0-4ecc-b3a2-12e2a04dcb6a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/88a9cc36-dcf0-4ecc-b3a2-12e2a04dcb6a/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a Project Coordinator to help keep projects organized and moving forward across our growing organization. You will support project planning, track tasks and deadlines, coordinate communication between teams, and maintain project documentation.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will work closely with Product, Engineering, Data, Operations, and other teams, helping turn plans into coordinated execution and making sure important details do not get lost along the way.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate day-to-day activities across multiple projects and workstreams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain project plans, task trackers, timelines, and documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track deadlines, dependencies, action items, and project status</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Schedule project meetings and prepare agendas and follow-up notes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate communication between project stakeholders and internal teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow up with task owners and help keep deliverables on schedule</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare project status updates, reports, and presentations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support project planning, kickoff, and review activities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify potential blockers, risks, and dependencies and escalate them when needed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Keep project documentation accurate, organized, and up to date</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help improve project coordination processes and team workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide administrative and coordination support for technology and business initiatives</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1+ year of experience in project coordination, operations, administration, or a similar role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational and time-management skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent attention to detail and follow-through</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written and verbal English communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to coordinate multiple tasks, stakeholders, and deadlines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactive approach to problem-solving and follow-up</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working independently in a remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work effectively with both technical and non-technical teams</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working in a SaaS or technology company</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with Jira, Confluence, Asana, <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Monday.com\">Monday.com</a>, Notion, or similar tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of Agile or Scrum methodologies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting software development or data projects</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic knowledge of project management practices</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with remote or distributed teams</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$55,000–$75,000 annually</strong>, depending on experience, qualifications, and overall fit for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → practical discussion → conversation with the team/manager → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.</p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please let us know and we will work with you to make the process accessible.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 55,000 - 75,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"CerebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.\n\n \n\nWe are looking for a Project Coordinator to help keep projects organized and moving forward across our growing organization. You will support project planning, track tasks and deadlines, coordinate communication between teams, and maintain project documentation.\n\n \n\nYou will work closely with Product, Engineering, Data, Operations, and other teams, helping turn plans into coordinated execution and making sure important details do not get lost along the way.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Coordinate day-to-day activities across multiple projects and workstreams\n\n - Maintain project plans, task trackers, timelines, and documentation\n\n - Track deadlines, dependencies, action items, and project status\n\n - Schedule project meetings and prepare agendas and follow-up notes\n\n - Coordinate communication between project stakeholders and internal teams\n\n - Follow up with task owners and help keep deliverables on schedule\n\n - Prepare project status updates, reports, and presentations\n\n - Support project planning, kickoff, and review activities\n\n - Identify potential blockers, risks, and dependencies and escalate them when needed\n\n - Keep project documentation accurate, organized, and up to date\n\n - Help improve project coordination processes and team workflows\n\n - Provide administrative and coordination support for technology and business initiatives\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 1+ year of experience in project coordination, operations, administration, or a similar role\n\n - Strong organizational and time-management skills\n\n - Excellent attention to detail and follow-through\n\n - Strong written and verbal English communication skills\n\n - Ability to coordinate multiple tasks, stakeholders, and deadlines\n\n - Proactive approach to problem-solving and follow-up\n\n - Comfortable working independently in a remote environment\n\n - Ability to work effectively with both technical and non-technical teams\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience working in a SaaS or technology company\n\n - Familiarity with Jira, Confluence, Asana, Monday.com http://Monday.com, Notion, or similar tools\n\n - Understanding of Agile or Scrum methodologies\n\n - Experience supporting software development or data projects\n\n - Basic knowledge of project management practices\n\n - Experience working with remote or distributed teams\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\n$55,000–$75,000 annually, depending on experience, qualifications, and overall fit for the role.\n\nCerebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → practical discussion → conversation with the team/manager → offer.\n\nWe aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nCerebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.\n\nIf you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please let us know and we will work with you to make the process accessible.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSalary Range: 55,000 - 75,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"213bb659-3324-4661-ba9b-9baf0bc098e6","title":"Administrative Assistant — Technology Team","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-02T15:26:55.574+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/213bb659-3324-4661-ba9b-9baf0bc098e6","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/213bb659-3324-4661-ba9b-9baf0bc098e6/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for an Administrative Assistant to support our Technology team and help keep day-to-day activities organized as CerebriOS grows. You will coordinate meetings, maintain documentation, track requests and follow-ups, and provide administrative support to team members working across Product, Engineering, Data, and other functions.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a practical, hands-on role for someone who is organized, dependable, and comfortable working with technology teams in a remote environment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide day-to-day administrative support to the Technology team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate meetings, calendars, agendas, and follow-ups</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain team documentation, trackers, and internal records</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Organize project materials, presentations, reports, and other documents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track action items, deadlines, and outstanding requests</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate communication between Technology and other internal teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support onboarding and offboarding activities for technology team members</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help organize team meetings, planning sessions, and internal events</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with vendor, software subscription, and administrative requests</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare routine reports, summaries, and status updates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help maintain clear and organized digital files and documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support Technology and company-wide projects as needed</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1+ year of experience in administrative support, coordination, operations, or a similar role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational skills and attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and verbal English communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to manage multiple tasks and deadlines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with technology and learning new tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactive approach to follow-ups and problem-solving</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable and comfortable working independently in a remote environment</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting a technology, SaaS, or software team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with Jira, Confluence, Notion, Asana, or similar tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Google Workspace or Microsoft Office</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience coordinating projects or cross-functional activities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic understanding of Agile or Scrum environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with remote or distributed teams</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$50,000–$68,000 annually</strong>, depending on experience, qualifications, and overall fit for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → practical discussion → conversation with the team/manager → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.</p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please let us know and we will work with you to make the process accessible.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 50,000 - 68,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"CerebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.\n\n \n\nWe are looking for an Administrative Assistant to support our Technology team and help keep day-to-day activities organized as CerebriOS grows. You will coordinate meetings, maintain documentation, track requests and follow-ups, and provide administrative support to team members working across Product, Engineering, Data, and other functions.\n\nThis is a practical, hands-on role for someone who is organized, dependable, and comfortable working with technology teams in a remote environment.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Provide day-to-day administrative support to the Technology team\n\n - Coordinate meetings, calendars, agendas, and follow-ups\n\n - Maintain team documentation, trackers, and internal records\n\n - Organize project materials, presentations, reports, and other documents\n\n - Track action items, deadlines, and outstanding requests\n\n - Coordinate communication between Technology and other internal teams\n\n - Support onboarding and offboarding activities for technology team members\n\n - Help organize team meetings, planning sessions, and internal events\n\n - Assist with vendor, software subscription, and administrative requests\n\n - Prepare routine reports, summaries, and status updates\n\n - Help maintain clear and organized digital files and documentation\n\n - Support Technology and company-wide projects as needed\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 1+ year of experience in administrative support, coordination, operations, or a similar role\n\n - Strong organizational skills and attention to detail\n\n - Excellent written and verbal English communication skills\n\n - Ability to manage multiple tasks and deadlines\n\n - Comfortable working with technology and learning new tools\n\n - Proactive approach to follow-ups and problem-solving\n\n - Reliable and comfortable working independently in a remote environment\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience supporting a technology, SaaS, or software team\n\n - Familiarity with Jira, Confluence, Notion, Asana, or similar tools\n\n - Experience with Google Workspace or Microsoft Office\n\n - Experience coordinating projects or cross-functional activities\n\n - Basic understanding of Agile or Scrum environments\n\n - Experience working with remote or distributed teams\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\n$50,000–$68,000 annually, depending on experience, qualifications, and overall fit for the role.\n\nCerebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → practical discussion → conversation with the team/manager → offer.\n\nWe aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nCerebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.\n\nIf you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please let us know and we will work with you to make the process accessible.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSalary Range: 50,000 - 68,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"fdc944f8-e798-451c-8fe7-7579620dcf24","title":"Business Analyst — Junior/Middle","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-02T15:28:16.137+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/fdc944f8-e798-451c-8fe7-7579620dcf24","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/fdc944f8-e798-451c-8fe7-7579620dcf24/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a Business Analyst to support the development of our new mid-market analytics platform. You will work between business stakeholders, product, engineering, and data teams to understand business needs, translate them into clear requirements, and help ensure that the solutions we build solve the right problems.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is suitable for both junior candidates with strong analytical fundamentals and middle-level Business Analysts ready to take more ownership of requirements and cross-functional initiatives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gather and clarify business requirements from internal stakeholders and users</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate business needs into clear requirements, user stories, and acceptance criteria</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with Product, Engineering, Data, and QA teams throughout the development process</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analyse existing business processes and identify opportunities for improvement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Document workflows, business rules, requirements, and process changes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support backlog refinement and help clarify requirements for development teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analyse data and operational information to support business and product decisions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in stakeholder meetings, discovery sessions, and project discussions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help validate delivered functionality against agreed business requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track open questions, dependencies, and requirement changes throughout projects</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1+ year of experience in business analysis, project coordination, operations, data analysis, or a related role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical and problem-solving skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to translate business needs into clear, structured requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written and verbal English communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good organizational skills and attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with both business and technical teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to manage multiple priorities in a remote environment</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with B2B SaaS or software products</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Jira, Confluence, Notion, or similar tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience writing user stories and acceptance criteria</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic understanding of Agile or Scrum development processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with process mapping or workflow documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic SQL, reporting, or data analysis experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with analytics, reporting, or business intelligence products</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$70,000–$95,000 annually</strong>, depending on experience, qualifications, and overall fit for the role.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → practical discussion → conversation with the team/manager → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.</p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CerebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please let us know and we will work with you to make the process accessible.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 70,000 - 95,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"CerebriOS is a software company building B2B SaaS products that help businesses make better decisions, streamline operations, and get more value from their data. Our products combine practical business workflows with intuitive technology designed for everyday use.\n\nWe are looking for a Business Analyst to support the development of our new mid-market analytics platform. You will work between business stakeholders, product, engineering, and data teams to understand business needs, translate them into clear requirements, and help ensure that the solutions we build solve the right problems.\n\nThis role is suitable for both junior candidates with strong analytical fundamentals and middle-level Business Analysts ready to take more ownership of requirements and cross-functional initiatives.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Gather and clarify business requirements from internal stakeholders and users\n\n - Translate business needs into clear requirements, user stories, and acceptance criteria\n\n - Work closely with Product, Engineering, Data, and QA teams throughout the development process\n\n - Analyse existing business processes and identify opportunities for improvement\n\n - Document workflows, business rules, requirements, and process changes\n\n - Support backlog refinement and help clarify requirements for development teams\n\n - Analyse data and operational information to support business and product decisions\n\n - Participate in stakeholder meetings, discovery sessions, and project discussions\n\n - Help validate delivered functionality against agreed business requirements\n\n - Track open questions, dependencies, and requirement changes throughout projects\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 1+ year of experience in business analysis, project coordination, operations, data analysis, or a related role\n\n - Strong analytical and problem-solving skills\n\n - Ability to translate business needs into clear, structured requirements\n\n - Strong written and verbal English communication skills\n\n - Good organizational skills and attention to detail\n\n - Comfortable working with both business and technical teams\n\n - Ability to manage multiple priorities in a remote environment\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience working with B2B SaaS or software products\n\n - Experience with Jira, Confluence, Notion, or similar tools\n\n - Experience writing user stories and acceptance criteria\n\n - Basic understanding of Agile or Scrum development processes\n\n - Experience with process mapping or workflow documentation\n\n - Basic SQL, reporting, or data analysis experience\n\n - Experience working with analytics, reporting, or business intelligence products\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\n$70,000–$95,000 annually, depending on experience, qualifications, and overall fit for the role.\n\nCerebriOS offers a remote-first working environment, professional development opportunities, and a benefits package designed to support our team. Full details of compensation, benefits, and other employment terms will be discussed during the interview process.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → practical discussion → conversation with the team/manager → offer.\n\nWe aim to keep the process focused and respectful of your time, with clear communication throughout the process.\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nCerebriOS is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.\n\nIf you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please let us know and we will work with you to make the process accessible.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSalary Range: 70,000 - 95,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"d6e46990-ea49-4726-9eac-aaebae7e6dc7","title":"Inventory Clerk","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-03T16:45:28.150+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/d6e46990-ea49-4726-9eac-aaebae7e6dc7","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/d6e46990-ea49-4726-9eac-aaebae7e6dc7/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilgewater Group is a Chicago-based diversified services company founded in 2003. We operate across two core divisions: food service and care.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our food service division manages a network of quick-service and counter-service locations across the greater Chicagoland area, serving thousands of customers every day at high-traffic venues, including commercial districts, transit hubs, and retail centers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>ABOUT THE ROLE</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for an <strong>Inventory Clerk</strong> to help maintain accurate inventory records and support day-to-day inventory administration. You will update inventory information, review records, track changes, and coordinate with internal teams to help ensure locations have the information and supplies they need.</p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enter, update, and maintain inventory information in spreadsheets and internal systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review inventory records and identify missing or inconsistent information</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track inventory changes, orders, and related documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with inventory reconciliation and record updates</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate with internal teams regarding inventory questions or discrepancies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain organized digital inventory records</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support routine inventory and administrative tasks</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous experience in inventory, data entry, administration, operations, or a similar role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and accuracy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with spreadsheets and digital systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good organization and record-keeping skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work with repetitive tasks and maintain consistency</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good communication and follow-up skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working independently in a fully remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable internet connection and workspace</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legally authorized to work in the United States</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous inventory or stock control experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Excel or Google Sheets</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with inventory, order management, or ERP systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in food service, retail, hospitality, or distribution</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$18–$24 per hour</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application Review → Initial Conversation → Interview → Offer</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to providing a workplace free from discrimination and value a diverse team with different backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Bilgewater Group is a Chicago-based diversified services company founded in 2003. We operate across two core divisions: food service and care.\n\nOur food service division manages a network of quick-service and counter-service locations across the greater Chicagoland area, serving thousands of customers every day at high-traffic venues, including commercial districts, transit hubs, and retail centers.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nWe are looking for an Inventory Clerk to help maintain accurate inventory records and support day-to-day inventory administration. You will update inventory information, review records, track changes, and coordinate with internal teams to help ensure locations have the information and supplies they need.\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Enter, update, and maintain inventory information in spreadsheets and internal systems\n\n - Review inventory records and identify missing or inconsistent information\n\n - Track inventory changes, orders, and related documentation\n\n - Assist with inventory reconciliation and record updates\n\n - Communicate with internal teams regarding inventory questions or discrepancies\n\n - Maintain organized digital inventory records\n\n - Support routine inventory and administrative tasks\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - Previous experience in inventory, data entry, administration, operations, or a similar role\n\n - Strong attention to detail and accuracy\n\n - Comfortable working with spreadsheets and digital systems\n\n - Good organization and record-keeping skills\n\n - Ability to work with repetitive tasks and maintain consistency\n\n - Good communication and follow-up skills\n\n - Comfortable working independently in a fully remote environment\n\n - Reliable internet connection and workspace\n\n - Legally authorized to work in the United States\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Previous inventory or stock control experience\n\n - Experience with Excel or Google Sheets\n\n - Experience with inventory, order management, or ERP systems\n\n - Background in food service, retail, hospitality, or distribution\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$18–$24 per hour, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication Review → Initial Conversation → Interview → Offer\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nBilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to providing a workplace free from discrimination and value a diverse team with different backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"586f19c6-a087-420d-bc22-182975fbb048","title":"Accounts Receivable Clerk","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Worldwide","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-03T16:53:09.728+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/586f19c6-a087-420d-bc22-182975fbb048","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/586f19c6-a087-420d-bc22-182975fbb048/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilgewater Group is a Chicago-based diversified services company founded in 2003. We operate across two core divisions: food service and care.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our food service division manages a network of quick-service and counter-service locations across the greater Chicagoland area, serving thousands of customers every day at high-traffic venues, including commercial districts, transit hubs, and retail centers.</p><h2>ABOUT THE ROLE</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for an <strong>Accounts Receivable Clerk</strong> to support day-to-day billing and receivables activities. You will help maintain accurate financial records, process payments, review account information, and follow up on outstanding balances while working closely with internal teams.</p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Process and record customer payments and account transactions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate accounts receivable records</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review invoices, payments, and account information for accuracy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with reconciling customer accounts and identifying discrepancies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow up on outstanding balances and payment questions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain organized financial documentation and records</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support routine billing and accounts receivable tasks</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous experience in accounts receivable, billing, accounting, bookkeeping, or a similar role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and accuracy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with numbers, spreadsheets, and financial records</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good organization and follow-up skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic proficiency with Microsoft Excel or Google Sheets</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to handle confidential financial information professionally</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working independently in a fully remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable internet connection and workspace</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legally authorized to work in the United States</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with accounting or accounts receivable software</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with invoice processing or payment reconciliation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in food service, retail, hospitality, or other multi-location businesses</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$20–$27 per hour</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application Review → Initial Conversation → Interview → Offer</p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to providing a workplace free from discrimination and value a diverse team with different backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Bilgewater Group is a Chicago-based diversified services company founded in 2003. We operate across two core divisions: food service and care.\n\nOur food service division manages a network of quick-service and counter-service locations across the greater Chicagoland area, serving thousands of customers every day at high-traffic venues, including commercial districts, transit hubs, and retail centers.\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nWe are looking for an Accounts Receivable Clerk to support day-to-day billing and receivables activities. You will help maintain accurate financial records, process payments, review account information, and follow up on outstanding balances while working closely with internal teams.\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Process and record customer payments and account transactions\n\n - Maintain accurate accounts receivable records\n\n - Review invoices, payments, and account information for accuracy\n\n - Assist with reconciling customer accounts and identifying discrepancies\n\n - Follow up on outstanding balances and payment questions\n\n - Maintain organized financial documentation and records\n\n - Support routine billing and accounts receivable tasks\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - Previous experience in accounts receivable, billing, accounting, bookkeeping, or a similar role\n\n - Strong attention to detail and accuracy\n\n - Comfortable working with numbers, spreadsheets, and financial records\n\n - Good organization and follow-up skills\n\n - Basic proficiency with Microsoft Excel or Google Sheets\n\n - Ability to handle confidential financial information professionally\n\n - Comfortable working independently in a fully remote environment\n\n - Reliable internet connection and workspace\n\n - Legally authorized to work in the United States\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with accounting or accounts receivable software\n\n - Experience with invoice processing or payment reconciliation\n\n - Background in food service, retail, hospitality, or other multi-location businesses\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$20–$27 per hour, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication Review → Initial Conversation → Interview → Offer\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nBilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to providing a workplace free from discrimination and value a diverse team with different backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"49e2c8e8-3d9c-4806-860d-02b4f41d56bf","title":"Logistics Coordinator","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-03T16:54:31.083+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/49e2c8e8-3d9c-4806-860d-02b4f41d56bf","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/49e2c8e8-3d9c-4806-860d-02b4f41d56bf/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilgewater Group is a Chicago-based diversified services company founded in 2003. We operate across two core divisions: food service and care.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our food service division manages a network of quick-service and counter-service locations across the greater Chicagoland area, serving thousands of customers every day at high-traffic venues, including commercial districts, transit hubs, and retail centers.</p><h2>ABOUT THE ROLE</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a <strong>Logistics Coordinator</strong> to help coordinate day-to-day logistics activities, track orders and deliveries, and keep information flowing between internal teams, locations, and external partners. This role is ideal for someone organized, responsive, and comfortable managing multiple priorities in a remote environment.</p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate orders, deliveries, and routine logistics requests</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track shipments, deliveries, and scheduled activities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate with vendors, locations, and internal teams regarding logistics needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate delivery, order, and logistics records</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow up on delays, missing information, or delivery issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Update spreadsheets and internal systems with logistics information</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support the resolution of routine logistics and scheduling issues</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous experience in logistics, operations, administration, customer service, or a similar role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organization and attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good communication and follow-up skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with spreadsheets and digital systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to manage multiple requests and deadlines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Practical problem-solving skills and a proactive approach</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working independently in a fully remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable internet connection and workspace</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legally authorized to work in the United States</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous logistics or transportation coordination experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with inventory, order management, or scheduling systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in food service, retail, hospitality, or distribution</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$45,000–$60,000 per year</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application Review → Initial Conversation → Interview → Offer</p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to providing a workplace free from discrimination and value a diverse team with different backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 45,000 - 60,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"Bilgewater Group is a Chicago-based diversified services company founded in 2003. We operate across two core divisions: food service and care.\n\nOur food service division manages a network of quick-service and counter-service locations across the greater Chicagoland area, serving thousands of customers every day at high-traffic venues, including commercial districts, transit hubs, and retail centers.\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nWe are looking for a Logistics Coordinator to help coordinate day-to-day logistics activities, track orders and deliveries, and keep information flowing between internal teams, locations, and external partners. This role is ideal for someone organized, responsive, and comfortable managing multiple priorities in a remote environment.\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Coordinate orders, deliveries, and routine logistics requests\n\n - Track shipments, deliveries, and scheduled activities\n\n - Communicate with vendors, locations, and internal teams regarding logistics needs\n\n - Maintain accurate delivery, order, and logistics records\n\n - Follow up on delays, missing information, or delivery issues\n\n - Update spreadsheets and internal systems with logistics information\n\n - Support the resolution of routine logistics and scheduling issues\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - Previous experience in logistics, operations, administration, customer service, or a similar role\n\n - Strong organization and attention to detail\n\n - Good communication and follow-up skills\n\n - Comfortable working with spreadsheets and digital systems\n\n - Ability to manage multiple requests and deadlines\n\n - Practical problem-solving skills and a proactive approach\n\n - Comfortable working independently in a fully remote environment\n\n - Reliable internet connection and workspace\n\n - Legally authorized to work in the United States\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Previous logistics or transportation coordination experience\n\n - Experience with inventory, order management, or scheduling systems\n\n - Experience in food service, retail, hospitality, or distribution\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$45,000–$60,000 per year, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication Review → Initial Conversation → Interview → Offer\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nBilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to providing a workplace free from discrimination and value a diverse team with different backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSalary Range: 45,000 - 60,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"6bd23775-d747-4a7b-b473-f04c1d110221","title":"Sales Representative","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-03T16:55:58.625+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/6bd23775-d747-4a7b-b473-f04c1d110221","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/6bd23775-d747-4a7b-b473-f04c1d110221/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilgewater Group is a Chicago-based diversified services company founded in 2003. We operate across two core divisions: food service and care.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our food service division manages a network of quick-service and counter-service locations across the greater Chicagoland area, serving thousands of customers every day at high-traffic venues, including commercial districts, transit hubs, and retail centers.</p><h2>ABOUT THE ROLE</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a <strong>Sales Representative</strong> to help grow our business by identifying potential customers, building relationships, and supporting the sales process from initial outreach through follow-up. This role is well suited for a motivated communicator who enjoys working with people and achieving results in a remote environment.</p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and contact potential customers through phone, email, and other channels</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Respond to inquiries and provide information about our services</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain relationships with prospective and existing customers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow up on leads and ongoing sales opportunities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate customer and sales information</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate with internal teams to support customer needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Keep track of sales activities and follow-ups</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous experience in sales, customer service, business development, or a similar role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and interpersonal skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Confident and professional approach to customer conversations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good organization and follow-up skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with computers and customer information systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Self-motivated and able to work independently in a remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable internet connection and workspace</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legally authorized to work in the United States</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous remote sales experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with CRM or sales management systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in food service, hospitality, retail, or care environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with outbound sales or lead generation</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$45,000–$60,000 per year</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application Review → Initial Conversation → Interview → Offer</p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to providing a workplace free from discrimination and value a diverse team with different backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 45,000 - 60,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"Bilgewater Group is a Chicago-based diversified services company founded in 2003. We operate across two core divisions: food service and care.\n\nOur food service division manages a network of quick-service and counter-service locations across the greater Chicagoland area, serving thousands of customers every day at high-traffic venues, including commercial districts, transit hubs, and retail centers.\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nWe are looking for a Sales Representative to help grow our business by identifying potential customers, building relationships, and supporting the sales process from initial outreach through follow-up. This role is well suited for a motivated communicator who enjoys working with people and achieving results in a remote environment.\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Identify and contact potential customers through phone, email, and other channels\n\n - Respond to inquiries and provide information about our services\n\n - Build and maintain relationships with prospective and existing customers\n\n - Follow up on leads and ongoing sales opportunities\n\n - Maintain accurate customer and sales information\n\n - Coordinate with internal teams to support customer needs\n\n - Keep track of sales activities and follow-ups\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - Previous experience in sales, customer service, business development, or a similar role\n\n - Strong communication and interpersonal skills\n\n - Confident and professional approach to customer conversations\n\n - Good organization and follow-up skills\n\n - Comfortable working with computers and customer information systems\n\n - Self-motivated and able to work independently in a remote environment\n\n - Reliable internet connection and workspace\n\n - Legally authorized to work in the United States\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Previous remote sales experience\n\n - Experience with CRM or sales management systems\n\n - Experience in food service, hospitality, retail, or care environments\n\n - Experience with outbound sales or lead generation\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$45,000–$60,000 per year, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication Review → Initial Conversation → Interview → Offer\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nBilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to providing a workplace free from discrimination and value a diverse team with different backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSalary Range: 45,000 - 60,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"c506ddb2-e7cf-4971-8406-2d02e5f2d545","title":"Remote Receptionist","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-03T16:57:10.870+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/c506ddb2-e7cf-4971-8406-2d02e5f2d545","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/c506ddb2-e7cf-4971-8406-2d02e5f2d545/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilgewater Group is a Chicago-based diversified services company founded in 2003. We operate across two core divisions: food service and care.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our food service division manages a network of quick-service and counter-service locations across the greater Chicagoland area, serving thousands of customers every day at high-traffic venues, including commercial districts, transit hubs, and retail centers.</p><h2>ABOUT THE ROLE</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a <strong>Remote Receptionist</strong> to serve as a first point of contact for customers, visitors, and internal teams. You will handle incoming calls and messages, provide basic information, route requests to the appropriate team, and support day-to-day administrative tasks.</p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Answer incoming calls, messages, and general inquiries</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide basic information and assistance to customers and other contacts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Direct calls and requests to the appropriate team or location</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Schedule appointments and coordinate basic requests</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain contact information and administrative records</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow up on requests when needed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide general administrative support to the team</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous experience in reception, customer service, administration, hospitality, or a similar role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional and friendly communication style</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organization and attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable handling calls, messages, and multiple requests</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic computer and Microsoft Office or Google Workspace skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable and comfortable working independently in a remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable internet connection and workspace</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legally authorized to work in the United States</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous remote receptionist or virtual receptionist experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with scheduling or appointment management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in food service, hospitality, retail, or care environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilingual communication skills - English / Spanish</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$18–$24 per hour</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application Review → Initial Conversation → Interview → Offer</p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to providing a workplace free from discrimination and value a diverse team with different backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Bilgewater Group is a Chicago-based diversified services company founded in 2003. We operate across two core divisions: food service and care.\n\nOur food service division manages a network of quick-service and counter-service locations across the greater Chicagoland area, serving thousands of customers every day at high-traffic venues, including commercial districts, transit hubs, and retail centers.\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nWe are looking for a Remote Receptionist to serve as a first point of contact for customers, visitors, and internal teams. You will handle incoming calls and messages, provide basic information, route requests to the appropriate team, and support day-to-day administrative tasks.\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Answer incoming calls, messages, and general inquiries\n\n - Provide basic information and assistance to customers and other contacts\n\n - Direct calls and requests to the appropriate team or location\n\n - Schedule appointments and coordinate basic requests\n\n - Maintain contact information and administrative records\n\n - Follow up on requests when needed\n\n - Provide general administrative support to the team\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - Previous experience in reception, customer service, administration, hospitality, or a similar role\n\n - Professional and friendly communication style\n\n - Strong organization and attention to detail\n\n - Comfortable handling calls, messages, and multiple requests\n\n - Basic computer and Microsoft Office or Google Workspace skills\n\n - Reliable and comfortable working independently in a remote environment\n\n - Reliable internet connection and workspace\n\n - Legally authorized to work in the United States\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Previous remote receptionist or virtual receptionist experience\n\n - Experience with scheduling or appointment management\n\n - Experience in food service, hospitality, retail, or care environments\n\n - Bilingual communication skills - English / Spanish\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$18–$24 per hour, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication Review → Initial Conversation → Interview → Offer\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nBilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to providing a workplace free from discrimination and value a diverse team with different backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"c67bf13c-7e2d-4c58-a5c7-918b5d496209","title":"Office Assistant","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-03T16:58:20.262+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/c67bf13c-7e2d-4c58-a5c7-918b5d496209","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/c67bf13c-7e2d-4c58-a5c7-918b5d496209/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilgewater Group is a Chicago-based diversified services company founded in 2003. We operate across two core divisions: food service and care.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our food service division manages a network of quick-service and counter-service locations across the greater Chicagoland area, serving thousands of customers every day at high-traffic venues, including commercial districts, transit hubs, and retail centers.</p><h2>ABOUT THE ROLE</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for an <strong>Office Assistant</strong> to provide day-to-day administrative support and help keep information, documents, and routine requests organized. This is an entry-level-friendly role for someone who is reliable, detail-oriented, and comfortable working independently in a remote environment.</p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support daily administrative tasks and requests</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enter, update, and maintain information in spreadsheets and internal systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Organize digital documents and records</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with scheduling, emails, and routine correspondence</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare basic documents, reports, and internal materials</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow up on outstanding requests and tasks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support managers and team members with general administrative needs</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous experience in an administrative, office, customer service, or similar role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organization and attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable using Microsoft Office or Google Workspace</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good written and verbal communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to manage multiple routine tasks and deadlines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable, self-motivated, and comfortable working independently</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working fully remotely with a reliable internet connection and workspace</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Legally authorized to work in the United States</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous remote administrative experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with scheduling, document management, or spreadsheets</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in food service, hospitality, retail, or care environments</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$18–$24 per hour</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application Review → Initial Conversation → Interview → Offer</p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to providing a workplace free from discrimination and value a diverse team with different backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Bilgewater Group is a Chicago-based diversified services company founded in 2003. We operate across two core divisions: food service and care.\n\nOur food service division manages a network of quick-service and counter-service locations across the greater Chicagoland area, serving thousands of customers every day at high-traffic venues, including commercial districts, transit hubs, and retail centers.\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nWe are looking for an Office Assistant to provide day-to-day administrative support and help keep information, documents, and routine requests organized. This is an entry-level-friendly role for someone who is reliable, detail-oriented, and comfortable working independently in a remote environment.\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Support daily administrative tasks and requests\n\n - Enter, update, and maintain information in spreadsheets and internal systems\n\n - Organize digital documents and records\n\n - Assist with scheduling, emails, and routine correspondence\n\n - Prepare basic documents, reports, and internal materials\n\n - Follow up on outstanding requests and tasks\n\n - Support managers and team members with general administrative needs\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - Previous experience in an administrative, office, customer service, or similar role\n\n - Strong organization and attention to detail\n\n - Comfortable using Microsoft Office or Google Workspace\n\n - Good written and verbal communication skills\n\n - Ability to manage multiple routine tasks and deadlines\n\n - Reliable, self-motivated, and comfortable working independently\n\n - Comfortable working fully remotely with a reliable internet connection and workspace\n\n - Legally authorized to work in the United States\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Previous remote administrative experience\n\n - Experience with scheduling, document management, or spreadsheets\n\n - Experience in food service, hospitality, retail, or care environments\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$18–$24 per hour, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication Review → Initial Conversation → Interview → Offer\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nBilgewater Group is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to providing a workplace free from discrimination and value a diverse team with different backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"8212c05d-1706-49ff-a6c7-038277385b52","title":"Appointment Setter, B2B","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-04T14:11:44.247+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/8212c05d-1706-49ff-a6c7-038277385b52","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/8212c05d-1706-49ff-a6c7-038277385b52/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CareerSwift is a technology company focused on making the job search process simpler, faster, and more effective. Our platform combines AI-powered tools and practical career solutions to help job seekers create stronger applications, improve their professional profiles, and navigate their job search with greater confidence.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are growing our team and are looking for a motivated and confident <strong>Appointment Setter, B2B</strong> to help us connect with potential business clients and create new sales opportunities.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a <strong>B2B Appointment Setter</strong>, you will be responsible for identifying potential business prospects, initiating conversations, and scheduling qualified meetings for the sales team.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will communicate with prospective clients through phone, email, and other digital channels, introduce them to CareerSwift, understand their basic needs, and determine whether there is a potential fit.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a strong opportunity for someone who wants to build a career in B2B sales, business development, or SaaS.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Research and identify potential B2B prospects that may benefit from CareerSwift's solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contact prospects through phone calls, email, LinkedIn, and other appropriate channels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Introduce CareerSwift and communicate the key value of our products and services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ask discovery questions to understand prospect needs and identify potential opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Qualify prospects based on agreed criteria and schedule meetings for the sales team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate prospect information, activity, and follow-up tasks in the CRM.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow up with prospects consistently and help maintain a healthy sales pipeline.</p></li></ul><h2>What We Are Looking For</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong verbal and written communication skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Confident and professional communication style.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Interest in B2B sales, business development, or technology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to handle outreach and conversations with prospective clients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organization and follow-up skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working independently in a remote environment.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous experience in appointment setting, telemarketing, SDR, or sales.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with CRM systems such as HubSpot, Salesforce, or similar tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with LinkedIn prospecting and outbound sales.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Interest in SaaS, AI, or digital products.</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$38,000 - $50,000 per year</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>What We Offer</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fully remote work environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Training and support to help you develop your B2B sales skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with an innovative AI-powered technology product.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunity to work directly with the sales and business development team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborative and supportive environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunities for career growth as CareerSwift expands.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Apply today and start building your B2B sales career with CareerSwift.</strong></p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 38,000 - 50,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"CareerSwift is a technology company focused on making the job search process simpler, faster, and more effective. Our platform combines AI-powered tools and practical career solutions to help job seekers create stronger applications, improve their professional profiles, and navigate their job search with greater confidence.\n\n \n\nWe are growing our team and are looking for a motivated and confident Appointment Setter, B2B to help us connect with potential business clients and create new sales opportunities.\n\n \n\nAs a B2B Appointment Setter, you will be responsible for identifying potential business prospects, initiating conversations, and scheduling qualified meetings for the sales team.\n\nYou will communicate with prospective clients through phone, email, and other digital channels, introduce them to CareerSwift, understand their basic needs, and determine whether there is a potential fit.\n\nThis is a strong opportunity for someone who wants to build a career in B2B sales, business development, or SaaS.\n\n\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Research and identify potential B2B prospects that may benefit from CareerSwift's solutions.\n\n - Contact prospects through phone calls, email, LinkedIn, and other appropriate channels.\n\n - Introduce CareerSwift and communicate the key value of our products and services.\n\n - Ask discovery questions to understand prospect needs and identify potential opportunities.\n\n - Qualify prospects based on agreed criteria and schedule meetings for the sales team.\n\n - Maintain accurate prospect information, activity, and follow-up tasks in the CRM.\n\n - Follow up with prospects consistently and help maintain a healthy sales pipeline.\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - Strong verbal and written communication skills.\n\n - Confident and professional communication style.\n\n - Interest in B2B sales, business development, or technology.\n\n - Ability to handle outreach and conversations with prospective clients.\n\n - Strong organization and follow-up skills.\n\n - Comfortable working independently in a remote environment.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Previous experience in appointment setting, telemarketing, SDR, or sales.\n\n - Experience with CRM systems such as HubSpot, Salesforce, or similar tools.\n\n - Familiarity with LinkedIn prospecting and outbound sales.\n\n - Interest in SaaS, AI, or digital products.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$38,000 - $50,000 per year, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Fully remote work environment.\n\n - Training and support to help you develop your B2B sales skills.\n\n - Experience working with an innovative AI-powered technology product.\n\n - Opportunity to work directly with the sales and business development team.\n\n - Collaborative and supportive environment.\n\n - Opportunities for career growth as CareerSwift expands.\n\nApply today and start building your B2B sales career with CareerSwift.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSalary Range: 38,000 - 50,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"02c2a02d-618b-4346-8b35-4a1467856c16","title":"Social Media Manager","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-04T14:47:31.184+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/02c2a02d-618b-4346-8b35-4a1467856c16","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/02c2a02d-618b-4346-8b35-4a1467856c16/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CareerSwift is a technology company focused on making the job search process simpler, faster, and more effective. Our platform combines AI-powered tools and practical career solutions to help job seekers create stronger applications, improve their professional profiles, and navigate their job search with greater confidence.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are growing our team and are looking for a creative and proactive <strong>Social Media Manager</strong> to grow CareerSwift's presence across social media and build an engaged community around our brand.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a <strong>Social Media Manager</strong>, you will manage CareerSwift's social media presence, create engaging content, interact with our audience, and help develop campaigns that increase brand awareness and engagement.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will work closely with the marketing and content teams to turn CareerSwift's products, career insights, and industry trends into relevant and engaging social media content.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and manage social media content calendars across relevant platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create and publish engaging posts, captions, short-form content, and promotional materials.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage day-to-day community engagement, including comments, messages, and audience interactions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor social media trends and identify opportunities for relevant and timely content.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with content, marketing, and design teams on campaigns and creative projects.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track social media performance and prepare basic reports on reach, engagement, and audience growth.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Continuously test and improve content based on performance data and audience feedback.</p></li></ul><h2>What We Are Looking For</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1–3 years of experience in social media management, digital marketing, content marketing, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of major social media platforms and their content formats.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written communication and copywriting skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Creative mindset with a strong understanding of what makes content engaging.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to analyze social media performance and use insights to improve content.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organization skills and ability to manage multiple content projects independently.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with SaaS, technology, AI, career, or digital products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with short-form video platforms such as TikTok, Instagram Reels, or YouTube Shorts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with tools such as Canva, Figma, Buffer, Hootsuite, or similar platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building or growing an online community or brand presence.</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$50,000 - $68,000 per year</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><h2>What We Offer</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fully remote work environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunity to grow the social presence of an innovative AI-powered product.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Creative freedom and the opportunity to contribute your own ideas.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborative and supportive team environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunities for professional growth as CareerSwift expands.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Apply today and help us build a social media presence that connects CareerSwift with the next generation of job seekers.</strong></p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 50,000 - 68,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"CareerSwift is a technology company focused on making the job search process simpler, faster, and more effective. Our platform combines AI-powered tools and practical career solutions to help job seekers create stronger applications, improve their professional profiles, and navigate their job search with greater confidence.\n\n \n\nWe are growing our team and are looking for a creative and proactive Social Media Manager to grow CareerSwift's presence across social media and build an engaged community around our brand.\n\n \n\nAs a Social Media Manager, you will manage CareerSwift's social media presence, create engaging content, interact with our audience, and help develop campaigns that increase brand awareness and engagement.\n\nYou will work closely with the marketing and content teams to turn CareerSwift's products, career insights, and industry trends into relevant and engaging social media content.\n\n\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Develop and manage social media content calendars across relevant platforms.\n\n - Create and publish engaging posts, captions, short-form content, and promotional materials.\n\n - Manage day-to-day community engagement, including comments, messages, and audience interactions.\n\n - Monitor social media trends and identify opportunities for relevant and timely content.\n\n - Collaborate with content, marketing, and design teams on campaigns and creative projects.\n\n - Track social media performance and prepare basic reports on reach, engagement, and audience growth.\n\n - Continuously test and improve content based on performance data and audience feedback.\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 1–3 years of experience in social media management, digital marketing, content marketing, or a related field.\n\n - Strong understanding of major social media platforms and their content formats.\n\n - Excellent written communication and copywriting skills.\n\n - Creative mindset with a strong understanding of what makes content engaging.\n\n - Ability to analyze social media performance and use insights to improve content.\n\n - Strong organization skills and ability to manage multiple content projects independently.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience working with SaaS, technology, AI, career, or digital products.\n\n - Experience with short-form video platforms such as TikTok, Instagram Reels, or YouTube Shorts.\n\n - Familiarity with tools such as Canva, Figma, Buffer, Hootsuite, or similar platforms.\n\n - Experience building or growing an online community or brand presence.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$50,000 - $68,000 per year, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Fully remote work environment.\n\n - Opportunity to grow the social presence of an innovative AI-powered product.\n\n - Creative freedom and the opportunity to contribute your own ideas.\n\n - Collaborative and supportive team environment.\n\n - Opportunities for professional growth as CareerSwift expands.\n\nApply today and help us build a social media presence that connects CareerSwift with the next generation of job seekers.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSalary Range: 50,000 - 68,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"3aae203b-79f4-485e-b338-42fae9a8de91","title":"Content Writer / Copywriter","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-04T14:48:52.263+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/3aae203b-79f4-485e-b338-42fae9a8de91","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/3aae203b-79f4-485e-b338-42fae9a8de91/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CareerSwift is a technology company focused on making the job search process simpler, faster, and more effective. Our platform combines AI-powered tools and practical career solutions to help job seekers create stronger applications, improve their professional profiles, and navigate their job search with greater confidence.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are growing our team and are looking for a creative and detail-oriented <strong>Content Writer / Copywriter</strong> to create clear, engaging, and conversion-focused content across CareerSwift's digital channels.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a <strong>Content Writer / Copywriter</strong>, you will create content that helps communicate CareerSwift's products, features, and value to job seekers. You will work with the marketing team to develop content for our website, blog, social media, email campaigns, and other marketing materials.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ideal candidate can adapt their writing style to different audiences and formats while keeping content clear, useful, and consistent with the CareerSwift brand.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Write and edit content for websites, blogs, social media, email campaigns, and marketing materials.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create engaging copy for product features, landing pages, campaigns, and promotional materials.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Research topics related to careers, job searching, recruitment, technology, and AI.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adapt messaging and tone for different audiences and digital channels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with marketing and other teams to develop content based on campaign and business goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Edit and proofread content to ensure accuracy, clarity, grammar, and consistency.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use performance insights and feedback to improve existing content.</p></li></ul><h2>What We Are Looking For</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1–3 years of experience in content writing, copywriting, marketing, journalism, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong English writing and editing skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to write clear, engaging, and audience-focused content.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent grammar, spelling, and attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to research topics and turn information into useful content.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working independently and meeting deadlines in a remote environment.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience writing for SaaS, technology, AI, career, or other digital products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic understanding of SEO and content marketing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience creating content for social media or email marketing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with AI writing and content creation tools.</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$50,000 - $68,000 per year</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><h2>What We Offer</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fully remote work environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunity to create content for an innovative AI-powered product.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to marketing, technology, AI, and career development.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborative and supportive team environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunities for professional growth as CareerSwift expands.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Apply today and help us tell the CareerSwift story through content that informs, engages, and inspires job seekers.</strong></p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 50,000 - 68,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"CareerSwift is a technology company focused on making the job search process simpler, faster, and more effective. Our platform combines AI-powered tools and practical career solutions to help job seekers create stronger applications, improve their professional profiles, and navigate their job search with greater confidence.\n\n \n\nWe are growing our team and are looking for a creative and detail-oriented Content Writer / Copywriter to create clear, engaging, and conversion-focused content across CareerSwift's digital channels.\n\n \n\nAs a Content Writer / Copywriter, you will create content that helps communicate CareerSwift's products, features, and value to job seekers. You will work with the marketing team to develop content for our website, blog, social media, email campaigns, and other marketing materials.\n\nThe ideal candidate can adapt their writing style to different audiences and formats while keeping content clear, useful, and consistent with the CareerSwift brand.\n\n\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Write and edit content for websites, blogs, social media, email campaigns, and marketing materials.\n\n - Create engaging copy for product features, landing pages, campaigns, and promotional materials.\n\n - Research topics related to careers, job searching, recruitment, technology, and AI.\n\n - Adapt messaging and tone for different audiences and digital channels.\n\n - Collaborate with marketing and other teams to develop content based on campaign and business goals.\n\n - Edit and proofread content to ensure accuracy, clarity, grammar, and consistency.\n\n - Use performance insights and feedback to improve existing content.\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 1–3 years of experience in content writing, copywriting, marketing, journalism, or a related field.\n\n - Strong English writing and editing skills.\n\n - Ability to write clear, engaging, and audience-focused content.\n\n - Excellent grammar, spelling, and attention to detail.\n\n - Ability to research topics and turn information into useful content.\n\n - Comfortable working independently and meeting deadlines in a remote environment.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience writing for SaaS, technology, AI, career, or other digital products.\n\n - Basic understanding of SEO and content marketing.\n\n - Experience creating content for social media or email marketing.\n\n - Familiarity with AI writing and content creation tools.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$50,000 - $68,000 per year, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Fully remote work environment.\n\n - Opportunity to create content for an innovative AI-powered product.\n\n - Exposure to marketing, technology, AI, and career development.\n\n - Collaborative and supportive team environment.\n\n - Opportunities for professional growth as CareerSwift expands.\n\nApply today and help us tell the CareerSwift story through content that informs, engages, and inspires job seekers.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSalary Range: 50,000 - 68,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"f061d8b4-c2ae-45bc-b0b8-1ebc5b90614d","title":"Client Account Manager","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-04T14:50:16.523+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/f061d8b4-c2ae-45bc-b0b8-1ebc5b90614d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/f061d8b4-c2ae-45bc-b0b8-1ebc5b90614d/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CareerSwift is a technology company focused on making the job search process simpler, faster, and more effective. Our platform combines AI-powered tools and practical career solutions to help job seekers create stronger applications, improve their professional profiles, and navigate their job search with greater confidence.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are growing our team and are looking for a proactive and customer-focused <strong>Client Account Manager</strong> to build strong relationships with clients and ensure they receive a positive experience with CareerSwift.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a <strong>Client Account Manager</strong>, you will be responsible for managing day-to-day communication with CareerSwift clients, understanding their needs, coordinating requests, and helping ensure they get the most value from our products and services.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will work closely with internal teams to resolve issues, communicate client feedback, and support the overall client experience. This role is ideal for someone who enjoys working with people, is highly organized, and can confidently manage multiple client relationships.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as a primary point of contact for assigned clients and manage day-to-day communication.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain positive, professional relationships with clients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understand client needs and help identify appropriate CareerSwift solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate client requests and follow up with internal teams to ensure timely resolution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor account activity and proactively address potential issues or concerns.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate client records, notes, and account information in internal systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collect client feedback and communicate relevant insights to the product, support, and marketing teams.</p></li></ul><h2>What We Are Looking For</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1–3 years of experience in account management, customer success, client services, or a related role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and relationship-building skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Customer-focused approach with strong problem-solving abilities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent organization and ability to manage multiple accounts and priorities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with CRM systems and other digital tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently in a remote environment.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with SaaS, technology, AI, or digital products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing B2B client accounts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with customer success or account management platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience identifying opportunities to improve client retention or engagement.</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$50,000 - $70,000 per year</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><h2>What We Offer</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fully remote work environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunity to work with an innovative AI-powered technology product.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Direct interaction with clients and exposure to different areas of the business.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborative and supportive team environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunities for professional growth as CareerSwift expands.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Apply today and help CareerSwift build lasting client relationships while making the job search experience smarter and more effective.</strong></p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 50,000 - 70,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"CareerSwift is a technology company focused on making the job search process simpler, faster, and more effective. Our platform combines AI-powered tools and practical career solutions to help job seekers create stronger applications, improve their professional profiles, and navigate their job search with greater confidence.\n\n \n\nWe are growing our team and are looking for a proactive and customer-focused Client Account Manager to build strong relationships with clients and ensure they receive a positive experience with CareerSwift.\n\n \n\nAs a Client Account Manager, you will be responsible for managing day-to-day communication with CareerSwift clients, understanding their needs, coordinating requests, and helping ensure they get the most value from our products and services.\n\nYou will work closely with internal teams to resolve issues, communicate client feedback, and support the overall client experience. This role is ideal for someone who enjoys working with people, is highly organized, and can confidently manage multiple client relationships.\n\n\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Serve as a primary point of contact for assigned clients and manage day-to-day communication.\n\n - Build and maintain positive, professional relationships with clients.\n\n - Understand client needs and help identify appropriate CareerSwift solutions.\n\n - Coordinate client requests and follow up with internal teams to ensure timely resolution.\n\n - Monitor account activity and proactively address potential issues or concerns.\n\n - Maintain accurate client records, notes, and account information in internal systems.\n\n - Collect client feedback and communicate relevant insights to the product, support, and marketing teams.\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 1–3 years of experience in account management, customer success, client services, or a related role.\n\n - Strong communication and relationship-building skills.\n\n - Customer-focused approach with strong problem-solving abilities.\n\n - Excellent organization and ability to manage multiple accounts and priorities.\n\n - Comfortable working with CRM systems and other digital tools.\n\n - Ability to work independently in a remote environment.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience working with SaaS, technology, AI, or digital products.\n\n - Experience managing B2B client accounts.\n\n - Familiarity with customer success or account management platforms.\n\n - Experience identifying opportunities to improve client retention or engagement.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$50,000 - $70,000 per year, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Fully remote work environment.\n\n - Opportunity to work with an innovative AI-powered technology product.\n\n - Direct interaction with clients and exposure to different areas of the business.\n\n - Collaborative and supportive team environment.\n\n - Opportunities for professional growth as CareerSwift expands.\n\nApply today and help CareerSwift build lasting client relationships while making the job search experience smarter and more effective.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSalary Range: 50,000 - 70,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"ba2c3b68-9252-4c65-9bd7-5a0033f60a95","title":"Graphic Designer","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-04T14:53:25.423+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/ba2c3b68-9252-4c65-9bd7-5a0033f60a95","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/ba2c3b68-9252-4c65-9bd7-5a0033f60a95/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CareerSwift is a technology company focused on making the job search process simpler, faster, and more effective. Our platform combines AI-powered tools and practical career solutions to help job seekers create stronger applications, improve their professional profiles, and navigate their job search with greater confidence.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are growing our team and are looking for a creative and detail-oriented <strong>Graphic Designer</strong> to help bring the CareerSwift brand and products to life across digital channels.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a <strong>Graphic Designer</strong>, you will create visual content for CareerSwift's marketing, social media, website, product, and internal communications. You will work closely with the marketing and other teams to turn ideas and campaigns into clear, engaging, and visually consistent designs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is a good fit for a designer who can combine creativity with strong attention to detail and understands how to adapt visual content for different digital formats.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create graphics and visual assets for social media, marketing campaigns, websites, and other digital channels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop designs for promotional materials, presentations, advertisements, and company communications.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain consistent use of CareerSwift's visual identity, typography, colors, and brand guidelines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adapt designs for different platforms, formats, and audience needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with marketing and other teams to understand creative requirements and deliver designs on time.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review and refine designs based on feedback and performance insights.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Organize and maintain design files and reusable visual assets.</p></li></ul><h2>What We Are Looking For</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1–3 years of experience in graphic design or a related field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong portfolio demonstrating digital and marketing design work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency with design tools such as Adobe Creative Cloud, Figma, Canva, or similar.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good understanding of typography, composition, layout, and visual hierarchy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and ability to follow brand guidelines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to manage multiple projects and meet deadlines in a remote environment.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing content for social media and digital advertising.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic understanding of UI/UX or web design principles.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with technology, SaaS, AI, or digital products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic motion design or video editing skills.</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$50,000 - $70,000 per year</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><h2>What We Offer</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fully remote work environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunity to work with an innovative AI-powered technology product.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Creative ownership and the opportunity to contribute to CareerSwift's visual identity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborative and supportive team environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunities for professional growth as the company expands.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Apply today and help us create visual experiences that make CareerSwift stand out.</strong></p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 50,000 - 70,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"CareerSwift is a technology company focused on making the job search process simpler, faster, and more effective. Our platform combines AI-powered tools and practical career solutions to help job seekers create stronger applications, improve their professional profiles, and navigate their job search with greater confidence.\n\n \n\nWe are growing our team and are looking for a creative and detail-oriented Graphic Designer to help bring the CareerSwift brand and products to life across digital channels.\n\n \n\nAs a Graphic Designer, you will create visual content for CareerSwift's marketing, social media, website, product, and internal communications. You will work closely with the marketing and other teams to turn ideas and campaigns into clear, engaging, and visually consistent designs.\n\nThis role is a good fit for a designer who can combine creativity with strong attention to detail and understands how to adapt visual content for different digital formats.\n\n\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Create graphics and visual assets for social media, marketing campaigns, websites, and other digital channels.\n\n - Develop designs for promotional materials, presentations, advertisements, and company communications.\n\n - Maintain consistent use of CareerSwift's visual identity, typography, colors, and brand guidelines.\n\n - Adapt designs for different platforms, formats, and audience needs.\n\n - Collaborate with marketing and other teams to understand creative requirements and deliver designs on time.\n\n - Review and refine designs based on feedback and performance insights.\n\n - Organize and maintain design files and reusable visual assets.\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 1–3 years of experience in graphic design or a related field.\n\n - Strong portfolio demonstrating digital and marketing design work.\n\n - Proficiency with design tools such as Adobe Creative Cloud, Figma, Canva, or similar.\n\n - Good understanding of typography, composition, layout, and visual hierarchy.\n\n - Strong attention to detail and ability to follow brand guidelines.\n\n - Ability to manage multiple projects and meet deadlines in a remote environment.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience designing content for social media and digital advertising.\n\n - Basic understanding of UI/UX or web design principles.\n\n - Experience working with technology, SaaS, AI, or digital products.\n\n - Basic motion design or video editing skills.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$50,000 - $70,000 per year, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Fully remote work environment.\n\n - Opportunity to work with an innovative AI-powered technology product.\n\n - Creative ownership and the opportunity to contribute to CareerSwift's visual identity.\n\n - Collaborative and supportive team environment.\n\n - Opportunities for professional growth as the company expands.\n\nApply today and help us create visual experiences that make CareerSwift stand out.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSalary Range: 50,000 - 70,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"ba0267d6-1ccd-47d2-b16c-ca2a720de7bc","title":"Call Centre Agent, Inbound","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-04T14:54:42.848+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/ba0267d6-1ccd-47d2-b16c-ca2a720de7bc","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/ba0267d6-1ccd-47d2-b16c-ca2a720de7bc/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CareerSwift is a technology company focused on making the job search process simpler, faster, and more effective. Our platform combines AI-powered tools and practical career solutions to help job seekers create stronger applications, improve their professional profiles, and navigate their job search with greater confidence.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are growing our team and are looking for a friendly, reliable, and customer-focused <strong>Call Centre Agent, Inbound</strong> to join our remote team.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a <strong>Call Centre Agent, Inbound</strong>, you will be one of the first points of contact for CareerSwift customers and users. You will handle incoming calls, answer questions, provide information about our products and services, and help customers resolve common issues.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is focused on delivering a positive customer experience rather than cold calling or aggressive sales. You will also work with internal teams when a customer request requires additional assistance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Answer incoming customer calls in a friendly and professional manner.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understand customer questions and provide accurate information and assistance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help customers resolve common issues and guide them through basic processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Escalate complex or technical issues to the appropriate team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Accurately document customer interactions and resolutions in internal systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow up on open customer requests when required.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Share recurring customer questions or issues with the relevant internal teams.</p></li></ul><h2>What We Are Looking For</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong verbal communication and active listening skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Friendly, patient, and customer-focused approach.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to communicate clearly and professionally over the phone.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong problem-solving skills and attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with computers and online systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently and manage multiple customer requests.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous experience in a call centre, customer service, help desk, or similar role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience using CRM or customer support platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working remotely or supporting customers online.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Interest in technology, AI-powered products, or career development.</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$36,000 - $45,000 per year</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><h2>What We Offer</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fully remote work environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Training and support to help you succeed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with modern digital and AI-powered products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborative team environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunities for professional growth as CareerSwift expands.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Apply today and join CareerSwift in helping people navigate their job search with smarter technology and better support.</strong></p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 36,000 - 45,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"CareerSwift is a technology company focused on making the job search process simpler, faster, and more effective. Our platform combines AI-powered tools and practical career solutions to help job seekers create stronger applications, improve their professional profiles, and navigate their job search with greater confidence.\n\nWe are growing our team and are looking for a friendly, reliable, and customer-focused Call Centre Agent, Inbound to join our remote team.\n\n\n\n\nAs a Call Centre Agent, Inbound, you will be one of the first points of contact for CareerSwift customers and users. You will handle incoming calls, answer questions, provide information about our products and services, and help customers resolve common issues.\n\nThis role is focused on delivering a positive customer experience rather than cold calling or aggressive sales. You will also work with internal teams when a customer request requires additional assistance.\n\n\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Answer incoming customer calls in a friendly and professional manner.\n\n - Understand customer questions and provide accurate information and assistance.\n\n - Help customers resolve common issues and guide them through basic processes.\n\n - Escalate complex or technical issues to the appropriate team.\n\n - Accurately document customer interactions and resolutions in internal systems.\n\n - Follow up on open customer requests when required.\n\n - Share recurring customer questions or issues with the relevant internal teams.\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - Strong verbal communication and active listening skills.\n\n - Friendly, patient, and customer-focused approach.\n\n - Ability to communicate clearly and professionally over the phone.\n\n - Strong problem-solving skills and attention to detail.\n\n - Comfortable working with computers and online systems.\n\n - Ability to work independently and manage multiple customer requests.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Previous experience in a call centre, customer service, help desk, or similar role.\n\n - Experience using CRM or customer support platforms.\n\n - Experience working remotely or supporting customers online.\n\n - Interest in technology, AI-powered products, or career development.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$36,000 - $45,000 per year, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Fully remote work environment.\n\n - Training and support to help you succeed.\n\n - Experience working with modern digital and AI-powered products.\n\n - Collaborative team environment.\n\n - Opportunities for professional growth as CareerSwift expands.\n\nApply today and join CareerSwift in helping people navigate their job search with smarter technology and better support.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSalary Range: 36,000 - 45,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"c77e3ea6-8e70-46bb-b7bf-8d491e331bd9","title":"Virtual Assistant","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-04T14:56:00.931+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/c77e3ea6-8e70-46bb-b7bf-8d491e331bd9","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/c77e3ea6-8e70-46bb-b7bf-8d491e331bd9/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CareerSwift is a technology company focused on making the job search process simpler, faster, and more effective. Our platform combines AI-powered tools and practical career solutions to help job seekers create stronger applications, improve their professional profiles, and navigate their job search with greater confidence.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are growing our team and are looking for an organized and proactive <strong>Virtual Assistant</strong> to support day-to-day administrative and operational activities across the company.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a <strong>Virtual Assistant</strong>, you will provide remote administrative support to different members of the CareerSwift team. You will help keep information organized, maintain internal records, coordinate schedules, prepare documents, and handle a variety of recurring operational tasks.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a great opportunity for someone who is highly organized, comfortable working online, and interested in gaining experience in a fast-moving technology environment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous experience as a Virtual Assistant is helpful, but it is not required. We are open to candidates at the beginning of their careers who demonstrate strong communication, reliability, and attention to detail.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide day-to-day administrative support to the CareerSwift team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage calendars, meetings, reminders, and basic scheduling activities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Organize documents, spreadsheets, folders, and internal records.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enter, update, and verify information in company systems and databases.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare simple reports, documents, presentations, and spreadsheets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support data collection and basic research tasks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor shared inboxes and help organize incoming requests.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with updating CRM records, contact lists, and internal trackers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate information between different team members when needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help prepare materials for internal meetings and follow up on action items.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Perform basic internet research and summarize findings clearly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support customer, operations, marketing, or recruitment teams with routine administrative tasks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify missing or incorrect information and communicate issues to the appropriate team member.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with other operational and administrative projects as the company grows.</p></li></ul><h2>What We Are Looking For</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational and time-management skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good written and verbal communication skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High attention to detail and accuracy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working independently in a remote environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic proficiency with Microsoft Office or Google Workspace.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Confidence working with spreadsheets, email, online documents, and web-based tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to prioritize multiple tasks and meet deadlines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Willingness to learn new systems and processes.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous experience as a Virtual Assistant, Administrative Assistant, or Operations Assistant.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with CRM or project management tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with tools such as Google Workspace, Microsoft Office, Slack, Notion, Trello, Asana, or similar platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting a remote or distributed team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Interest in AI, technology, career development, or digital products.</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$38,000 - $48,000 per year</strong>, depending on experience and qualifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Additional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>What We Offer</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fully remote work environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunity to gain hands-on experience in a growing technology company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to different areas of the business, including operations, customer experience, marketing, and product.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Practical experience with modern digital and AI-powered tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Supportive and collaborative team environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunities to expand your responsibilities as the company grows.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you are organized, dependable, comfortable working with digital tools, and looking for an opportunity to build your experience in a remote technology company, we would be happy to hear from you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Apply today and join CareerSwift as we build smarter tools and experiences for modern job seekers.</strong></p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary Range:</strong> 38,000 - 48,000 USD (gross, annually)</p>","descriptionPlain":"CareerSwift is a technology company focused on making the job search process simpler, faster, and more effective. Our platform combines AI-powered tools and practical career solutions to help job seekers create stronger applications, improve their professional profiles, and navigate their job search with greater confidence.\n\n \n\nWe are growing our team and are looking for an organized and proactive Virtual Assistant to support day-to-day administrative and operational activities across the company.\n\n \n\nAs a Virtual Assistant, you will provide remote administrative support to different members of the CareerSwift team. You will help keep information organized, maintain internal records, coordinate schedules, prepare documents, and handle a variety of recurring operational tasks.\n\nThis is a great opportunity for someone who is highly organized, comfortable working online, and interested in gaining experience in a fast-moving technology environment.\n\nPrevious experience as a Virtual Assistant is helpful, but it is not required. We are open to candidates at the beginning of their careers who demonstrate strong communication, reliability, and attention to detail.\n\n\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Provide day-to-day administrative support to the CareerSwift team.\n\n - Manage calendars, meetings, reminders, and basic scheduling activities.\n\n - Organize documents, spreadsheets, folders, and internal records.\n\n - Enter, update, and verify information in company systems and databases.\n\n - Prepare simple reports, documents, presentations, and spreadsheets.\n\n - Support data collection and basic research tasks.\n\n - Monitor shared inboxes and help organize incoming requests.\n\n - Assist with updating CRM records, contact lists, and internal trackers.\n\n - Coordinate information between different team members when needed.\n\n - Help prepare materials for internal meetings and follow up on action items.\n\n - Perform basic internet research and summarize findings clearly.\n\n - Support customer, operations, marketing, or recruitment teams with routine administrative tasks.\n\n - Identify missing or incorrect information and communicate issues to the appropriate team member.\n\n - Assist with other operational and administrative projects as the company grows.\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - Strong organizational and time-management skills.\n\n - Good written and verbal communication skills.\n\n - High attention to detail and accuracy.\n\n - Comfortable working independently in a remote environment.\n\n - Basic proficiency with Microsoft Office or Google Workspace.\n\n - Confidence working with spreadsheets, email, online documents, and web-based tools.\n\n - Ability to prioritize multiple tasks and meet deadlines.\n\n - Willingness to learn new systems and processes.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Previous experience as a Virtual Assistant, Administrative Assistant, or Operations Assistant.\n\n - Experience working with CRM or project management tools.\n\n - Familiarity with tools such as Google Workspace, Microsoft Office, Slack, Notion, Trello, Asana, or similar platforms.\n\n - Experience supporting a remote or distributed team.\n\n - Interest in AI, technology, career development, or digital products.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$38,000 - $48,000 per year, depending on experience and qualifications.\n\nAdditional benefits and employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Fully remote work environment.\n\n - Opportunity to gain hands-on experience in a growing technology company.\n\n - Exposure to different areas of the business, including operations, customer experience, marketing, and product.\n\n - Practical experience with modern digital and AI-powered tools.\n\n - Supportive and collaborative team environment.\n\n - Opportunities to expand your responsibilities as the company grows.\n\nIf you are organized, dependable, comfortable working with digital tools, and looking for an opportunity to build your experience in a remote technology company, we would be happy to hear from you.\n\nApply today and join CareerSwift as we build smarter tools and experiences for modern job seekers.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nSalary Range: 38,000 - 48,000 USD (gross, annually)","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"b30b1d15-7eb5-4db8-9a39-15c04d63d1d5","title":"Revenue Cycle Manager","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-07T13:52:52.835+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/b30b1d15-7eb5-4db8-9a39-15c04d63d1d5","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/b30b1d15-7eb5-4db8-9a39-15c04d63d1d5/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raventra Health</strong> is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a Revenue Cycle Manager to lead day-to-day Revenue Cycle Management operations and oversee the performance of the Revenue Cycle team. This role is responsible for operational efficiency, team performance, account resolution, revenue cycle KPIs, and continuous improvement across the patient financial lifecycle.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead and manage Revenue Cycle Specialists and other assigned team members.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Oversee daily billing, claims, payment, accounts receivable, and denial management activities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor revenue cycle performance and key operational metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review aging, denials, payment trends, and outstanding account balances.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify process gaps and implement improvements to increase efficiency and reimbursement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish priorities, workflows, and performance expectations for the Revenue Cycle team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review complex account issues and support escalation and resolution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with billing, coding, patient financial services, and other operational teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare and communicate performance updates and recommendations to internal stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure team activities follow established procedures, quality standards, and healthcare compliance requirements.</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing Revenue Cycle Management operations in a healthcare environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of the healthcare revenue cycle and reimbursement processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with billing, claims, accounts receivable, and denials management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven ability to lead, coach, and develop operational teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical and problem-solving skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience monitoring operational KPIs and performance metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational skills and ability to manage competing priorities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with healthcare, billing, and reporting systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to identify operational risks and drive practical improvements.</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing Revenue Cycle teams for provider groups or hospitals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with outsourced Revenue Cycle Management services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge of payer contracting, underpayments, credentialing, or patient financial services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience implementing new processes, systems, or client workflows.</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant Revenue Cycle Management leadership expertise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → Introductory conversation → Hiring manager interview → Offer</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Raventra Health is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals.\n\n \n\nWe are looking for a Revenue Cycle Manager to lead day-to-day Revenue Cycle Management operations and oversee the performance of the Revenue Cycle team. This role is responsible for operational efficiency, team performance, account resolution, revenue cycle KPIs, and continuous improvement across the patient financial lifecycle.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Lead and manage Revenue Cycle Specialists and other assigned team members.\n\n - Oversee daily billing, claims, payment, accounts receivable, and denial management activities.\n\n - Monitor revenue cycle performance and key operational metrics.\n\n - Review aging, denials, payment trends, and outstanding account balances.\n\n - Identify process gaps and implement improvements to increase efficiency and reimbursement.\n\n - Establish priorities, workflows, and performance expectations for the Revenue Cycle team.\n\n - Review complex account issues and support escalation and resolution.\n\n - Collaborate with billing, coding, patient financial services, and other operational teams.\n\n - Prepare and communicate performance updates and recommendations to internal stakeholders.\n\n - Ensure team activities follow established procedures, quality standards, and healthcare compliance requirements.\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - Experience managing Revenue Cycle Management operations in a healthcare environment.\n\n - Strong understanding of the healthcare revenue cycle and reimbursement processes.\n\n - Experience with billing, claims, accounts receivable, and denials management.\n\n - Proven ability to lead, coach, and develop operational teams.\n\n - Strong analytical and problem-solving skills.\n\n - Experience monitoring operational KPIs and performance metrics.\n\n - Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills.\n\n - Strong organizational skills and ability to manage competing priorities.\n\n - Comfortable working with healthcare, billing, and reporting systems.\n\n - Ability to identify operational risks and drive practical improvements.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience managing Revenue Cycle teams for provider groups or hospitals.\n\n - Experience with outsourced Revenue Cycle Management services.\n\n - Knowledge of payer contracting, underpayments, credentialing, or patient financial services.\n\n - Experience implementing new processes, systems, or client workflows.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant Revenue Cycle Management leadership expertise.\n\nBenefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → Introductory conversation → Hiring manager interview → Offer\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nRaventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"696ee589-f08a-44d3-b780-73b0479e6295","title":"Revenue Cycle Specialist","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-07T13:53:59.198+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/696ee589-f08a-44d3-b780-73b0479e6295","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/696ee589-f08a-44d3-b780-73b0479e6295/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raventra Health</strong> is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a Revenue Cycle Specialist to support day-to-day Revenue Cycle Management operations across the patient account lifecycle. This role may work across billing, claims, payment posting, accounts receivable, denials, and other revenue cycle activities to help ensure accurate and timely reimbursement for provider and hospital clients.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Process and review revenue cycle transactions across assigned client accounts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support claim submission, claim status follow-up, payment posting, and accounts receivable activities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review accounts for missing information, billing issues, and payment discrepancies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Investigate unpaid, rejected, and denied claims and route issues to the appropriate team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with account reconciliation and resolution of outstanding balances.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review payer and patient account information for accuracy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate records and documentation within relevant systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify recurring issues and escalate trends affecting revenue cycle performance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with billing, coding, denials, and patient financial services teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow established workflows, quality standards, and healthcare compliance requirements.</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in Revenue Cycle Management, medical billing, healthcare administration, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">General understanding of the healthcare revenue cycle from registration through payment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with claims, payer processes, billing, and accounts receivable.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and accuracy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to research account issues and resolve discrepancies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good organizational and time-management skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with healthcare and billing software.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and collaboration skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to manage multiple accounts or priorities independently.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Willingness to learn different revenue cycle functions and workflows.</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with outsourced Revenue Cycle Management services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge of medical coding, denials management, or payer processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with electronic health records or practice management systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with Revenue Cycle Management KPIs and reporting.</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant Revenue Cycle Management expertise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → Introductory conversation → Hiring manager interview → Offer</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Raventra Health is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals.\n\n \n\nWe are looking for a Revenue Cycle Specialist to support day-to-day Revenue Cycle Management operations across the patient account lifecycle. This role may work across billing, claims, payment posting, accounts receivable, denials, and other revenue cycle activities to help ensure accurate and timely reimbursement for provider and hospital clients.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Process and review revenue cycle transactions across assigned client accounts.\n\n - Support claim submission, claim status follow-up, payment posting, and accounts receivable activities.\n\n - Review accounts for missing information, billing issues, and payment discrepancies.\n\n - Investigate unpaid, rejected, and denied claims and route issues to the appropriate team.\n\n - Assist with account reconciliation and resolution of outstanding balances.\n\n - Review payer and patient account information for accuracy.\n\n - Maintain accurate records and documentation within relevant systems.\n\n - Identify recurring issues and escalate trends affecting revenue cycle performance.\n\n - Collaborate with billing, coding, denials, and patient financial services teams.\n\n - Follow established workflows, quality standards, and healthcare compliance requirements.\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - Experience in Revenue Cycle Management, medical billing, healthcare administration, or a related field.\n\n - General understanding of the healthcare revenue cycle from registration through payment.\n\n - Familiarity with claims, payer processes, billing, and accounts receivable.\n\n - Strong attention to detail and accuracy.\n\n - Ability to research account issues and resolve discrepancies.\n\n - Good organizational and time-management skills.\n\n - Comfortable working with healthcare and billing software.\n\n - Strong communication and collaboration skills.\n\n - Ability to manage multiple accounts or priorities independently.\n\n - Willingness to learn different revenue cycle functions and workflows.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience working with outsourced Revenue Cycle Management services.\n\n - Knowledge of medical coding, denials management, or payer processes.\n\n - Experience with electronic health records or practice management systems.\n\n - Familiarity with Revenue Cycle Management KPIs and reporting.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant Revenue Cycle Management expertise.\n\nBenefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → Introductory conversation → Hiring manager interview → Offer\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nRaventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"71611745-0920-44c6-aee6-90aed5b1ee93","title":"Patient Financial Services Specialist","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-07T13:55:08.789+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/71611745-0920-44c6-aee6-90aed5b1ee93","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/71611745-0920-44c6-aee6-90aed5b1ee93/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raventra Health</strong> is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a Patient Financial Services Specialist to support patient-facing financial operations, including account review, billing inquiries, payment coordination, and resolution of outstanding patient balances. This role works closely with billing, accounts receivable, and other Revenue Cycle teams to help ensure accurate account information and a positive patient financial experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review patient accounts, balances, payments, and billing information for accuracy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Respond to patient questions regarding statements, balances, payments, and insurance-related charges.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist patients with payment arrangements and available financial options.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Research and resolve patient account discrepancies and billing issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Process and document patient payments and account adjustments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate with billing and accounts receivable teams to resolve outstanding balances.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review insurance information and identify issues affecting patient responsibility.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate and complete documentation of patient financial interactions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Escalate complex billing or account issues when additional review is required.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow established privacy, compliance, and patient communication procedures.</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in patient financial services, medical billing, healthcare administration, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of healthcare billing, insurance, and patient responsibility.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and account reconciliation skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and verbal communication skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to handle sensitive financial and patient information professionally.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational and time-management skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working with healthcare billing and practice management systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to investigate issues and identify practical solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Customer-focused approach with strong interpersonal skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently in a remote environment.</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with a healthcare provider, hospital, or Revenue Cycle Management company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with patient payment portals and electronic billing systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with payment plans, financial assistance, or patient collections.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge of HIPAA requirements and healthcare privacy practices.</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant patient financial services expertise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → Introductory conversation → Hiring manager interview → Offer</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Raventra Health is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals.\n\n \n\nWe are looking for a Patient Financial Services Specialist to support patient-facing financial operations, including account review, billing inquiries, payment coordination, and resolution of outstanding patient balances. This role works closely with billing, accounts receivable, and other Revenue Cycle teams to help ensure accurate account information and a positive patient financial experience.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Review patient accounts, balances, payments, and billing information for accuracy.\n\n - Respond to patient questions regarding statements, balances, payments, and insurance-related charges.\n\n - Assist patients with payment arrangements and available financial options.\n\n - Research and resolve patient account discrepancies and billing issues.\n\n - Process and document patient payments and account adjustments.\n\n - Coordinate with billing and accounts receivable teams to resolve outstanding balances.\n\n - Review insurance information and identify issues affecting patient responsibility.\n\n - Maintain accurate and complete documentation of patient financial interactions.\n\n - Escalate complex billing or account issues when additional review is required.\n\n - Follow established privacy, compliance, and patient communication procedures.\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - Experience in patient financial services, medical billing, healthcare administration, or a related field.\n\n - Understanding of healthcare billing, insurance, and patient responsibility.\n\n - Strong attention to detail and account reconciliation skills.\n\n - Excellent written and verbal communication skills.\n\n - Ability to handle sensitive financial and patient information professionally.\n\n - Strong organizational and time-management skills.\n\n - Comfortable working with healthcare billing and practice management systems.\n\n - Ability to investigate issues and identify practical solutions.\n\n - Customer-focused approach with strong interpersonal skills.\n\n - Ability to work independently in a remote environment.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with a healthcare provider, hospital, or Revenue Cycle Management company.\n\n - Familiarity with patient payment portals and electronic billing systems.\n\n - Experience with payment plans, financial assistance, or patient collections.\n\n - Knowledge of HIPAA requirements and healthcare privacy practices.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant patient financial services expertise.\n\nBenefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → Introductory conversation → Hiring manager interview → Offer\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nRaventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"11965666-0ded-4236-a283-6f526fc7de00","title":"Health Information Management Operations Specialist","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-07T13:56:13.897+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/11965666-0ded-4236-a283-6f526fc7de00","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/11965666-0ded-4236-a283-6f526fc7de00/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raventra Health</strong> is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Health Information Management Operations Specialist, you will support the organization, accuracy, and availability of health information used across Raventra Health’s revenue cycle operations. You will coordinate medical records workflows, monitor documentation processes, and work with provider, coding, billing, and compliance teams to ensure information is handled accurately and appropriately.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate health information management workflows across assigned provider and hospital clients</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor the organization, completeness, and availability of medical records and supporting documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review health information processes for accuracy, consistency, and compliance with established procedures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate with provider teams to resolve documentation and record-management issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support medical records retrieval for coding, billing, claims, audits, and appeals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track outstanding documentation requests and ensure timely follow-up</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate records and documentation within applicable healthcare information systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify recurring documentation or information management issues and recommend process improvements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with coding, billing, compliance, and medical records teams to resolve operational issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support internal reviews and audits involving health information and documentation</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in Health Information Management, medical records, healthcare administration, or a related healthcare operations role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of medical records, health information workflows, and healthcare documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with electronic health records or health information systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge of HIPAA and appropriate handling of protected health information</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and ability to identify incomplete or inconsistent documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent organizational and time-management skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to coordinate multiple requests and deadlines across different teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and problem-solving skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently and effectively in a fully remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIPAA-compliant private workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">RHIT or RHIA certification</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or another major electronic health record system</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Health Information Management or medical records training</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting coding, billing, claims, or clinical documentation teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with provider groups or hospitals</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, certifications, and relevant healthcare operations expertise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Raventra Health is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Health Information Management Operations Specialist, you will support the organization, accuracy, and availability of health information used across Raventra Health’s revenue cycle operations. You will coordinate medical records workflows, monitor documentation processes, and work with provider, coding, billing, and compliance teams to ensure information is handled accurately and appropriately.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Coordinate health information management workflows across assigned provider and hospital clients\n\n - Monitor the organization, completeness, and availability of medical records and supporting documentation\n\n - Review health information processes for accuracy, consistency, and compliance with established procedures\n\n - Coordinate with provider teams to resolve documentation and record-management issues\n\n - Support medical records retrieval for coding, billing, claims, audits, and appeals\n\n - Track outstanding documentation requests and ensure timely follow-up\n\n - Maintain accurate records and documentation within applicable healthcare information systems\n\n - Identify recurring documentation or information management issues and recommend process improvements\n\n - Collaborate with coding, billing, compliance, and medical records teams to resolve operational issues\n\n - Support internal reviews and audits involving health information and documentation\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 2+ years of experience in Health Information Management, medical records, healthcare administration, or a related healthcare operations role\n\n - Strong understanding of medical records, health information workflows, and healthcare documentation\n\n - Experience working with electronic health records or health information systems\n\n - Knowledge of HIPAA and appropriate handling of protected health information\n\n - Strong attention to detail and ability to identify incomplete or inconsistent documentation\n\n - Excellent organizational and time-management skills\n\n - Ability to coordinate multiple requests and deadlines across different teams\n\n - Strong communication and problem-solving skills\n\n - Ability to work independently and effectively in a fully remote environment\n\n - HIPAA-compliant private workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - RHIT or RHIA certification\n\n - Experience with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or another major electronic health record system\n\n - Health Information Management or medical records training\n\n - Experience supporting coding, billing, claims, or clinical documentation teams\n\n - Experience working with provider groups or hospitals\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, certifications, and relevant healthcare operations expertise.\n\nBenefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nRaventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"ec165f43-42ce-4608-8ae5-381723a867bd","title":"Revenue Cycle Management Implementation Specialist","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-07T13:57:28.706+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/ec165f43-42ce-4608-8ae5-381723a867bd","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/ec165f43-42ce-4608-8ae5-381723a867bd/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raventra Health</strong> is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Revenue Cycle Management Implementation Specialist, you will support the onboarding of new provider and hospital clients and help transition their revenue cycle operations to Raventra Health. You will coordinate requirements, documentation, workflows, systems, and internal teams to ensure a smooth and well-organized implementation.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate implementation activities for new provider and hospital clients</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gather and document client requirements, workflows, systems, and operational processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate the collection and transfer of information needed to establish client operations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Map existing client workflows and identify requirements for Raventra Health processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with billing, coding, claims, AR, payment posting, and other operational teams to prepare for go-live</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track implementation milestones, dependencies, risks, and outstanding action items</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate system setup, workflow configuration, testing, and issue resolution with relevant teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support user acceptance testing and validate that processes meet documented client requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare implementation documentation, training materials, and operational handoff information</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate implementation progress, risks, and next steps to internal and client stakeholders</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in implementation, project coordination, healthcare operations, revenue cycle management, or a related field</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of healthcare revenue cycle workflows and provider operations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience gathering requirements, documenting processes, and coordinating cross-functional activities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong project organization and ability to manage multiple implementation tasks and deadlines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication skills and ability to work with both clients and internal operational teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong problem-solving skills and ability to identify and resolve implementation issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to manage changing priorities while maintaining clear documentation and follow-through</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently and effectively in a fully remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIPAA-compliant private workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience implementing revenue cycle management or healthcare systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or other healthcare platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with project management tools such as Jira, Asana, or <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Monday.com\">Monday.com</a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge of billing, coding, claims, or accounts receivable operations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with provider groups or hospitals</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare implementation expertise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Raventra Health is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As a Revenue Cycle Management Implementation Specialist, you will support the onboarding of new provider and hospital clients and help transition their revenue cycle operations to Raventra Health. You will coordinate requirements, documentation, workflows, systems, and internal teams to ensure a smooth and well-organized implementation.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Coordinate implementation activities for new provider and hospital clients\n\n - Gather and document client requirements, workflows, systems, and operational processes\n\n - Coordinate the collection and transfer of information needed to establish client operations\n\n - Map existing client workflows and identify requirements for Raventra Health processes\n\n - Work with billing, coding, claims, AR, payment posting, and other operational teams to prepare for go-live\n\n - Track implementation milestones, dependencies, risks, and outstanding action items\n\n - Coordinate system setup, workflow configuration, testing, and issue resolution with relevant teams\n\n - Support user acceptance testing and validate that processes meet documented client requirements\n\n - Prepare implementation documentation, training materials, and operational handoff information\n\n - Communicate implementation progress, risks, and next steps to internal and client stakeholders\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 2+ years of experience in implementation, project coordination, healthcare operations, revenue cycle management, or a related field\n\n - Understanding of healthcare revenue cycle workflows and provider operations\n\n - Experience gathering requirements, documenting processes, and coordinating cross-functional activities\n\n - Strong project organization and ability to manage multiple implementation tasks and deadlines\n\n - Excellent communication skills and ability to work with both clients and internal operational teams\n\n - Strong problem-solving skills and ability to identify and resolve implementation issues\n\n - Ability to manage changing priorities while maintaining clear documentation and follow-through\n\n - Ability to work independently and effectively in a fully remote environment\n\n - HIPAA-compliant private workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience implementing revenue cycle management or healthcare systems\n\n - Familiarity with Epic, Athena, eClinicalWorks, or other healthcare platforms\n\n - Experience with project management tools such as Jira, Asana, or Monday.com http://Monday.com\n\n - Knowledge of billing, coding, claims, or accounts receivable operations\n\n - Experience working with provider groups or hospitals\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare implementation expertise.\n\nBenefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nRaventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"7fb07103-1d8f-49c8-8e9d-f90497effb87","title":"Underpayment & Contract Variance Analyst","department":"R&D","team":"R&D","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-07T13:58:39.945+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Remote"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/7fb07103-1d8f-49c8-8e9d-f90497effb87","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/careerswift.ai/7fb07103-1d8f-49c8-8e9d-f90497effb87/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raventra Health</strong> is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As an Underpayment &amp; Contract Variance Analyst, you will analyze payer payments to identify instances where provider clients may have been reimbursed below their contracted rates. You will compare claims and payment data against payer contract terms, investigate discrepancies, and work with revenue cycle teams to support payment recovery and prevent recurring reimbursement issues.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>WHAT YOU WILL DO</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review paid claims and compare reimbursement against applicable payer contract terms and fee schedules</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify underpayments, incorrect adjustments, and other contract-related payment variances</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Research claim history, payment details, and contract provisions to determine the cause of discrepancies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Quantify potential revenue recovery opportunities and prioritize issues for follow-up</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare supporting documentation for payment disputes, reconsiderations, and appeals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate with AR, denials, revenue integrity, and payer contracting teams to resolve identified variances</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track recovery activity and maintain accurate records of identified underpayments and outcomes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify recurring payer payment patterns and communicate findings to relevant teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare reports summarizing underpayments, recovery opportunities, and contract variance trends</p></li></ul><h2>WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in healthcare revenue cycle, reimbursement analysis, payment integrity, or a related role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of healthcare reimbursement, payer payments, and revenue cycle processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience comparing payments against contracts, fee schedules, or expected reimbursement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to interpret EOBs, ERAs, payment details, and payer information</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with excellent attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to research payment discrepancies and identify their root causes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong Excel skills and experience working with financial or claims data</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to communicate findings clearly and collaborate with billing, AR, and payer teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently and manage multiple analysis and recovery priorities in a remote environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HIPAA-compliant private workspace</p></li></ul><h2>NICE TO HAVE</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Medicare, Medicaid, and commercial payer reimbursement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge of payer contracts and fee schedules</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical billing or coding experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with revenue integrity or payment variance analysis</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">SQL, Power BI, or other data analysis experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with provider groups or hospitals</p></li></ul><h2>COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare revenue cycle expertise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Benefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>HIRING PROCESS</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Application review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>EQUAL OPPORTUNITY</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote</p>","descriptionPlain":"Raventra Health is a medical services company providing outsourced billing, coding, and claims processing solutions for provider groups and hospitals. As an Underpayment & Contract Variance Analyst, you will analyze payer payments to identify instances where provider clients may have been reimbursed below their contracted rates. You will compare claims and payment data against payer contract terms, investigate discrepancies, and work with revenue cycle teams to support payment recovery and prevent recurring reimbursement issues.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\n - Review paid claims and compare reimbursement against applicable payer contract terms and fee schedules\n\n - Identify underpayments, incorrect adjustments, and other contract-related payment variances\n\n - Research claim history, payment details, and contract provisions to determine the cause of discrepancies\n\n - Quantify potential revenue recovery opportunities and prioritize issues for follow-up\n\n - Prepare supporting documentation for payment disputes, reconsiderations, and appeals\n\n - Coordinate with AR, denials, revenue integrity, and payer contracting teams to resolve identified variances\n\n - Track recovery activity and maintain accurate records of identified underpayments and outcomes\n\n - Identify recurring payer payment patterns and communicate findings to relevant teams\n\n - Prepare reports summarizing underpayments, recovery opportunities, and contract variance trends\n\n\nWHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 2+ years of experience in healthcare revenue cycle, reimbursement analysis, payment integrity, or a related role\n\n - Strong understanding of healthcare reimbursement, payer payments, and revenue cycle processes\n\n - Experience comparing payments against contracts, fee schedules, or expected reimbursement\n\n - Ability to interpret EOBs, ERAs, payment details, and payer information\n\n - Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with excellent attention to detail\n\n - Ability to research payment discrepancies and identify their root causes\n\n - Strong Excel skills and experience working with financial or claims data\n\n - Ability to communicate findings clearly and collaborate with billing, AR, and payer teams\n\n - Ability to work independently and manage multiple analysis and recovery priorities in a remote environment\n\n - HIPAA-compliant private workspace\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with Medicare, Medicaid, and commercial payer reimbursement\n\n - Knowledge of payer contracts and fee schedules\n\n - Medical billing or coding experience\n\n - Experience with revenue integrity or payment variance analysis\n\n - SQL, Power BI, or other data analysis experience\n\n - Experience working with provider groups or hospitals\n\n\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS\n\nCompensation will be discussed during the interview and will reflect the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and relevant healthcare revenue cycle expertise.\n\nBenefits and additional employment details will be discussed during the hiring process.\n\n\n\n\nHIRING PROCESS\n\nApplication review → introductory conversation → hiring manager interview → offer.\n\n\n\n\nEQUAL OPPORTUNITY\n\nRaventra Health is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. If you need an accommodation at any stage of the hiring process, please contact us and we will work with you to provide appropriate support.\n\n\n\n\nLocation: Remote","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}}],"apiVersion":"1"}